7889d315-63f7-48ae-ac5d-fe49266a074d	b201a860-05a3-4ddc-bb89-4c4271177271	biomarker_chat	[{"role": "user", "content": "What affects ALT (SGPT) levels? List the main factors briefly.", "timestamp": "2025-12-31T00:52:09.243Z"}, {"role": "assistant", "content": "Here are the main factors that affect ALT (SGPT) levels:\\n\\n**Factors that raise ALT:**\\n• Liver damage (hepatitis, fatty liver, cirrhosis)\\n• Medications (acetaminophen, statins, antibiotics)\\n• Alcohol consumption\\n• Muscle damage/injury\\n• Heart attack or heart failure\\n• Obesity and metabolic syndrome\\n• Infections (viral, bacterial)\\n\\n**Factors that lower ALT:**\\n• Kidney disease\\n• Certain medications\\n• Vitamin B6 deficiency\\n• Age (levels naturally decrease)\\n\\nYour recent ALT of 54 IU/L is slightly elevated (normal is typically <40 IU/L for men, <32 for women). Consider discussing this with your healthcare provider to identify the cause.", "timestamp": "2025-12-31T00:52:09.243Z"}]	\N	2025-12-31 00:52:09.243+00	2025-12-31 00:52:09.243+00	ALT (SGPT)	Chat about ALT (SGPT)
