2\\n- Triglycerides (100) are excellent\\n\\n**Other Markers** ⭐⭐⭐\\n- Thyroid function looks normal, though TSH (2.1) is in the higher-normal range\\n- Vitamin D (45) is adequate but could be optimized\\n- B12, iron, and ferritin all look good\\n\\n## 🎯 **Optimization Opportunities**\\n\\n1. **LDL Fine-tuning**: You're close to optimal! Consider discussing with your doctor:\\n   - Increasing soluble fiber intake\\n   - Plant sterols/stanols\\n   - Evaluating if current approach needs tweaking\\n\\n2. **Vitamin D**: At 45 ng/mL, you might benefit from modest supplementation to reach 50-70 ng/mL range\\n\\n3. **TSH Monitoring**: While normal, some feel better with TSH closer to 1.0-2.0 range\\n\\n## 📈 **What's Working Well**\\nWhatever you've been doing since 2023 is paying off - your cholesterol trend is moving in the right direction while maintaining excellent glucose control!\\n\\nWould you like me to dive deeper into any specific area or discuss potential optimization strategies?", "timestamp": "2025-12-31T03:03:57.133Z"}]	\N	2025-12-31 03:03:57.133+00	2025-12-31 03:03:57.133+00	\N	\N
