814c38ad-c6d4-4811-acbf-6db049e3ede1	b201a860-05a3-4ddc-bb89-4c4271177271	30-Day Portugal Family Road Trip (OLD)	Circular loop - Lisbon → Algarve → Central Coast → Porto → Lisbon. Flying LAX → Lisbon round trip, ~1,200 km driving over 30 days.	2026-06-15	2026-07-14	Los Angeles (LAX)	Lisbon, Portugal	both	\N	5	\N	[]	planning	f	\N	\N	\N	2026-01-10 19:02:33.52+00	2026-01-13 15:21:21.566806+00	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	{"basics": {"completed": false, "auto_suggested": false}, "segments": {"completed": false, "auto_suggested": false}, "accommodations": {"completed": false, "auto_suggested": false}, "days_activities": {"completed": false, "auto_suggested": false}}
2e2ae20a-832b-4e7c-9419-2afdb506b6ab	b201a860-05a3-4ddc-bb89-4c4271177271	Portugal Summer 2026 CORRECT	A month-long family adventure through Portugal, designed around the philosophy of 'depth over breadth.' Rather than racing between tourist highlights, this itinerary establishes six distinct bases where the Liu family can settle in, explore authentically, and experience Portugal as residents rather than tourists.\n\nThe route moves strategically: beginning in Lisbon to ease jet lag while exploring Age of Discovery history, then south to the sun-baked Alentejo plains and the dramatic western Algarv	2026-06-14	2026-07-14	Los Angeles	Portugal	flying	\N	5	\N	[]	planning	f	\N	\N	\N	2026-01-11 15:15:47.986+00	2026-02-06 17:53:46.388323+00	{"trains": [], "ferries": [], "flights": {"return": {"to": "LAX", "date": "2026-07-17", "from": "LIS", "notes": "18h 15m layover in Montreal. Arrives LAX same day.", "airline": "Air Canada", "arrival_time": "11:02", "flight_number": "AC 813 + AC 775", "departure_time": "11:25"}, "outbound": {"to": "LIS", "date": "2026-06-16", "from": "LAX", "notes": "Departs June 16, arrives June 17 at 9:20am. Connection in Montreal (1h 15m layover).", "airline": "Air Canada", "arrival_time": "09:20", "flight_number": "AC 778 + AC 812", "departure_time": "12:05"}, "internal_flights": []}, "car_rental": {"notes": "30-day rental. Request Via Verde transponder for electronic tolls.", "needed": true, "child_seats": "Bring Mifold boosters for Parker/Charlotte. Rent or bring travel seat for Xander.", "pick_up_date": "2026-06-17", "pick_up_time": "10:00", "vehicle_type": "SUV or minivan", "drop_off_date": "2026-07-17", "drop_off_time": "08:30", "insurance_notes": "Decline CDW - Chase Ink Preferred provides primary coverage", "pick_up_location": "Lisbon Airport (LIS)", "drop_off_location": "Lisbon Airport (LIS)", "company_preference": "Flexible - compare rates"}, "driving_summary": {"toll_notes": "Portugal uses electronic tolls (Via Verde). Rent transponder with car or register plate online.", "route_notes": "Circular route: Lisbon → South (Alentejo, Sagres) → North (Douro, Porto, Gerês) → Lisbon airport. Only 2 drives over 2 hours.", "total_hours": 17, "driving_days": 6, "longest_single_drive": "4 hours (Sagres to Douro Valley, broken with lunch stop)"}}	A month-long family adventure through Portugal, designed for depth over breadth. The Lius will experience the real Portugal: from the Age of Discovery history in Lisbon to the wild mountains of Peneda-Gerês, with strategic stops in the sun-baked Alentejo plains, the dramatic cliffs of the western Algarve, the terraced wine country of the Douro Valley, and the tile-covered charm of Porto. With only 6 true bases plus an airport hotel, the family minimizes packing and unpacking while maximizing immersion in each region.	Starting in Lisbon, the family heads south into the Alentejo — Portugal's rural heartland. From there, a detour to the southwestern tip at Sagres for dramatic sea cliffs. Then the long drive north to the Douro Valley wine country, followed by Porto, and finally deep into the Peneda-Gerês National Park — Portugal's wildest corner. The trip ends with a 4-hour drive to an airport hotel for stress-free departure.	Rest days built into Alentejo (Day 5), Douro (Day 6), and Peneda-Gerês (Day 6). Day 1 in Lisbon is jet lag recovery only. Every day assumes pool/rest from 12-3pm. Seven nights in final destination allows maximum flexibility.	Portugal	PT	31	30	{"notes": "Alentejo and Peneda-Gerês are very affordable regions. Douro quintas and Lisbon will be the highest accommodation costs.", "strategy": "Mix of points and paid, splurge on unique experiences (quinta stay, fado dinner), save on basics", "save_moments": ["Grocery runs for breakfast/snacks", "Picnic lunches", "Alentejo accommodations (affordable region)"], "estimated_daily": "€250-350/day excluding accommodation", "splurge_moments": ["Douro Valley quinta stay", "Fado dinner in Lisbon", "Kayak tour at Benagil caves"], "accommodation_split": "40% points (Lisbon, Porto), 60% paid (rural areas)"}	{"basics": {"completed": false, "auto_suggested": false}, "segments": {"completed": false, "auto_suggested": false}, "accommodations": {"completed": false, "auto_suggested": false}, "days_activities": {"completed": false, "auto_suggested": false}}
