ae0d4ade-f91a-43d8-b81e-0c9126f695e2	2e2ae20a-832b-4e7c-9419-2afdb506b6ab	\N	Slave Market Museum (Mercado de Escravos)	\N	attraction	\N	\N	\N	\N	Praça do Infante D. Henrique	\N	\N	https://maps.google.com/?q=Slave+Market+Museum+Lagos	\N	\N	\N	\N	USD	\N	\N	f	\N	t	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	999	\N	2026-02-06 17:40:11.216936+00	2026-02-06 17:40:11.216936+00	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	optional	unconfirmed	\N	\N	4f5d2d2f-c4d2-4427-95f4-1e5facc954da	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	f	\N	{"hours": "Tue-Sun 10am-1pm, 2-6pm (closed Mondays)"}	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	{"what_it_is": "Europe's first African slave market, established in 1444. Museum documents this dark chapter with bilingual exhibits explaining trade routes, conditions, and resistance movements. Exhibits are somber but not graphically disturbing.", "parental_guidance": "For Parker (8): 'A long time ago, people from Europe—including from right here in Lagos—did something terribly wrong. They captured people from Africa and forced them to work, treating them as property instead of people. This was called slavery. We visit places like this to remember what happened, honor those who suffered, and make sure nothing like it happens again.'"}	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	general_option	Parker ready for deeper historical context; want to address difficult history; homeschool curriculum connection; rainy day indoor option	Heavy subject matter. Parker (8) can begin to understand, but requires parental judgment on timing and readiness. Charlotte (5) and Xander (3) too young—would require family split with one parent staying outside with younger children. Listed as optional museum visit rather than scheduled activity to leave decision to parents.
