48619dd4-be4e-4293-b335-e8cc4065ebf0	2e2ae20a-832b-4e7c-9419-2afdb506b6ab	\N	Igreja de Santo António (Church of St. Anthony)	\N	attraction	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	https://maps.google.com/?q=Igreja+de+Santo+Antonio+Lagos	\N	\N	\N	\N	USD	\N	\N	f	\N	t	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	999	\N	2026-02-06 17:40:11.419147+00	2026-02-06 17:40:11.419147+00	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	optional	unconfirmed	\N	\N	4f5d2d2f-c4d2-4427-95f4-1e5facc954da	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	f	\N	{"hours": "Tue-Sun 10am-1pm, 2-6pm (closed Mondays)"}	{"parker": {"scripts": ["This church has so much gold it looks fake, but it's all real—hundreds of years old! Can you find St. Anthony and the fish in the blue tiles?"], "age_at_trip": 8}, "xander": {"scripts": ["Look! So shiny! Gold! Pretty! Can you see the angels?"], "age_at_trip": 3}, "charlotte": {"scripts": ["This church is covered in GOLD! It's like a treasure chest inside! Can you find any angels?"], "age_at_trip": 5}}	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	{"what_it_is": "Baroque masterpiece considered one of finest church interiors in Portugal. Extraordinary gilded woodwork (talha dourada), blue-and-white azulejo tiles, ceiling paintings depicting St. Anthony's miracles."}	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	general_option	Want cultural depth; kids interested in gold/treasure; rainy day indoor option; have 30 min to fill in Lagos Old Town	Brief visit (20-30 min) that's not essential given limited time. The boat tour and fortress provide sufficient cultural immersion. However, if walking through Lagos Old Town, this is worth ducking into—the gilded interior genuinely impresses even children.
