ation—they stand exactly as they have for two centuries. For kids, they look like fairy houses. The flat granite threshing floor offers safe, open space for exploration. The communal nature tells a story of village cooperation."}, "interesting_facts": ["The oldest espigueiro predates the French Revolution", "A single espigueiro could store 500-1000kg of grain", "Classified as National Monument since 1938"]}	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N
