0584552a-c397-49ff-9b87-23db892e509c	2e2ae20a-832b-4e7c-9419-2afdb506b6ab	0fe7865d-80e7-4c28-8bca-569f7cbefab6	Estremoz Saturday Market	One of Portugal's biggest markets. Buy Bonecos figurines, sample cheese, browse antiques. SATURDAY ONLY.	activity	\N	10:15:00	\N	Feira de Estremoz	Rossio Marquês de Pombal, Estremoz	\N	\N	https://maps.google.com/?q=38.8413,-7.5877	One of Portugal's largest and most authentic markets. Not tourist-focused—serves locals. Perfect combination with morning Almendres Cromlech visit (on the way back to Évora).	\N	\N	\N	USD	\N	\N	f	\N	f	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	4	\N	2026-02-06 17:48:29.539456+00	2026-02-06 17:48:29.539456+00	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	unconfirmed	\N	\N	909968ea-bcec-49ea-b7a8-fffcd9249552	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	f	\N	\N	{"parker": {"scripts": ["Parker, this market isn't for tourists—it's where local farmers come to sell what they grow. Real Portuguese life!", "See those little clay figurines? Each one is handmade by families who have been making them for 400 years.", "Want to try some local cheese? Point to any one and they'll give you a sample.", "The whole town is made of white marble—even the benches and doorsteps. Can you find something made of marble?"], "age_at_trip": 8}, "xander": {"scripts": ["Xander, look at all the colors! Red tomatoes! Yellow lemons! Orange oranges!", "Can you find a chicken? A piggy? Point to the animal!", "Want to taste? Open wide! Yummy cheese!", "Let's find a toy! A little person made of clay!"], "age_at_trip": 3}, "charlotte": {"scripts": ["Charlotte, let's find the most colorful thing in the market! Maybe a fruit? A toy? A blanket?", "Can you find a little clay person? There are farmers, dancers, animals... which one is your favorite?", "Want to taste some honey? The bees that made it live right here in Portugal!", "Let's find something for you to bring home from Portugal!"], "age_at_trip": 5}}	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	{"the_story": {"content": "Weekly markets have been held in Estremoz since the Middle Ages, when the town's strategic position made it a natural trading hub. Today's market continues traditions centuries old: farmers display produce on blankets, animals change hands, and Bonecos de Estremoz—the famous clay figurines unique to this town—are sold by the families who have made them for generations.\\n\\nThe figurines are UNESCO-recognized intangible heritage, handcrafted using techniques unchanged since the 17th century. Each figure tells a story of Alentejo life: farmers, musicians, religious figures, everyday scenes. Buying one directly from the maker—rather than from a Lisbon tourist shop—ensures authenticity and supports the tradition."}, "what_it_is": "One of Portugal's largest and most authentic weekly markets, held every Saturday in the 'White Marble City,' featuring fresh produce, antiques, crafts, and the famous colorful Bonecos de Estremoz clay figurines.", "what_youll_see": [{"area": "Produce Section", "highlights": ["Fresh fruits and vegetables", "Local cheeses (Évora, Serpa, Nisa)", "Cured meats", "Honey and olive oil"]}, {"area": "Crafts Section", "highlights": ["Bonecos de Estremoz clay figurines", "Cork products", "Textiles", "Pottery"]}, {"area": "Antiques Section", "highlights": ["Vintage items", "Traditional tools", "Linens", "Ceramics"]}], "why_it_matters": {"content": "The Feira de Estremoz isn't a tourist market—it serves local residents from across the Alentejo. Farmers bring produce they grew, grandmothers sell vegetables from their gardens, craftspeople display work made in home workshops. This authenticity provides a window into rural Portuguese life that curated experiences can't match.\\n\\nEstremoz itself is called the 'White Marble City' for the famous quarries nearby. The town center features marble everywhere—fountains, benches, even doorsteps. The 27-meter Torre das Três Coroas offers panoramic views. Combined with the Almendres Cromlech visit (Estremoz is on the return route to Évora), the market fills a natural gap in your Saturday schedule."}, "interesting_facts": ["One of Portugal's largest weekly markets", "Bonecos de Estremoz are UNESCO intangible heritage", "Estremoz marble is world-famous—even doorsteps are marble", "Market has operated for centuries", "46 km from Évora (45 minutes)"]}	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N
