7ea608cf-0cd5-4072-8583-02e484796e70	2e2ae20a-832b-4e7c-9419-2afdb506b6ab	5616876d-5789-4b88-93ae-35bec3bc1ca4	Drive to Grilo's Farm	15-20 minute drive. Contact farm for exact directions.	transport	\N	08:00:00	\N	Route to farm	15 minutes from Évora center	\N	\N	Contact for directions	Horseback riding is a family must-do requirement. Lusitano horses are Portugal's iconic breed with 25,000-year history in Alentejo. Farm accommodates all ages—trail rides for older kids, pony/petting zoo for little ones.	\N	\N	\N	USD	\N	\N	f	\N	f	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	1	\N	2026-02-06 17:48:29.764841+00	2026-02-06 17:48:29.764841+00	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	unconfirmed	\N	\N	909968ea-bcec-49ea-b7a8-fffcd9249552	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	f	\N	\N	{"parker": {"scripts": ["Parker, would you like to ride a horse whose ancestors carried soldiers into battle thousands of years ago?", "Lusitano horses are one of the oldest horse breeds in the world. Cave paintings show horses just like these from 17,000 years ago!", "When you learn to ride, the horse will respond to even tiny signals from your hands and legs. That's because for thousands of years, riders trained these horses to move super quickly.", "Look at the trees with the red-brown bark—that's cork! The horses live surrounded by the same cork forests we visited at Almendres.", "Watch how the horse moves—Lusitanos have a special smooth gait because they were bred to carry riders comfortably for hours."], "age_at_trip": 8}, "xander": {"scripts": ["Xander, we're going to see HORSES! Big horses! Can you say 'horse'?", "Let's feel the horse's soft nose—so soft! Like velvet!", "Smell the hay—can you smell it? Horses eat hay!", "Watch the horse eat a carrot from your flat hand—hold FLAT like a plate!", "And there's piggies! Chickens! A donkey! Can you make animal sounds?"], "age_at_trip": 3}, "charlotte": {"scripts": ["Charlotte, today we're going to meet some very special horses! There's also a pony just your size!", "Horses talk with their ears—when a horse puts its ears forward, it's saying 'I'm happy to see you!'", "You can help brush the pony's mane—gently, gently, like brushing your own hair.", "There's also a donkey named Tobias who loves to say hello! What sound does a donkey make?", "And a piggy named Rosa! She's a special kind of pig called a Vietnamese pig."], "age_at_trip": 5}}	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	{"the_story": {"content": "Cave paintings in Alentejo's Escoural Caves (17,000 BCE) depict horses virtually identical to modern Lusitanos—making this breed one of the oldest recognizable horse types still in existence. Portugal's geographical isolation allowed these horses to develop independently for 15,000 years.\\n\\nThe breed was perfected through an extraordinary partnership with wild bulls along the Tejo River floodplains. Horses learned that staying near bulls protected them from predators (wolves avoided bulls), but getting too close risked attack from aggressive animals. This 'dance' between horse and bull, refined over millennia, created the Lusitano's legendary intelligence, agility, and 'cow sense.'\\n\\nSpanish conquistadors brought Iberian horses to the Americas, where they founded every major horse breed from the Argentine Criollo to the American Mustang. The Lusitano's DNA runs through horses across two continents. When your family rides at Grilo's Farm, you're experiencing a living tradition stretching back to the Neolithic."}, "what_it_is": "A family-friendly working farm offering horse rides, pony experiences, and a petting zoo—where visitors can experience Portugal's legendary Lusitano horses in their native landscape.", "what_youll_see": [{"area": "Horse Paddocks", "highlights": ["Lusitano and Portuguese horses", "Working farm environment", "Cork oak landscape"]}, {"area": "Petting Zoo", "highlights": ["Donkey Tobias", "Vietnamese pig Rosa", "Sheep, guinea pigs, chickens, ducks", "Pony for young children"]}, {"area": "Trail Ride Route", "highlights": ["Cork oak montado landscape", "Rolling Alentejo plains", "Traditional farm buildings"]}], "why_it_matters": {"content": "The Lusitano is Portugal's iconic horse breed—one of the oldest saddle horses in the world with origins traced 25,000 years to cave paintings in the Alentejo's Escoural Caves. These horses shaped history, serving in Roman cavalry, dancing with bulls in mounted bullfights, and sailing with Portuguese explorers to found horse populations across the Americas.\\n\\nGrilo's Farm offers the rare opportunity to experience these legendary horses on family-friendly terms. Parker can take a real trail ride through the Alentejo landscape, experiencing the same rolling plains that have bred Lusitanos for millennia. Charlotte and Xander can meet friendly farm animals including pony, donkey Tobias, sheep, Vietnamese pig Rosa, guinea pigs, and chickens.\\n\\nThe morning timing serves two purposes: avoiding dangerous midday heat and experiencing the farm when horses are most active and comfortable. The 2-3 hour duration allows for a full experience without exhausting young children."}, "interesting_facts": ["Lusitanos are depicted in cave paintings 17,000+ years old", "Portugal's geographical isolation allowed independent breed development", "All American horse breeds trace partial ancestry to Iberian horses", "The breed's agility was developed through 'dancing' with wild bulls", "Lusitanos are still used in Portuguese mounted bullfighting"]}	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N
f3ef9bde-c547-4caa-b9d9-31aa950f3c6c	2e2ae20a-832b-4e7c-9419-2afdb506b6ab	5616876d-5789-4b88-93ae-35bec3bc1ca4	Family Horseback Riding at Grilo's Farm	Parker: trail ride. Charlotte/Xander: pony, farm animals. Split parents if needed. Book 24hrs ahead.	activity	\N	08:30:00	\N	Grilo's Farm	15 minutes from Évora center	\N	\N	Contact for directions	Horseback riding is a family must-do requirement. Lusitano horses are Portugal's iconic breed with 25,000-year history in Alentejo. Farm accommodates all ages—trail rides for older kids, pony/petting zoo for little ones.	\N	\N	\N	USD	\N	\N	f	\N	f	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	2	\N	2026-02-06 17:48:29.764841+00	2026-02-06 17:48:29.764841+00	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	unconfirmed	\N	\N	909968ea-bcec-49ea-b7a8-fffcd9249552	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	f	\N	\N	{"parker": {"scripts": ["Parker, would you like to ride a horse whose ancestors carried soldiers into battle thousands of years ago?", "Lusitano horses are one of the oldest horse breeds in the world. Cave paintings show horses just like these from 17,000 years ago!", "When you learn to ride, the horse will respond to even tiny signals from your hands and legs. That's because for thousands of years, riders trained these horses to move super quickly.", "Look at the trees with the red-brown bark—that's cork! The horses live surrounded by the same cork forests we visited at Almendres.", "Watch how the horse moves—Lusitanos have a special smooth gait because they were bred to carry riders comfortably for hours."], "age_at_trip": 8}, "xander": {"scripts": ["Xander, we're going to see HORSES! Big horses! Can you say 'horse'?", "Let's feel the horse's soft nose—so soft! Like velvet!", "Smell the hay—can you smell it? Horses eat hay!", "Watch the horse eat a carrot from your flat hand—hold FLAT like a plate!", "And there's piggies! Chickens! A donkey! Can you make animal sounds?"], "age_at_trip": 3}, "charlotte": {"scripts": ["Charlotte, today we're going to meet some very special horses! There's also a pony just your size!", "Horses talk with their ears—when a horse puts its ears forward, it's saying 'I'm happy to see you!'", "You can help brush the pony's mane—gently, gently, like brushing your own hair.", "There's also a donkey named Tobias who loves to say hello! What sound does a donkey make?", "And a piggy named Rosa! She's a special kind of pig called a Vietnamese pig."], "age_at_trip": 5}}	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	{"the_story": {"content": "Cave paintings in Alentejo's Escoural Caves (17,000 BCE) depict horses virtually identical to modern Lusitanos—making this breed one of the oldest recognizable horse types still in existence. Portugal's geographical isolation allowed these horses to develop independently for 15,000 years.\\n\\nThe breed was perfected through an extraordinary partnership with wild bulls along the Tejo River floodplains. Horses learned that staying near bulls protected them from predators (wolves avoided bulls), but getting too close risked attack from aggressive animals. This 'dance' between horse and bull, refined over millennia, created the Lusitano's legendary intelligence, agility, and 'cow sense.'\\n\\nSpanish conquistadors brought Iberian horses to the Americas, where they founded every major horse breed from the Argentine Criollo to the American Mustang. The Lusitano's DNA runs through horses across two continents. When your family rides at Grilo's Farm, you're experiencing a living tradition stretching back to the Neolithic."}, "what_it_is": "A family-friendly working farm offering horse rides, pony experiences, and a petting zoo—where visitors can experience Portugal's legendary Lusitano horses in their native landscape.", "what_youll_see": [{"area": "Horse Paddocks", "highlights": ["Lusitano and Portuguese horses", "Working farm environment", "Cork oak landscape"]}, {"area": "Petting Zoo", "highlights": ["Donkey Tobias", "Vietnamese pig Rosa", "Sheep, guinea pigs, chickens, ducks", "Pony for young children"]}, {"area": "Trail Ride Route", "highlights": ["Cork oak montado landscape", "Rolling Alentejo plains", "Traditional farm buildings"]}], "why_it_matters": {"content": "The Lusitano is Portugal's iconic horse breed—one of the oldest saddle horses in the world with origins traced 25,000 years to cave paintings in the Alentejo's Escoural Caves. These horses shaped history, serving in Roman cavalry, dancing with bulls in mounted bullfights, and sailing with Portuguese explorers to found horse populations across the Americas.\\n\\nGrilo's Farm offers the rare opportunity to experience these legendary horses on family-friendly terms. Parker can take a real trail ride through the Alentejo landscape, experiencing the same rolling plains that have bred Lusitanos for millennia. Charlotte and Xander can meet friendly farm animals including pony, donkey Tobias, sheep, Vietnamese pig Rosa, guinea pigs, and chickens.\\n\\nThe morning timing serves two purposes: avoiding dangerous midday heat and experiencing the farm when horses are most active and comfortable. The 2-3 hour duration allows for a full experience without exhausting young children."}, "interesting_facts": ["Lusitanos are depicted in cave paintings 17,000+ years old", "Portugal's geographical isolation allowed independent breed development", "All American horse breeds trace partial ancestry to Iberian horses", "The breed's agility was developed through 'dancing' with wild bulls", "Lusitanos are still used in Portuguese mounted bullfighting"]}	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N
