6ac6407f-922d-4d4c-a872-918b46497678	2e2ae20a-832b-4e7c-9419-2afdb506b6ab	a5653997-917a-4a85-86d7-390497d9457e	Pool and rest	Long break before Monsaraz evening. Pool, lunch, naps. ESSENTIAL—big evening ahead.	rest	\N	11:30:00	\N	Convento do Espinheiro	Canaviais, 7000-502 Évora	\N	\N	https://maps.google.com/?q=38.6008,-7.8883	Maximum loyalty benefits with Marriott Gold status. Exceptional pools (essential). Historic 15th-century monastery with 5th night free on points. Daily complimentary activities for families.	\N	\N	\N	USD	\N	\N	f	\N	f	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	4	\N	2026-02-06 17:48:29.987079+00	2026-02-06 17:48:29.987079+00	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	unconfirmed	\N	\N	909968ea-bcec-49ea-b7a8-fffcd9249552	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	f	\N	\N	{"parker": {"scripts": ["Parker, we're staying in a real castle-monastery where actual Portuguese kings lived 500 years ago!", "King João II made important decisions here about explorers sailing around the world.", "Tomorrow at the hotel tour, you can ask about secret passages and look for the oldest stone in the building.", "The monks who lived here took vows of silence—can you imagine not talking for a whole day?"], "age_at_trip": 8}, "xander": {"scripts": ["Xander, big pool! See the big trees? Those trees are OLD—older than Mommy and Daddy!", "We sleep in a castle with big, big doors!", "Splash splash in the pool!", "Look at all the grass to run on! Run run run!"], "age_at_trip": 3}, "charlotte": {"scripts": ["Charlotte, our hotel used to be home to monks who wore long brown robes and sang songs every day!", "But guess what? REAL princesses also stayed here!", "There are TWO pools—one where you can splash and one where the grown-ups swim.", "We'll have dinner in a room with a curved ceiling that looks like a cave!"], "age_at_trip": 5}}	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	{"the_story": {"content": "The monastery was founded around 1400 after a shepherd reported a vision of the Virgin Mary above a thorn bush (espinheiro means 'thorn bush'). The site was consecrated in 1458 for the Hieronymite Order, the same order that built Lisbon's Jerónimos Monastery.\\n\\nPortuguese royalty regularly visited and stayed at the Convento do Espinheiro. Kings João II, Manuel I, Afonso V, and Sebastião all slept within these walls. The church contains one of Portugal's most prestigious noble family pantheons—generations of Portuguese aristocracy are interred here.\\n\\nA three-year restoration transformed the monastery into a luxury hotel while preserving original frescoes, Gothic architecture, and sacred spaces. The conversion maintained the cloister, chapel, and monastic atmosphere while adding modern comforts. Today's guests walk the same corridors as medieval monks and Renaissance kings."}, "what_it_is": "A meticulously restored 15th-century monastery converted into a 5-star luxury hotel, part of Marriott's Luxury Collection, featuring 92 rooms across 8 hectares of gardens with multiple pools and daily complimentary activities.", "what_youll_see": [{"area": "Historic Monastery", "highlights": ["15th-century church", "Gothic cloisters", "Original frescoes", "Noble family pantheon"]}, {"area": "Pool Complex", "highlights": ["Outdoor infinity pool", "Two children's pools", "17-meter indoor heated pool", "Poolside service"]}, {"area": "Gardens", "highlights": ["8 hectares", "Ancient olive groves", "Tennis court", "Children's playground"]}, {"area": "Dining", "highlights": ["Divinus Restaurant in Gothic wine cellar", "Olive Restaurant for family-friendly Italian", "Poolside service"]}], "why_it_matters": {"content": "The Convento do Espinheiro represents the optimal balance of luxury experience, loyalty benefits, and family functionality for your Alentejo stay. As a Marriott Luxury Collection property, your Gold Elite status provides meaningful benefits: 25% bonus points, room upgrades when available, and 2:00 PM late checkout.\\n\\nThe property addresses every family accommodation criterion. Pools are essential in Alentejo's June heat—the hotel delivers with outdoor infinity pool, two children's pools, AND a 17-meter indoor heated pool for backup. The 8 hectares of gardens provide space for children to run. Connecting rooms accommodate your family of 5. And the 5th Night Free benefit on points bookings makes the 5-night stay 20% more efficient.\\n\\nBeyond logistics, the hotel offers an experience unavailable elsewhere: sleeping in a 15th-century monastery where Portuguese kings once stayed, dining in a Gothic wine cellar, and participating in daily complimentary activities including wine tasting and historical tours."}, "interesting_facts": ["Founded after shepherd's vision of Virgin Mary above thorn bush (1400)", "Kings João II, Manuel I, Afonso V, and Sebastião all stayed here", "Three-year restoration preserved original frescoes", "8 hectares of gardens with ancient olive trees", "Daily complimentary wine tasting in Gothic cistern", "Children's playground on property"]}	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N
