9d0e8faa-0bab-49c3-9f41-70ea9ee229e7	2e2ae20a-832b-4e7c-9419-2afdb506b6ab	a5653997-917a-4a85-86d7-390497d9457e	Explore Monsaraz village	Medieval village with only 150 residents. Castle, walls, church, wandering. Carry Xander—cobblestones defeat strollers.	activity	\N	05:30:00	\N	Monsaraz	Monsaraz, Reguengos de Monsaraz	\N	\N	https://maps.google.com/?q=38.4400,-7.3836	Perfectly preserved hilltop medieval village with only 150 residents. Castle with unique bullring, panoramic views over Europe's largest artificial lake, and world's first certified Dark Sky destination for stargazing.	\N	\N	\N	USD	\N	\N	f	\N	f	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	6	\N	2026-02-06 17:48:29.987079+00	2026-02-06 17:48:29.987079+00	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	unconfirmed	\N	\N	909968ea-bcec-49ea-b7a8-fffcd9249552	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	f	\N	\N	{"parker": {"scripts": ["Parker, this castle was built by KNIGHTS TEMPLAR—the same knights from stories about crusaders and treasure!", "They wore white cloaks with red crosses. Can you find the Templar crosses hidden around the village?", "From these towers, you could see the enemy coming from SPAIN—can you spot that country over there?", "The bullring inside the castle is super unusual—most castles didn't have places for bullfights!", "Count how many towers you can see on the walls. Medieval defenders needed to see every direction!"], "age_at_trip": 8}, "xander": {"scripts": ["Xander, let's count the doors in the big wall! One... two... three... FOUR giant doors!", "Can you find a BLUE door? A WHITE wall? A YELLOW flower?", "Look at the BIG WATER down there! So much water!", "The walls go all the way around like a circle. Let's walk along the wall!", "Can you find a kitty cat? Village cats like to hide in sunny spots!"], "age_at_trip": 3}, "charlotte": {"scripts": ["Charlotte, only 150 people live in this whole village—that's like your class times five!", "Can you imagine living in a real castle? This village is like a GIANT BLANKET FORT with stone walls!", "Let's find the prettiest flower growing on a white house. Can you find a blue door? A green door?", "The streets are made of bumpy stones. Let's walk like princesses—carefully, carefully!", "Look at the BIG WATER down there! That lake is SO big you can't see the other side!"], "age_at_trip": 5}}	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	{"the_story": {"content": "Evidence of fortified settlement at Monsaraz dates to prehistoric times. Known as 'Saris' under Moorish rule, the village was captured in 1167 by Geraldo the Fearless—the same warrior who took Évora. Definitively reconquered in 1232 by King Sancho II with crucial support from the Knights Templar, whose Order of Christ cross symbols still appear throughout the village.\\n\\nThe current castle was built by King Dinis in the 14th century. Uniquely, its inner courtyard was converted to a bullring—still used during annual festivals—making this possibly the only castle arena in Portugal. The village's strategic position on the Spanish border made it an important military outpost for centuries.\\n\\nLake Alqueva, the vast body of water visible below the village walls, is actually Europe's largest artificial lake (250 km²), created by a dam completed in 2002. The lake transformed the landscape—and the local economy—while the ancient village watches from above, unchanged by progress.\\n\\nIn 2011, the region became the world's first certified Starlight Tourism Destination, recognized by UNESCO for its exceptionally dark skies. Light pollution is virtually absent, allowing views of the Milky Way that most Europeans never experience."}, "what_it_is": "A perfectly preserved hilltop medieval village perched 899 feet above the Guadiana Valley, overlooking Europe's largest artificial lake (Alqueva), with only ~150 permanent residents—and the world's first certified Starlight Tourism Destination.", "what_youll_see": [{"area": "Castle and Bullring", "highlights": ["14th-century walls", "Unique bullring in castle courtyard", "Panoramic views over Lake Alqueva"]}, {"area": "Main Street (Rua Direita)", "highlights": ["Whitewashed houses", "Traditional shops", "Stone streets worn by centuries of use"]}, {"area": "Village Gates", "highlights": ["Four original gates", "Porta da Vila with Gothic arch", "Two defensive towers"]}, {"area": "Igreja Matriz", "highlights": ["Medieval fresco 'The Good and Bad Judge'", "Templar tomb", "Cool interior"]}], "why_it_matters": {"content": "Monsaraz represents one of the most authentic medieval experiences in Europe. Unlike over-touristed villages, Monsaraz receives only about 50,000 visitors annually, preserving its genuine character. It won '7 Wonders of Portugal – Villages' (2017) in the Monument Villages category.\\n\\nThe village's magic lies in its accidental preservation. In the mid-19th century, the municipality seat transferred away, and Monsaraz essentially 'turned its back on time'—no modern development occurred within the walls, creating today's living museum. The 150 residents live in homes their families have occupied for generations.\\n\\nFor families, Monsaraz offers multiple draws: the castle with its unique bullring, panoramic views over Lake Alqueva, car-free streets safe for children to explore, and the Dark Sky Reserve for stargazing. The timing (arrive 5 PM, stay for sunset) allows the village to reveal itself as light changes from golden afternoon to pink sunset to star-filled night."}, "interesting_facts": ["Only 150 residents live within the walls", "The castle bullring is unique in Portugal—possibly the only castle arena still used", "Cars are banned inside the walls during daytime", "Lake Alqueva below is Europe's largest artificial lake (250 km²)", "Dark Sky Alqueva Reserve was the world's first certified Starlight Tourism Destination", "Won '7 Wonders of Portugal – Villages' in 2017", "The famous medieval fresco 'The Good and Bad Judge' is one of Portugal's rarest surviving secular medieval paintings"]}	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N
