262ed6b8-88b3-4e8b-8cea-1ebe24a77f96	2e2ae20a-832b-4e7c-9419-2afdb506b6ab	488e96b4-8858-4ace-9aa9-2678000d2cf7	Drive to Herdade do Esporão	45 minutes. Scenic drive through wine country.	transport	\N	09:30:00	\N	Route to Reguengos	Apartado 31, 7200-999 Reguengos de Monsaraz	\N	\N	https://maps.google.com/?q=38.3801,-7.5607	Comprehensive wine experience on 1,840-hectare organic estate. Michelin-starred restaurant. Activities for children (gardens, tunnel, wildlife). 11 AM English tour works with family schedule.	\N	\N	\N	USD	\N	\N	f	\N	f	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	1	\N	2026-02-06 17:48:30.207648+00	2026-02-06 17:48:30.207648+00	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	unconfirmed	\N	\N	909968ea-bcec-49ea-b7a8-fffcd9249552	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	f	\N	\N	{"parker": {"scripts": ["Parker, this farm has been owned by the same families for 750 years! The tower on every wine bottle was built in 1267.", "People were making wine here when knights still fought with swords. Can you imagine farming the same land for 30 generations?", "The tunnel we're walking through is filled with barrels aging wine. Can you smell the oak?", "This place is SO old that archaeologists found 5,000-year-old settlements here—about as old as Almendres Cromlech!"], "age_at_trip": 8}, "xander": {"scripts": ["Xander, look at the big tower! It's SO tall! Can you count the windows?", "Let's find vegetables in the garden! Red tomatoes! Green peppers!", "Walk through the tunnel—is it cold or warm? Dark or light?", "Look at the BIG water! Can you see any ducks?"], "age_at_trip": 3}, "charlotte": {"scripts": ["Charlotte, let's explore the garden! Can you find tomatoes? Peppers? Herbs that smell like pizza?", "The cooks in the restaurant pick vegetables from THIS garden to make dinner. Farm to table!", "Let's walk through the tunnel—it's dark and cool and full of big barrels!", "Can you spot any birds near the lake? People have seen almost EVERY kind of bird in Portugal here!"], "age_at_trip": 5}}	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	{"the_story": {"content": "The estate's boundaries haven't changed since 1267, when King Afonso III granted the land to Fernão Anes de Aboim. The iconic Esporão Tower appearing on every wine label dates to this period. For 750 years, the land has produced wine under the same family names and boundaries.\\n\\nModern transformation began in 1973, and the first wines appeared in 1985. Since 2022, all 700+ hectares operate under organic certification—making this one of Portugal's largest organic estates. The Michelin-starred restaurant earned a Green Star for sustainability, recognizing their commitment to environmental responsibility."}, "what_it_is": "A comprehensive wine tourism experience on an 1,840-hectare organic estate with unchanged boundaries since 1267, featuring vineyard tours, Michelin-starred restaurant, and family-friendly activities.", "what_youll_see": [{"area": "Winery Tour", "highlights": ["15-meter Barrels Tunnel", "Modern winemaking facilities", "Historic tower and chapel"]}, {"area": "Gardens", "highlights": ["2 hectares of vegetable gardens", "Seasonal fruits and herbs", "Kitchen supplies for restaurant"]}, {"area": "Landscape", "highlights": ["120-hectare reservoir", "90% of Alentejo birds spotted here", "Ancient olive groves"]}], "why_it_matters": {"content": "Alentejo is Portugal's largest wine-producing region, and Esporão represents the pinnacle of wine tourism in the region. The estate contains the Perdigões Archaeological Complex with Neolithic settlements dating back 5,000 years—proving this terroir has been valued for agriculture since prehistoric times.\\n\\nFor families, Esporão offers more than wine tasting. Children can explore 2 hectares of vegetable gardens, walk through the dramatic 15-meter Barrels Tunnel, visit the historic tower and chapel, and watch wildlife around the 120-hectare reservoir (90% of Alentejo birds have been spotted here). Parker and Charlotte can taste grape juice while parents taste wine—everyone has their beverage."}, "interesting_facts": ["Estate boundaries unchanged since 1267", "Contains 5,000-year-old Neolithic archaeological site", "700+ hectares organic certified since 2022", "Michelin-starred + Green Star for sustainability", "120-hectare reservoir supports 90% of Alentejo bird species"]}	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N
