3572db24-eed7-494c-abcb-66316c4d66e0	2e2ae20a-832b-4e7c-9419-2afdb506b6ab	b63eb49d-9258-4cca-a272-ac3b39f0fc4c	Walk to Jerónimos	5-minute walk.	hike	\N	08:45:00	\N	Belém	Av. Brasília, 1400-038 Lisboa	38.6916000	-9.2160000	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	USD	\N	\N	f	\N	f	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	1	\N	2026-02-06 17:49:05.017242+00	2026-02-06 17:49:05.017242+00	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	unconfirmed	\N	\N	ae7c1aaf-2a96-485b-9fa6-afe1724a55fb	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	f	\N	\N	{"parker": {"scripts": ["Parker, there's a rhinoceros carved here—based on a REAL rhino from 1515! First live rhino in Europe in a thousand years. Find it!", "Parker, the king tried to send that rhino to the Pope, but the ship SANK.", "Parker, count the cannon positions. Soldiers would fire at enemy ships."], "activities": ["Find rhinoceros carving", "Count cannon embrasures"]}, "xander": {"scripts": ["Xander, look at the BIG tower!", "Xander, there's a RHINO hiding!"], "activities": ["Point at tower", "Run on promenade"], "carrier_needed": false}, "charlotte": {"scripts": ["Charlotte, let's play! There's a RHINO hiding on this tower. Find it before me!", "Charlotte, see the holes? That's where cannons would go BOOM!"], "activities": ["Rhino hunt!", "Count 'BOOM holes'"]}}	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	{"the_story": "The famous rhinoceros appeared in 1515 when Sultan Muzaffar Shah II of Gujarat sent the beast as a diplomatic gift—the first living rhinoceros Europeans had seen since Roman times. King Manuel tried to regift it to the Pope, but the ship sank. The stone carving may be the only permanent memorial.", "what_it_is": "UNESCO World Heritage defensive tower built 1514-1520 to guard Tagus River entrance, famous for Manueline architecture and a carved rhinoceros—first in Western European art.", "why_it_matters": "The Tower stood where Vasco da Gama's ships passed as they sailed toward India—the last bit of Portugal explorers saw departing, the first thing upon returning.", "interesting_facts": ["Rhinoceros based on real animal", "Tower originally stood in middle of river—shoreline shifted", "Dürer's famous woodcut based on same rhino"]}	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N
e4297cc4-f610-459e-a39b-4ff91695752e	2e2ae20a-832b-4e7c-9419-2afdb506b6ab	b63eb49d-9258-4cca-a272-ac3b39f0fc4c	Jerónimos Monastery	MAIN ACTIVITY. Church FREE. Da Gama's tomb.	activity	\N	10:00:00	\N	Jerónimos Monastery	Praça do Império, 1400-206 Lisboa	38.6979000	-9.2068000	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	USD	\N	\N	f	\N	f	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	2	\N	2026-02-06 17:49:05.017242+00	2026-02-06 17:49:05.017242+00	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	unconfirmed	\N	\N	ae7c1aaf-2a96-485b-9fa6-afe1724a55fb	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	f	\N	\N	{"parker": {"scripts": ["Parker, count how many different things carved in stone—ropes, anchors, shells, armillary spheres. I bet you can find at least 10!", "Parker, Vasco da Gama is buried right here. He sailed 24,000 miles when no one knew if it was possible.", "Parker, look up at the ceiling. See how the stone pillars look like palm trees?"], "activities": ["Scavenger hunt: 10 carved motifs", "Find da Gama's tomb", "Count church pillars"]}, "xander": {"scripts": ["Let Xander run in cloister—enclosed and safe", "The church echo will fascinate him"], "activities": ["Running in cloister", "Echoes in church"], "carrier_needed": true}, "charlotte": {"scripts": ["Charlotte, look at the ceiling! Does it look like trees growing up?", "Charlotte, can you find a stone lion? A stone elephant? A stone sea monster?", "Charlotte, let's run (carefully!) in the cloister!"], "activities": ["Stone creature hunt", "Run in cloister garden"]}}	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	{"the_story": "Construction began in 1501 under master architect Diogo de Boitaca, who established the Manueline style—late Gothic forms draped in carved stone ropes, anchors, armillary spheres, and sea creatures. The church's single vaulted nave appears supported by six slender pillars that look like palm trees growing into the vault.\\n\\nThe monastery housed monks of the Order of Saint Jerome for 400 years, who prayed continuously for the royal family and explorers. Remarkably, Jerónimos survived the 1755 earthquake that destroyed 85% of Lisbon—its solid granite foundations and Gothic engineering held firm.", "what_it_is": "UNESCO World Heritage monastery built to commemorate Vasco da Gama's discovery of the sea route to India, featuring Portugal's finest Manueline architecture.", "why_it_matters": "Jerónimos Monastery is where Portugal's Age of Discovery becomes real and touchable. On July 8, 1497, Vasco da Gama and approximately 170 sailors spent their final night on Portuguese soil in a small chapel on this exact spot, praying before departing into the complete unknown. No European had ever sailed to India. Most of those men would never return.\\n\\nWhen da Gama succeeded—returning in 1499 after a two-year voyage of 24,000 miles—King Manuel I decided to build something magnificent. The monastery was funded by the 'Vintena da Pimenta'—a 5% tax on pepper, spices, and precious stones, bringing in approximately 70 kg of gold annually.", "interesting_facts": ["Only ~55 of 170 men survived da Gama's voyage", "5% spice tax would be worth billions today", "Monks prayed here 24/7 for 400 years"]}	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N
