ess Atlantic into arches, pinnacles, and secret grottos that only small boats can access. You'll pass through caves nicknamed 'The Cathedral' (dome-shaped), 'The Kitchen,' and 'The Living Room,' while guides point out rock formations resembling elephants, skulls, and intertwined lovers.", "what_it_is": "Small boats (10-12 passengers) thread through narrow sea arches and enter caves carved over millennia into golden limestone cliffs. The water glows emerald and turquoise as light filters through rock formations.", "what_youll_see": [{"area": "Sea Caves", "highlights": ["Cathedral Grotto (dome-shaped)", "Kitchen Cave", "Living Room Cave"]}, {"area": "Rock Formations", "highlights": ["Elephant Rock", "Lovers embracing", "Skull formation"]}, {"area": "Water Effects", "highlights": ["Turquoise water glowing in caves", "Light beams through rock openings"]}], "why_it_matters": "This is the Algarve's signature experience—seeing these cliffs from sea level reveals a hidden world invisible from above. For families, it's the rare adventure that works for all ages: short enough for a 3-year-old's attention span, visually spectacular enough for a 5-year-old's imagination, and geologically fascinating for an 8-year-old who loves science.", "interesting_facts": ["The limestone is 20 million years old—predating most dinosaur extinctions", "Small boats can access caves that larger tourist vessels cannot reach", "The turquoise color comes from sunlight reflecting off white sandy bottom", "Fishing families still use these waters—you may see traditional boats"]}	\N	{"cost": "€25/person (Lagos Boat Tours); €22.50 with code 'blue15' (BlueFleet)", "hours": "Tours depart 9am-6pm, every 30-60 min", "duration": "60-75 minutes", "best_time": "9-10am departure for calmest seas and best cave light", "age_minimum": "None—infants welcome", "booking_url": "https://lagosboattours.com", "reservation": "Required in June; book 2-3 days ahead", "meeting_point": "Lagos Marina, Gate 'Passeios de Barco'"}