13be3c69-ad74-4d86-9c93-eb95a2de0eb6	2e2ae20a-832b-4e7c-9419-2afdb506b6ab	4f5d2d2f-c4d2-4427-95f4-1e5facc954da	viewpoint	\N	Cabo de São Vicente Sunset	\N	\N	\N	Claude Research Agent	2026-02-06	\N	\N	Cabo de São Vicente, 8650-370 Vila do Bispo	\N	\N	https://maps.google.com/?q=37.0227,-8.9958	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	Cape accessible 24/7; lighthouse courtyard 10am-6pm	\N	\N	\N	EUR	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	approved	must_do	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	{"parker": {"scripts": ["A long time ago, people thought this was the actual edge of the world—the last solid ground before you fell off into nothing. Roman sailors were terrified to go past here.", "Can you imagine believing the ocean just... ended? The explorers who finally sailed past were incredibly brave. They discovered that the world kept going—and eventually circled all the way back home.", "That lighthouse beam can be seen 60 miles away! Ships far out in the Atlantic use it to know where the coast is."], "age_at_trip": 8}, "xander": {"scripts": ["BIG WATER! See allllll the water?", "See the sun? It's going night-night! The sun is going SPLASH into the water!", "Can you wave bye-bye to the sun? See all the birds flying?"], "age_at_trip": 3}, "charlotte": {"scripts": ["This is called 'The End of the World!' People used to think if you sailed past here, you'd fall off the edge.", "But guess what? They were wrong! Brave sailors discovered there were whole new lands out there.", "Tonight we're going to watch the sun go to sleep—it's going to dive right into the water and turn the sky all pink and orange!"], "age_at_trip": 5}}	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	2026-02-06 17:40:11.771071+00	2026-02-06 17:40:11.771071+00	{"the_story": "Greeks called this land 'Ophiussa' (Land of Serpents). Romans named it 'Promontorium Sacrum' (Sacred Promontory) and built temples here. The current name honors St. Vincent of Saragossa, a Spanish priest martyred by Romans around 304 AD. Legend claims his body washed ashore here, guarded by ravens. In 1173, King Afonso moved the relics to Lisbon—the ship and ravens now appear on Lisbon's coat of arms. Sir Francis Drake destroyed the fortress here in 1587 during his attacks on Portugal. Today, a quirky food truck called 'Last Bratwurst Before America' serves German sausages to sunset-watchers from around the world.", "what_it_is": "The southwesternmost point of mainland Europe—a windswept headland with sheer 75-meter cliffs dropping into the Atlantic. A striking red-and-white lighthouse (1846) houses one of Europe's most powerful lights, visible 60 miles at sea.", "what_youll_see": [{"area": "Cape", "highlights": ["75-meter sheer cliffs", "Endless Atlantic panorama", "Lighthouse (1846)"]}, {"area": "Wildlife", "highlights": ["Seabirds riding updrafts", "Possibly dolphins in distance"]}, {"area": "Human Interest", "highlights": ["'Last Bratwurst Before America' food truck", "Sunset crowd gathering"]}], "why_it_matters": "For ancient civilizations, this was literally the end of the known world. Roman geographer Strabo recorded that common people believed the sun 'sank hissing into the ocean' here each evening. Standing at sunset, watching the sun drop directly into the Atlantic while the crowd cheers, your family will experience something humans have gathered to witness for millennia.", "interesting_facts": ["The lighthouse beam reaches 60 miles (95 km) out to sea", "Romans built temples here believing it was where gods lived", "Wind speeds regularly exceed 100 km/h in winter", "The 'Last Bratwurst Before America' is a real German food truck that's become a landmark"]}	\N	{"cost": "FREE", "hours": "Cape accessible 24/7; lighthouse courtyard 10am-6pm", "parking": "Large free lot at lighthouse", "duration": "45-60 minutes for sunset experience", "reservation": "Not needed", "arrive_before": "45 minutes before sunset for parking", "sunset_time_june": "~9:00-9:10pm"}	{"lat": 37.0227, "lng": -8.9958, "name": "Cabo de São Vicente", "address": "Cabo de São Vicente, 8650-370 Vila do Bispo", "google_maps_url": "https://maps.google.com/?q=37.0227,-8.9958"}	\N	\N
1c8002b5-c794-4ce6-aaf5-e4b1b74401b5	2e2ae20a-832b-4e7c-9419-2afdb506b6ab	4f5d2d2f-c4d2-4427-95f4-1e5facc954da	attraction	\N	Fortaleza de Sagres (Sagres Fortress)	\N	\N	\N	Claude Research Agent	2026-02-06	\N	\N	Ponta de Sagres, 8650-360 Sagres	\N	\N	https://maps.google.com/?q=36.9972,-8.9485	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	9:30am-8pm (May-Sept); last entry 30 min before closing	\N	\N	\N	EUR	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	approved	must_do	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	{"parker": {"scripts": ["This is where the Age of Discovery started! Prince Henry gathered the smartest scientists, mapmakers, and sailors right here.", "They drew maps of places no European had ever seen, built new types of ships, and figured out how to sail home by going way out into the ocean first.", "See that giant compass on the ground? It's 43 meters across—nobody knows exactly what it was for. What do you think they used it for?"], "age_at_trip": 8}, "xander": {"scripts": ["Big castle! Look at the BIG circle on the ground!", "Can you walk around the circle? Let's count your steps!", "Let's go find the maze! [At maze] Can you hear the whooshing sound? That's the sea talking!"], "age_at_trip": 3}, "charlotte": {"scripts": ["Prince Henry had a BIG dream—he wanted to find out what was on the other side of the ocean! He invited all the best explorers to come here and make plans.", "They drew treasure maps and built special ships.", "Look—there's a magical maze over there called 'The Voice of the Sea.' When you walk inside, you can hear the ocean whispering secrets!"], "age_at_trip": 5}}	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	2026-02-06 17:40:11.771071+00	2026-02-06 17:40:11.771071+00	{"the_story": "Prince Henry (1394-1460) was the fourth son of Portugal's King John I. Though his nickname is 'the Navigator,' Henry himself never sailed on long voyages. Instead, he was the visionary organizer—gathering experts, funding expeditions, and pushing past the boundaries of the known world from this remote headland. His teams developed the caravel (a nimble ship that could sail against the wind) and perfected the 'volta do mar' technique (sailing far out to sea to catch favorable winds home). When Henry died here in 1460, his ships had explored the African coast past Cape Verde. Forty years later, his methods enabled Vasco da Gama to reach India. The fortress was raided by Francis Drake in 1587 and devastated by the 1755 earthquake, but its connection to maritime history remains powerful.", "what_it_is": "A dramatic promontory fortress protected by 60-meter cliffs on three sides. Inside you'll find the mysterious 43-meter stone 'Rosa dos Ventos' (Wind Compass)—an enormous circular pattern whose exact purpose remains debated—plus a 16th-century church, museum exhibitions, and 'A Voz do Mar' (Voice of the Sea), a concrete labyrinth sculpture that creates haunting acoustic effects.", "what_youll_see": [{"area": "Rosa dos Ventos", "highlights": ["43-meter stone compass/sundial", "Mystery of its true purpose"]}, {"area": "A Voz do Mar", "highlights": ["Concrete labyrinth", "Acoustic echoes of ocean"]}, {"area": "Cliffs & Views", "highlights": ["60-meter cliff drops", "Panoramic Atlantic views"]}, {"area": "Church & Museum", "highlights": ["16th-century Igreja de Nossa Senhora da Graça", "Maritime exhibitions"]}], "why_it_matters": "This is the birthplace of Portugal's Age of Discovery. From this windswept headland, Prince Henry the Navigator gathered cartographers, astronomers, and shipbuilders in the 1440s-50s, organizing expeditions that would eventually lead Vasco da Gama to India and change the world forever.", "interesting_facts": ["The Rosa dos Ventos (Wind Compass) is 43 meters across—no one knows its exact purpose", "Prince Henry never actually sailed on voyages himself—he was the organizer and funder", "Francis Drake raided this fortress in 1587", "The 1755 earthquake that destroyed Lisbon also damaged Sagres"]}	\N	{"cost": "Adults €10; Family ticket €5/person; Children under 12 FREE", "hours": "9:30am-8pm (May-Sept); last entry 30 min before closing", "parking": "Free lot at entrance", "duration": "1.5-2 hours", "reservation": "Walk-up, no advance booking needed"}	{"lat": 36.9972, "lng": -8.9485, "name": "Fortaleza de Sagres", "address": "Ponta de Sagres, 8650-360 Sagres", "google_maps_url": "https://maps.google.com/?q=36.9972,-8.9485"}	\N	\N
b653aeb2-4c06-4f88-b643-c0454b365851	2e2ae20a-832b-4e7c-9419-2afdb506b6ab	4f5d2d2f-c4d2-4427-95f4-1e5facc954da	hike	\N	Ponta da Piedade Cliff Walk (Boardwalk Trail)	\N	\N	\N	Claude Research Agent	2026-02-06	\N	\N	Ponta da Piedade, Lagos	\N	\N	https://maps.google.com/?q=37.0833,-8.6706	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	EUR	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	{}	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	approved	must_do	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	{"parker": {"scripts": ["These cliffs are made of limestone that's 20 million years old. The waves slowly dissolved the rock and carved out all these caves and arches.", "From up here, you can look down and see the boats going into the caves—that'll be us later today!", "See if you can spot the rock that looks like an elephant."], "age_at_trip": 8}, "xander": {"scripts": ["Look at the boats WAY down there! Can you see them? They're so tiny!", "Look at the pretty water! It's so blue! Do you hear the waves going CRASH?"], "age_at_trip": 3}, "charlotte": {"scripts": ["We're walking along secret treasure cliffs! Down below are hidden mermaid caves—can you see the boats going inside?", "Look at the water—it's BLUE like a swimming pool! That's because the sandy bottom is so white it makes the water glow."], "age_at_trip": 5}}	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	2026-02-06 17:40:11.771071+00	2026-02-06 17:40:11.771071+00	{"what_it_is": "A recently constructed wooden boardwalk system connecting Lagos beaches to the Ponta da Piedade lighthouse along spectacular golden limestone cliffs. Four railed viewing platforms with benches offer dramatic vertical views into turquoise coves.", "why_it_matters": "This is the Algarve's most accessible cliff walk—wide, flat boardwalks safe for families with railed viewpoints. You'll see the same dramatic formations from above that the boat tours show from below, giving kids a complete picture of this unique landscape."}	\N	{"cost": "FREE", "distance": "1.6 km one-way (can do shorter sections)", "duration": "1-2 hours", "best_time": "Before 9am (no shade; before crowds)", "elevation": "77m total (mostly flat boardwalk)", "difficulty": "Easy", "alltrails_url": "https://www.alltrails.com/trail/portugal/faro/trilho-da-ponta-da-piedade"}	{"lat": 37.0833, "lng": -8.6706, "name": "Ponta da Piedade Lighthouse", "address": "Ponta da Piedade, Lagos", "google_maps_url": "https://maps.google.com/?q=37.0833,-8.6706"}	\N	\N
