 for ages 3, 5, and 8 simultaneously is the holy grail. Reservoir water warms to 25°C in July—dramatically warmer than frigid waterfall pools. The calm, wave-free surface eliminates undertow concerns. Sandy beach for Charlotte and Xander, Water Park adventure for Parker. NO LIFEGUARDS—constant parental supervision required."}, "interesting_facts": ["Water temperature can reach 25°C in July—warmer than many swimming pools", "Gold Quality certification means regular water testing", "Reservoir level drops in late summer, expanding beaches"]}	\N	{"cost": "Parking €5/day; Water Park €10-15 additional", "hours": "Beach 24/7; Water Park 10am-7pm summer", "duration": "3-4 hours", "reservation_required": false}	{"lat": 41.678516, "lng": -8.176218, "name": "Praia Fluvial do Alqueirão", "address": "After bridge linking Rio Caldo to Vila do Gerês", "google_maps_url": "https://maps.google.com/?q=41.678516,-8.176218"}	\N	\N
c5356ab3-3b5e-4b6c-ada4-44f9d9aafb35	2e2ae20a-832b-4e7c-9419-2afdb506b6ab	8e5d2c22-331b-4399-90b6-574bac6205a8	hike	Hiking & Nature	Cascata de São Miguel Trail (Mata da Albergaria)	\N	"Easy shaded hike combining Roman milestones, ancient oak forest, and waterfall swimming—education, adventure, and refreshment in one 4km package."	\N	Claude Research Agent	2026-02-06	\N	\N	Old border station with Spain	\N	\N	https://maps.google.com/?q=41.8089,-8.1381	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	Daylight; Mata da Albergaria gate 8am-8pm summer	\N	\N	\N	EUR	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	{}	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	approved	must_do	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	{"parker": {"scripts": ["Can you decode the Roman numerals? XVI means 16 Roman miles from Braga!", "Touch these wheel ruts—2,000 years of carts made those grooves!"], "age_at_trip": 8}, "xander": {"scripts": ["BIG ROCK! Touch the big rock!", "BRIDGE! We're crossing the bridge!"], "age_at_trip": 3}, "charlotte": {"scripts": ["Let's follow in the footsteps of Roman soldiers! March march march!", "Feel these grooves? Wagon wheels made them!"], "age_at_trip": 5}}	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	2026-02-06 17:40:43.863395+00	2026-02-06 17:40:43.863395+00	{"the_story": {"content": "The Via XVIII Roman Road was built in 79-80 CE under Emperor Vespasian. The milestones document successive emperors—Titus, Hadrian, Antoninus Pius—their names carved in granite while their empire turned to dust."}, "what_it_is": "A trail through Portugal's oldest oak forest passing 2,000-year-old Roman milestones to a waterfall swimming hole at the Spanish border.", "what_youll_see": [{"area": "Mata da Albergaria Forest", "highlights": ["Ancient oak trees", "Roman milestones", "Original paving with wheel ruts", "Wooden bridges"]}, {"area": "Cascata de São Miguel", "highlights": ["Multi-tiered waterfall", "Swimming pool at base", "Flat rocks for picnicking"]}], "why_it_matters": {"content": "This trail solves July hiking with young children: constant shade, gentle gradient, Roman milestones for natural rest stops with built-in education, and waterfall pool reward at the end. The milestones aren't reproductions but actual 2,000-year-old stones with legible inscriptions."}, "interesting_facts": ["This section has more Roman milestones than any comparable road in the former Roman Empire", "Wheel ruts were worn by 2,000 years of cart traffic", "Some oaks here may be 800+ years old"]}	\N	{"cost": "Entrance €2-5 CASH ONLY", "hours": "Daylight; Mata da Albergaria gate 8am-8pm summer", "duration": "2-3 hours including swimming", "difficulty": "Easy", "distance_km": 4.2, "alltrails_url": "https://www.alltrails.com/trail/portugal/braga/cascata-de-sao-miguel-cascata-das-lagoas-da-mata-da-albergaria", "elevation_gain_m": 124, "reservation_required": false}	{"lat": 41.8089, "lng": -8.1381, "name": "Portela do Homem Trailhead", "address": "Old border station with Spain", "google_maps_url": "https://maps.google.com/?q=41.8089,-8.1381"}	\N	\N
