s what happens when a king with unlimited resources and deep love of art decides to build his childhood fantasy in stone. King Ferdinand II—a German prince who married Portugal's Queen Maria II—purchased hilltop monastery ruins in 1838 and spent 16 years creating Europe's most original 19th-century building.\\n\\nFor the Liu kids, Pena is the ultimate fairy-tale castle—but REAL. Every tower and terrace was designed to look like a storybook.", "interesting_facts": ["Ferdinand spoke seven languages", "Original chapel inside the palace", "On clear days, see Lisbon and Atlantic"]}	[{"shot": "Classic view with red and yellow towers", "when": "Morning 9:30-11am", "where": "Queen's Terrace"}, {"tip": "One kid points while making surprised face", "shot": "Kids at Triton window", "where": "Main entrance"}]	{"cost": {"adult": "€14", "child": "€12.50 (6-17), FREE under 6", "family_total": "€40.50"}, "tips": ["Private cars CANNOT drive to palace—Uber from Sintra town", "Triton window is famous photo spot"], "hours": "Palace: 9:30am-6:30pm; Park: 9:00am-7:00pm. Daily.", "stroller": "NOT stroller-friendly. Steep cobblestones, spiral stairs. Carrier essential.", "best_time": "9:00am park opening, 9:30am palace first slot", "reservation": {"url": "https://www.parquesdesintra.pt/", "required": true}, "time_needed": "2-2.5 hours"}	{"area": "Sintra", "address": "Estrada da Pena, 2710-609 Sintra", "latitude": 38.7876, "longitude": -9.3905}	\N	9:00am-11:00am
