st point, fortified by every civilization that occupied the city. The 1147 siege that won the castle for Portugal is a genuine medieval action story—complete with a knight who sacrificed himself by jamming his body in a gate.", "interesting_facts": ["Site fortified for 2,000+ years", "Vasco da Gama received here after India voyage", "Peacocks are intentional—royalty kept them as wealth symbols"]}	[{"shot": "Kids on walls with city panorama", "when": "Morning light", "where": "West-facing walls"}, {"tip": "Wait for tail display", "shot": "Peacock encounter", "where": "Praça d'Armas garden"}]	{"cost": {"adult": "€17", "child": "FREE under 12", "family_total": "€34"}, "tips": ["Take Bus 737 directly to castle gate", "Peacocks roam freely", "Camera Obscura limited spots—ask at entrance"], "hours": "Mar-Oct: 9am-9pm; Nov-Feb: 9am-6pm. Daily.", "stroller": "NOT recommended. Medieval stairs, uneven cobblestones.", "best_time": "9am opening—cooler and less crowded", "reservation": {"url": "https://castelodesaojorge.bol.pt/", "required": false}, "time_needed": "2-2.5 hours"}	{"area": "Alfama", "address": "Rua de Santa Cruz do Castelo, 1100-129 Lisboa", "latitude": 38.7139, "longitude": -9.1337}	\N	9:30am-11:30am
