1fe032a0-44b0-4681-bed0-6827d3e96628	b201a860-05a3-4ddc-bb89-4c4271177271	Anza-Borrego Desert State Park	This is one of the only California state parks offering free dispersed camping without permits. Your 5th wheel fits at Borrego Palm Canyon Campground (35-foot max, $35-45/night with hookups) or Blair Valley's dispersed area (free, flat dry lakebed, no reservations). The Galleta Meadows sculptures—a massive serpent, elephants, prehistoric creatures—turn the desert into a treasure hunt.	California's largest state park wraps around an International Dark Sky Community and features 130+ life-sized metal dinosaur and animal sculptures scattered across the desert—free to explore anytime, perfect for Xander.	state_parks	\N	California, USA	Borrego Springs	CA	33.1004920	-116.3013266	ChIJc8yYOrgr2oAR_iZBqLm2Q8I	4.7	3954	\N	{"hookups": "water_electric", "cell_coverage": "spotty", "road_accessibility": "Enter via Palm Canyon Drive from the north (avoid steep S-22 from Julian with 5th wheel)", "max_trailer_length_ft": 35}	f	\N	\N	35.00	USD	$35-45/night with hookups, or free dispersed camping	{"best": ["october", "november", "december", "january", "february", "march", "april"], "avoid": ["june", "july", "august"], "notes": "Summer exceeds 110°F"}	2.5 hours	\N	{"scenic_beauty": 5, "solitude_level": 4, "adventure_level": 4, "family_friendly": 5, "relaxation_factor": 4}	{"topics": ["Desert ecology", "Stargazing", "Fossil dig simulation"], "visitor_center": true, "ranger_programs": true, "junior_ranger_program": true}	{"parker": {"suitable": true, "activities": ["Geology exploration at badlands", "Bighorn sheep tracking"], "engagement_level": 5}, "xander": {"suitable": true, "activities": ["Chasing metal dinosaurs", "Free desert exploration"], "engagement_level": 5}, "charlotte": {"suitable": true, "activities": ["Sculpture scavenger hunts", "Junior Ranger programs"], "engagement_level": 5}}	https://www.parks.ca.gov/?page_id=638	(760) 767-4205	\N	researching	0	{free-camping,dark-sky,sculptures,family-friendly}	{"Free dispersed camping available","130+ metal sculptures","International Dark Sky Community","Junior Ranger programs"}	{"Cell coverage spotty","Summer too hot"}	\N	\N	2026-02-02 15:20:31.066+00	2026-02-06 04:09:17.604005+00	[{"name": "places/ChIJc8yYOrgr2oAR_iZBqLm2Q8I/reviews/Ci9DQUlRQUNvZENodHljRjlvT21Sb2VVUnFabVkwVDFOd2EzZ3plRTA0V1d0elZsRRAB", "text": {"text": "Stay at Julian for a night. Enioyed its famous Julian Cafe Bakery classic burger and apple cider. Go to the park in the next morning. Park fee is 10 paid online or at kiosk in the visitor center.  Most of the park is untamed. Almost park roads are wilderly dirt roads. The wilderflowers on are blooming now, earlier than we thought. Many trails for lovers.", "languageCode": "en"}, "rating": 5, "publishTime": "2026-01-17T01:14:08.962668029Z", "originalText": {"text": "Stay at Julian for a night. Enioyed its famous Julian Cafe Bakery classic burger and apple cider. Go to the park in the next morning. Park fee is 10 paid online or at kiosk in the visitor center.  Most of the park is untamed. Almost park roads are wilderly dirt roads. The wilderflowers on are blooming now, earlier than we thought. Many trails for lovers.", "languageCode": "en"}, "googleMapsUri": "https://www.google.com/maps/reviews/data=!4m6!14m5!1m4!2m3!1sCi9DQUlRQUNvZENodHljRjlvT21Sb2VVUnFabVkwVDFOd2EzZ3plRTA0V1d0elZsRRAB!2m1!1s0x80da2bb83a98cc73:0xc243b6b9a84126fe", "flagContentUri": "https://www.google.com/local/content/rap/report?postId=Ci9DQUlRQUNvZENodHljRjlvT21Sb2VVUnFabVkwVDFOd2EzZ3plRTA0V1d0elZsRRAB&d=17924085&t=1", "authorAttribution": {"uri": "https://www.google.com/maps/contrib/100289034675984588606/reviews", "photoUri": "https://lh3.googleusercontent.com/a-/ALV-UjW1E0n4Q1mYGxrwH9twLEkhmFnQEPuqB2E7zJmrMZzWRZ7sCBE27A=s128-c0x00000000-cc-rp-mo-ba6", "displayName": "Green Ox"}, "relativePublishTimeDescription": "2 weeks ago"}, {"name": "places/ChIJc8yYOrgr2oAR_iZBqLm2Q8I/reviews/Ci9DQUlRQUNvZENodHljRjlvT25kSGVGbEROelZhZDNSQlNUTlZjV0ZYWXpZdFRXYxAB", "text": {"text": "It’s an amazing desert, I really loved to be there and enjoy it with a Jeep Wrangler, it was an amazing experience to which I often think. I wish I could go back there one day🧡", "languageCode": "en"}, "rating": 5, "publishTime": "2025-11-19T15:53:34.320464084Z", "originalText": {"text": "It’s an amazing desert, I really loved to be there and enjoy it with a Jeep Wrangler, it was an amazing experience to which I often think. I wish I could go back there one day🧡", "languageCode": "en"}, "googleMapsUri": "https://www.google.com/maps/reviews/data=!4m6!14m5!1m4!2m3!1sCi9DQUlRQUNvZENodHljRjlvT25kSGVGbEROelZhZDNSQlNUTlZjV0ZYWXpZdFRXYxAB!2m1!1s0x80da2bb83a98cc73:0xc243b6b9a84126fe", "flagContentUri": "https://www.google.com/local/content/rap/report?postId=Ci9DQUlRQUNvZENodHljRjlvT25kSGVGbEROelZhZDNSQlNUTlZjV0ZYWXpZdFRXYxAB&d=17924085&t=1", "authorAttribution": {"uri": "https://www.google.com/maps/contrib/111061558923967021456/reviews", "photoUri": "https://lh3.googleusercontent.com/a-/ALV-UjW9URu_PYan42sLfJC5deKUll8ioTPjbuFxNRBIxCIsndyPgFAL=s128-c0x00000000-cc-rp-mo-ba6", "displayName": "Raoul"}, "relativePublishTimeDescription": "2 months ago"}, {"name": "places/ChIJc8yYOrgr2oAR_iZBqLm2Q8I/reviews/Ci9DQUlRQUNvZENodHljRjlvT2tKdGFtSkRTMlJHVjJWbGRqSnRlbHBtZGtZdGFWRRAB", "text": {"text": "Relocated to SoCal 5 months ago and I am starting my journey in the state in Julian, with Anza being a very short drive! Anza Borrego has become my favorite place so far, every time I go there are moments of epic proportions I embrace, thank you nature for allowing us to be here and take you in…most of us do not respect you, but I do, I do profoundly.", "languageCode": "en"}, "rating": 5, "publishTime": "2026-01-30T14:17:59.623122442Z", "originalText": {"text": "Relocated to SoCal 5 months ago and I am starting my journey in the state in Julian, with Anza being a very short drive! Anza Borrego has become my favorite place so far, every time I go there are moments of epic proportions I embrace, thank you nature for allowing us to be here and take you in…most of us do not respect you, but I do, I do profoundly.", "languageCode": "en"}, "googleMapsUri": "https://www.google.com/maps/reviews/data=!4m6!14m5!1m4!2m3!1sCi9DQUlRQUNvZENodHljRjlvT2tKdGFtSkRTMlJHVjJWbGRqSnRlbHBtZGtZdGFWRRAB!2m1!1s0x80da2bb83a98cc73:0xc243b6b9a84126fe", "flagContentUri": "https://www.google.com/local/content/rap/report?postId=Ci9DQUlRQUNvZENodHljRjlvT2tKdGFtSkRTMlJHVjJWbGRqSnRlbHBtZGtZdGFWRRAB&d=17924085&t=1", "authorAttribution": {"uri": "https://www.google.com/maps/contrib/100697094384229216315/reviews", "photoUri": "https://lh3.googleusercontent.com/a-/ALV-UjWQoBONbW72Le6WkQBDSqiocehnzdWDz9Pi-eJSWW4UQGE3V1E=s128-c0x00000000-cc-rp-mo", "displayName": "Ancient African Blood"}, "relativePublishTimeDescription": "in the last week"}, {"name": "places/ChIJc8yYOrgr2oAR_iZBqLm2Q8I/reviews/Ci9DQUlRQUNvZENodHljRjlvT2tKWVRTMDROM0puV1VKdk9UTmpWSE5qVkRKTGRuYxAB", "text": {"text": "A walk up Palm Canyon is enjoyable. The visitors bureau is a great place for detailed information on other canyon hikes. There is a lot to do here. Great history.", "languageCode": "en"}, "rating": 5, "publishTime": "2025-12-08T19:23:13.249720326Z", "originalText": {"text": "A walk up Palm Canyon is enjoyable. The visitors bureau is a great place for detailed information on other canyon hikes. There is a lot to do here. Great history.", "languageCode": "en"}, "googleMapsUri": "https://www.google.com/maps/reviews/data=!4m6!14m5!1m4!2m3!1sCi9DQUlRQUNvZENodHljRjlvT2tKWVRTMDROM0puV1VKdk9UTmpWSE5qVkRKTGRuYxAB!2m1!1s0x80da2bb83a98cc73:0xc243b6b9a84126fe", "flagContentUri": "https://www.google.com/local/content/rap/report?postId=Ci9DQUlRQUNvZENodHljRjlvT2tKWVRTMDROM0puV1VKdk9UTmpWSE5qVkRKTGRuYxAB&d=17924085&t=1", "authorAttribution": {"uri": "https://www.google.com/maps/contrib/100874810067304024813/reviews", "photoUri": "https://lh3.googleusercontent.com/a-/ALV-UjVhvQC0KU-MqBZ8QDSmnJgps_Js56C9-u-Jg4N1yn79zut35tw=s128-c0x00000000-cc-rp-mo-ba4", "displayName": "Roy Carter"}, "relativePublishTimeDescription": "a month ago"}, {"name": "places/ChIJc8yYOrgr2oAR_iZBqLm2Q8I/reviews/Ci9DQUlRQUNvZENodHljRjlvT2pabldVTlhZMTlhU0Uxck4xY3Rja3hSTFZvNFdsRRAB", "text": {"text": "This place is one of my favorite places in California because of the amazing hike into the canyon.  I love the dinosaurs nearby and the town feels like it was frozen in time.  Very much old California and the Wild West.  Plus you have the mountains that are snowcapped in the winter about half an hour away and the beach 2 hours away.  Beautiful place to explore the desert and see wild sheep (borregos) if you are lucky! 🐏", "languageCode": "en"}, "rating": 5, "publishTime": "2025-09-11T05:10:02.126182833Z", "originalText": {"text": "This place is one of my favorite places in California because of the amazing hike into the canyon.  I love the dinosaurs nearby and the town feels like it was frozen in time.  Very much old California and the Wild West.  Plus you have the mountains that are snowcapped in the winter about half an hour away and the beach 2 hours away.  Beautiful place to explore the desert and see wild sheep (borregos) if you are lucky! 🐏", "languageCode": "en"}, "googleMapsUri": "https://www.google.com/maps/reviews/data=!4m6!14m5!1m4!2m3!1sCi9DQUlRQUNvZENodHljRjlvT2pabldVTlhZMTlhU0Uxck4xY3Rja3hSTFZvNFdsRRAB!2m1!1s0x80da2bb83a98cc73:0xc243b6b9a84126fe", "flagContentUri": "https://www.google.com/local/content/rap/report?postId=Ci9DQUlRQUNvZENodHljRjlvT2pabldVTlhZMTlhU0Uxck4xY3Rja3hSTFZvNFdsRRAB&d=17924085&t=1", "authorAttribution": {"uri": "https://www.google.com/maps/contrib/103275993150452471490/reviews", "photoUri": "https://lh3.googleusercontent.com/a/ACg8ocJb8ANSGlZ2tcgLUywRmB_xVKZa2041BCVDHvYp4EbGEx6yNg=s128-c0x00000000-cc-rp-mo-ba3", "displayName": "maymie Noble"}, "relativePublishTimeDescription": "4 months ago"}]	Anza-Borrego Desert State Park receives overwhelmingly positive reviews, with visitors praising it as an amazing desert destination for hiking, off-road adventures, and wildflower viewing. The park offers diverse experiences from canyon walks to wildlife spotting, with many considering it one of California's premier desert locations. Families should note that much of the park features unpaved dirt roads and untamed wilderness areas.	{"summary": "Anza-Borrego Desert State Park receives overwhelmingly positive reviews, with visitors praising it as an amazing desert destination for hiking, off-road adventures, and wildflower viewing. The park offers diverse experiences from canyon walks to wildlife spotting, with many considering it one of California's premier desert locations. Families should note that much of the park features unpaved dirt roads and untamed wilderness areas.", "negative": [{"text": "Most of the park is untamed. Almost park roads are wilderly dirt roads.", "author": "Green Ox", "rating": 5}], "positive": [{"text": "I love the dinosaurs nearby and the town feels like it was frozen in time. Very much old California and the Wild West.", "author": "maymie Noble", "rating": 5}, {"text": "A walk up Palm Canyon is enjoyable. The visitors bureau is a great place for detailed information on other canyon hikes.", "author": "Roy Carter", "rating": 5}, {"text": "Beautiful place to explore the desert and see wild sheep (borregos) if you are lucky!", "author": "maymie Noble", "rating": 5}], "last_updated": "2026-02-06T04:09:17.465Z"}	2026-02-06 04:09:12.486+00	state_park	\N	\N
019f3636-af50-40c9-a357-cd2695f364cf	b201a860-05a3-4ddc-bb89-4c4271177271	Death Valley National Park	Furnace Creek Campground offers 18 sites with full hookups (30/50 amp) and accepts RVs up to 100 feet—the best National Park camping logistics you'll find anywhere. Pull-through sites 67-77 simplify parking. Walking distance to the visitor center, pool, and restaurant means maximum adventure with minimum hassle.	The hottest, driest, lowest point in North America—where Star Wars was filmed, pupfish survive in salt creeks, and the Milky Way stretches horizon to horizon. Kids will never forget sandboarding the dunes at sunset.	national_parks	\N	Echo Canyon Rd, California 92328, USA	Death Valley	CA	36.4436480	-116.8072709	ChIJzU7GUcw_x4AR-1jE8kfdb-Y	\N	\N	\N	{"hookups": "full", "cell_coverage": "limited", "road_accessibility": "Pull-through sites 67-77 simplify parking", "max_trailer_length_ft": 100}	t	\N	\N	30.00	USD	$30-44/night; hookup sites require reservations October-April via Recreation.gov (6 months ahead)	{"best": ["october", "november", "december", "january", "february", "march", "april"], "avoid": ["may", "june", "july", "august", "september"], "notes": "Winter only—summer exceeds 120°F"}	4-5 hours	\N	{"scenic_beauty": 5, "solitude_level": 4, "adventure_level": 5, "family_friendly": 5, "relaxation_factor": 3}	{"topics": ["Geology", "Wildlife", "Stargazing", "Extreme environments"], "visitor_center": true, "ranger_programs": true, "junior_ranger_program": true}	{"parker": {"suitable": true, "activities": ["Star Wars filming site hunting", "Mosaic Canyon scrambles", "Sunset sandboarding"], "engagement_level": 5}, "xander": {"suitable": true, "activities": ["Sand dune play with toys", "Boardwalk walks", "Pool swimming"], "engagement_level": 5}, "charlotte": {"suitable": true, "activities": ["Pupfish spotting at Salt Creek", "Badwater Basin salt formations", "Junior Ranger badge"], "engagement_level": 5}}	\N	\N	\N	researching	0	{top-pick,national-park,stargazing,star-wars,extreme}	{"Best NP logistics (100ft, full hookups)","Walking distance to visitor center/pool","Darkest skies accessible by RV","Multi-age engagement"}	{"Limited cell coverage","Must visit October-April only"}	\N	\N	2026-02-02 15:20:35.31+00	2026-02-06 04:02:47.499387+00	\N	\N	\N	2026-02-06 04:02:47.395+00	national_park	\N	\N
8689e027-0094-42b3-a366-487cf6b3e90b	b201a860-05a3-4ddc-bb89-4c4271177271	Santa Ynez Valley via Flying Flags Resort	Flying Flags scores 9.3 for couples on Booking.com but works equally well for families. The splash pad entertains Xander while Parker explores the soccer field and Charlotte bounces between pools. On-site restaurant, ice cream, and weekly BBQ mean minimal logistics. OstrichLand USA sits 5 minutes away for animal feeding; Solvang's Danish village offers aebleskivers and windmills 4 miles down the road.	Award-winning resort with splash pad, multiple pools, vintage Airstream rentals, and walking distance to OstrichLand USA—all in 'Sideways' wine country.	other	\N	180 Ave of Flags, Buellton, CA 93427, USA	Buellton	CA	34.6108892	-120.1937694	ChIJuTUsqRyr7oAR3J8mJgyej1s	4.5	1904	\N	{"hookups": "full", "road_accessibility": "Standard sites don't accommodate 5th wheels—book premium/large sites only by calling (805) 688-3716", "max_trailer_length_ft": 35}	t	\N	\N	70.00	USD	$70-150/night depending on site and season	{"best": ["march", "april", "may", "september", "october", "november"], "notes": "Spring wildflowers and fall harvest are optimal"}	2.5 hours	\N	{"scenic_beauty": 4, "solitude_level": 2, "adventure_level": 3, "family_friendly": 5, "relaxation_factor": 5}	\N	{"parker": {"suitable": true, "activities": ["Soccer field", "Pool activities"], "engagement_level": 4}, "xander": {"suitable": true, "activities": ["Splash pad", "On-site ice cream"], "engagement_level": 5}, "charlotte": {"suitable": true, "activities": ["Pool hopping", "OstrichLand animal feeding"], "engagement_level": 5}}	https://flyingflags.com/?utm_source=google&utm_medium=organic&utm_campaign=gbp	(805) 688-3716	\N	researching	0	{resort,wine-country,family-friendly,ostrichland}	{}	{}	\N	\N	2026-02-02 15:20:32.631+00	2026-02-06 04:07:23.791928+00	[{"name": "places/ChIJuTUsqRyr7oAR3J8mJgyej1s/reviews/Ci9DQUlRQUNvZENodHljRjlvT25wVFprNXlZek5JU2w5RlQzVnNjMFp6YzJKRWJtYxAB", "text": {"text": "I have been coming to this RV resort for several years. During my visit last year, I experienced poor service and a negative attitude from staff. I decided to give the resort another chance this year, but unfortunately, the experience was no different.\\nMy children were riding their scooters and enjoying themselves when the assistant manager, Maygen, approached me in a very disrespectful manner. She immediately stated that riding scooters was not allowed in the park. I explained that we were on our third day, the park was extremely quiet (with roughly 13 trailers present), and the children were simply having fun.\\nInstead of handling the situation professionally, she threatened to remove us from the park and told me we would never be allowed to return if it continued. The way this was communicated was rude, unwelcoming, and completely lacking in basic courtesy. As a law enforcement officer, I can confidently say I do not even speak to suspects in the manner I was spoken to.\\nThe interaction was shocking and unacceptable. There was no effort to be respectful or customer-focused. Because of this repeated behavior over multiple visits, I will not be returning. I was also informed by another staff member that the property is being sold, which may explain the decline in customer service—but it does not excuse it.", "languageCode": "en"}, "rating": 1, "publishTime": "2025-12-22T22:13:57.874232974Z", "originalText": {"text": "I have been coming to this RV resort for several years. During my visit last year, I experienced poor service and a negative attitude from staff. I decided to give the resort another chance this year, but unfortunately, the experience was no different.\\nMy children were riding their scooters and enjoying themselves when the assistant manager, Maygen, approached me in a very disrespectful manner. She immediately stated that riding scooters was not allowed in the park. I explained that we were on our third day, the park was extremely quiet (with roughly 13 trailers present), and the children were simply having fun.\\nInstead of handling the situation professionally, she threatened to remove us from the park and told me we would never be allowed to return if it continued. The way this was communicated was rude, unwelcoming, and completely lacking in basic courtesy. As a law enforcement officer, I can confidently say I do not even speak to suspects in the manner I was spoken to.\\nThe interaction was shocking and unacceptable. There was no effort to be respectful or customer-focused. Because of this repeated behavior over multiple visits, I will not be returning. I was also informed by another staff member that the property is being sold, which may explain the decline in customer service—but it does not excuse it.", "languageCode": "en"}, "googleMapsUri": "https://www.google.com/maps/reviews/data=!4m6!14m5!1m4!2m3!1sCi9DQUlRQUNvZENodHljRjlvT25wVFprNXlZek5JU2w5RlQzVnNjMFp6YzJKRWJtYxAB!2m1!1s0x80eeab1ca92c35b9:0x5b8f9e0c26269fdc", "flagContentUri": "https://www.google.com/local/content/rap/report?postId=Ci9DQUlRQUNvZENodHljRjlvT25wVFprNXlZek5JU2w5RlQzVnNjMFp6YzJKRWJtYxAB&d=17924085&t=1", "authorAttribution": {"uri": "https://www.google.com/maps/contrib/109626737898004482698/reviews", "photoUri": "https://lh3.googleusercontent.com/a/ACg8ocIld7lPML95Gry6L0906vvb0LFQqdn4AXJwaqiyjufDYWT_5Q=s128-c0x00000000-cc-rp-mo", "displayName": "Edmon Muradyan"}, "relativePublishTimeDescription": "a month ago"}, {"name": "places/ChIJuTUsqRyr7oAR3J8mJgyej1s/reviews/Ci9DQUlRQUNvZENodHljRjlvT2kweFJqZGxURW96UkVSdVdUWnBOR1EyVjNnNWNuYxAB", "text": {"text": "Nice cozy place to stay if you don't like floor/outdoor tent camping. The cottage has a full kitchen, propane BBQ pit & nice little patio/deck area with seats. Heater/AC inside unit along with hot water. We had a small issue with the toilet and the front desk sent a maintenance person IMMEDIATELY. I honestly thought I'd be waiting hours. Will definitely be coming back again next year.", "languageCode": "en"}, "rating": 5, "publishTime": "2025-12-16T12:42:35.548472488Z", "originalText": {"text": "Nice cozy place to stay if you don't like floor/outdoor tent camping. The cottage has a full kitchen, propane BBQ pit & nice little patio/deck area with seats. Heater/AC inside unit along with hot water. We had a small issue with the toilet and the front desk sent a maintenance person IMMEDIATELY. I honestly thought I'd be waiting hours. Will definitely be coming back again next year.", "languageCode": "en"}, "googleMapsUri": "https://www.google.com/maps/reviews/data=!4m6!14m5!1m4!2m3!1sCi9DQUlRQUNvZENodHljRjlvT2kweFJqZGxURW96UkVSdVdUWnBOR1EyVjNnNWNuYxAB!2m1!1s0x80eeab1ca92c35b9:0x5b8f9e0c26269fdc", "flagContentUri": "https://www.google.com/local/content/rap/report?postId=Ci9DQUlRQUNvZENodHljRjlvT2kweFJqZGxURW96UkVSdVdUWnBOR1EyVjNnNWNuYxAB&d=17924085&t=1", "authorAttribution": {"uri": "https://www.google.com/maps/contrib/101795350946402288522/reviews", "photoUri": "https://lh3.googleusercontent.com/a-/ALV-UjVk_omMh3X2TsYL_6cH3_sUu4XN6sWT_yjpGgDH3O1lBjhkTWBqdA=s128-c0x00000000-cc-rp-mo-ba4", "displayName": "Richard Beas"}, "relativePublishTimeDescription": "a month ago"}, {"name": "places/ChIJuTUsqRyr7oAR3J8mJgyej1s/reviews/Ci9DQUlRQUNvZENodHljRjlvT21WQlRIZGFOWHBSUnpOM2NVUXRSRTlZZG1WUmRsRRAB", "text": {"text": "We inadvertently locked our keys in our coach. Everything, and I mean everything was locked in the coach. We had no phones. No keys.  Nothing.  We went to the registration / store and Des was amazing. She looked up locksmiths and allowed me to use the phone for the local calls. When they needed a return number to call back, Des had me give them her cell number so she would get the call and get back a hold of me. When Grace (store manager) saw us loitering in the store and heard what happened she gave my wife and I water and snacks.\\n\\nWe returned to our coach and waited for the locksmith. As we sat outside laughing about the situation, the General Manager (I believe her name is Jen) came by and dropped off two Flying Flags glasses and a bottle of wine.\\n\\nThe locksmith arrived and opened our coach. We went back to the store to pay for the water and snacks and we were told they were on the house.\\n\\nTalk about amazing customer service!  They could not have been more helpful and accommodating.\\n\\nBTW: the facility is top notch!  Clean, new E/W/S connections, and large spaces. Check in and check out was quick and painless. This is our favorite RV Park!  See you soon!", "languageCode": "en"}, "rating": 5, "publishTime": "2025-11-17T21:45:21.578797172Z", "originalText": {"text": "We inadvertently locked our keys in our coach. Everything, and I mean everything was locked in the coach. We had no phones. No keys.  Nothing.  We went to the registration / store and Des was amazing. She looked up locksmiths and allowed me to use the phone for the local calls. When they needed a return number to call back, Des had me give them her cell number so she would get the call and get back a hold of me. When Grace (store manager) saw us loitering in the store and heard what happened she gave my wife and I water and snacks.\\n\\nWe returned to our coach and waited for the locksmith. As we sat outside laughing about the situation, the General Manager (I believe her name is Jen) came by and dropped off two Flying Flags glasses and a bottle of wine.\\n\\nThe locksmith arrived and opened our coach. We went back to the store to pay for the water and snacks and we were told they were on the house.\\n\\nTalk about amazing customer service!  They could not have been more helpful and accommodating.\\n\\nBTW: the facility is top notch!  Clean, new E/W/S connections, and large spaces. Check in and check out was quick and painless. This is our favorite RV Park!  See you soon!", "languageCode": "en"}, "googleMapsUri": "https://www.google.com/maps/reviews/data=!4m6!14m5!1m4!2m3!1sCi9DQUlRQUNvZENodHljRjlvT21WQlRIZGFOWHBSUnpOM2NVUXRSRTlZZG1WUmRsRRAB!2m1!1s0x80eeab1ca92c35b9:0x5b8f9e0c26269fdc", "flagContentUri": "https://www.google.com/local/content/rap/report?postId=Ci9DQUlRQUNvZENodHljRjlvT21WQlRIZGFOWHBSUnpOM2NVUXRSRTlZZG1WUmRsRRAB&d=17924085&t=1", "authorAttribution": {"uri": "https://www.google.com/maps/contrib/101432631405919367149/reviews", "photoUri": "https://lh3.googleusercontent.com/a-/ALV-UjWi-aRQjBkoatv5FX4u8pfgvzMUxQ68lujMDDDwSf9LxTdZ2jOB=s128-c0x00000000-cc-rp-mo-ba3", "displayName": "Todd Peterson"}, "relativePublishTimeDescription": "2 months ago"}, {"name": "places/ChIJuTUsqRyr7oAR3J8mJgyej1s/reviews/Ci9DQUlRQUNvZENodHljRjlvT25WR05XYzRVRFY2VDNoS01YbFJOazVUVURka1UzYxAB", "text": {"text": "I had to wipe the outside toilet bowl due to feces. When I lifted the toilet seat, there was a urine mark. The bed sheet had hair everywhere. The window frame next to the bed where we slept was so dusty. We’ve been itchy inside the Airstream. The oldish style of the Airstream is fine, but the cleanliness is unacceptable. I was so tired due to traffic and when I got inside the airstream I had to clean the place. The floor was dirty. My white socks turned black. Around 8-ish I woke up because of the loud noise. Someone is cutting a tree or blowing leaves, it was so loud and disturbing.", "languageCode": "en"}, "rating": 3, "publishTime": "2025-09-07T00:26:03.548708240Z", "originalText": {"text": "I had to wipe the outside toilet bowl due to feces. When I lifted the toilet seat, there was a urine mark. The bed sheet had hair everywhere. The window frame next to the bed where we slept was so dusty. We’ve been itchy inside the Airstream. The oldish style of the Airstream is fine, but the cleanliness is unacceptable. I was so tired due to traffic and when I got inside the airstream I had to clean the place. The floor was dirty. My white socks turned black. Around 8-ish I woke up because of the loud noise. Someone is cutting a tree or blowing leaves, it was so loud and disturbing.", "languageCode": "en"}, "googleMapsUri": "https://www.google.com/maps/reviews/data=!4m6!14m5!1m4!2m3!1sCi9DQUlRQUNvZENodHljRjlvT25WR05XYzRVRFY2VDNoS01YbFJOazVUVURka1UzYxAB!2m1!1s0x80eeab1ca92c35b9:0x5b8f9e0c26269fdc", "flagContentUri": "https://www.google.com/local/content/rap/report?postId=Ci9DQUlRQUNvZENodHljRjlvT25WR05XYzRVRFY2VDNoS01YbFJOazVUVURka1UzYxAB&d=17924085&t=1", "authorAttribution": {"uri": "https://www.google.com/maps/contrib/117699323848223845695/reviews", "photoUri": "https://lh3.googleusercontent.com/a-/ALV-UjWHAk1rVFnSlJLIZAzfLdlnqI-BonVd6E6j4ANpSGR0vz5NxCI=s128-c0x00000000-cc-rp-mo-ba3", "displayName": "Mharje J"}, "relativePublishTimeDescription": "5 months ago"}, {"name": "places/ChIJuTUsqRyr7oAR3J8mJgyej1s/reviews/Ci9DQUlRQUNvZENodHljRjlvT2xkS2RqSnZjM2hSV1haVVZEUk9hakZwVFVKNmExRRAB", "text": {"text": "Great place to stop for a night or stay a few days. They provide a variety of RV sites as well as several iterations of \\"glamping\\" facilities. Two pools, playground, and general bike riding space for kids. Food service (good ice cream cones!) With pizza oven, sandwiches,  breakfast items. Meaningful store for both food and trailer and camping items. Kind and helpful staff. Grounds as close to immaculate as possible outside.", "languageCode": "en"}, "rating": 5, "publishTime": "2025-08-27T16:18:14.948550457Z", "originalText": {"text": "Great place to stop for a night or stay a few days. They provide a variety of RV sites as well as several iterations of \\"glamping\\" facilities. Two pools, playground, and general bike riding space for kids. Food service (good ice cream cones!) With pizza oven, sandwiches,  breakfast items. Meaningful store for both food and trailer and camping items. Kind and helpful staff. Grounds as close to immaculate as possible outside.", "languageCode": "en"}, "googleMapsUri": "https://www.google.com/maps/reviews/data=!4m6!14m5!1m4!2m3!1sCi9DQUlRQUNvZENodHljRjlvT2xkS2RqSnZjM2hSV1haVVZEUk9hakZwVFVKNmExRRAB!2m1!1s0x80eeab1ca92c35b9:0x5b8f9e0c26269fdc", "flagContentUri": "https://www.google.com/local/content/rap/report?postId=Ci9DQUlRQUNvZENodHljRjlvT2xkS2RqSnZjM2hSV1haVVZEUk9hakZwVFVKNmExRRAB&d=17924085&t=1", "authorAttribution": {"uri": "https://www.google.com/maps/contrib/118136153002686295296/reviews", "photoUri": "https://lh3.googleusercontent.com/a/ACg8ocLMo6iW0amKgzmxk6_JcevAt_-7a6UZWYa6emafwqymBr5FkA=s128-c0x00000000-cc-rp-mo-ba4", "displayName": "Edward Spilsbury"}, "relativePublishTimeDescription": "5 months ago"}]	Flying Flags Resort offers a family-friendly RV and glamping experience with excellent facilities including pools, playground, and bike riding areas, plus helpful amenities like food service and a well-stocked store. While most guests praise the exceptional customer service and immaculate grounds, there are concerning reports of inconsistent staff attitudes and cleanliness issues in some accommodations. The resort seems to excel at going above and beyond for guests in need, though experiences can vary significantly.	{"summary": "Flying Flags Resort offers a family-friendly RV and glamping experience with excellent facilities including pools, playground, and bike riding areas, plus helpful amenities like food service and a well-stocked store. While most guests praise the exceptional customer service and immaculate grounds, there are concerning reports of inconsistent staff attitudes and cleanliness issues in some accommodations. The resort seems to excel at going above and beyond for guests in need, though experiences can vary significantly.", "negative": [{"text": "She immediately stated that riding scooters was not allowed in the park... threatened to remove us from the park and told me we would never be allowed to return.", "author": "Edmon Muradyan", "rating": 1}, {"text": "The bed sheet had hair everywhere... My white socks turned black. Around 8-ish I woke up because of the loud noise.", "author": "Mharje J", "rating": 3}], "positive": [{"text": "Two pools, playground, and general bike 