4fdb8a4e-56a2-420b-a19b-bfd78b3a37c2	b201a860-05a3-4ddc-bb89-4c4271177271	Quartzsite, Arizona	La Posa LTVA offers $40/14 days or $180/seven months (September-April) with water and dump stations. Free areas at Plomosa Road, Hi Jolly, and Scaddan Wash allow 14-day stays with camp host registration. All areas easily accommodate your 5th wheel on flat, hard-packed desert. Kofa National Wildlife Refuge sits 30 minutes south for day-trip adventures.	The 'Boondocking Capital of the World' where hundreds of thousands of RVers gather each winter—plus the famous Big Tent RV Show and gem/mineral shows in January make this kid heaven for rock hunters.	boondocking	\N	Quartzsite, AZ 85346, USA	Quartzsite	AZ	33.6639137	-114.2299486	ChIJfXLdFmRZ0YARMgvdi2SYeZA	\N	\N	\N	{"hookups": "dry", "dump_station": "La Posa LTVA has dump stations", "cell_coverage": "good"}	f	\N	\N	3.00	USD	Free to $40/14 days depending on area. La Posa LTVA $40/14 days or $180/7 months	{"best": ["november", "december", "january", "february"], "avoid": ["may", "june", "july", "august", "september"], "notes": "65-75°F days in winter. Avoid summer entirely"}	4.5 hours	\N	{"scenic_beauty": 3, "solitude_level": 1, "adventure_level": 3, "family_friendly": 5, "other_kids_around": 5, "relaxation_factor": 4}	\N	{"parker": {"suitable": true, "activities": ["Rock hounding at gem shows", "Crystal Hill quartz collecting"], "engagement_level": 5}, "xander": {"suitable": true, "activities": ["Wide-open running space", "Community atmosphere"], "engagement_level": 4}, "charlotte": {"suitable": true, "activities": ["Gem show treasure hunting", "Meeting other RV families"], "engagement_level": 5}}	http://www.ci.quartzsite.az.us/	\N	\N	researching	0	{boondocking,community,gem-shows,rock-hunting,winter}	{}	{}	\N	\N	2026-02-02 15:20:38.237+00	2026-02-06 03:50:46.602371+00	\N	\N	\N	2026-02-06 03:50:45.044+00	blm	\N	\N
b166f65e-93d8-47dc-bd09-654135677067	b201a860-05a3-4ddc-bb89-4c4271177271	Montana de Oro via Morro Bay	Montana de Oro limits vehicles to 27 feet. Base at Morro Dunes RV Park (full hookups, big-rig friendly, Morro Bay views) and day-trip 10 miles to the park. Tide pools at Corallina Cove teem with sea stars, anemones, and hermit crabs for hands-on discovery. Spooner's Cove offers sea caves and protected beach play. Sea otters bob offshore.	Called 'Mountain of Gold' for spring wildflower carpets, this hidden 8,000-acre park delivers tide pools, sea caves, and dramatic bluffs without Big Sur crowds—but your 5th wheel can't enter.	state_parks	\N	3550 Pecho Valley Rd, Los Osos, CA 93402, USA	Morro Bay	CA	35.2576395	-120.8556366	ChIJ1UtZAt_87IARjq4YpC394I4	4.9	4095	\N	{"hookups": "full", "cell_coverage": "none", "road_accessibility": "Base at Morro Bay, day-trip 10 miles to park (27ft max in park)", "max_trailer_length_ft": 27}	f	\N	\N	\N	USD	\N	{"best": ["march", "april", "may"], "notes": "Spring wildflowers March-May, winter whale migration"}	3.5-4 hours	\N	{"scenic_beauty": 5, "solitude_level": 4, "adventure_level": 4, "family_friendly": 5, "relaxation_factor": 4}	\N	{"parker": {"suitable": true, "activities": ["Valencia Peak summit challenge (4 miles)"], "engagement_level": 5}, "xander": {"suitable": true, "activities": ["Sand play at Spooner's Cove", "Watching pelicans dive"], "engagement_level": 4}, "charlotte": {"suitable": true, "activities": ["Tide pool creature touching", "Shell collecting"], "engagement_level": 5}}	http://www.parks.ca.gov/?page_id=592	(805) 528-0513	\N	researching	0	{tide-pools,sea-caves,wildflowers,sea-otters}	{"Far fewer crowds than Big Sur","Better tide pools","RV options nearby"}	{"Park max 27ft—requires day-trip from Morro Bay","No cell service in park"}	\N	\N	2026-02-02 15:20:34.244+00	2026-02-06 04:04:40.406766+00	[{"name": "places/ChIJ1UtZAt_87IARjq4YpC394I4/reviews/Ci9DQUlRQUNvZENodHljRjlvT2xnNVlrbFVUMVp5TldkQ01HeE1OMHBNY0ZGUGJrRRAB", "text": {"text": "Try the Spooner beach and Bluff trails.  Very nice view and the surrounding is quite, the only sound is the sound of water wave touch the rocks…. the sound of sea… and the sky is blue… the air is fresh…\\n\\nShort walking trail (0.3-2 mile) but worthy.  Quite a few benches/wooden seats along the trails.\\n\\nWe got the driving instructions (from San Luis Obispo downtown to Bluff Trail), from the car’s GPS and the Google map… My car’s GPS shows less than half hour driving, and the Google map shows about 1.5 hours driving.  Surprisingly, my car’s GPS is correct.", "languageCode": "en"}, "rating": 5, "publishTime": "2025-12-20T10:49:36.181111684Z", "originalText": {"text": "Try the Spooner beach and Bluff trails.  Very nice view and the surrounding is quite, the only sound is the sound of water wave touch the rocks…. the sound of sea… and the sky is blue… the air is fresh…\\n\\nShort walking trail (0.3-2 mile) but worthy.  Quite a few benches/wooden seats along the trails.\\n\\nWe got the driving instructions (from San Luis Obispo downtown to Bluff Trail), from the car’s GPS and the Google map… My car’s GPS shows less than half hour driving, and the Google map shows about 1.5 hours driving.  Surprisingly, my car’s GPS is correct.", "languageCode": "en"}, "googleMapsUri": "https://www.google.com/maps/reviews/data=!4m6!14m5!1m4!2m3!1sCi9DQUlRQUNvZENodHljRjlvT2xnNVlrbFVUMVp5TldkQ01HeE1OMHBNY0ZGUGJrRRAB!2m1!1s0x80ecfcdf02594bd5:0x8ee0fd2da418ae8e", "flagContentUri": "https://www.google.com/local/content/rap/report?postId=Ci9DQUlRQUNvZENodHljRjlvT2xnNVlrbFVUMVp5TldkQ01HeE1OMHBNY0ZGUGJrRRAB&d=17924085&t=1", "authorAttribution": {"uri": "https://www.google.com/maps/contrib/108366559494383927586/reviews", "photoUri": "https://lh3.googleusercontent.com/a-/ALV-UjV403naQ-SljY_tcfpOHSdmAS9vmMFHb1Xd7p74rVP0-jkb0-1E=s128-c0x00000000-cc-rp-mo", "displayName": "violamy"}, "relativePublishTimeDescription": "a month ago"}, {"name": "places/ChIJ1UtZAt_87IARjq4YpC394I4/reviews/Ci9DQUlRQUNvZENodHljRjlvT25wbVoydFRWMU5PWWxwcWREZFJTM3A2YzNCWFEyYxAB", "text": {"text": "We hiked the Bluff Trail and got the most striking views of the coastline and wildlife. Easy level hike good for an hour or longer on the outer loop.  Even an outhouse for those weak of .....\\nPathways are well maintained.  Parking limited so go earlier.  Central Coast beauty at its best!", "languageCode": "en"}, "rating": 5, "publishTime": "2025-10-02T23:29:38.197780798Z", "originalText": {"text": "We hiked the Bluff Trail and got the most striking views of the coastline and wildlife. Easy level hike good for an hour or longer on the outer loop.  Even an outhouse for those weak of .....\\nPathways are well maintained.  Parking limited so go earlier.  Central Coast beauty at its best!", "languageCode": "en"}, "googleMapsUri": "https://www.google.com/maps/reviews/data=!4m6!14m5!1m4!2m3!1sCi9DQUlRQUNvZENodHljRjlvT25wbVoydFRWMU5PWWxwcWREZFJTM3A2YzNCWFEyYxAB!2m1!1s0x80ecfcdf02594bd5:0x8ee0fd2da418ae8e", "flagContentUri": "https://www.google.com/local/content/rap/report?postId=Ci9DQUlRQUNvZENodHljRjlvT25wbVoydFRWMU5PWWxwcWREZFJTM3A2YzNCWFEyYxAB&d=17924085&t=1", "authorAttribution": {"uri": "https://www.google.com/maps/contrib/106393052962737593575/reviews", "photoUri": "https://lh3.googleusercontent.com/a-/ALV-UjViHvp5RXWjt-MX0Gpq78vxZMYTmCG4S-WKE6FKaAJ2BvXw5KBB=s128-c0x00000000-cc-rp-mo-ba4", "displayName": "John Miekosz"}, "relativePublishTimeDescription": "4 months ago"}, {"name": "places/ChIJ1UtZAt_87IARjq4YpC394I4/reviews/Ci9DQUlRQUNvZENodHljRjlvT25OblJsOXRUbkp6YkZONVFXMVRSM0JOZURCSWIxRRAB", "text": {"text": "Such a beautiful park with stunning trails overlooking dramatic cliffs and the ocean. Every path offers breathtaking coastal views — peaceful, scenic, and absolutely worth the visit. Best of all, it’s free!", "languageCode": "en"}, "rating": 5, "publishTime": "2025-10-25T03:45:09.183661288Z", "originalText": {"text": "Such a beautiful park with stunning trails overlooking dramatic cliffs and the ocean. Every path offers breathtaking coastal views — peaceful, scenic, and absolutely worth the visit. Best of all, it’s free!", "languageCode": "en"}, "googleMapsUri": "https://www.google.com/maps/reviews/data=!4m6!14m5!1m4!2m3!1sCi9DQUlRQUNvZENodHljRjlvT25OblJsOXRUbkp6YkZONVFXMVRSM0JOZURCSWIxRRAB!2m1!1s0x80ecfcdf02594bd5:0x8ee0fd2da418ae8e", "flagContentUri": "https://www.google.com/local/content/rap/report?postId=Ci9DQUlRQUNvZENodHljRjlvT25OblJsOXRUbkp6YkZONVFXMVRSM0JOZURCSWIxRRAB&d=17924085&t=1", "authorAttribution": {"uri": "https://www.google.com/maps/contrib/109858671527097458166/reviews", "photoUri": "https://lh3.googleusercontent.com/a-/ALV-UjUjL0Mi2BXF7hWHn1mrU2EC8SPJ4wK2EkmTHya0oLjoAB4ypLzE=s128-c0x00000000-cc-rp-mo-ba5", "displayName": "Vy T. Zunker"}, "relativePublishTimeDescription": "3 months ago"}, {"name": "places/ChIJ1UtZAt_87IARjq4YpC394I4/reviews/Ci9DQUlRQUNvZENodHljRjlvT2pKcFRrTmhVM1JYZG05R1JUVmtOM1pLZFhwS2FtYxAB", "text": {"text": "I just love this part of the Central Coast! Realize that this is dry camping- no electrical, no flush toilets (pit), there are reservoirs of water to use, but not for dish washing. Loved the cool weather as an escape from Sacramento. Will definitely come back! Space 48 was a great ADA space for us.", "languageCode": "en"}, "rating": 4, "publishTime": "2025-08-01T21:20:05.038806642Z", "originalText": {"text": "I just love this part of the Central Coast! Realize that this is dry camping- no electrical, no flush toilets (pit), there are reservoirs of water to use, but not for dish washing. Loved the cool weather as an escape from Sacramento. Will definitely come back! Space 48 was a great ADA space for us.", "languageCode": "en"}, "googleMapsUri": "https://www.google.com/maps/reviews/data=!4m6!14m5!1m4!2m3!1sCi9DQUlRQUNvZENodHljRjlvT2pKcFRrTmhVM1JYZG05R1JUVmtOM1pLZFhwS2FtYxAB!2m1!1s0x80ecfcdf02594bd5:0x8ee0fd2da418ae8e", "flagContentUri": "https://www.google.com/local/content/rap/report?postId=Ci9DQUlRQUNvZENodHljRjlvT2pKcFRrTmhVM1JYZG05R1JUVmtOM1pLZFhwS2FtYxAB&d=17924085&t=1", "authorAttribution": {"uri": "https://www.google.com/maps/contrib/105957972089947771246/reviews", "photoUri": "https://lh3.googleusercontent.com/a-/ALV-UjXoUtgx1dRqJdcolvhn7kWvRBM_hAm7F0UcUeoC92eLXRNPQ7vtYg=s128-c0x00000000-cc-rp-mo-ba3", "displayName": "Tracey Lilley"}, "relativePublishTimeDescription": "6 months ago"}, {"name": "places/ChIJ1UtZAt_87IARjq4YpC394I4/reviews/Ci9DQUlRQUNvZENodHljRjlvT2pGNFQyazNVRzUzVTNaT2Qya3pka1F4U1U1cmMwRRAB", "text": {"text": "It's a great park with many different things to do and I love they don't charge for entry or parking. Trails are pretty eroded and could use maintenance, but still a fun place to ride MTB with family and always a great view at the top of Hazard Peak. Sand dunes and tide pools are great fun with the family as well.", "languageCode": "en"}, "rating": 4, "publishTime": "2025-11-30T16:23:48.955688263Z", "originalText": {"text": "It's a great park with many different things to do and I love they don't charge for entry or parking. Trails are pretty eroded and could use maintenance, but still a fun place to ride MTB with family and always a great view at the top of Hazard Peak. Sand dunes and tide pools are great fun with the family as well.", "languageCode": "en"}, "googleMapsUri": "https://www.google.com/maps/reviews/data=!4m6!14m5!1m4!2m3!1sCi9DQUlRQUNvZENodHljRjlvT2pGNFQyazNVRzUzVTNaT2Qya3pka1F4U1U1cmMwRRAB!2m1!1s0x80ecfcdf02594bd5:0x8ee0fd2da418ae8e", "flagContentUri": "https://www.google.com/local/content/rap/report?postId=Ci9DQUlRQUNvZENodHljRjlvT2pGNFQyazNVRzUzVTNaT2Qya3pka1F4U1U1cmMwRRAB&d=17924085&t=1", "authorAttribution": {"uri": "https://www.google.com/maps/contrib/112517324604049190014/reviews", "photoUri": "https://lh3.googleusercontent.com/a-/ALV-UjVIMV6wdZFX0cTTBaePU65b5UgCwAebW5glFnRYKfVXZ95m8I_2Mw=s128-c0x00000000-cc-rp-mo-ba4", "displayName": "Clint Claassen"}, "relativePublishTimeDescription": "2 months ago"}]	Montana de Oro State Park is a beloved Central Coast destination that offers stunning coastal views, well-maintained trails, and diverse family activities including tide pools and sand dunes. Visitors consistently praise the dramatic clifftop scenery, peaceful atmosphere, and the fact that it's completely free to visit. The park provides easy hiking options suitable for families, though some trails show signs of erosion.	{"summary": "Montana de Oro State Park is a beloved Central Coast destination that offers stunning coastal views, well-maintained trails, and diverse family activities including tide pools and sand dunes. Visitors consistently praise the dramatic clifftop scenery, peaceful atmosphere, and the fact that it's completely free to visit. The park provides easy hiking options suitable for families, though some trails show signs of erosion.", "negative": [{"text": "Trails are pretty eroded and could use maintenance", "author": "Clint Claassen", "rating": 4}, {"text": "Parking limited so go earlier", "author": "John Miekosz", "rating": 5}], "positive": [{"text": "Sand dunes and tide pools are great fun with the family", "author": "Clint Claassen", "rating": 4}, {"text": "Every path offers breathtaking coastal views — peaceful, scenic, and absolutely worth the visit. Best of all, it's free!", "author": "Vy T. Zunker", "rating": 5}, {"text": "Short walking trail (0.3-2 mile) but worthy. Quite a few benches/wooden seats along the trails.", "author": "violamy", "rating": 5}], "last_updated": "2026-02-06T04:04:40.331Z"}	2026-02-06 04:04:33.891+00	state_park	\N	\N
c975aa3c-4117-4bec-8673-109f8e72a758	b201a860-05a3-4ddc-bb89-4c4271177271	Giving Tree Family Farm	This isn't a petting zoo with crowds. Tulip the potbellied pig performs tricks. Nubian dairy goats get fed, petted, and milked. Baby emus (hand-raised) welcome hugs. Cheese-making and soap-making classes add educational depth. The principal-turned-farmer designs experiences specifically for children's development.	A former elementary school principal runs privately scheduled tours for one family at a time—meaning your kids get hands-on time with goats, alpacas, pigs who do tricks, and baby emus raised for human interaction.	harvest_hosts	\N	6135 Parkhill Rd, Santa Margarita, CA 93453, USA	Santa Margarita	CA	35.4063833	-120.5467198	ChIJPZ-9j9zs7IARAFCMHz5cBeM	5.0	12	\N	\N	t	\N	\N	\N	USD	Tours $20/adult, $10/children 3-12, free under 3. Duration 1-1.5 hours	\N	3 hours	\N	{"scenic_beauty": 3, "solitude_level": 5, "adventure_level": 3, "family_friendly": 5, "relaxation_factor": 4}	{"topics": ["Animal care", "Cheese-making", "Soap-making", "Farm life"]}	{"parker": {"suitable": true, "activities": ["Animal interaction", "Farm education"], "engagement_level": 4}, "xander": {"suitable": true, "activities": ["Pig tricks", "Goat petting and feeding"], "engagement_level": 5}, "charlotte": {"suitable": true, "activities": ["Baby animal hugging", "Cheese-making class"], "engagement_level": 5}}	https://www.givingtreefamilyfarm.com/contact-us/	(805) 438-4989	\N	researching	0	{farm,animals,educational,private-tours}	{}	{}	\N	\N	2026-02-02 15:20:33.046+00	2026-02-06 04:06:43.919694+00	[{"name": "places/ChIJPZ-9j9zs7IARAFCMHz5cBeM/reviews/ChZDSUhNMG9nS0VJQ0FnTUN3bE8yQWN3EAE", "text": {"text": "We had a wonderful experience with Tina and her family farm. Our two kids got to pet baby goats and feed pigs and alpacas. The guard dogs were actually our favorite.", "languageCode": "en"}, "rating": 5, "publishTime": "2025-03-16T20:31:36.917987Z", "originalText": {"text": "We had a wonderful experience with Tina and her family farm. Our two kids got to pet baby goats and feed pigs and alpacas. The guard dogs were actually our favorite.", "languageCode": "en"}, "googleMapsUri": "https://www.google.com/maps/reviews/data=!4m6!14m5!1m4!2m3!1sChZDSUhNMG9nS0VJQ0FnTUN3bE8yQWN3EAE!2m1!1s0x80ececdc8fbd9f3d:0xe3055c3e1f8c5000", "flagContentUri": "https://www.google.com/local/content/rap/report?postId=ChZDSUhNMG9nS0VJQ0FnTUN3bE8yQWN3EAE&d=17924085&t=1", "authorAttribution": {"uri": "https://www.google.com/maps/contrib/100068347390703334283/reviews", "photoUri": "https://lh3.googleusercontent.com/a-/ALV-UjVUIeqe-5e1d9UgxVYunpd4DnpSDsNuxqHQ2ocgsRkZnUDyl9bF=s128-c0x00000000-cc-rp-mo-ba4", "displayName": "Greg Agius"}, "relativePublishTimeDescription": "10 months ago"}, {"name": "places/ChIJPZ-9j9zs7IARAFCMHz5cBeM/reviews/ChZDSUhNMG9nS0VJQ0FnSURKeC1URU9BEAE", "text": {"text": "My family had a wonderful time. (I have two daughters, 9 and 13 years old.) Tina gave us a great tour! She taught us a lot and told us cute anecdotes about the different animals. We loved feeding the goats, alpacas, and pigs. Watching Tulip's (the pig) tricks was a highlight! I definitely recommend stopping by The Giving Tree Family Farm.", "languageCode": "en"}, "rating": 5, "publishTime": "2023-07-24T03:16:45.939666Z", "originalText": {"text": "My family had a wonderful time. (I have two daughters, 9 and 13 years old.) Tina gave us a great tour! She taught us a lot and told us cute anecdotes about the different animals. We loved feeding the goats, alpacas, and pigs. Watching Tulip's (the pig) tricks was a highlight! I definitely recommend stopping by The Giving Tree Family Farm.", "languageCode": "en"}, "googleMapsUri": "https://www.google.com/maps/reviews/data=!4m6!14m5!1m4!2m3!1sChZDSUhNMG9nS0VJQ0FnSURKeC1URU9BEAE!2m1!1s0x80ececdc8fbd9f3d:0xe3055c3e1f8c5000", "flagContentUri": "https://www.google.com/local/content/rap/report?postId=ChZDSUhNMG9nS0VJQ0FnSURKeC1URU9BEAE&d=17924085&t=1", "authorAttribution": {"uri": "https://www.google.com/maps/contrib/106939461083996154148/reviews", "photoUri": "https://lh3.googleusercontent.com/a/ACg8ocISKUECd3aUOhqYjaXbPizhpwgTjbpeP-SBEXkDs8nErMYIbw=s128-c0x00000000-cc-rp-mo", "displayName": "Jaime"}, "relativePublishTimeDescription": "2 years ago"}, {"name": "places/ChIJPZ-9j9zs7IARAFCMHz5cBeM/reviews/ChdDSUhNMG9nS0VJQ0FnSUNxeTVYQjVBRRAB", "text": {"text": "I loved this farm! Very clean and well kept up. Animals are very healthy and everyone was friendly. This farm has Alpacas, goats, turkeys and pigs. The farm tour was very interesting and we had a chance to feed and interact with the animals. Tina was an excellent host. She is very knowledgeable and  shared her experience raising and caring for these animals. She also shared interesting information about soap making a wool felting. When we visited, we made felted soap. We enjoyed this activity outside on a beautiful day listening to nature. There is good parking here and a port a potty. Wear closed toed shoes and expect to walk around. Bring layered clothing. There are big cattle dogs here too.", "languageCode": "en"}, "rating": 5, "publishTime": "2021-06-18T21:13:59.803304Z", "originalText": {"text": "I loved this farm! Very clean and well kept up. Animals are very healthy and everyone was friendly. This farm has Alpacas, goats, turkeys and pigs. The farm tour was very interesting and we had a chance to feed and interact with the animals. Tina was an excellent host. She is very knowledgeable and  shared her experience raising and caring for these animals. She also shared interesting information about soap making a wool felting. When we visited, we made felted soap. We enjoyed this activity outside on a beautiful day listening to nature. There is good parking here and a port a potty. Wear closed toed shoes and expect to walk around. Bring layered clothing. There are big cattle dogs here too.", "languageCode": "en"}, "googleMapsUri": "https://www.google.com/maps/reviews/data=!4m6!14m5!1m4!2m3!1sChdDSUhNMG9nS0VJQ0FnSUNxeTVYQjVBRRAB!2m1!1s0x80ececdc8fbd9f3d:0xe3055c3e1f8c5000", "flagContentUri": "https://www.google.com/local/content/rap/report?postId=ChdDSUhNMG9nS0VJQ0FnSUNxeTVYQjVBRRAB&d=17924085&t=1", "authorAttribution": {"uri": "https://www.google.com/maps/contrib/105306173198965189829/reviews", "photoUri": "https://lh3.googleusercontent.com/a-/ALV-UjWbOj_rdRVz5UmMCPMDY82riVewUcVo2X5W3lXI2bxqBN4CJvy2Bw=s128-c0x00000000-cc-rp-mo-ba4", "displayName": "Karyn Kleinmann"}, "relativePublishTimeDescription": "4 years ago"}, {"name": "places/ChIJPZ-9j9zs7IARAFCMHz5cBeM/reviews/Ci9DQUlRQUNvZENodHljRjlvT2pKU1JDMDJjMkZFVDJGRmIwdHZZbTF0WVhZNGVrRRAB", "text": {"text": "We had the best time at their cheese workshop and saying hi to their animals. Such a memorable morning at the farm! Wish we lived closer so we could visit again.", "languageCode": "en"}, "rating": 5, "publishTime": "2025-11-09T03:54:13.741494254Z", "originalText": {"text": "We had the best time at their cheese workshop and saying hi to their animals. Such a memorable morning at the farm! Wish we lived closer so we could visit again.", "languageCode": "en"}, "googleMapsUri": "https://www.google.com/maps/reviews/data=!4m6!14m5!1m4!2m3!1sCi9DQUlRQUNvZENodHljRjlvT2pKU1JDMDJjMkZFVDJGRmIwdHZZbTF0WVhZNGVrRRAB!2m1!1s0x80ececdc8fbd9f3d:0xe3055c3e1f8c5000", "flagContentUri": "https://www.google.com/local/content/rap/report?postId=Ci9DQUlRQUNvZENodHljRjlvT2pKU1JDMDJjMkZFVDJGRmIwdHZZbTF0WVhZNGVrRRAB&d=17924085&t=1", "authorAttribution": {"uri": "https://www.google.com/maps/contrib/110284672953496027204/reviews", "photoUri": "https://lh3.googleusercontent.com/a-/ALV-UjWJcJCOGRNFh9SOif1z0XYiBCXZvKwvPkpzSmLdJWaNuirfRhkK0Q=s128-c0x00000000-cc-rp-mo", "displayName": "Victoria Calvert"}, "relativePublishTimeDescription": "2 months ago"}, {"name": "places/ChIJPZ-9j9zs7IARAFCMHz5cBeM/reviews/ChdDSUhNMG9nS0VJQ0FnSUNhc3Q3U2xBRRAB", "text": {"text": "We had a really great time here! Tina was very nice and showed us around the property. The little ones really enjoyed seeing the animals and we would come back in a heartbeat.", "languageCode": "en"}, "rating": 5, "publishTime": "2021-07-27T17:14:32.221313Z", "originalText": {"text": "We had a really great time here! Tina was very nice and showed us around the property. The little ones really enjoyed seeing the animals and we would come back in a heartbeat.", "languageCode": "en"}, "googleMapsUri": "https://www.google.com/maps/reviews/data=!4m6!14m5!1m4!2m3!1sChdDSUhNMG9nS0VJQ0FnSUNhc3Q3U2xBRRAB!2m1!1s0x80ececdc8fbd9f3d:0xe3055c3e1f8c5000", "flagContentUri": "https://www.google.com/local/content/rap/report?postId=ChdDSUhNMG9nS0VJQ0FnSUNhc3Q3U2xBRRAB&d=17924085&t=1", "authorAttribution": {"uri": "https://www.google.com/maps/contrib/101315542022178928297/reviews", "photoUri": "https://lh3.googleusercontent.com/a-/ALV-UjXGOuXuDeJj_yRwrHN1R1Lm19lkuxQV45SuGXSH4_EHgXY7CxBPPg=s128-c0x00000000-cc-rp-mo-ba3", "displayName": "Jacob Silberfarb"}, "relativePublishTimeDescription": "4 years ago"}]	Giving Tree Family Farm receives consistently excellent reviews for its family-friendly farm tours led by knowledgeable host Tina. Families with children particularly love the hands-on experience of feeding and interacting with well-cared-for animals including goats, pigs, alpacas, and turkeys, plus engaging activities like soap making and cheese workshops.	{"summary": "Giving Tree Family Farm receives consistently excellent reviews for its family-friendly farm tours led by knowledgeable host Tina. Families with children particularly love the hands-on experience of feeding and interacting with well-cared-for animals including goats, pigs, alpacas, and turkeys, plus engaging activities like soap making and cheese workshops.", "negative": [], "positive": [{"text": "Our two kids got to pet baby goats and feed pigs and alpacas.", "author": "Greg Agius", "rating": 5}, {"text": "Watching Tulip's (the pig) tricks was a highlight!", "author": 