1fa28ff3-dca3-49ee-94f4-b4b93e583615	b201a860-05a3-4ddc-bb89-4c4271177271	June Lake Loop	This isn't just a lake—it's a high Sierra experience. Oh! Ridge Campground accepts RVs up to 40 feet with 140+ dry-camping sites near the June Lake Beach swimming area. Fall colors (September-October) turn surrounding aspen groves golden. Mornings offer glass-calm paddling before afternoon winds arrive.	Four interconnected alpine lakes with turquoise-emerald water, dramatic 11,000-foot peaks, and the 'Switzerland of California' moniker—plus electric-motors-only restrictions on Gull Lake mean calm water for paddlers.	lake_river	\N	CA-158, June Lake, CA, USA	June Lake	CA	37.7712962	-119.0869809	EhpDQS0xNTgsIEp1bmUgTGFrZSwgQ0EsIFVTQSIuKiwKFAoSCYcZ475KQJaAETFNVa0sguKcEhQKEgmr0E3r5mqWgBG0_j--eYxkZQ	\N	\N	\N	{"hookups": "dry", "cell_coverage": "good", "max_trailer_length_ft": 40}	t	\N	\N	28.00	USD	$28-35/night at Oh! Ridge (no hookups). June Lake RV Park and Silver Lake Resort offer full hookups for similar prices	{"best": ["june", "july", "august", "september", "october"], "notes": "Late June-September operation; fall colors September-October are magical"}	5-6 hours	\N	{"scenic_beauty": 5, "solitude_level": 3, "adventure_level": 4, "family_friendly": 5, "relaxation_factor": 5}	\N	{"parker": {"suitable": true, "activities": ["Attempting to paddle all four lakes", "Trophy trout fishing"], "engagement_level": 5}, "xander": {"suitable": true, "activities": ["Wading in shallow beach areas", "Collecting smooth rocks"], "engagement_level": 4}, "charlotte": {"suitable": true, "activities": ["Sandy June Lake Beach play", "Watching chipmunks"], "engagement_level": 5}}	\N	\N	\N	researching	0	{top-pick,paddleboarding,alpine-lakes,fall-colors,sierra}	{}	{}	\N	\N	2026-02-02 15:20:36.152+00	2026-02-06 04:02:02.573754+00	\N	\N	\N	2026-02-06 04:02:00.967+00	national_forest	\N	\N
00c935ec-90ca-479a-ae8c-c7261cdde2b7	b201a860-05a3-4ddc-bb89-4c4271177271	Convict Lake	Convict Lake Campground reserves 37 of its 88 sites for RVs 25-55 feet, with 50% reservable through Recreation.gov and 50% first-come-first-served. The marina rents kayaks and paddleboards. The 3.5-mile lakeside loop trail offers multiple wading spots. Keough Hot Springs sits a short drive away for evening soaking.	Arguably the most photogenic lake in the Eastern Sierra—turquoise water reflecting 12,241-foot Mount Morrison—with electric motors only ensuring peaceful conditions for paddle boarders.	lake_river	\N	Convict Lake, California 93546, USA	Mammoth Lakes	CA	37.5898951	-118.8582239	ChIJj3ImONYHloAR4_qdimtpnzQ	4.8	741	\N	{"hookups": "dry", "cell_coverage": "limited", "max_trailer_length_ft": 55}	t	\N	\N	31.00	USD	$31-35/night, no hookups. Bear lockers required at every site. Showers at resort (fee)	{"best": ["april", "may", "june", "july", "august", "september", "october"], "notes": "Open mid-April through early October. Fall foliage late September-October rivals June Lake without the crowds"}	5 hours	\N	{"scenic_beauty": 5, "solitude_level": 4, "adventure_level": 3, "family_friendly": 5, "relaxation_factor": 5}	\N	{"parker": {"suitable": true, "activities": ["Fishing for rainbow, brown, and brook trout"], "engagement_level": 5}, "xander": {"suitable": true, "activities": ["Splashing in Convict Creek", "Smooth rock collecting"], "engagement_level": 4}, "charlotte": {"suitable": true, "activities": ["Nature trail deer spotting", "Hot Creek visit"], "engagement_level": 4}}	\N	\N	\N	researching	0	{top-pick,paddleboarding,photography,serene,sierra}	{"Most photogenic Sierra lake","Electric-motor only (peaceful)","Smaller and quieter than June Lake"}	{"Limited to no cell coverage","No hookups"}	\N	\N	2026-02-02 15:20:36.736+00	2026-02-06 04:01:15.966391+00	[{"name": "places/ChIJj3ImONYHloAR4_qdimtpnzQ/reviews/Ci9DQUlRQUNvZENodHljRjlvT200emFrMVVNa3BHTW1kUWFXbGxVRmx3YjBKcE4wRRAB", "text": {"text": "Visited Convict Lake in Mammoth and did the loop hike around the lake—absolutely amazing! The trail is easy and relaxing, offering stunning visuals of the crystal-clear lake surrounded by dramatic mountain backdrops. Every turn gives you a new angle that’s picture-perfect. The reflections on the water are gorgeous, and the peaceful atmosphere makes it a must-do whether you’re hiking, fishing, or just soaking in the views. A true gem in the Mammoth area!", "languageCode": "en"}, "rating": 5, "publishTime": "2025-09-24T23:12:27.439920234Z", "originalText": {"text": "Visited Convict Lake in Mammoth and did the loop hike around the lake—absolutely amazing! The trail is easy and relaxing, offering stunning visuals of the crystal-clear lake surrounded by dramatic mountain backdrops. Every turn gives you a new angle that’s picture-perfect. The reflections on the water are gorgeous, and the peaceful atmosphere makes it a must-do whether you’re hiking, fishing, or just soaking in the views. A true gem in the Mammoth area!", "languageCode": "en"}, "googleMapsUri": "https://www.google.com/maps/reviews/data=!4m6!14m5!1m4!2m3!1sCi9DQUlRQUNvZENodHljRjlvT200emFrMVVNa3BHTW1kUWFXbGxVRmx3YjBKcE4wRRAB!2m1!1s0x809607d63826728f:0x349f696b8a9dfae3", "flagContentUri": "https://www.google.com/local/content/rap/report?postId=Ci9DQUlRQUNvZENodHljRjlvT200emFrMVVNa3BHTW1kUWFXbGxVRmx3YjBKcE4wRRAB&d=17924085&t=1", "authorAttribution": {"uri": "https://www.google.com/maps/contrib/111995896153963207597/reviews", "photoUri": "https://lh3.googleusercontent.com/a/ACg8ocKRNGKSwrSd5a9ucTnqB-hJ7XqjjrBAT0E1gjanFtqFVnZ0wBg=s128-c0x00000000-cc-rp-mo-ba6", "displayName": "Harry"}, "relativePublishTimeDescription": "4 months ago"}, {"name": "places/ChIJj3ImONYHloAR4_qdimtpnzQ/reviews/Ci9DQUlRQUNvZENodHljRjlvT2tSRmFEQm9jMWh1ZVUxRmFGbGpiRWt3UTBoMlRVRRAB", "text": {"text": "Beautiful lake, several bathrooms, and informative and helpful boat rental center.\\n\\nThe lake loop hike, if done counter clockwise around the lake, starts with little shade and fairly even terrain, before becoming shaded with a few small, shallow stream crossings at an approximate half way point. After this, the terrain becomes slightly more difficult, with much more up and down hill spots. Overall an easy hike.\\n\\nThere is a small section of fairly well maintained accessible trail along the eastern, southeastern edge of the lake.", "languageCode": "en"}, "rating": 5, "publishTime": "2025-07-25T19:01:08.490024905Z", "originalText": {"text": "Beautiful lake, several bathrooms, and informative and helpful boat rental center.\\n\\nThe lake loop hike, if done counter clockwise around the lake, starts with little shade and fairly even terrain, before becoming shaded with a few small, shallow stream crossings at an approximate half way point. After this, the terrain becomes slightly more difficult, with much more up and down hill spots. Overall an easy hike.\\n\\nThere is a small section of fairly well maintained accessible trail along the eastern, southeastern edge of the lake.", "languageCode": "en"}, "googleMapsUri": "https://www.google.com/maps/reviews/data=!4m6!14m5!1m4!2m3!1sCi9DQUlRQUNvZENodHljRjlvT2tSRmFEQm9jMWh1ZVUxRmFGbGpiRWt3UTBoMlRVRRAB!2m1!1s0x809607d63826728f:0x349f696b8a9dfae3", "flagContentUri": "https://www.google.com/local/content/rap/report?postId=Ci9DQUlRQUNvZENodHljRjlvT2tSRmFEQm9jMWh1ZVUxRmFGbGpiRWt3UTBoMlRVRRAB&d=17924085&t=1", "authorAttribution": {"uri": "https://www.google.com/maps/contrib/103215967825909479559/reviews", "photoUri": "https://lh3.googleusercontent.com/a-/ALV-UjWDrytDwtyKxQihKRH7iloNCjV1Lvo-HHZNMTzb7Wr7WXEi5tk9NQ=s128-c0x00000000-cc-rp-mo-ba3", "displayName": "Grayson Mx"}, "relativePublishTimeDescription": "6 months ago"}, {"name": "places/ChIJj3ImONYHloAR4_qdimtpnzQ/reviews/Ci9DQUlRQUNvZENodHljRjlvT21wTVRsSk1jMk5yVm5abFVsRnFOa1JrY0ZCamFVRRAB", "text": {"text": "Beautiful lake in midst of mountains. Perfect gateway for peace and family picnic", "l