599ee782-faa0-4e5b-809e-def12644e327	b201a860-05a3-4ddc-bb89-4c4271177271	Alabama Hills	Since 2021, dispersed camping requires a free permit (online or at Eastern Sierra Visitor Center) and is limited to approximately 50 designated sites. Only 2-4 sites accommodate 30-foot 5th wheels—arrive midweek before 3 PM for best selection. Main Movie Road is well-maintained dirt, accessible in 2WD.	Otherworldly rock formations where 400+ Westerns and sci-fi films were shot—Iron Man, Django Unchained, Lone Ranger—set against the dramatic backdrop of Mount Whitney, the highest peak in the lower 48.	boondocking	\N	Alabama Hills, Lone Pine, CA 93545, USA	Lone Pine	CA	36.5677116	-118.0898097	ChIJrfUrCwyGv4ARPZV1q-OY8P4	\N	\N	\N	{"hookups": "dry", "cell_coverage": "spotty", "road_accessibility": "Only 2-4 sites accommodate 30-foot 5th wheels—arrive midweek before 3 PM. Main Movie Road is well-maintained dirt, accessible in 2WD"}	t	\N	\N	0.00	USD	Free with required permit. 14-day limit. Water available in Lone Pine only. Backup: Tuttle Creek BLM Campground ($6/night)	{"best": ["march", "april", "may", "september", "october", "november"], "avoid": ["june", "july", "august"], "notes": "Summer exceeds 100°F"}	4.5 hours	\N	{"scenic_beauty": 5, "solitude_level": 5, "adventure_level": 5, "family_friendly": 4, "relaxation_factor": 4}	\N	{"parker": {"suitable": true, "activities": ["Expedition leader finding arches and movie locations"], "engagement_level": 5}, "xander": {"suitable": true, "activities": ["Spotting roadrunners, lizards, and jackrabbits"], "engagement_level": 4}, "charlotte": {"suitable": true, "activities": ["Scrambling through 'alien landscape' boulders"], "engagement_level": 5}}	\N	\N	\N	researching	0	{boondocking,movie-locations,arches,mount-whitney,wow-factor}	{"Free camping","400+ film locations","100+ natural arches","Mount Whitney backdrop"}	{"Only 2-4 sites fit 30ft 5th wheel","Spotty cell coverage","Water in Lone Pine only"}	\N	\N	2026-02-02 15:20:37.244+00	2026-02-