04b4ce03-72af-42e1-ac70-45e2ea93a12e	b201a860-05a3-4ddc-bb89-4c4271177271	Volcanic Tablelands	Multiple cleared pull-off sites accommodate 5th wheels along Casa Diablo Road (washboarded but passable). The petroglyphs at Fish Slough, Chidago Canyon, and Red Canyon sites let kids touch history. Happy/Sad Boulders draw world-class rock climbers, but easy scrambling suits all ages. The Ancient Bristlecone Pine Forest (world's oldest trees) sits 42 miles away.	A vast volcanic plateau formed 765,000 years ago, scattered with ancient Native American petroglyphs and offering 360-degree views of both the Sierra Nevada and White Mountains—one of the darkest skies accessible by RV in California.	boondocking	\N	\N	Bishop	CA	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	{"hookups": "dry", "dump_station": "Horton Creek ($5)", "cell_coverage": "good", "road_accessibility": "Casa Diablo Road is washboarded but passable"}	f	\N	\N	0.00	USD	Free dispersed camping. Free water at Bishop Speedway gas station; dump at Horton Creek ($5)	{"best": ["march", "april", "may", "september", "october", "november"], "notes": "Wind warning: Can reach 70+ mph gusts—check forecast"}	5 hours	\N	{"scenic_beauty": 5, "solitude_level": 5, "adventure_level": 4, "family_friendly": 4, "relaxation_factor": 4}	{"topics": ["Petroglyphs", "Volcanic geology", "Ancient Bristlecone Pines"]}	{"parker": {"suitable": true, "activities": ["Ancient rock art exploration", "Learning about volcano formation"], "engagement_level": 5}, "xander": {"suitable": true, "activities": ["Watching kangaroo rats emerge at dusk", "Counting shooting stars"], "engagement_level": 4}, "charlotte": {"suitable": true, "activities": ["Treasure hunts among boulders", "Searching for petroglyph symbols"], "engagement_level": 4}}	\N	\N	\N	researching	0	{boondocking,petroglyphs,dark-sky,free-camping}	{"Free camping","Darkest skies in CA by RV",Petroglyphs,"Good cell (50 mbps AT&T)"}	{"70+ mph wind gusts possible","Remote location"}	\N	\N	2026-02-02 15:20:37.756+00	2026-02-02 