06295e85-87b2-4826-8c0d-cd9479cf67cc	b201a860-05a3-4ddc-bb89-4c4271177271	Lake Isabella / Kern River	Lake Isabella offers water access closer than any Eastern Sierra lake, and the KOA provides pull-through sites with 30/50-amp service. The Kern River adds calm-water paddleboarding sections alongside whitewater kayaking for experienced paddlers. Trail of 100 Giants delivers sequoia awe without the 22-foot vehicle restrictions of Generals Highway.	California's largest body of water in Kern County plus the Trail of 100 Giants (ancient sequoias without Sequoia National Park's RV restrictions)—all 3.5 hours from LA.	lake_river	\N	Isabella Lake, California, USA	Lake Isabella	CA	35.6691264	-118.4338345	ChIJg7wrKi_MwYARFOoylHyr-Hw	4.4	304	\N	{"hookups": "full", "road_accessibility": "KOA has pull-through sites"}	f	\N	\N	50.00	USD	$50-80/night at KOA (15 minutes from lake, not waterfront). Non-potable water—bring drinking water	{"best": ["march", "april", "may", "september", "october", "november"], "notes": "Summer very hot. Critical wind warning: Lake generates 60 mph wind gusts without warning"}	3-3.5 hours	\N	{"scenic_beauty": 4, "solitude_level": 3, "adventure_level": 4, "family_friendly": 4, "relaxation_factor": 3}	{"topics": ["Sequoia ecology", "Gold rush history", "Water safety"]}	{"parker": {"suitable": true, "activities": ["OHV trails", "Sequoia exploration"], "engagement_level": 4}, "xander": {"suitable": true, "activities": ["Shallow water play", "Tree viewing"], "engagement_level": 3}, "charlotte": {"suitable": true, "activities": ["Trail of 100 Giants walk", "Beach play"], "engagement_level": 4}}	\N	\N	\N	researching	0	{lake,sequoias,paddleboarding}	{"Closest significant lake to LA","Sequoia access without RV restrictions"}	{"Notorious 60 mph wind gusts","Non-potable water","KOA not lakefront"}	\N	\N	2026-02-02 15:20:33.85+00	2026-02-06 04:05:25.447313+00	[{"name": "places/ChIJg7wrKi_MwYARFOoylHyr-Hw/reviews/Ci9DQUlRQUNvZENodHljRjlvT210SmNVVm5ObkY2YkhneWRIWXdWVl