tps://lh3.googleusercontent.com/a/ACg8ocIAgA7PDmBEwI1Bt2u-tWqiCYlkdi2V7GN86KqKEsTGqLmVfg=s128-c0x00000000-cc-rp-mo", "displayName": "Shea Reinhold"}, "relativePublishTimeDescription": "a year ago"}, {"name": "places/ChIJg7wrKi_MwYARFOoylHyr-Hw/reviews/ChdDSUhNMG9nS0VJQ0FnSUNVc0pDOWtnRRAB", "text": {"text": "We started going here 4 years ago and love it it's a great place to chill but when it gets windy it can become annoying we stay away from the river and stick to the lake . They have a dump station sometimes on holidays you will see porta potties near the parking by the lake and also there is bathrooms in the entrance we usually get the year pass since we go more than once a year plus you get a free yearly pass to give to a friend or family member.", "languageCode": "en"}, "rating": 5, "publishTime": "2020-01-06T08:57:55.293287Z", "originalText": {"text": "We started going here 4 years ago and love it it's a great place to chill but when it gets windy it can become annoying we stay away from the river and stick to the lake . They have a dump station sometimes on holidays you will see porta potties near the parking by the lake and also there is bathrooms in the entrance we usually get the year pass since we go more than once a year plus you get a free yearly pass to give to a friend or family member.", "languageCode": "en"}, "googleMapsUri": "https://www.google.com/maps/reviews/data=!4m6!14m5!1m4!2m3!1sChdDSUhNMG9nS0VJQ0FnSUNVc0pDOWtnRRAB!2m1!1s0x80c1cc2f2a2bbc83:0x7cf8ab7c9432ea14", "flagContentUri": "https://www.google.com/local/content/rap/report?postId=ChdDSUhNMG9nS0VJQ0FnSUNVc0pDOWtnRRAB&d=17924085&t=1", "authorAttribution": {"uri": "https://www.google.com/maps/contrib/112227022156377092418/reviews", "photoUri": "https://lh3.googleusercontent.com/a-/ALV-UjUqyKNU3tHUPCXVcfUPjym65DvABSD6asngXKu2zt0bzKQQ3oNn=s128-c0x00000000-cc-rp-mo-ba4", "displayName": "Victor Yucute"}, "relativePublishTimeDescription": "6 years ago"}, {"name": "places/ChIJg7wrKi_MwYARFOoylHyr-Hw/reviews/ChZDSUhNMG9nS0VJQ0FnSUQ4ejV5UlZ3EAE", "text": {"text": "Really a great place for a short adventure... ideal to take RV truck out there,l. There is no shadow other than the one you can create with tents orbother. We went for 2 days and we had a great adventure. Take the sun blocker with you!", "languageCode": "en"}, "rating": 4, "publishTime": "2020-08-03T18:06:51.349173Z", "originalText": {"text": "Really a great place for a short adventure... ideal to take RV truck out there,l. There is no shadow other than the one you can create with tents orbother. We went for 2 days and we had a great adventure. Take the sun blocker with you!", "languageCode": "en"}, "googleMapsUri": "https://www.google.com/maps/reviews/data=!4m6!14m5!1m4!2m3!1sChZDSUhNMG9nS0VJQ0FnSUQ4ejV5UlZ3EAE!2m1!1s0x80c1cc2f2a2bbc83:0x7cf8ab7c9432ea14", "flagContentUri": "https://www.google.com/local/content/rap/report?postId=ChZDSUhNMG9nS0VJQ0FnSUQ4ejV5UlZ3EAE&d=17924085&t=1", "authorAttribution": {"uri": "https://www.google.com/maps/contrib/118277392565291665170/reviews", "photoUri": "https://lh3.googleusercontent.com/a-/ALV-UjUtobY5KDbf3kggdneBv9jMEdDAyec10lhkNVfYiP1MsRn9jQtR=s128-c0x00000000-cc-rp-mo-ba7", "displayName": "Omar Barboza"}, "relativePublishTimeDescription": "5 years ago"}, {"name": "places/ChIJg7wrKi_MwYARFOoylHyr-Hw/reviews/ChZDSUhNMG9nS0VJQ0FnSUN3czZXSUtnEAE", "text": {"text": "This is a great place for a summer visit, but it can be precarious getting down to the water on some areas. Great to take the family to play and swim.", "languageCode": "en"}, "rating": 4, "publishTime": "2018-07-12T04:55:38.861Z", "originalText": {"text": "This is a great place for a summer visit, but it can be precarious getting down to the water on some areas. Great to take the family to play and swim.", "languageCode": "en"}, "googleMapsUri": "https://www.google.com/maps/reviews/data=!4m6!14m5!1m4!2m3!1sChZDSUhNMG9nS0VJQ0FnSUN3czZXSUtnEAE!2m1!1s0x80c1cc2f2a2bbc83:0x7cf8ab7c9432ea14", "flagContentUri": "https://www.google.com/local/content/rap/report?postId=ChZDSUhNMG9nS0VJQ0FnSUN3czZXSUtnEAE&d=17924085&t=1", "authorAttribution": {"uri": "https://www.google.com/maps/contrib/108207024363948432965/reviews", "photoUri": "https://lh3.googleusercontent.com/a-/ALV-UjVjhpXHm4PhhHMSulh8rnhWMHEjzA7h_aaq7FipdqbVN2qqctl_cQ=s128-c0x00000000-cc-rp-mo-ba4", "displayName": "April Hutchison"}, "relativePublishTimeDescription": "7 years ago"}]	Lake Isabella / Kern River is highly regarded as a beautiful summer destination that's perfect for families, offering free dispersed camping, great fishing, and swimming opportunities. Visitors consistently praise it as an ideal place to relax and chill, though the frequent windy conditions can be bothersome. The area appears well-suited for RV camping and family adventures, with basic amenities available.	{"summary": "Lake Isabella / Kern River is highly regarded as a beautiful summer destination that's perfect for families, offering free dispersed camping, great fishing, and swimming opportunities. Visitors consistently praise it as an ideal place to relax and chill, though the frequent windy conditions can be bothersome. The area appears well-suited for RV camping and family adventures, with basic amenities available.", "negative": [{"text": "It can be precarious getting down to the water on some areas.", "author": "April Hutchison", "rating": 4}, {"text": "When it gets windy it can become annoying... There is no shadow other than the one you can create with tents.", "author": "Victor Yucute / Omar Barboza", "rating": 4}], "positive": [{"text": "Great to take the family to play and swim.", "author": "April Hutchison", "rating": 4}, {"text": "I like the free camping. It's dispersed and quite. Fishing is great too.", "author": "Shea Reinhold", "rating": 5}, {"text": "Really a great place for a short adventure... ideal to take RV truck out there.", "author": "Omar Barboza", "rating": 4}], "last_updated": "2026-02-06T04:05:25.337Z"}	2026-02-06 04:05:17.538+00	army_corps	\N	\N
f6fe50ae-379a-4c49-8cda-892b9009eac8	b201a860-05a3-4ddc-bb89-4c4271177271	Grand Canyon South Rim	Trailer Village RV Park offers pull-through paved sites up to 50 feet with full hookups (30/50 amp, water, sewer)—exceptional infrastructure for a national park. Walking distance (0.5 miles) to the rim means no shuttle logistics. Market Plaza provides showers, laundry, and groceries.	Two billion years of Earth's history exposed in colorful rock layers—a natural time machine where California condors soar below the rim and kids walk on rocks older than complex life itself.	national_parks	\N	Grand Canyon Village, AZ 86023, USA	Grand Canyon Village	AZ	36.0569695	-112.1400606	ChIJ-TVGP4QRM4cRtENFnXs0_c0	4.9	1408	\N	{"hookups": "full", "cell_coverage": "reliable", "road_accessibility": "Pull-through paved sites", "max_trailer_length_ft": 50}	t	\N	\N	65.00	USD	~$65+/night. Book through Xanterra Parks (not Recreation.gov)	{"best": ["march", "april", "may", "september", "october"], "notes": "Summer is hot and crowded, winter is cold but magical"}	7-8 hours	\N	{"scenic_beauty": 5, "solitude_level": 2, "adventure_level": 5, "family_friendly": 5, "relaxation_factor": 3}	{"topics": ["Geology (2 billion years)", "Condor recovery", "Native American history", "Paleontology"], "visitor_center": true, "ranger_programs": true, "junior_ranger_program": true}	{"parker": {"suitable": true, "activities": ["Ooh Aah Point hike challenge", "Condor spotting", "Geology layer photography"], "engagement_level": 5}, "xander": {"suitable": true, "activities": ["Stroller on Rim Trail", "Watching ravens and squirrels", "Shuttle bus rides"], "engagement_level": 4}, "charlotte": {"suitable": true, "activities": ["Touching 2-billion-year-old rocks on Trail of Time", "Shuttle rides between viewpoints", "Junior Ranger activities"], "engagement_level": 5}}	\N	\N	\N	researching	0	{top-pick,national-park,bucket-list,geology,condors}	{"Exceptional infrastructure (50ft, full hookups)","Walking distance to rim","Junior Ranger programs"}	{"7-8 hour drive","Below-rim trails have steep drop-offs with no railings"}	Critical safety: Below-rim trails have steep drop-offs with no railings. Use carriers for younger children, keep hands on all kids	\N	2026-02-02 15:20:40.282+00	2026-02-06 03:47:21.750341+00	[{"name": "places/ChIJ-TVGP4QRM4cRtENFnXs0_c0/reviews/Ci9DQUlRQUNvZENodHljRjlvT25oR1NUQTJZVU5rWlZOb2JsUmlkbDk2WDNaNVYwRRAB", "text": {"text": "A Serene, Breathtaking Way to Experience the Canyon\\nThe North Rim offers a completely different Grand Canyon experience — higher elevation, cooler temperatures, and far fewer people. The viewpoints are stunning, and the sense of scale and depth is overwhelming in the best way.\\nThe drive in is beautiful, the overlooks are well spaced, and the trails are peaceful and well maintained. Perfect for hiking, photography, and quiet reflection.\\nTips:\\n• Open seasonally (usually mid-May to mid-October)\\n• Bring layers — weather can change quickly\\n• Sunrise and sunset here are next level\\n• Gas up before arriving — services are limited\\nIf you want the Grand Canyon without crowds, this is the place.", "languageCode": "en"}, "rating": 5, "publishTime": "2026-01-14T10:11:06.388847496Z", "originalText": {"text": "A Serene, Breathtaking Way to Experience the Canyon\\nThe North Rim offers a completely different Grand Canyon experience — higher elevation, cooler temperatures, and far fewer people. The viewpoints are stunning, and the sense of scale and depth is overwhelming in the best way.\\nThe drive in is beautiful, the overlooks are well spaced, and the trails are peaceful and well maintained. Perfect for hiking, photography, and quiet reflection.\\nTips:\\n• Open seasonally (usually mid-May to mid-October)\\n• Bring layers — weather can change quickly\\n• Sunrise and sunset here are next level\\n• Gas up before arriving — services are limited\\nIf you want the Grand Canyon without crowds, this is the place.", "languageCode": "en"}, "googleMapsUri": "https://www.google.com/maps/reviews/data=!4m6!14m5!1m4!2m3!1sCi9DQUlRQUNvZENodHljRjlvT25oR1NUQTJZVU5rWlZOb2JsUmlkbDk2WDNaNVYwRRAB!2m1!1s0x873311843f4635f9:0xcdfd347b9d4543b4", "flagContentUri": "https://www.google.com/local/content/rap/report?postId=Ci9DQUlRQUNvZENodHljRjlvT25oR1NUQTJZVU5rWlZOb2JsUmlkbDk2WDNaNVYwRRAB&d=17924085&t=1", "authorAttribution": {"uri": "https://www.google.com/maps/contrib/116348710655391386905/reviews", "photoUri": "https://lh3.googleusercontent.com/a-/ALV-UjW1wf77hTtXGIN6wmv27Ri0Eu7hicXlawHiXI1LESdmyMFl_QrC=s128-c0x00000000-cc-rp-mo-ba3", "displayName": "Harley Hook"}, "relativePublishTimeDescription": "3 weeks ago"}, {"name": "places/ChIJ-TVGP4QRM4cRtENFnXs0_c0/reviews/Ci9DQUlRQUNvZENodHljRjlvT21KWVlrVXRUSEZaUjBGQlZ6bEVNMmhQU3psRkxXYxAB", "text": {"text": "We visited in late September, and it was the best time to go there (we are told). Weather was amazing (clear skies, temperate climate and the crowds were sparse'ish). We took an organised tour from Vegas - an early start at 5:30am, weird pick up time and place - long drive to the South Rim , with three stops for food / restrooms along the way (including a stop by a quaint shop on Route 66).  Quick view of the Hoover Dam on the way and back (did not stop).\\nThe Grand Canyon... its all been said before so all I can say is just go and see it for yourself. Simply Vast and majestic. The amenities, trails etc are all very well laid out and easy to follow.  Lots of spots to stop and take pics. The place is huge to walk around so you need time. Nice shops to look around at the Village once you reach there (though the prices are ...pricey! to be expected.) . Do make sure you do some trails to feel the atmosphere. I would have preferred to drive there myself but the tour guide provided a good overview.", "languageCode": "en"}, "rating": 5, "publishTime": "2025-10-11T14:03:41.457132791Z", "originalText": {"text": "We visited in late September, and it was the best time to go there (we are told). Weather was amazing (clear skies, temperate climate and the crowds were sparse'ish). We took an organised tour from Vegas - an early start at 5:30am, weird pick up time and place - long drive to the South Rim , with three stops for food / restrooms along the way (including a stop by a quaint shop on Route 66).  Quick view of the Hoover Dam on the way and back (did not stop).\\nThe Grand Canyon... its all been said before so all I can say is just go and see it for yourself. Simply Vast and majestic. The amenities, trails etc are all very well laid out and easy to follow.  Lots of spots to stop and take pics. The place is huge to walk around so you need time. Nice shops to look around at the Village once you reach there (though the prices are ...pricey! to be expected.) . Do make sure you do some trails to feel the atmosphere. I would have preferred to drive there myself but the tour guide provided a good overview.", "languageCode": "en"}, "googleMapsUri": "https://www.google.com/maps/reviews/data=!4m6!14m5!1m4!2m3!1sCi9DQUlRQUNvZENodHljRjlvT21KWVlrVXRUSEZaUjBGQlZ6bEVNMmhQU3psRkxXYxAB!2m1!1s0x873311843f4635f9:0xcdfd347b9d4543b4", "flagContentUri": "https://www.google.com/local/content/rap/report?postId=Ci9DQUlRQUNvZENodHljRjlvT21KWVlrVXRUSEZaUjBGQlZ6bEVNMmhQU3psRkxXYxAB&d=17924085&t=1", "authorAttribution": {"uri": "https://www.google.com/maps/contrib/111824895583933300009/reviews", "photoUri": "https://lh3.googleusercontent.com/a-/ALV-UjVxQGdo5PSulvEXWsI8_6q2OYsZIGSu-gBz5tPZjkik5qr0lUBa=s128-c0x00000000-cc-rp-mo-ba4", "displayName": "Sunil Inamdar"}, "relativePublishTimeDescription": "3 months ago"}, {"name": "places/ChIJ-TVGP4QRM4cRtENFnXs0_c0/reviews/Ci9DQUlRQUNvZENodHljRjlvT21SMGJuZG1NSGRIUzJoSkxUVkpSRWRaYm5wQlNXYxAB", "text": {"text": "Always worth the visit ✨🍬🥳🎉\\nI’ve been during hot days and during winter time - make sure to monitor for gusty winds and wear layers!\\n-\\nThe views and the drive and the canyon and the whole experience is great!\\n-\\nMilitary and seniors get huge discount and a card for all national parks in the country!", "languageCode": "en"}, "rating": 5, "publishTime": "2026-01-02T03:54:53.140222078Z", "originalText": {"text": "Always worth the visit ✨🍬🥳🎉\\nI’ve been during hot days and during winter time - make sure to monitor for gusty winds and wear layers!\\n-\\nThe views and the drive and the canyon and the whole experience is great!\\n-\\nMilitary and seniors get huge discount and a card for all national parks in the country!", "languageCode": "en"}, "googleMapsUri": "https://www.google.com/maps/reviews/data=!4m6!14m5!1m4!2m3!1sCi9DQUlRQUNvZENodHljRjlvT21SMGJuZG1NSGRIUzJoSkxUVkpSRWRaYm5wQlNXYxAB!2m1!1s0x873311843f4635f9:0xcdfd347b9d4543b4", "flagContentUri": "https://www.google.com/local/content/rap/report?postId=Ci9DQUlRQUNvZENodHljRjlvT21SMGJuZG1NSGRIUzJoSkxUVkpSRWRaYm5wQlNXYxAB&d=17924085&t=1", "authorAttribution": {"uri": "https://www.google.com/maps/contrib/109870003975800170383/reviews", "photoUri": "https://lh3.googleusercontent.com/a-/ALV-UjXV4KlZh0UoRplTr_1Y_8yWSxeesoB4f7wO3riDju2YDKWzu81b=s128-c0x00000000-cc-rp-mo-ba5", "displayName": "Sadda Shaker"}, "relativePublishTimeDescription": "a month ago"}, {"name": "places/ChIJ-TVGP4QRM4cRtENFnXs0_c0/reviews/Ci9DQUlRQUNvZENodHljRjlvT2tWM1MxOVBPVXhwY1VWVVlubHNNMDlJYVhkWFlYYxAB", "text": {"text": "Awe-inspiring, breath taking views!! Words and photos don't quite capture the splendor and beauty! Wonderful drive with views from stopping points or hike along the South rim trail. So much to see and do. Would recommend charting where you want to go if you only have 1 day as some places can only be seen by taking the shuttle busses. Restrooms are plentiful throughout the park. Cost $30 for passenger car and 7 day entry pass.", "languageCode": "en"}, "rating": 5, "publishTime": "2025-09-30T17:37:21.004543845Z", "originalText": {"text": "Awe-inspiring, breath taking views!! Words and photos don't quite capture the splendor and beauty! Wonderful drive with views from stopping points or hike along the South rim trail. So much to see and do. Would recommend charting where you want to go if you only have 1 day as some places can only be seen by taking the shuttle busses. Restrooms are plentiful throughout the park. Cost $30 for passenger car and 7 day entry pass.", "languageCode": "en"}, "googleMapsUri": "https://www.google.com/maps/reviews/data=!4m6!14m5!1m4!2m3!1sCi9DQUlRQUNvZENodHljRjlvT2tWM1MxOVBPVXhwY1VWVVlubHNNMDlJYVhkWFlYYxAB!2m1!1s0x873311843f4635f9:0xcdfd347b9d4543b4", "flagContentUri": "https://www.google.com/local/content/rap/report?postId=Ci9DQUlRQUNvZENodHljRjlvT2tWM1MxOVBPVXhwY1VWVVlubHNNMDlJYVhkWFlYYxAB&d=17924085&t=1", "authorAttribution": {"uri": "https://www.google.com/maps/contrib/105951943685431503621/reviews", "photoUri": "https://lh3.googleusercontent.com/a/ACg8ocKrjVvagYdOlbJqIE6pnAdYdyVoVsa1TCWn_nesndu10OGHTGA=s128-c0x00000000-cc-rp-mo-ba4", "displayName": "holly nagel"}, "relativePublishTimeDescription": "4 months ago"}, {"name": "places/ChIJ-TVGP4QRM4cRtENFnXs0_c0/reviews/Ci9DQUlRQUNvZENodHljRjlvT25wa1FVbENjV3R2TVcxMmJHVmFTVWhOUzB3eFdFRRAB", "text": {"text": "Well worth a visit and its an easy rim walk and bus access that helps evey ability.\\nParking can be tough if you arrive late restroom we're super busy ( thanksgiving) nice gift shop. Athe views are to die for.", "languageCode": "en"}, "rating": 5, "publishTime": "2025-11-29T23:59:18.241398399Z", "originalText": {"text": "Well worth a visit and its an easy rim walk and bus access that helps evey ability.\\nParking can be tough if you arrive late restroom we're super busy ( thanksgiving) nice gift shop. Athe views are to die for.", "languageCode": "en"}, "googleMapsUri": "https://www.google.com/maps/reviews/data=!4m6!14m5!1m4!2m3!1sCi9DQUlRQUNvZENodHljRjlvT25wa1FVbENjV3R2TVcxMmJHVmFTVWhOUzB3eFdFRRAB!2m1!1s0x873311843f4635f9:0xcdfd347b9d4543b4", "flagContentUri": "https://www.google.com/local/content/rap/report?postId=Ci9DQUlRQUNvZENodHljRjlvT25wa1FVbENjV3R2TVcxMmJHVmFTVWhOUzB3eFdFRRAB&d=17924085&t=1", "authorAttribution": {"uri": "https://www.google.com/maps/contrib/106705358712899471476/reviews", "photoUri": "https://lh3.googleusercontent.com/a-/ALV-UjViuXiVdHubNV42LxttwdcnPbacpTYrx16k0UnQrETRcLDyyuM=s128-c0x00000000-cc-rp-mo-ba6", "displayName": "Lee James"}, "relativePublishTimeDescription": "2 months ago"}]	The Grand Canyon South Rim consistently delivers awe-inspiring, breathtaking views that visitors describe as vast and majestic, with well-maintained trails and facilities that accommodate all ability levels. The experience is enhanced by excellent amenities, shuttle bus access, and multiple viewpoints, though visitors should plan ahead due to the enormous size of the area and potential parking challenges during busy periods.	{"summary": "The Grand Canyon South Rim consistently delivers awe-inspiring, breathtaking views that visitors describe as vast and majestic, with well-maintained trails and facilities that accommodate all ability levels. The experience is enhanced by excellent amenities, shuttle bus access, and multiple viewpoints, though visitors should plan ahead due to the enormous size of the area and potential parking challenges during busy periods.", "negative": [{"text": "Parking can be tough if you arrive late restroom we're super busy (thanksgiving)", "author": "Lee James", "rating": 5}, {"text": "Would recommend charting where you want to go if you only have 1 day as some places can only be seen by taking the shuttle busses.", "author": "holly nagel", "rating": 5}], "positive": [{"text": "Well worth a visit and its an easy rim walk and bus access that helps every ability.", "author": "Lee James", "rating": 5}, {"text": "The amenities, trails etc are all very well laid out and easy to follow. Lots of spots to stop and take pics.", "author": "Sunil Inamdar", "rating": 5}, {"text": "Restrooms are plentiful throughout the park.", "author": "holly nagel", "rating": 5}], "last_updated": "2026-02-06T03:47:21.650Z"}	2026-02-06 03:47:14.312+00	national_park	\N	\N
7b18be70-d4df-4ac0-8eb4-91fe68b76b34	b201a860-05a3-4ddc-bb89-4c4271177271	Lake Havasu	Lake Havasu State Park offers 54 sites with 50-amp electric and water hookups ($50/night). Crazy Horse Campgrounds sprawls across 617 sites with lakefront options ($40-80). The water temperature allows comfortable swimming spring through fall while Sierra lakes remain frigid. Morning paddles before afternoon winds deliver ideal conditions.	300+ days of sunshine, warm water year-round (unlike cold Sierra lakes), and the actual London Bridge transported stone-by-stone from England—plus sandy white beaches perfect for Xander.	lake_river	\N	Lake Havasu City, AZ, USA	Lake Havasu City	AZ	34.4769588	-114.3191952	ChIJI-CJ7hby0YAR4tMqt8-D3pg	\N	\N	\N	{"hookups": "water_electric", "cell_coverage": "excellent"}	f	\N	\N	50.00	USD	State Park $50/night (50-amp + water). Crazy Horse $40-80 with lakefront options	{"best": ["march", "april", "may", "october", "november"], "avoid": ["june", "july", "august"], "notes": "Avoid spring break (college crowds) and summer (100°F+)"}	4-5 hours	\N	{"scenic_beauty": 4, "solitude_level": 2, "adventure_level": 4, "family_friendly": 4, "relaxation_factor": 4}	\N	{"parker": {"suitable": true, "activities": ["Exploring hidden coves by paddleboard"], "engagement_level": 4}, "xander": {"suitable": true, "activities": ["Beach sand play", "Warm water without cold shock"], "engagement_level": 5}, "charlotte": {"suitable": true, "activities": ["Warm shallow water play", "Sandy beaches"], "engagement_level": 5}}	http://www.lhcaz.gov/	\N	\N	researching	0	{lake,warm-water,london-bridge,beaches}	{"Warm water year-round","300+ sunny days","London Bridge"}	{"Powerboat lake with high traffic","Spring break party crowds"}	\N	\N	2026-02-02 15:20:38.751+00	2026-02-06 03:50:13.495824+00	\N	\N	\N	2026-02-06 03:50:11.422+00	\N	\N	\N
b44a2e78-2448-425d-88d1-ccfc0c0413c2	b201a860-05a3-4ddc-bb89-4c4271177271	Pinnacles National Park	Pinnacles Campground accepts RVs up to 42 feet and offers electric hookups—rare for national parks. Bear Gulch Cave lets families scramble through talus passages by flashlight (bring your own). The High Peaks trail features iron handholds bolted into rock. And the endangered condor recovery program means regular sightings of 9-foot wingspans from the campground itself.	Two different cave systems where kids crawl through darkness with flashlights, plus California condors soaring overhead and a campground swimming pool for afternoon cool-down.	national_parks	\N	California 95043, USA	Paicines	CA	36.4905655	-121.1824925	ChIJn93OiYBDkoAR7kSomO77gps	4.7	4916	\N	{"hookups": "electric_only", "cell_coverage": "none", "max_trailer_length_ft": 42}	t	\N	\N	59.00	USD	$59/night + $12 weekend surcharge for RV sites with 30-amp electric	{"best": ["march", "april", "may", "september", "october", "november"], "notes": "Bear Gulch closes late spring/early summer for bat maternity season. Check status before planning"}	4.5-5 hours	\N	{"scenic_beauty": 5, "solitude_level": 4, "adventure_level": 5, "family_friendly": 5, "relaxation_factor": 3}	{"topics": ["Cave geology", "California condor recovery", "Volcanic formations"]}	{"parker": {"suitable": true, "activities": ["Cave navigation as leader", "High Peaks trail iron handholds"], "engagement_level": 5}, "xander": {"suitable": true, "activities": ["Watching turkeys and deer at campground", "Swimming pool"], "engagement_level": 4}, "charlotte": {"suitable": true, "activities": ["Crawling through tight cave passages", "Condor spotting"], "engagement_level": 5}}	https://www.nps.gov/pinn/index.htm	(831) 389-4486	\N	researching	0	{caves,condors,national-park,pool}	{"42-foot RV capacity","Electric hookups (rare for NP)","Swimming pool","Condor sightings"}	{"No cell service","Cave may be closed for bats"}	\N	\N	2026-02-02 15:20:33.463+00	2026-02-06 04:06:01.522003+00	[{"name": "places/ChIJn93OiYBDkoAR7kSomO77gps/reviews/Ci9DQUlRQUNvZENodHljRjlvT21SdWNYRkVWRkV4ZERsbVYyWnJRMHhCT0d4dlNXYxAB", "text": {"text": "Absolutely amazing park!\\nBring hiking poles, head lamps, lots of water, snacks, and food. I could spend several days here. We had absolutely perfect weather. We visited on the West side.\\nWould definitely NOT want to come here in the summer! It would be way too hot!", "languageCode": "en"}, "rating": 5, "publishTime": "2026-01-21T05:56:28.222488344Z", "originalText": {"text": "Absolutely amazing park!\\nBring hiking poles, head lamps, lots of water, snacks, and food. I could spend several days here. We had absolutely perfect weather. We visited on the West side.\\nWould definitely NOT want to come here in the summer! It would be way too hot!", "languageCode": "en"}, "googleMapsUri": "https://www.google.com/maps/reviews/data=!4m6!14m5!1m4!2m3!1sCi9DQUlRQUNvZENodHljRjlvT21SdWNYRkVWRkV4ZERsbVYyWnJRMHhCT0d4dlNXYxAB!2m1!1s0x8092438089cedd9f:0x9b82fbee98a844ee", "flagContentUri": "https://www.google.com/local/content/rap/report?postId=Ci9DQUlRQUNvZENodHljRjlvT21SdWNYRkVWRkV4ZERsbVYyWnJRMHhCT0d4dlNXYxAB&d=17924085&t=1", "authorAttribution": {"uri": "https://www.google.com/maps/contrib/105557152872666164486/reviews", "photoUri": "https://lh3.googleusercontent.com/a-/ALV-UjWSKfQq_Z8iCX3RgAZBcG-ngU2bh7MZIIU2TFb3ru6F-xYAmULd=s128-c0x00000000-cc-rp-mo-ba7", "displayName": "Allison Wright"}, "relativePublishTimeDescription": "2 weeks ago"}, {"name": "places/ChIJn93OiYBDkoAR7kSomO77gps/reviews/Ci9DQUlRQUNvZENodHljRjlvT2pGdGFFeHVTME40WXpKaVoyZHpjbGhxV1Y5TGVuYxAB", "text": {"text": "Pinnacles National Park is a very cool place to visit and one I return to a few times each year. The hikes are excellent, and it’s incredibly impressive to see the California condors here—every visit feels different. On one hike, a condor passed within about three feet of us, which was unforgettable. Bring lunch to enjoy at the top, and be sure to pack out your trash back to the parking area. There are plenty of bathrooms throughout the park, which makes the visit even more convenient.", "languageCode": "en"}, "rating": 5, "publishTime": "2026-01-24T20:18:49.538905377Z", "originalText": {"text": "Pinnacles National Park is a very cool place to visit and one I return to a few times each year. The hikes are excellent, and it’s incredibly impressive to see the California condors here—every visit feels different. On one hike, a condor passed within about three feet of us, which was unforgettable. Bring lunch to enjoy at the top, and be sure to pack out your trash back to the parking area. There are plenty of bathrooms throughout the park, which makes the visit even more convenient.", "languageCode": "en"}, "googleMapsUri": "https://www.google.com/maps/reviews/data=!4m6!14m5!1m4!2m3!1sCi9DQUlRQUNvZENodHljRjlvT2pGdGFFeHVTME40WXpKaVoyZHpjbGhxV1Y5TGVuYxAB!2m1!1s0x8092438089cedd9f:0x9b82fbee98a844ee", "flagContentUri": "https://www.google.com/local/content/rap/report?postId=Ci9DQUlRQUNvZENodHljRjlvT2pGdGFFeHVTME40WXpKaVoyZHpjbGhxV1Y5TGVuYxAB&d=17924085&t=1", "authorAttribution": {"uri": "https://www.google.com/maps/contrib/109692438617834530100/reviews", "photoUri": "https://lh3.googleusercontent.com/a-/ALV-UjVc4pmQsciEuBujEBhz1euiXKJSuNh8W-gshfDE3Y6OrLmmwqI=s128-c0x00000000-cc-rp-mo-ba4", "displayName": "Ruben D."}, "relativePublishTimeDescription": "a week ago"}, {"name": "places/ChIJn93OiYBDkoAR7kSomO77gps/reviews/Ci9DQUlRQUNvZENodHljRjlvT2tOUU9HbElaSHBPT0U5ellYa3plR05QVEdkRFdXYxAB", "text": {"text": "One of the most underestimated parks!\\nAnd most unique parks! Dramatic volcanic rock formations, talus caves, and soaring condors make it unforgettable. The hikes range from easy to challenging — Bear Gulch and High Peaks are must-dos. We visited in early fall — pleasant weather, not crowded, and plenty of parking. Perfect mix of adventure, views, and quiet beauty.", "languageCode": "en"}, "rating": 5, "publishTime": "2025-11-07T07:30:46.724118426Z", "originalText": {"text": "One of the most underestimated parks!\\nAnd most unique parks! Dramatic volcanic rock formations, talus caves, and soaring condors make it unforgettable. The hikes range from easy to challenging — Bear Gulch and High Peaks are must-dos. We visited in early fall — pleasant weather, not crowded, and plenty of parking. Perfect mix of adventure, views, and quiet beauty.", "languageCode": "en"}, "googleMapsUri": "https://www.google.com/maps/reviews/data=!4m6!14m5!1m4!2m3!1sCi9DQUlRQUNvZENodHljRjlvT2tOUU9HbElaSHBPT0U5ellYa3plR05QVEdkRFdXYxAB!2m1!1s0x8092438089cedd9f:0x9b82fbee98a844ee", "flagContentUri": "https://www.google.com/local/content/rap/report?postId=Ci9DQUlRQUNvZENodHljRjlvT2tOUU9HbElaSHBPT0U5ellYa3plR05QVEdkRFdXYxAB&d=17924085&t=1", "authorAttribution": {"uri": "https://www.google.com/maps/contrib/108103075028697848941/reviews", "photoUri": "https://lh3.googleusercontent.com/a-/ALV-UjVVZTgup420wRHuZqsMxEfuP235j4YXqM13KmWTGmLwCGJSwYcALQ=s128-c0x00000000-cc-rp-mo-ba6", "displayName": "Marta Stashevska"}, "relativePublishTimeDescription": "3 months ago"}, {"name": "places/ChIJn93OiYBDkoAR7kSomO77gps/reviews/Ci9DQUlRQUNvZENodHljRjlvT25BME1WbGZPV2w2YUVwd1ZVcGpaRlpXYjJaNFkxRRAB", "text": {"text": "A friend and I went for a small day trip and this didn't disappoint, the trails we took were both well marked and provided fun opportunities climbing under and on top of rocks I will preface it does help to be more on the leaner side when going through the cave sections. But overall the lake, cliffs, giant rock walls and everything in between fantastic, I will be coming again", "languageCode": "en"}, "rating": 5, "publishTime": "2025-12-18T07:03:14.308054528Z", "originalText": {"text": "A friend and I went for a small day trip and this didn't disappoint, the trails we took were both well marked and provided fun opportunities climbing under and on top of rocks I will preface it does help to be more on the leaner side when going through the cave sections. But overall the lake, cliffs, giant rock walls and everything in between fantastic, I will be coming again", "languageCode": "en"}, "googleMapsUri": "https://www.google.com/maps/reviews/data=!4m6!14m5!1m4!2m3!1sCi9DQUlRQUNvZENodHljRjlvT25BME1WbGZPV2w2YUVwd1ZVcGpaRlpXYjJaNFkxRRAB!2m1!1s0x8092438089cedd9f:0x9b82fbee98a844ee", "flagContentUri": "https://www.google.com/local/content/rap/report?postId=Ci9DQUlRQUNvZENodHljRjlvT25BME1WbGZPV2w2YUVwd1ZVcGpaRlpXYjJaNFkxRRAB&d=17924085&t=1", "authorAttribution": {"uri": "https://www.google.com/maps/contrib/104255451323939116902/reviews", "photoUri": "https://lh3.googleusercontent.com/a-/ALV-UjWcrmzsD3_2ha96lHxldcrZz81NXiyFSQ06tTycPqgwBfYU5amI=s128-c0x00000000-cc-rp-mo-ba4", "displayName": "Carter Jergensen"}, "relativePublishTimeDescription": "a month ago"}, {"name": "places/ChIJn93OiYBDkoAR7kSomO77gps/reviews/Ci9DQUlRQUNvZENodHljRjlvT2t4TFJUUTFiM1F4YTFoTU9IRmpXbVZ2V0c1U1JYYxAB", "text": {"text": "First time being here and it was a great visit. Lots of open space and beautiful trails. I only explored the west side of the park but it had tons to see. Saw a small part of the caves but once I come back, ill check out the rest, along with the west part of the park.", "languageCode": "en"}, "rating": 5, "publishTime": "2025-11-30T00:51:31.162753440Z", "originalText": {"text": "First time being here and it was a great visit. Lots of open space and beautiful trails. I only explored the west side of the park but it had tons to see. Saw a small part of the caves but once I come back, ill check out the rest, along with the west part of the park.", "languageCode": "en"}, "googleMapsUri": "https://www.google.com/maps/reviews/data=!4m6!14m5!1m4!2m3!1sCi9DQUlRQUNvZENodHljRjlvT2t4TFJUUTFiM1F4YTFoTU9IRmpXbVZ2V0c1U1JYYxAB!2m1!1s0x8092438089cedd9f:0x9b82fbee98a844ee", "flagContentUri": "https://www.google.com/local/content/rap/report?postId=Ci9DQUlRQUNvZENodHljRjlvT2t4TFJUUTFiM1F4YTFoTU9IRmpXbVZ2V0c1U1JYYxAB&d=17924085&t=1", "authorAttribution": {"uri": "https://www.google.com/maps/contrib/100019572311896520698/reviews", "photoUri": "https://lh3.googleusercontent.com/a-/ALV-UjWOJMEJjc9X2sLR5XcLEJV_S98OMbENm-QB82HtKMPg9OAzGVSKaA=s128-c0x00000000-cc-rp-mo-ba3", "displayName": "Frank Martinez"}, "relativePublishTimeDescription": "2 months ago"}]	Pinnacles National Park receives outstanding reviews as an underrated gem featuring dramatic volcanic rock formations, talus caves, and the chance to see California condors up close. Visitors consistently praise the excellent hiking trails, unique cave experiences, and stunning scenery, with many planning return visits. The park offers a perfect mix of adventure and natural beauty, though reviewers emphasize the importance of proper preparation and timing.	{"summary": "Pinnacles National Park receives outstanding reviews as an underrated gem featuring dramatic volcanic rock formations, talus caves, and the chance to see California condors up close. Visitors consistently praise the excellent hiking trails, unique cave experiences, and stunning scenery, with many planning return visits. The park offers a perfect mix of adventure and natural beauty, though reviewers emphasize the importance of proper preparation and timing.", "negative": [{"text": "I will preface it does help to be more on the leaner side when going through the cave sections.", "author": "Carter Jergensen", "rating": 5}, {"text": "Would definitely NOT want to come here in the summer! It would be way too hot!", "author": "Allison Wright", "rating": 5}], "positive": [{"text": "The hikes range from easy to challenging — Bear Gulch and High Peaks are must-dos.", "author": "Marta Stashevska", "rating": 5}, {"text": "The trails we took were both well marked and provided fun opportunities climbing under and on top of rocks", "author": "Carter Jergensen", "rating": 5}, {"text": "There are plenty of bathrooms throughout the park, which makes the visit even more c