64c22c93-c9ab-43a9-a498-6c883de25962	b201a860-05a3-4ddc-bb89-4c4271177271	California Hot Springs Resort	Small deli and ice cream shop on site. Complete digital detox experience in Sierra foothills.	Full RV hookups across from natural hot spring pools in Sierra foothills. Near Sequoia National Monument trails. Complete digital detox—no cell service or internet.	couples_getaway	\N	42177 Hot Springs Rd, California Hot Springs, CA 93207, USA	California Hot Springs	CA	35.8804516	-118.6697289	ChIJf7qK9hWd6oARuibLXsl7tco	4.5	245	\N	{"hookups": "full", "cell_coverage": "none"}	t	\N	\N	\N	USD	\N	{"best": ["march", "april", "may", "september", "october", "november"], "notes": "Spring and fall optimal"}	3 hours	\N	{"scenic_beauty": 4, "solitude_level": 5, "adventure_level": 2, "family_friendly": 3, "relaxation_factor": 5}	\N	\N	http://cahotsprings.net/	(661) 548-6582	\N	researching	0	{couples,hot-springs,digital-detox,sequoia-access}	{}	{}	\N	\N	2026-02-02 15:20:44.534+00	2026-02-02 18:55:12.061728+00	[{"name": "places/ChIJf7qK9hWd6oARuibLXsl7tco/reviews/ChdDSUhNMG9nS0VJQ0FnSUR2dVA2WnpnRRAB", "text": {"text": "This place was such a magical gem during my cross country trip with 2 small kids in tow.\\n\\nI was towing my camper and they had great camping sites located across the street that was very secluded and private. Cell service was limited.\\n\\nThe pool and hot tubs were just heaven. The main pool was like bathwater while the other tubs had varying degrees of hot. Loved loved loved it.\\n\\nStaff was pleasant and stay was very memorable. Would love to return someday.", "languageCode": "en"}, "rating": 5, "publishTime": "2024-12-17T12:23:19.853933Z", "originalText": {"text": "This place was such a magical gem during my cross country trip with 2 small kids in tow.\\n\\nI was towing my camper and they had great camping sites located across the street that was very secluded and private. Cell service was limited.\\n\\nThe pool and hot tubs were just heaven. The main pool was like bathwater while the other tubs had varying degrees of hot. Loved loved loved it.\\n\\nStaff was pleasant and stay was very memorable. Would love to return someday.", "languageCode": "en"}, "googleMapsUri": "https://www.google.com/maps/reviews/data=!4m6!14m5!1m4!2m3!1sChdDSUhNMG9nS0VJQ0FnSUR2dVA2WnpnRRAB!2m1!1s0x80ea9d15f68aba7f:0xcab57bc95ecb26ba", "flagContentUri": "https://www.google.com/local/content/rap/report?postId=ChdDSUhNMG9nS0VJQ0FnSUR2dVA2WnpnRRAB&d=17924085&t=1", "authorAttribution": {"uri": "https://www.google.com/maps/contrib/103650646527619725254/reviews", "photoUri": "https://lh3.googleusercontent.com/a/ACg8ocLCXnSbbC3DLoJUVV8NxqXAFnXBr72IB0jqYA8WLBzTKbmlQTo=s128-c0x00000000-cc-rp-mo-ba5", "displayName": "E Hi-Chang"}, "relativePublishTimeDescription": "a year ago"}, {"name": "places/ChIJf7qK9hWd6oARuibLXsl7tco/reviews/ChdDSUhNMG9nS0VJQ0FnSUNPcVphaHhBRRAB", "text": {"text": "We camped with another couple at a nearby campground and came here our second day.\\n\\nPros:\\n-It was great to use a real bathroom.\\n-They also have showers in the locker rooms.\\n-Their mini store has odds and ends we wound up needing.\\n-Salted Caramel Ice Cream was delicious\\n-The main pool felt great.\\n-Did not smell sulfuric and water was super soft\\n-Free water was available in the store for swimmers.\\n-Perfect for the day after a hike to sooth muscles.\\n-Had no issues with staff. Other reviews mentioned bad attitudes and discrimination. We were a mixed group of races. The ladies were not overly nice but weren't rude either. They were very matter of fact but I tend to like that about people.\\n\\nOther Facts:\\n-We went on a hot day, bring sandals to wear up to the waters edge. We burned our feet.\\n-$20 per person to swim\\n-Hot Tub closer to the road seemed much hotter\\n-They do not allow dogs (even well behaved on a leash tied up).\\n\\nThis is a great stop, especially for anyone camping at one of the dry campgrounds like we did. It may not be the Hilton of hot springs for some, but for us, it was perfect! Thank you for a great time, we'll be back.", "languageCode": "en"}, "rating": 5, "publishTime": "2022-06-13T15:09:55.377259Z", "originalText": {"text": "We camped with another couple at a nearby campground and came here our second day.\\n\\nPros:\\n-It was great to use a real bathroom.\\n-They also have showers in the locker rooms.\\n-Their mini store has odds and ends we wound up needing.\\n-Salted Caramel Ice Cream was delicious\\n-The main pool felt great.\\n-Did not smell sulfuric and water was super soft\\n-Free water was available in the store for swimmers.\\n-Perfect for the day after a hike to sooth muscles.\\n-Had no issues with staff. Other reviews mentioned bad attitudes and discrimination. We were a mixed group of races. The ladies were not overly nice but weren't rude either. They were very matter of fact but I tend to like that about people.\\n\\nOther Facts:\\n-We went on a hot day, bring sandals to wear up to the waters edge. We burned our feet.\\n-$20 per person to swim\\n-Hot Tub closer to the road seemed much hotter\\n-They do not allow dogs (even well behaved on a leash tied up).\\n\\nThis is a great stop, especially for anyone camping at one of the dry campgrounds like we did. It may not be the Hilton of hot springs for some, but for us, it was perfect! Thank you for a great time, we'll be back.", "languageCode": "en"}, "googleMapsUri": "https://www.google.com/maps/reviews/data=!4m6!14m5!1m4!2m3!1sChdDSUhNMG9nS0VJQ0FnSUNPcVphaHhBRRAB!2m1!1s0x80ea9d15f68aba7f:0xcab57bc95ecb26ba", "flagContentUri": "https://www.google.com/local/content/rap/report?postId=ChdDSUhNMG9nS0VJQ0FnSUNPcVphaHhBRRAB&d=17924085&t=1", "authorAttribution": {"uri": "https://www.google.com/maps/contrib/117582847551511261043/reviews", "photoUri": "https://lh3.googleusercontent.com/a-/ALV-UjVMOKxoqCZ8JM8XIT-4AjSh5NmcX0zfRw870OL0FkfFDeCRVMpz5A=s128-c0x00000000-cc-rp-mo-ba4", "displayName": "Brooke Ward"}, "relativePublishTimeDescription": "3 years ago"}, {"name": "places/ChIJf7qK9hWd6oARuibLXsl7tco/reviews/ChdDSUhNMG9nS0VJQ0FnSUNONTVXTXRBRRAB", "text": {"text": "He was a little piece of history for you. I’ve loved looking at all these photos of California Hot Springs being complete. I lived at Laver market, which was the general store over by Pine Flats with my family. I was 12 years old now 62, and we used to have church meetings in the California Hot Springs when it was in complete and they started doing some renovations. Never thought they would finish that thing so it’s fun to look back and see the completed product. Fond memories.", "languageCode": "en"}, "rating": 5, "publishTime": "2024-01-18T16:57:13.951710Z", "originalText": {"text": "He was a little piece of history for you. I’ve loved looking at all these photos of California Hot Springs being complete. I lived at Laver market, which was the general store over by Pine Flats with my family. I was 12 years old now 62, and we used to have church meetings in the California Hot Springs when it was in complete and they started doing some renovations. Never thought they would finish that thing so it’s fun to look back and see the completed product. Fond memories.", "languageCode": "en"}, "googleMapsUri": "https://www.google.com/maps/reviews/data=!4m6!14m5!1m4!2m3!1sChdDSUhNMG9nS0VJQ0FnSUNONTVXTXRBRRAB!2m1!1s0x80ea9d15f68aba7f:0xcab57bc95ecb26ba", "flagContentUri": "https://www.google.com/local/content/rap/report?postId=ChdDSUhNMG9nS0VJQ0FnSUNONTVXTXRBRRAB&d=17924085&t=1", "authorAttribution": {"uri": "https://www.google.com/maps/contrib/111395346409230408355/reviews", "photoUri": "https://lh3.googleusercontent.com/a/ACg8ocLZp1gHHHubg_kpdSPRqrnjQdzfguMZnrePnFEDe0KjL6z09w=s128-c0x00000000-cc-rp-mo", "displayName": "bev dickson"}, "relativePublishTimeDescription": "2 years ago"}, {"name": "places/ChIJf7qK9hWd6oARuibLXsl7tco/reviews/ChZDSUhNMG9nS0VJQ0FnSUNnd0lid2VREAE", "text": {"text": "REVIEW UPDATED OCT 2019,\\n\\nFIRST VISIT MAY, 2018 = 4 STARS\\nThis is a humble, reasonably priced, fantastic gem tucked into the mountains.\\n\\nI arrived late so I only had an hour in the pools, but really enjoyed it.\\n\\nI camped there one night and loved it. It wasn't crowded. The bathrooms were old but clean, with hot water coming directly from the mineral springs.\\n\\nSeveral people in the reviews mentioned the staff was rude. I admit they sound a little grumpy, but I don't think they are. I think they're no-nonsense folks who were really helpful and friendly.\\n\\nI'd stay again in a heartbeat!\\n\\nSECOND ATTEMPTED VISIT SUMMER, 2019 = 1 STAR\\nwith a much lower score for a horrible experience with not telling customers they were closed.\\n\\nSummer 2019, I called and called the hot springs to confirm they were open. No one answered.  I checked their website, which had no mention of being closed permanently or short term.\\n\\nI assumed they were busy and drove 2 hours to the hot springs only to find they were closed -- for a planned power outage by the local electric company. There was a note taped on the door saying they were closed. The note did not even say when they would reopen.  Power trucks were everywhere in the area!  Clearly this was a planned outage, possibly lasting several days.\\n\\nI see no reason why the hot springs could not notify their customers they were closed.\\n1) get a digital voice mail and say you are closed!  Be sure to include how long you are going to be closed.\\n2) update your website!  Put a large pop up box saying your closed and for how many hours or days.\\n\\nPlus, they no longer allows tents at their camp area- only RVs.\\nI don't imagine I'll every go back here, which is a shame because I really enjoyed my first visit.", "languageCode": "en"}, "rating": 2, "publishTime": "2022-11-17T22:28:28.479778Z", "originalText": {"text": "REVIEW UPDATED OCT 2019,\\n\\nFIRST VISIT MAY, 2018 = 4 STARS\\nThis is a humble, reasonably priced, fantastic gem tucked into the mountains.\\n\\nI arrived late so I only had an hour in the pools, but really enjoyed it.\\n\\nI camped there one night and loved it. It wasn't crowded. The bathrooms were old but clean, with hot water coming directly from the mineral springs.\\n\\nSeveral people in the reviews mentioned the staff was rude. I admit they sound a little grumpy, but I don't think they are. I think they're no-nonsense folks who were really helpful and friendly.\\n\\nI'd stay again in a heartbeat!\\n\\nSECOND ATTEMPTED VISIT SUMMER, 2019 = 1 STAR\\nwith a much lower score for a horrible experience with not telling customers they were closed.\\n\\nSummer 2019, I called and called the hot springs to confirm they were open. No one answered.  I checked their website, which had no mention of being closed permanently or short term.\\n\\nI assumed they were busy and drove 2 hours to the hot springs only to find they were closed -- for a planned power outage by the local electric company. There was a note taped on the door saying they were closed. The note did not even say when they would reopen.  Power trucks were everywhere in the area!  Clearly this was a planned outage, possibly lasting several days.\\n\\nI see no reason why the hot springs could not notify their customers they were closed.\\n1) get a digital voice mail and say you are closed!  Be sure to include how long you are going to be closed.\\n2) update your website!  Put a large pop up box saying your closed and for how many hours or days.\\n\\nPlus, they no longer allows tents at their camp area- only RVs.\\nI don't imagine I'll every go back here, which is a shame because I really enjoyed my first visit.", "languageCode": "en"}, "googleMapsUri": "https://www.google.com/maps/reviews/data=!4m6!14m5!1m4!2m3!1sChZDSUhNMG9nS0VJQ0FnSUNnd0lid2VREAE!2m1!1s0x80ea9d15f68aba7f:0xcab57bc95ecb26ba", "flagContentUri": "https://www.google.com/local/content/rap/report?postId=ChZDSUhNMG9nS0VJQ0FnSUNnd0lid2VREAE&d=17924085&t=1", "authorAttribution": {"uri": "https://www.google.com/maps/contrib/100458706506108561610/reviews", "photoUri": "https://lh3.googleusercontent.com/a-/ALV-UjWsn8V2kBmHhJy07l5jwj-RTs5VehMpzwGungYVYpwAkBIUw2pT=s128-c0x00000000-cc-rp-mo-ba3", "displayName": "Teresa Sigmon"}, "relativePublishTimeDescription": "3 years ago"}, {"name": "places/ChIJf7qK9hWd6oARuibLXsl7tco/reviews/ChdDSUhNMG9nS0VJQ0FnSUNXb3V6b2xnRRAB", "text": {"text": "Nice place to chill. The big pool is heated to a temp close to the Caribbean sea in the dead of summer. One if the two hot tubs is about 10 degrees hotter than the other. The place serves a basic menu and alcoholic drinks and has a cute gift shop. Very laid back atmosphere to hang out for the day with friends or family.", "languageCode": "en"}, "rating": 5, "publishTime": "2022-02-21T20:59:37.785238Z", "originalText": {"text": "Nice place to chill. The big pool is heated to a temp close to the Caribbean sea in the dead of summer. One if the two hot tubs is about 10 degrees hotter than the other. The place serves a basic menu and alcoholic drinks and has a cute gift shop. Very laid back atmosphere to hang out for the day with friends or family.", "languageCode": "en"}, "googleMapsUri": "https://www.google.com/maps/reviews/data=!4m6!14m5!1m4!2m3!1sChdDSUhNMG9nS0VJQ0FnSUNXb3V6b2xnRRAB!2m1!1s0x80ea9d15f68aba7f:0xcab57bc95ecb26ba", "flagContentUri": "https://www.google.com/local/content/rap/report?postId=ChdDSUhNMG9nS0VJQ0FnSUNXb3V6b2xnRRAB&d=17924085&t=1", "authorAttribution": {"uri": "https://www.google.com/maps/contrib/117543471951091830084/reviews", "photoUri": "https://lh3.googleusercontent.com/a/ACg8ocKRUlHrfYn-U3PmG00_oIGvs0qcEtOTiRw4OKmkkAD4Uj-OxQ=s128-c0x00000000-cc-rp-mo-ba4", "displayName": "Sylvia Maniscalco"}, "relativePublishTimeDescription": "3 years ago"}]	California Hot Springs Resort is described as a 'magical gem' that offers a relaxing, family-friendly experience with naturally heated pools and hot tubs of varying temperatures. Visitors consistently praise the laid-back atmosphere, clean facilities, and therapeutic waters that are perfect for unwinding after outdoor activities. While the staff is described as no-nonsense rather than overly friendly, most guests find the experience memorable and worth returning to.	{"summary": "California Hot Springs Resort is described as a 'magical gem' that offers a relaxing, family-friendly experience with naturally heated pools and hot tubs of varying temperatures. Visitors consistently praise the laid-back atmosphere, clean facilities, and therapeutic waters that are perfect for unwinding after outdoor activities. While the staff is described as no-nonsense rather than overly friendly, most guests find the experience memorable and worth returning to.", "negative": [{"text": "We went on a hot day, bring sandals to wear up to the waters edge. We burned our feet.", "author": "Brooke Ward", "rating": 5}, {"text": "They do not allow dogs (even well behaved on a leash tied up).", "author": "Brooke Ward", "rating": 5}], "positive": [{"text": "This place was such a magical gem during my cross country trip with 2 small kids in tow.", "author": "E Hi-Chang", "rating": 5}, {"text": "The pool and hot tubs were just heaven. The main pool was like bathwater while the other tubs had varying degrees of hot.", "author": "E Hi-Chang", "rating": 5}, {"text": "The big pool is heated to a temp close to the Caribbean sea in the dead of summer. Very laid back atmosphere to hang out for the day with friends or family.", "author": "Sylvia Maniscalco", "rating": 5}], "last_updated": "2026-02-02T18:55:11.943Z"}	2026-02-02 18:55:05.593+00	\N	\N	\N
c60ad079-62ef-4b90-88c4-9c1997f4a049	b201a860-05a3-4ddc-bb89-4c4271177271	Catalina Spa RV Resort (Desert Hot Springs)	Joshua Tree 45 minutes away, Palm Springs dining 20 minutes. Five odorless natural mineral hot spring pools provide year-round soaking with exceptional stargazing.	Five odorless natural mineral hot spring pools open late for midnight soaking under stars. Free electricity and water.	couples_getaway	\N	18800 Corkill Rd, Desert Hot Springs, CA 92241, USA	Desert Hot Springs	CA	33.9120500	-116.4372550	ChIJb1Fr9Dke24ARfQ1r4uJw9sA	4.3	623	\N	{"hookups": "full"}	f	\N	\N	60.00	USD	$60-80/night	{"best": ["october", "november", "december", "january", "february", "march", "april"], "notes": "October-April for hot springs enjoyment"}	2 hours	\N	{"scenic_beauty": 4, "solitude_level": 3, "adventure_level": 2, "family_friendly": 3, "relaxation_factor": 5}	\N	\N	http://www.catalinasparvresort.com/	(760) 329-4431	\N	researching	0	{couples,hot-springs,stargazing}	{}	{}	\N	\N	2026-02-02 15:20:43.452+00	2026-02-06 03:26:37.500531+00	[{"name": "places/ChIJb1Fr9Dke24ARfQ1r4uJw9sA/reviews/Ci9DQUlRQUNvZENodHljRjlvT21KbGNtVjFhVTVmYURsemExZFllbDh3ZG1aVVMyYxAB", "text": {"text": "We stayed here for three weeks in November 2025. This is one of my favorite RV parks I’ve ever stayed at! It is so clean and quiet. Very low key. The pools (there are two!) and hot tubs were great. Dog park was a good size compared to a lot of others I’ve seen in RV parks. Staff was nice and friendly. Sites are big and spread out. We would have stayed longer but the monthly rate is a little high for us (though electricity is included in the rate so that helps).\\nI didn’t want to leave!", "languageCode": "en"}, "rating": 5, "publishTime": "2026-01-05T03:02:30.423214793Z", "originalText": {"text": "We stayed here for three weeks in November 2025. This is one of my favorite RV parks I’ve ever stayed at! It is so clean and quiet. Very low key. The pools (there are two!) and hot tubs were great. Dog park was a good size compared to a lot of others I’ve seen in RV parks. Staff was nice and friendly. Sites are big and spread out. We would have stayed longer but the monthly rate is a little high for us (though electricity is included in the rate so that helps).\\nI didn’t want to leave!", "languageCode": "en"}, "googleMapsUri": "https://www.google.com/maps/reviews/data=!4m6!14m5!1m4!2m3!1sCi9DQUlRQUNvZENodHljRjlvT21KbGNtVjFhVTVmYURsemExZFllbDh3ZG1aVVMyYxAB!2m1!1s0x80db1e39f46b516f:0xc0f670e2e26b0d7d", "flagContentUri": "https://www.google.com/local/content/rap/report?postId=Ci9DQUlRQUNvZENodHljRjlvT21KbGNtVjFhVTVmYURsemExZFllbDh3ZG1aVVMyYxAB&d=17924085&t=1", "authorAttribution": {"uri": "https://www.google.com/maps/contrib/108418883078796792975/reviews", "photoUri": "https://lh3.googleusercontent.com/a-/ALV-UjVPzK2uSA3Es-TcGUX47Qx3q3ab6BGVNPaqV0nY5amdwhzPh9a8=s128-c0x00000000-cc-rp-mo", "displayName": "amanda williams"}, "relativePublishTimeDescription": "a month ago"}, {"name": "places/ChIJb1Fr9Dke24ARfQ1r4uJw9sA/reviews/Ci9DQUlRQUNvZENodHljRjlvT25STWNXUlZPVVJ2WHpsYVkzaFhXSEozVVhOQk0zYxAB", "text": {"text": "We stayed here over New Year’s Eve and had a blast at their community party.  They had a DJ, dancing, food. The place was decorated so lovely. They did all this and didn’t charge extra as so many parks I’ve stayed at try to gouge you for every extra penny. The park is clean. The staff is helpful and friendly. Would recommend and will be back.", "languageCode": "en"}, "rating": 5, "publishTime": "2026-01-01T05:28:22.586774605Z", "originalText": {"text": "We stayed here over New Year’s Eve and had a blast at their community party.  They had a DJ, dancing, food. The place was decorated so lovely. They did all this and didn’t charge extra as so many parks I’ve stayed at try to gouge you for every extra penny. The park is clean. The staff is helpful and friendly. Would recommend and will be back.", "languageCode": "en"}, "googleMapsUri": "https://www.google.com/maps/reviews/data=!4m6!14m5!1m4!2m3!1sCi9DQUlRQUNvZENodHljRjlvT25STWNXUlZPVVJ2WHpsYVkzaFhXSEozVVhOQk0zYxAB!2m1!1s0x80db1e39f46b516f:0xc0f670e2e26b0d7d", "flagContentUri": "https://www.google.com/local/content/rap/report?postId=Ci9DQUlRQUNvZENodHljRjlvT25STWNXUlZPVVJ2WHpsYVkzaFhXSEozVVhOQk0zYxAB&d=17924085&t=1", "authorAttribution": {"uri": "https://www.google.com/maps/contrib/108503129960007865393/reviews", "photoUri": "https://lh3.googleusercontent.com/a-/ALV-UjVovQSeKqx-Ju-zNMs9PIT-DrgtTuLmGNste2ImKLNC0Gszo1Pz1g=s128-c0x00000000-cc-rp-mo-ba3", "displayName": "Sophia Langan"}, "relativePublishTimeDescription": "a month ago"}, {"name": "places/ChIJb1Fr9Dke24ARfQ1r4uJw9sA/reviews/Ci9DQUlRQUNvZENodHljRjlvT2tsa2FHaFliM28wVWtkNVJXRktiSEF4UjFFMlRuYxAB", "text": {"text": "This is an easy to navigate campground built for big rigs. Nice level spots that are relatively big with privacy bushes. The pool area is nice and large with a very big hot tub but it could have been hotter.", "languageCode": "en"}, "rating": 5, "publishTime": "2025-12-01T17:06:01.067542303Z", "originalText": {"text": "This is an easy to navigate campground built for big rigs. Nice level spots that are relatively big with privacy bushes. The pool area is nice and large with a very big hot tub but it could have been hotter.", "languageCode": "en"}, "googleMapsUri": "https://www.google.com/maps/reviews/data=!4m6!14m5!1m4!2m3!1sCi9DQUlRQUNvZENodHljRjlvT2tsa2FHaFliM28wVWtkNVJXRktiSEF4UjFFMlRuYxAB!2m1!1s0x80db1e39f46b516f:0xc0f670e2e26b0d7d", "flagContentUri": "https://www.google.com/local/content/rap/report?postId=Ci9DQUlRQUNvZENodHljRjlvT2tsa2FHaFliM28wVWtkNVJXRktiSEF4UjFFMlRuYxAB&d=17924085&t=1", "authorAttribution": {"uri": "https://www.google.com/maps/contrib/104135444086290392610/reviews", "photoUri": "https://lh3.googleusercontent.com/a/ACg8ocKqNsTpK6OM_MPgPUjr0kKzSey7qu_R2tckIdjJ-4uCytte9Q=s128-c0x00000000-cc-rp-mo-ba6", "displayName": "Marie Taylor"}, "relativePublishTimeDescription": "2 months ago"}, {"name": "places/ChIJb1Fr9Dke24ARfQ1r4uJw9sA/reviews/Ci9DQUlRQUNvZENodHljRjlvT2tkRlFVeEVUazV3Y0ZWcFNGcG1iMHByY1hsYVZFRRAB", "text": {"text": "The pools & meeting areas are gorgeous, clean, & close.\\nStaff is constantly looking to make your stay pleasurable.\\nThe am trash pick up is fun.", "languageCode": "en"}, "rating": 5, "publishTime": "2026-01-19T17:02:56.504368621Z", "originalText": {"text": "The pools & meeting areas are gorgeous, clean, & close.\\nStaff is constantly looking to make your stay pleasurable.\\nThe am trash pick up is fun.", "languageCode": "en"}, "googleMapsUri": "https://www.google.com/maps/reviews/data=!4m6!14m5!1m4!2m3!1sCi9DQUlRQUNvZENodHljRjlvT2tkRlFVeEVUazV3Y0ZWcFNGcG1iMHByY1hsYVZFRRAB!2m1!1s0x80db1e39f46b516f:0xc0f670e2e26b0d7d", "flagContentUri": "https://www.google.com/local/content/rap/report?postId=Ci9DQUlRQUNvZENodHljRjlvT2tkRlFVeEVUazV3Y0ZWcFNGcG1iMHByY1hsYVZFRRAB&d=17924085&t=1", "authorAttribution": {"uri": "https://www.google.com/maps/contrib/111755046977786196872/reviews", "photoUri": "https://lh3.googleusercontent.com/a-/ALV-UjWDBsycXvy5VjHh0rKHbKFKEzJHjA8wILX3ll1D5uZtA1lC_cbo=s128-c0x00000000-cc-rp-mo-ba4", "displayName": "Lily Wakeman"}, "relativePublishTimeDescription": "2 weeks ago"}, {"name": "places/ChIJb1Fr9Dke24ARfQ1r4uJw9sA/reviews/ChZDSUhNMG9nS0VJQ0FnTUNJOWRyUVlBEAE", "text": {"text": "Great Experience with a Few Suggestions\\n\\nWe had a really great stay at Catalina Spa RV Resort! The place was super clean, the amenities were well-kept, and the staff and most of the guests were genuinely friendly and welcoming. It’s one of those spots where you can really relax and enjoy the vibe.\\n\\nThere was a recurring concern from other guests about things getting stolen, but we personally never had any issues. That said, having some light security at night—maybe someone doing rounds in a golf cart—could really help ease that worry and make the place feel even more secure.\\n\\nOne thing worth mentioning is the dynamic with some of the long-term residents. While many of them were incredibly kind and made the place feel like a little community, a few seemed to have an “ownership” vibe when it came to common areas like the pools. It wasn’t a huge deal, but it did feel a little off-putting at times.\\n\\nOverall, though, we loved our time here and would definitely come back. Catalina Spa has a lot going for it—beautiful setting, clean facilities, and a chill atmosphere.", "languageCode": "en"}, "rating": 5, "publishTime": "2025-04-03T19:34:27.129554Z", "originalText": {"text": "Great Experience with a Few Suggestions\\n\\nWe had a really great stay at Catalina Spa RV Resort! The place was super clean, the amenities were well-kept, and the staff and most of the guests were genuinely friendly and welcoming. It’s one of those spots where you can really relax and enjoy the vibe.\\n\\nThere was a recurring concern from other guests about things getting stolen, but we personally never had any issues. That said, having some light security at night—maybe someone doing rounds in a golf cart—could really help ease that worry and make the place feel even more secure.\\n\\nOne thing worth mentioning is the dynamic with some of the long-term residents. While many of them were incredibly kind and made the place feel like a little community, a few seemed to have an “ownership” vibe when it came to common areas like the pools. It wasn’t a huge deal, but it did feel a little off-putting at times.\\n\\nOverall, though, we loved our time here and would definitely come back. Catalina Spa has a lot going for it—beautiful setting, clean facilities, and a chill atmosphere.", "languageCode": "en"}, "googleMapsUri": "https://www.google.com/maps/reviews/data=!4m6!14m5!1m4!2m3!1sChZDSUhNMG9nS0VJQ0FnTUNJOWRyUVlBEAE!2m1!1s0x80db1e39f46b516f:0xc0f670e2e26b0d7d", "flagContentUri": "https://www.google.com/local/content/rap/report?postId=ChZDSUhNMG9nS0VJQ0FnTUNJOWRyUVlBEAE&d=17924085&t=1", "authorAttribution": {"uri": "https://www.google.com/maps/contrib/106427154592685822026/reviews", "photoUri": "https://lh3.googleusercontent.com/a-/ALV-UjU1INwYCNnih8cK2o06vwmEzQ2vlpij3MwLKyOLNehz84KdzQ9X=s128-c0x00000000-cc-rp-mo-ba3", "displayName": "Zane Buxton"}, "relativePublishTimeDescription": "10 months ago"}]	Catalina Spa RV Resort is consistently praised as an exceptionally clean, quiet, and well-maintained resort with friendly staff, spacious sites, great pools and hot tubs, and a welcoming community atmosphere. Guests particularly love the peaceful environment, excellent amenities including two pools and a good-sized dog park, and thoughtful touches like complimentary community events. The main concerns center around higher monthly rates and occasional issues with theft reported by some guests.	{"summary": "Catalina Spa RV Resort is consistently praised as an exceptionally clean, quiet, and well-maintained resort with friendly staff, spacious sites, great pools and hot tubs, and a welcoming community atmosphere. Guests particularly love the peaceful environment, excellent amenities including two pools and a good-sized dog park, and thoughtful touches like complimentary community events. The main concerns center around higher monthly rates and occasional issues with theft reported by some guests.", "negative": [{"text": "There was a recurring concern from other guests about things getting stolen, but we personally never had any issues.", "author": "Zane Buxton", "rating": 5}, {"text": "The monthly rate is a little high for us (though electricity is included in the rate so that helps).", "author": "amanda williams", "rating": 5}], "positive": [{"text": "It is so clean and quiet. Very low key.", "author": "amanda williams", "rating": 5}, {"text": "They had a DJ, dancing, food... They did all this and didn't charge extra as so many parks I've stayed at try to gouge you for every extra penny.", "author": "Sophia Langan", "rating": 5}, {"text": "Nice level spots that are relatively big with privacy bushes. The pool area is nice and large with a very big hot tub.", "author": "Marie Taylor", "rating": 5}], "last_updated": "2026-02-06T03:26:37.434Z"}	2026-02-06 03:26:31.511+00	private_rv_park	\N	\N
b7010166-1b37-4216-8716-d11293a6dfce	b201a860-05a3-4ddc-bb89-4c4271177271	Prairie Creek Redwoods via Elk Country RV Resort	State park campgrounds max at 24 feet for trailers. Base at Elk Country RV Resort (Trinidad, 35 miles south) or Village Camper Inn (Crescent City, 25 miles north) with full hookups and day-trip into the park. Fern Canyon permits required May-September (reserve 30 days ahead through Redwood Parks Conservancy).	Fern Canyon—a prehistoric gorge with 50-80-foot walls draped entirely in ferns—was featured in Jurassic Park: The Lost World. Plus Roosevelt elk herds graze openly in meadows, often dozens at a time.	state_parks	\N	127011 Newton B. Drury Scenic Pkwy, Orick, CA 95555, USA	Orick	CA	41.4015995	-124.0416249	ChIJD1FhIXUB0VQR2nkbAWI5Mbc	4.9	1244	\N	{"hookups": "full", "cell_coverage": "none", "road_accessibility": "State park max 24ft—base at Elk Country RV Resort (Trinidad) or Village Camper Inn (Crescent City)", "max_trailer_length_ft": 24}	t	\N	\N	\N	USD	\N	{"best": ["june", "july", "august"], "notes": "Summer offers best weather (40-75°F), Junior Ranger programs, and seasonal footbridges"}	9-10 hours	\N	{"scenic_beauty": 5, "solitude_level": 4, "adventure_level": 5, "family_friendly": 5, "relaxation_factor": 4}	\N	{"parker": {"suitable": true, "activities": ["Making the Jurassic Park connection", "Expedition leader through Fern Canyon"], "engagement_level": 5}, "xander": {"suitable": true, "activities": ["Watching wild elk from safe distance", "Playing in Fern Canyon streams (summer)", "Living canyon walls sensory experience"], "engagement_level": 5}, "charlotte": {"suitable": true, "activities": ["Touching 50-foot fern walls", "Splashing through shallow streams"], "engagement_level": 5}}	http://www.parks.ca.gov/?page_id=415	(707) 465-7354	\N	researching	0	{jurassic-park,fern-canyon,redwoods,elk}	{"Jurassic Park filming location","Roosevelt elk sightings","Magical Fern Canyon"}	{"9-10 hour drive (combine with multi-week trip)","Park max 24ft","No cell service"}	\N	\N	2026-02-02 15:20:42.24+00	2026-02-06 03:28:19.061893+00	[{"name": "places/ChIJD1FhIXUB0VQR2nkbAWI5Mbc/reviews/Ci9DQUlRQUNvZENodHljRjlvT2taUVNtRXRZV1ZxU0U1M2NrY3hRVkpDWDJ0U1JtYxAB", "text": {"text": "Gorgeous. Went today. Big Tree trail was fabulous, following the creek, falling leaves everywhere, ferns everywhere, so much moss and greenery. Thick forest that provided shelter from the rain. The air was damp and cool and smelled lovely. Exactly as I imagined the redwoods would be. Saw Bear scat but no bears.", "languageCode": "en"}, "rating": 5, "publishTime": "2025-10-25T01:04:39.972084985Z", "originalText": {"text": "Gorgeous. Went today. Big Tree trail was fabulous, following the creek, falling leaves everywhere, ferns everywhere, so much moss and greenery. Thick forest that provided shelter from the rain. The air was damp and cool and smelled lovely. Exactly as I imagined the redwoods would be. Saw Bear scat but no bears.", "languageCode": "en"}, "googleMapsUri": "https://www.google.com/maps/reviews/data=!4m6!14m5!1m4!2m3!1sCi9DQUlRQUNvZENodHljRjlvT2taUVNtRXRZV1ZxU0U1M2NrY3hRVkpDWDJ0U1JtYxAB!2m1!1s0x54d101752161510f:0xb7313962011b79da", "flagContentUri": "https://www.google.com/local/content/rap/report?postId=Ci9DQUlRQUNvZENodHljRjlvT2taUVNtRXRZV1ZxU0U1M2NrY3hRVkpDWDJ0U1JtYxAB&d=17924085&t=1", "authorAttribution": {"uri": "https://www.google.com/maps/contrib/117512019868097993502/reviews", "photoUri": "https://lh3.googleusercontent.com/a-/ALV-UjUGwdhrWwDHQQLGI_THzuUx78rcMUQuKnhqzAb1Z8Fhf9_FBIFY2g=s128-c0x00000000-cc-rp-mo-ba3", "displayName": "Melissa"}, "relativePublishTimeDescription": "3 months ago"}, {"name": "places/ChIJD1FhIXUB0VQR2nkbAWI5Mbc/reviews/Ci9DQUlRQUNvZENodHljRjlvT25ZdFMwbFpWbkV0V0ZCR1gxRk1RMXBhUzFoblVWRRAB", "text": {"text": "Great park! The information center when you first arrive is extremely helpful. Parking can be tight at some of the trails but parking along the main road has plenty of space. Big Tree wayside was my favorite. There's a good number of people at the beginning of the trail but once you start walking more than 10 minutes you're by yourself. Its absolutely gorgeous.", "languageCode": "en"}, "rating": 5, "publishTime": "2025-09-06T19:00:45.790495889Z", "originalText": {"text": "Great park! The information center when you first arrive is extremely helpful. Parking can be tight at some of the trails but parking along the main road has plenty of space. Big Tree wayside was my favorite. There's a good number of people at the beginning of the trail but once you start walking more than 10 minutes you're by yourself. Its absolutely gorgeous.", "languageCode": "en"}, "googleMapsUri": "https://www.google.com/maps/reviews/data=!4m6!14m5!1m4!2m3!1sCi9DQUlRQUNvZENodHljRjlvT25ZdFMwbFpWbkV0V0ZCR1gxRk1RMXBhUzFoblVWRRAB!2m1!1s0x54d101752161510f:0xb7313962011b79da", "flagContentUri": "https://www.google.com/local/content/rap/report?postId=Ci9DQUlRQUNvZENodHljRjlvT25ZdFMwbFpWbkV0V0ZCR1gxRk1RMXBhUzFoblVWRRAB&d=17924085&t=1", "authorAttribution": {"uri": "https://www.google.com/maps/contrib/110425235827991309702/reviews", "photoUri": "https://lh3.googleusercontent.com/a-/ALV-UjWgLGWwJ83W6428rdxKYk4-_Fe4n9mmkzh32D5JJc51Xbac_enkYg=s128-c0x00000000-cc-rp-mo-ba4", "displayName": "Austin"}, "relativePublishTimeDescription": "5 months ago"}, {"name": "places/ChIJD1FhIXUB0VQR2nkbAWI5Mbc/reviews/Ci9DQUlRQUNvZENodHljRjlvT25JM2NHaExNRWxyUTBWM2FHbHZZWEU0TVVWclptYxAB", "text": {"text": "This park has so much to offer. From camping to hiking to wildlife viewing it's all right here.\\nI've been visiting here for over 40 years.\\n\\nThe staff at the information center can help you find the best activity to match your interests. But I'd recommend Trillium Falls or a hike along the trails adjacent to the Drury Parkway to get a taste. If you want more, and have the time, hike or drive to Fern Canyon. Personally, I like to hike the James Irvine Trail to get there. The trail will take you through some majestic and ancient groves of redwoods.\\n\\nThe Elk Prairie campground is a good place to camp. Some of the facilities are a bit old. But the location is hard to beat.\\n\\nYou'll likely see Roosevelt Elk in the prairie meadow. Give them plenty of space. Particularly during calving season (May-June) they can be aggressive.", "languageCode": "en"}, "rating": 4, "publishTime": "2025-08-23T05:27:45.174238960Z", "originalText": {"text": "This park has so much to offer. From camping to hiking to wildlife viewing it's all right here.\\nI've been visiting here for over 40 years.\\n\\nThe staff at the information center can help you find the best activity to match your interests. But I'd recommend Trillium Falls or a hike along the trails adjacent to the Drury Parkway to get a taste. If you want more, and have the time, hike or drive to Fern Canyon. Personally, I like to hike the James Irvine Trail to get there. The trail will take you through some majestic and ancient groves of redwoods.\\n\\nThe Elk Prairie campground is a good place to camp. Some of the facilities are a bit old. But the location is hard to beat.\\n\\nYou'll likely see Roosevelt Elk in the prairie meadow. Give them plenty of space. Particularly during calving season (May-June) they can be aggressive.", "languageCode": "en"}, "googleMapsUri": "https://www.google.com/maps/reviews/data=!4m6!14m5!1m4!2m3!1sCi9DQUlRQUNvZENodHljRjlvT25JM2NHaExNRWxyUTBWM2FHbHZZWEU0TVVWclptYxAB!2m1!1s0x54d101752161510f:0xb7313962011b79da", "flagContentUri": "https://www.google.com/local/content/rap/report?postId=Ci9DQUlRQUNvZENodHljRjlvT25JM2NHaExNRWxyUTBWM2FHbHZZWEU0TVVWclptYxAB&d=17924085&t=1", "authorAttribution": {"uri": "https://www.google.com/maps/contrib/116052163994442728657/reviews", "photoUri": "https://lh3.googleusercontent.com/a-/ALV-UjUYWSqbFibjR8SgFBMqdEMfczHcDNhwDJNcXGO6T4i_buL3e0gU=s128-c0x00000000-cc-rp-mo-ba5", "displayName": "Tino Plank"}, "relativePublishTimeDescription": "5 months ago"}, {"name": "places/ChIJD1FhIXUB0VQR2nkbAWI5Mbc/reviews/Ci9DQUlRQUNvZENodHljRjlvT2tkdWN5MVBhSGxyUjFwV1VHZ3diVzE1VTNoVGFtYxAB", "text": {"text": "It really ranks as one of the best state parks you will ever visit.  Where else can you possibly see giant elk on the beach next to ocean waves.  Fern canyon is a once in a lifetime experience. Plus, giant redwoods on a scenic drive. It has a wonderful combination of views, drives, trails, and wildlife.   Overall, the best stops in the greater Redwood park system.", "languageCode": "en"}, "rating": 5, "publishTime": "2025-07-24T02:44:48.866794839Z", "originalText": {"text": "It really ranks as one of the best state parks you will ever visit.  Where else can you possibly see giant elk on the beach next to ocean waves.  Fern canyon is a once in a lifetime experience. Plus, giant redwoods on a scenic drive. It has a wonderful combination of views, drives, trails, and wildlife.   Overall, the best stops in the greater Redwood park system.", "languageCode": "en"}, "googleMapsUri": "https://www.google.com/maps/reviews/data=!4m6!14m5!1m4!2m3!1sCi9DQUlRQUNvZENodHljRjlvT2tkdWN5MVBhSGxyUjFwV1VHZ3diVzE1VTNoVGFtYxAB!2m1!1s0x54d101752161510f:0xb7313962011b79da", "flagContentUri": "https://www.google.com/local/content/rap/report?postId=Ci9DQUlRQUNvZENodHljRjlvT2tkdWN5MVBhSGxyUjFwV1VHZ3diVzE1VTNoVGFtYxAB&d=17924085&t=1", "authorAttribution": {"uri": "https://www.google.com/maps/contrib/106332438377360754249/reviews", "photoUri": "https://lh3.googleusercontent.com/a-/ALV-UjU1iU4ukW3wTBQ-OESOq37qFPqRNrN75Q6FXF07nQRVOebye1ri=s128-c0x00000000-cc-rp-mo-ba8", "displayName": "Wyatt W. Penke"}, "relativePublishTimeDescription": "6 months ago"}, {"name": "places/ChIJD1FhIXUB0VQR2nkbAWI5Mbc/reviews/Ci9DQUlRQUNvZENodHljRjlvT2t4UlVqRldSV3hKVld0M1dGOXFVbm93ZHpkbmVtYxAB", "text": {"text": "Beautiful area up north with plenty of campgrounds and things to do. The air is so clean you can taste it. Everyone is so friendly and the campground was fantastic! Its a long drive but on US 101 it was a beautiful drive with VERY LITTLE TRAFFIC. I have made this an annual trip.", "languageCode": "en"}, "rating": 5, "publishTime": "2025-07-03T03:02:03.702858127Z", "originalText": {"text": "Beautiful area up north with plenty of campgrounds and things to do. The air is so clean you can taste it. Everyone is so friendly and the campground was fantastic! Its a long drive but on US 101 it was a beautiful drive with VERY LITTLE TRAFFIC. I have made this an annual trip.", "languageCode": "en"}, "googleMapsUri": "https://www.google.com/maps/reviews/data=!4m6!14m5!1m4!2m3!1sCi9DQUlRQUNvZENodHljRjlvT2t4UlVqRldSV3hKVld0M1dGOXFVbm93ZHpkbmVtYxAB!2m1!1s0x54d101752161510f:0xb7313962011b79da", "flagContentUri": "https://www.google.com/local/content/rap/report?postId=Ci9DQUlRQUNvZENodHljRjlvT2t4UlVqRldSV3hKVld0M1dGOXFVbm93ZHpkbmVtYxAB&d=17924085&t=1", "authorAttribution": {"uri": "https://www.google.com/maps/contrib/110031387966993099334/reviews", "photoUri": "https://lh3.googleusercontent.com/a/ACg8ocKcWM2ztI8RLgXLzExWvzBB6Ub3qsGgEfoLmIdiHifzxdH9dw=s128-c0x00000000-cc-rp-mo-ba4", "displayName": "Ben A. Williams"}, "relativePublishTimeDescription": "7 months ago"}]	Prairie Creek Redwoods via Elk Country RV Resort is consistently praised as one of the best state parks to visit, offering a magical combination of ancient redwood groves, unique wildlife viewing (including Roosevelt Elk), and diverse activities from easy trails to the famous Fern Canyon. Visitors are enchanted by the pristine natural beauty, clean air, and the variety of experiences available, from scenic drives to hiking trails that quickly become peaceful and secluded.	{"summary": "Prairie Creek Redwoods via Elk Country RV Resort is consistently praised as one of the best state parks to visit, offering a magical combination of ancient redwood groves, unique wildlife viewing (including Roosevelt Elk), and diverse activities from easy trails to the famous Fern Canyon. Visitors are enchanted by the pristine natural beauty, clean air, and the variety of experiences available, from scenic drives to hiking trails that quickly become peaceful and secluded.", "negative": [{"text": "Some of the facilities are a bit old.", "author": "Tino Plank", "rating": 4}, {"text": "Parking can be tight at some of the trails", "author": "Austin", "rating": 5}], "positive": [{"text": "Where else can you possibly see giant elk on the beach next to ocean waves. It has a wonderful combination of views, drives, trails, and wildlife.", "author": "Wyatt W. Penke", "rating": 5}, {"text": "There's a good number of people at the beginning of the trail but once you start walking more than 10 minutes you're by yourself.", "author": "Austin", "rating": 5}, {"text": "The air is so clean you can taste it. Everyone is so friendly and the campground was fantastic!", "author": "Ben A. Williams", "rating": 5}], "last_updated": "2026-02-06T03:28:18.961Z"}	2026-02-06 03:28:12.736+00	private_rv_park	\N	\N
9c0322cf-7c2e-48bc-82a8-e1f36a46d89e	b201a860-05a3-4ddc-bb89-4c4271177271	Tecopa Hot Springs	Tecopa Palms Resort offers crystal-clear mineral pools, gender-separated private soaking rooms, and genuine hospitality. Ray's biscuits and gravy have earned legendary status among winter RVers. Your 5th wheel gets concrete-slab full hookups with 50-amp service—one of only two Tecopa parks offering this. Death Valley sits one hour north, making this an ideal base camp.	Natural geothermal water emerging at 128°F from 180 miles underground, classified as one of the best therapeutic hot springs in North America—and the owners serve free freshly cooked breakfast every morning.	hot_springs	\N	Tecopa Hot Springs, Tecopa, CA 92389, USA	Tecopa	CA	35.8739184	-116.2314259	ChIJGahDK4hlxoARN_r6BmdwKBU	\N	\N	\N	{"hookups": "full", "cell_coverage": "good"}	t	\N	\N	75.00	USD	$75-85/night for 2 people (includes pool, WiFi, breakfast)	{"best": ["october", "november", "december", "january", "february", "march", "april"], "avoid": ["june", "july", "august"], "notes": "Summer too hot for hot springs enjoyment"}	3.5-4 hours	\N	{"scenic_beauty": 4, "solitude_level": 4, "adventure_level": 3, "family_friendly": 4, "relaxation_factor": 5}	\N	{"parker": {"suitable": true, "activities": ["Death Valley geology exploration", "Rock hunting"], "engagement_level": 4}, "xander": {"suitable": true, "activities": ["Warm mineral water sensory experience"], "engagement_level": 4}, "charlotte": {"suitable": true, "activities": ["Pool splashing", "China Ranch Date Farm visit"], "engagement_level": 4}}	\N	\N	\N	researching	0	{hot-springs,death-valley-staging,free-breakfast}	{}	{}	\N	\N	2026-02-02 15:20:32.039+00	2026-02-06 04:08:08.14976+00	\N	\N	\N	2026-02-06 04:08:08.08+00	blm	\N	\N
81b7610b-5f8d-4cb7-88dd-2bd3becca8b9	b201a860-05a3-4ddc-bb89-4c4271177271	Temecula Wine Country via Native Falls Campground	Native Falls offers the water experience Lake Cachuma can't (Cachuma prohibits all body contact with water). The private setting means controlled environment for Xander, while proximity to 40+ Temecula tasting rooms gives adults evening options. Modern amenities include pickleball, pool table, and fire pits.	A private lake with waterfall, sandy beach, and catch-and-release fishing—plus kayaks, paddle boards, and pedal boats for rent—all 90 minutes from LA.	lake_river	\N	38120 E Benton Rd, Temecula, CA 92592, USA	Temecula	CA	33.5777870	-116.9965530	ChIJM-SjofB524AR9gq-KsBR2aI	4.5	366	\N	\N	t	\N	\N	\N	USD	Day use $25-35/vehicle; camping rates vary	\N	1.5 hours	\N	{"scenic_beauty": 4, "solitude_level": 3, "adventure_level": 3, "family_friendly": 5, "relaxation_factor": 5}	\N	{"parker": {"suitable": true, "activities": ["Kayaking", "Fishing"], "engagement_level": 4}, "xander": {"suitable": true, "activities": ["Sandy beach", "Controlled water environment"], "engagement_level": 5}, "charlotte": {"suitable": true, "activities": ["Paddle boarding", "Beach play"], "engagement_level": 4}}	https://nativefalls.com/?utm_source=google&utm_medium=gbp	(951) 302-5399	\N	researching	0	{water-activities,wine-country,family-friendly}	{}	{}	\N	\N	2026-02-02 15:20:31.606+00	2026-02-06 04:08:45.699321+00	[{"name": "places/ChIJM-SjofB524AR9gq-KsBR2aI/reviews/Ci9DQUlRQUNvZENodHljRjlvT25sbk1qZG9aRzVWVjFFd2RuRkpiMHhGTlhkbFduYxAB", "text": {"text": "My family and I tent camped here this past weekend and had the worst (nonexistent) management experience. Their EMPLOYEES hosted a Halloween party in the cabin close to my tent site that continued to play loud music and people yelling till 4 in the morning! Mind you the camp rules state quiet starts at 10 pm. At 1 am my husband went to the cabin to ask them to quiet down and someone tried to get PHYSICALLY VIOLENT with him. Then I proceeded to call the “after hours/emergency” phone number 10 times to no answer. Then at 3am I had to go ask again for the party to be quiet. My husband, my two young daughters and I didn’t sleep at all that night. I then sent a email hoping to get a response. The most upsetting part was that I never received a call back, not a follow up email, nothing. For $80 a night I expected so much more.\\n\\nAlso I hope you don’t have to do laundry because the office won’t give you change for your dollars because she couldn’t be bothered to open a roll of quarters.\\n\\nI’m giving 2 stars because the gentleman who runs maintenance during the day was very sweet and the older lady who stays on site was also very nice.", "languageCode": "en"}, "rating": 2, "publishTime": "2025-10-28T04:21:44.373053080Z", "originalText": {"text": "My family and I tent camped here this past weekend and had the worst (nonexistent) management experience. Their EMPLOYEES hosted a Halloween party in the cabin close to my tent site that continued to play loud music and people yelling till 4 in the morning! Mind you the camp rules state quiet starts at 10 pm. At 1 am my husband went to the cabin to ask them to quiet down and someone tried to get PHYSICALLY VIOLENT with him. Then I proceeded to call the “after hours/emergency” phone number 10 times to no answer. Then at 3am I had to go ask again for the party to be quiet. My husband, my two young daughters and I didn’t sleep at all that night. I then sent a email hoping to get a response. The most upsetting part was that I never received a call back, not a follow up email, nothing. For $80 a night I expected so much more.\\n\\nAlso I hope you don’t have to do laundry because the office won’t give you change for your dollars because she couldn’t be bothered to open a roll of quarters.\\n\\nI’m giving 2 stars because the gentleman who runs maintenance during the day was very sweet and the older lady who stays on site was also very nice.", "languageCode": "en"}, "googleMapsUri": "https://www.google.com/maps/reviews/data=!4m6!14m5!1m4!2m3!1sCi9DQUlRQUNvZENodHljRjlvT25sbk1qZG9aRzVWVjFFd2RuRkpiMHhGTlhkbFduYxAB!2m1!1s0x80db79f0a1a3e433:0xa2d951c02abe0af6", "flagContentUri": "https://www.google.com/local/content/rap/report?postId=Ci9DQUlRQUNvZENodHljRjlvT25sbk1qZG9aRzVWVjFFd2RuRkpiMHhGTlhkbFduYxAB&d=17924085&t=1", "authorAttribution": {"uri": "https://www.google.com/maps/contrib/104329070273353935751/reviews", "photoUri": "https://lh3.googleusercontent.com/a/ACg8ocKTmFZBUDutUS99KJFiISaLjJDRzvQEUH-SQEy18aPP4MAl6A=s128-c0x00000000-cc-rp-mo", "displayName": "michelle Johnson"}, "relativePublishTimeDescription": "3 months ago"}, {"name": "places/ChIJM-SjofB524AR9gq-KsBR2aI/reviews/Ci9DQUlRQUNvZENodHljRjlvT21RNFowZFRZV3RTVTFabVEwWjBaa05KTURKelExRRAB", "text": {"text": "We had a fantastic weekend at Native Falls Campground! Our family of four stayed in one of the cabins, and it was the perfect blend of comfort and nature. The cabin was clean, cozy, and well-equipped, great for a relaxing escape but still close to all the fun outdoor activities. The grounds are peaceful and beautifully maintained, and the staff was welcoming and helpful from the moment we arrived. Our kids loved exploring the area, and we really appreciated the family-friendly vibe. Highly recommend this spot for anyone looking for a laid-back, nature-filled getaway!", "languageCode": "en"}, "rating": 5, "publishTime": "2025-08-02T21:32:03.166248104Z", "originalText": {"text": "We had a fantastic weekend at Native Falls Campground! Our family of four stayed in one of the cabins, and it was the perfect blend of comfort and nature. The cabin was clean, cozy, and well-equipped, great for a relaxing escape but still close to all the fun outdoor activities. The grounds are peaceful and beautifully maintained, and the staff was welcoming and helpful from the moment we arrived. Our kids loved exploring the area, and we really appreciated the family-friendly vibe. Highly recommend this spot for anyone looking for a laid-back, nature-filled getaway!", "languageCode": "en"}, "googleMapsUri": "https://www.google.com/maps/reviews/data=!4m6!14m5!1m4!2m3!1sCi9DQUlRQUNvZENodHljRjlvT21RNFowZFRZV3RTVTFabVEwWjBaa05KTURKelExRRAB!2m1!1s0x80db79f0a1a3e433:0xa2d951c02abe0af6", "flagContentUri": "https://www.google.com/local/content/rap/report?postId=Ci9DQUlRQUNvZENodHljRjlvT21RNFowZFRZV3RTVTFabVEwWjBaa05KTURKelExRRAB&d=17924085&t=1", "authorAttribution": {"uri": "https://www.google.com/maps/contrib/116504462738966429491/reviews", "photoUri": "https://lh3.googleusercontent.com/a-/ALV-UjXTQB4PF39J0R-fO0LqFUUan1FrdIhAfb6HIDdiLhIWVx9eHXSTgA=s128-c0x00000000-cc-rp-mo-ba2", "displayName": "Carolina Haddad"}, "relativePublishTimeDescription": "6 months ago"}, {"name": "places/ChIJM-SjofB524AR9gq-KsBR2aI/reviews/Ci9DQUlRQUNvZENodHljRjlvT2s1WFVVSlBka2hUY25SelExUm1WMDl4V0RkaWJuYxAB", "text": {"text": "We had a great time at Native Falls. We camp every month all year long and my 12 year old son commented that Native Falls was the best managed campground we have been to. It was clean, the employees are friendly, the fishing was great, the swimming was fun, the property is really cool. Overall we had an excellent experience and we will definitely return for more fun.", "languageCode": "en"}, "rating": 5, "publishTime": "2025-09-06T13:20:47.414883386Z", "originalText": {"text": "We had a great time at Native Falls. We camp every month all year long and my 12 year old son commented that Native Falls was the best managed campground we have been to. It was clean, the employees are friendly, the fishing was great, the swimming was fun, the property is really cool. Overall we had an excellent experience and we will definitely return for more fun.", "languageCode": "en"}, "googleMapsUri": "https://www.google.com/maps/reviews/data=!4m6!14m5!1m4!2m3!1sCi9DQUlRQUNvZENodHljRjlvT2s1WFVVSlBka2hUY25SelExUm1WMDl4V0RkaWJuYxAB!2m1!1s0x80db79f0a1a3e433:0xa2d951c02abe0af6", "flagContentUri": "https://www.google.com/local/content/rap/report?postId=Ci9DQUlRQUNvZENodHljRjlvT2s1WFVVSlBka2hUY25SelExUm1WMDl4V0RkaWJuYxAB&d=17924085&t=1", "authorAttribution": {"uri": "https://www.google.com/maps/contrib/106043249030351364720/reviews", "photoUri": "https://lh3.googleusercontent.com/a-/ALV-UjWc1ubJiTot-EKbkMOpFGKbv6CE0x_jgNL1FlQ5CINlvTNzLVU54g=s128-c0x00000000-cc-rp-mo-ba2", "displayName": "Kevin Dette"}, "relativePublishTimeDescription": "5 months ago"}, {"name": "places/ChIJM-SjofB524AR9gq-KsBR2aI/reviews/Ci9DQUlRQUNvZENodHljRjlvT20xc1dGOUxVbVJYZUd0d1prWlhZWGh3YVZjMlNIYxAB", "text": {"text": "Great location. Very scenic and relaxing.  We bought a Day Use pass.  Brought our 14-year-old granddaughter here to go swimming at the lake and rented a paddle board.  (First time and she did great)) Played Shuffleboard (Grandpa won) and enjoyed our picnic lunch alongside the lake under a lovely shade tree. Staff is friendly & welcoming.  Great place!", "languageCode": "en"}, "rating": 5, "publishTime": "2025-08-02T20:34:07.590240090Z", "originalText": {"text": "Great location. Very scenic and relaxing.  We bought a Day Use pass.  Brought our 14-year-old granddaughter here to go swimming at the lake and rented a paddle board.  (First time and she did great)) Played Shuffleboard (Grandpa won) and enjoyed our picnic lunch alongside the lake under a lovely shade tree. Staff is friendly & welcoming.  Great place!", "languageCode": "en"}, "googleMapsUri": "https://www.google.com/maps/reviews/data=!4m6!14m5!1m4!2m3!1sCi9DQUlRQUNvZENodHljRjlvT20xc1dGOUxVbVJYZUd0d1prWlhZWGh3YVZjMlNIYxAB!2m1!1s0x80db79f0a1a3e433:0xa2d951c02abe0af6", "flagContentUri": "https://www.google.com/local/content/rap/report?postId=Ci9DQUlRQUNvZENodHljRjlvT20xc1dGOUxVbVJYZUd0d1prWlhZWGh3YVZjMlNIYxAB&d=17924085&t=1", "authorAttribution": {"uri": "https://www.google.com/maps/contrib/106672450659678698401/reviews", "photoUri": "https://lh3.googleusercontent.com/a/ACg8ocIt4IaJ1o_KXNOJUiVWROGJe0UfSyUdFFj1U1JHgpIhRX_WGA=s128-c0x00000000-cc-rp-mo", "displayName": "JK ALOIA"}, "relativePublishTimeDescription": "6 months ago"}, {"name": "places/ChIJM-SjofB524AR9gq-KsBR2aI/reviews/Ci9DQUlRQUNvZENodHljRjlvT21rNE5IbFJRWHBuTW05bGIxVkdTR1JGZDFWemFtYxAB", "text": {"text": "This is a fantastic spot for a weekend getaway! The lake is beautiful and perfect for swimming, kayaking, and fishing. The campground itself is well-maintained, with clean restrooms and spacious campsites. The staff is friendly and helpful, always ready to assist with any needs.\\n\\nPros:\\n- Stunning lake views\\n- Great for water activities\\n- Clean facilities\\n- Friendly staff\\n- Well-maintained grounds\\n\\nCons:\\n- Can get crowded on weekends\\n- Some campsites are a bit close together\\n\\nOverall, I highly recommend for anyone looking to enjoy a relaxing and fun camping experience by the lake. We'll definitely be back!", "languageCode": "en"}, "rating": 5, "publishTime": "2025-08-23T20:01:39.891690366Z", "originalText": {"text": "This is a fantastic spot for a weekend getaway! The lake is beautiful and perfect for swimming, kayaking, and fishing. The campground itself is well-maintained, with clean restrooms and spacious campsites. The staff is friendly and helpful, always ready to assist with any needs.\\n\\nPros:\\n- Stunning lake views\\n- Great for water activities\\n- Clean facilities\\n- Friendly staff\\n- Well-maintained grounds\\n\\nCons:\\n- Can get crowded on weekends\\n- Some campsites are a bit close together\\n\\nOverall, I highly recommend for anyone looking to enjoy a relaxing and fun camping experience by the lake. We'll definitely be back!", "languageCode": "en"}, "googleMapsUri": "https://www.google.com/maps/reviews/data=!4m6!14m5!1m4!2m3!1sCi9DQUlRQUNvZENodHljRjlvT21rNE5IbFJRWHBuTW05bGIxVkdTR1JGZDFWemFtYxAB!2m1!1s0x80db79f0a1a3e433:0xa2d951c02abe0af6", "flagContentUri": "https://www.google.com/local/content/rap/report?postId=Ci9DQUlRQUNvZENodHljRjlvT21rNE5IbFJRWHBuTW05bGIxVkdTR1JGZDFWemFtYxAB&d=17924085&t=1", "authorAttribution": {"uri": "https://www.google.com/maps/contrib/110540851499616638099/reviews", "photoUri": "https://lh3.googleusercontent.com/a/ACg8ocL8JXxknVUPzuxEfW4mKQy3BReG6WHLC0B2KY4O1JphHBcgIQ=s128-c0x00000000-cc-rp-mo", "displayName": "Lenea Sullivan"}, "relativePublishTimeDescription": "5 months ago"}]	Native Falls Campground is generally praised as a well-managed, family-friendly destination with a beautiful lake perfect for swimming, fishing, and water activities. Most visitors love the clean facilities, friendly staff, and peaceful natural setting, though there are occasional management issues with noise control and customer service response.	{"summary": "Native Falls Campground is generally praised as a well-managed, family-friendly destination with a beautiful lake perfect for swimming, fishing, and water activities. Most visitors love the clean facilities, friendly staff, and peaceful natural setting, though there are occasional management issues with noise control and customer service response.", "negative": [{"text": "Their EMPLOYEES hosted a Halloween party in the cabin close to my tent site that continued to play loud music and people yelling till 4 in the morning! My husband, my two young daughters and I didn't sleep at all that night.", "author": "michelle Johnson", "rating": 2}, {"text": "Can get crowded on weekends and some campsites are a bit close together.", "author": "Lenea Sullivan", "rating": 5}], "positive": [{"text": "Our kids loved exploring the area, and we really appreciated the family-friendly vibe.", "author": "Carolina Haddad", "rating": 5}, {"text": "My 12 year old son commented that Native Falls was the best managed campground we have been to.", "author": "Kevin Dette", "rating": 5}, {"text": "Brought our 14-year-old granddaughter here to go swimming at the lake and rented a paddle board. The lake is beautiful and perfect for swimming, kayaking, and fishing.", "author": "JK ALOIA", "rating": 5}], "last_updated": "2026-02-06T04:08:45.586Z"}	2026-02-06 04:08:38.102+00	private_rv_park	\N	\N
a79f6a63-cf62-4c1b-9835-4d1b49223c8a	b201a860-05a3-4ddc-bb89-4c4271177271	McArthur-Burney Falls	The campground lists maximum 32 feet for trailers, making your 30-foot 5th wheel a borderline fit. Call the park (530-335-2777) to verify specific sites can accommodate your rig length. If tight, North Shore Campground on Lake Britton (6 miles away) provides backup.	Theodore Roosevelt called this 129-foot waterfall 'the eighth wonder of the world.' It flows at 100 million gallons per day year-round—even in drought—because underground springs push through volcanic basalt.	state_parks	\N	24898 CA-89, Burney, CA 96013, USA	Burney	CA	41.0124498	-121.6502456	ChIJC7sGQeynzVQRYpZS1d2szTs	4.8	2823	\N	{"cell_coverage": "fair", "max_trailer_length_ft": 32}	t	\N	\N	35.00	USD	$35-70/night via ReserveCalifornia. Uses monthly Reservation Draw lottery for high-demand periods	{"best": ["april", "may", "june", "september", "october"], "notes": "Summer fills to capacity and may close entrance"}	7-8 hours	\N	{"scenic_beauty": 5, "solitude_level": 3, "adventure_level": 3, "family_friendly": 5, "relaxation_factor": 5}	\N	{"parker": {"suitable": true, "activities": ["Hiking to 1800s settler cemetery (2.5 miles)", "Spotting black swifts"], "engagement_level": 4}, "xander": {"suitable": true, "activities": ["Waterfall sound and spray sensory experience", "Wading in creek shallows"], "engagement_level": 5}, "charlotte": {"suitable": true, "activities": ["Walking through waterfall mist seeking rainbows"], "engagement_level": 5}}	https://www.parks.ca.gov/?page_id=455	(530) 335-2777	\N	researching	0	{waterfall,eighth-wonder,volcanic}	{"Theodore Roosevelt's 'eighth wonder'","100 million gallons/day year-round","Black swifts nest behind falls"}	{"30-foot 5th wheel is borderline fit—call ahead","Summer fills to capacity"}	\N	\N	2026-02-02 15:20:42.643+00	2026-02-04 14:57:42.278754+00	[{"name": "places/ChIJC7sGQeynzVQRYpZS1d2szTs/reviews/Ci9DQUlRQUNvZENodHljRjlvT2t0VU1tOVNjRGRMY0VsU1JEaFlTM2t6WkhVdFYxRRAB", "text": {"text": "One of the most beautiful waterfalls I’ve ever seen! The best part is that a short 0.3 mile hike takes you right to the falls, and you can admire them the entire way since they’re visible throughout. We reached at noon - while the view from the top was stunning, we couldn’t get good pictures at the bottom because the sunlight was directly behind the falls. For better shots, try visiting in the morning or late afternoon. The trail is friendly and can easily be done with elderly visitors or infants, which makes it even better.", "languageCode": "en"}, "rating": 5, "publishTime": "2025-12-24T06:08:18.814800467Z", "originalText": {"text": "One of the most beautiful waterfalls I’ve ever seen! The best part is that a short 0.3 mile hike takes you right to the falls, and you can admire them the entire way since they’re visible throughout. We reached at noon - while the view from the top was stunning, we couldn’t get good pictures at the bottom because the sunlight was directly behind the falls. For better shots, try visiting in the morning or late afternoon. The trail is friendly and can easily be done with elderly visitors or infants, which makes it even better.", "languageCode": "en"}, "googleMapsUri": "https://www.google.com/maps/reviews/data=!4m6!14m5!1m4!2m3!1sCi9DQUlRQUNvZENodHljRjlvT2t0VU1tOVNjRGRMY0VsU1JEaFlTM2t6WkhVdFYxRRAB!2m1!1s0x54cda7ec4106bb0b:0x3bcdacddd5529662", "flagContentUri": "https://www.google.com/local/content/rap/report?postId=Ci9DQUlRQUNvZENodHljRjlvT2t0VU1tOVNjRGRMY0VsU1JEaFlTM2t6WkhVdFYxRRAB&d=17924085&t=1", "authorAttribution": {"uri": "https://www.google.com/maps/contrib/100501123520467642882/reviews", "photoUri": "https://lh3.googleusercontent.com/a-/ALV-UjWNf7cmYXR7SHbjEY_1H3oXgxPltYTl8RafeWrGYgZmwt9HisC8_g=s128-c0x00000000-cc-rp-mo-ba6", "displayName": "Nikhil"}, "relativePublishTimeDescription": "a month ago"}, {"name": "places/ChIJC7sGQeynzVQRYpZS1d2szTs/reviews/Ci9DQUlRQUNvZENodHljRjlvT2tscGVtRXhVMmxwWWtrMFRXRkdPR2szYVVSRWRXYxAB", "text": {"text": "Definitely one of the most beautiful places I have ever seen. I look forward to camping here. The hike down the trail to the water fall is not that bad and coming up was either.  I definitely recommend this to everyone. Everyone should visit this place atleast once in life. It is truly a beautiful place.", "languageCode": "en"}, "rating": 5, "publishTime": "2025-10-20T06:19:34.906806127Z", "originalText": {"text": "Definitely one of the most beautiful places I have ever seen. I look forward to camping here. The hike down the trail to the water fall is not that bad and coming up was either.  I definitely recommend this to everyone. Everyone should visit this place atleast once in life. It is truly a beautiful place.", "languageCode": "en"}, "googleMapsUri": "https://www.google.com/maps/reviews/data=!4m6!14m5!1m4!2m3!1sCi9DQUlRQUNvZENodHljRjlvT2tscGVtRXhVMmxwWWtrMFRXRkdPR2szYVVSRWRXYxAB!2m1!1s0x54cda7ec4106bb0b:0x3bcdacddd5529662", "flagContentUri": "https://www.google.com/local/content/rap/report?postId=Ci9DQUlRQUNvZENodHljRjlvT2tscGVtRXhVMmxwWWtrMFRXRkdPR2szYVVSRWRXYxAB&d=17924085&t=1", "authorAttribution": {"uri": "https://www.google.com/maps/contrib/113023338400922831762/reviews", "photoUri": "https://lh3.googleusercontent.com/a-/ALV-UjVobTIYQuwyrq-Gnh_VToorieYAJ9qY5gNbtzSazmUcZcIdsTEE=s128-c0x00000000-cc-rp-mo-ba5", "displayName": "Omar Lopez (Marejo)"}, "relativePublishTimeDescription": "3 months ago"}, {"name": "places/ChIJC7sGQeynzVQRYpZS1d2szTs/reviews/Ci9DQUlRQUNvZENodHljRjlvT2pCdldHTldXamxaZWtaMFpFZ3dVVmxwVTFsVVJrRRAB", "text": {"text": "Burney Falls is absolutely breathtaking — truly one of the most beautiful places I’ve ever visited. The waterfall is stunning, with water cascading down into a crystal-clear pool surrounded by lush greenery. The sound of the falls creates such a peaceful and refreshing atmosphere, and the cool mist makes it an amazing spot to relax on a warm day. The trails are well-kept, offering gorgeous views from different angles, and the whole park is very clean and inviting. Whether you’re hiking, taking photos, or just enjoying nature, Burney Falls is a must-see destination in California. I can’t wait to come back! The only thing is the facilities could use some upkeeps no soap no hand dryer or a way to dry your hands and most of the bathrooms were closed", "languageCode": "en"}, "rating": 5, "publishTime": "2025-09-28T13:14:42.443714707Z", "originalText": {"text": "Burney Falls is absolutely breathtaking — truly one of the most beautiful places I’ve ever visited. The waterfall is stunning, with water cascading down into a crystal-clear pool surrounded by lush greenery. The sound of the falls creates such a peaceful and refreshing atmosphere, and the cool mist makes it an amazing spot to relax on a warm day. The trails are well-kept, offering gorgeous views from different angles, and the whole park is very clean and inviting. Whether you’re hiking, taking photos, or just enjoying nature, Burney Falls is a must-see destination in California. I can’t wait to come back! The only thing is the facilities could use some upkeeps no soap no hand dryer or a way to dry your hands and most of the bathrooms were closed", "languageCode": "en"}, "googleMapsUri": "https://www.google.com/maps/reviews/data=!4m6!14m5!1m4!2m3!1sCi9DQUlRQUNvZENodHljRjlvT2pCdldHTldXamxaZWtaMFpFZ3dVVmxwVTFsVVJrRRAB!2m1!1s0x54cda7ec4106bb0b:0x3bcdacddd5529662", "flagContentUri": "https://www.google.com/local/content/rap/report?postId=Ci9DQUlRQUNvZENodHljRjlvT2pCdldHTldXamxaZWtaMFpFZ3dVVmxwVTFsVVJrRRAB&d=17924085&t=1", "authorAttribution": {"uri": "https://www.google.com/maps/contrib/111540693262976522320/reviews", "photoUri": "https://lh3.googleusercontent.com/a-/ALV-UjV1lXtmq1fgmQA9oKLnUoudxi6kyac4k5K-eQfFOttUWEXkmgSNtw=s128-c0x00000000-cc-rp-mo-ba4", "displayName": "Nick Schenck"}, "relativePublishTimeDescription": "4 months ago"}, {"name": "places/ChIJC7sGQeynzVQRYpZS1d2szTs/reviews/Ci9DQUlRQUNvZENodHljRjlvT21OWlkwSjBkbVJuVlY5MVpteExOWEZ0U0RscFprRRAB", "text": {"text": "Absolutely breath-taking waterfall! Easy walk/hike on paved path down to the waterfall and then you have the option to walk the trail loop which is a little over 1 mile.", "languageCode": "en"}, "rating": 5, "publishTime": "2025-12-09T06:49:47.758421210Z", "originalText": {"text": "Absolutely breath-taking waterfall! Easy walk/hike on paved path down to the waterfall and then you have the option to walk the trail loop which is a little over 1 mile.", "languageCode": "en"}, "googleMapsUri": "https://www.google.com/maps/reviews/data=!4m6!14m5!1m4!2m3!1sCi9DQUlRQUNvZENodHljRjlvT21OWlkwSjBkbVJuVlY5MVpteExOWEZ0U0RscFprRRAB!2m1!1s0x54cda7ec4106bb0b:0x3bcdacddd5529662", "flagContentUri": "https://www.google.com/local/content/rap/report?postId=Ci9DQUlRQUNvZENodHljRjlvT21OWlkwSjBkbVJuVlY5MVpteExOWEZ0U0RscFprRRAB&d=17924085&t=1", "authorAttribution": {"uri": "https://www.google.com/maps/contrib/106467919449151012278/reviews", "photoUri": "https://lh3.googleusercontent.com/a-/ALV-UjXO8EGBymUSJH-0ILlCQma54Aq5u5edOgABBQ-ObVluPi3v6lpUUg=s128-c0x00000000-cc-rp-mo-ba5", "displayName": "Diana Tamburo"}, "relativePublishTimeDescription": "a month ago"}, {"name": "places/ChIJC7sGQeynzVQRYpZS1d2szTs/reviews/Ci9DQUlRQUNvZENodHljRjlvT2s1QlEwbDBObkJRYjBGbFpHcEpjWHBaU1hCV2FYYxAB", "text": {"text": "What a beautiful walk to see an amazing waterfall, all downhill and up around.\\nUnfortunately as you walk closer to the ice cold water at the bottom you are greeted by the trail of trash, debris, brown foam (build up from people just being gross) clothing that has been left behind on and inbetween the rocks. It's sad to see such a beautiful piece of nature being treated so poorly - don't complain and stomp your feet when it gets shut down.", "languageCode": "en"}, "rating": 5, "publishTime": "2025-08-28T19:57:45.714063550Z", "originalText": {"text": "What a beautiful walk to see an amazing waterfall, all downhill and up around.\\nUnfortunately as you walk closer to the ice cold water at the bottom you are greeted by the trail of trash, debris, brown foam (build up from people just being gross) clothing that has been left behind on and inbetween the rocks. It's sad to see such a beautiful piece of nature being treated so poorly - don't complain and stomp your feet when it gets shut down.", "languageCode": "en"}, "googleMapsUri": "https://www.google.com/maps/reviews/data=!4m6!14m5!1m4!2m3!1sCi9DQUlRQUNvZENodHljRjlvT2s1QlEwbDBObkJRYjBGbFpHcEpjWHBaU1hCV2FYYxAB!2m1!1s0x54cda7ec4106bb0b:0x3bcdacddd5529662", "flagContentUri": "https://www.google.com/local/content/rap/report?postId=Ci9DQUlRQUNvZENodHljRjlvT2s1QlEwbDBObkJRYjBGbFpHcEpjWHBaU1hCV2FYYxAB&d=17924085&t=1", "authorAttribution": {"uri": "https://www.google.com/maps/contrib/118010228030063518822/reviews", "photoUri": "https://lh3.googleusercontent.com/a/ACg8ocLNxKJrLsLk-w4ljpmCjD4fkHCRCTHi8t08s7ANWX0fzSjk8KM=s128-c0x00000000-cc-rp-mo-ba5", "displayName": "Running ThePeralta Household"}, "relativePublishTimeDescription": "5 months ago"}]	McArthur-Burney Falls is universally praised as a breathtakingly beautiful waterfall with an easy, family-friendly 0.3-mile hike that's accessible for elderly visitors and infants. The stunning cascade into crystal-clear pools creates a peaceful, refreshing atmosphere that visitors describe as a must-see destination. However, some concerns exist about facility maintenance and visitor impact on the natural environment.	{"summary": "McArthur-Burney Falls is universally praised as a breathtakingly beautiful waterfall with an easy, family-friendly 0.3-mile hike that's accessible for elderly visitors and infants. The stunning cascade into crystal-clear pools creates a peaceful, refreshing atmosphere that visitors describe as a must-see destination. However, some concerns exist about facility maintenance and visitor impact on the natural environment.", "negative": [{"text": "The only thing is the facilities could use some upkeeps no soap no hand dryer or a way to dry your hands and most of the bathrooms were closed", "author": "Nick Schenck", "rating": 5}, {"text": "Unfortunately as you walk closer to the ice cold water at the bottom you are greeted by the trail of trash, debris, brown foam (build up from people just being gross) clothing that has been left behind", "author": "Running ThePeralta Household", "rating": 5}], "positive": [{"text": "The trail is friendly and can easily be done with elderly visitors or infants, which makes it even better.", "author": "Nikhil", "rating": 5}, {"text": "Easy walk/hike on paved path down to the waterfall and then you have the option to walk the trail loop which is a little over 1 mile.", "author": "Diana Tamburo", "rating": 5}, {"text": "The cool mist makes it an amazing spot to relax on a warm day. The trails are well-kept, offering gorgeous views from different angles, and the whole park is very clean and inviting.", "author": "Nick Schenck", "rating": 5}], "last_updated": "2026-02-04T14:57:42.137Z"}	2026-02-04 14:57:33.955+00	\N	\N	\N
02e8e850-de77-430e-bc0f-c37cf5f7f97b	b201a860-05a3-4ddc-bb89-4c4271177271	Pismo Coast Village RV Resort	Pismo Coast Village is a large, well-maintained RV resort right on the beach in Pismo Beach. With over 400 sites offering full hookups, pool, hot tub, mini golf, arcade, and a general store, it's a comfortable base camp for families. The real magic is what's nearby: the Oceano Dunes for off-road fun, the Monarch Butterfly Grove (one of the largest winter roosts in the US), clam digging on the beach, and the charming downtown Pismo Beach boardwalk.	A full-hookup beachfront RV resort where you can walk to the sand, ride ATVs on the Oceano Dunes, watch thousands of monarch butterflies in a eucalyptus grove, and dig for Pismo clams—all in one weekend.	other	\N	165 S Dolliver St, Pismo Beach, CA 93449, USA	Pismo Beach	CA	35.1342374	-120.6379334	ChIJ8eyjrthY7IARxYyy8ZMcRxE	4.5	1883	\N	{"hookups": "full", "cell_coverage": "excellent", "road_accessibility": "Easy access off US-101. Flat, paved interior roads. No issues for any rig size.", "max_trailer_length_ft": 40, "fifth_wheel_accessible": true}	t	\N	Book directly through resort website. Popular weekends book months ahead. Midweek is easier to get. Minimum stays may apply on holiday weekends.	80.00	USD	\N	{"best": ["september", "october", "november", "march", "april", "may"], "avoid": [], "notes": "Monarch butterflies are October-February (peak November-January). Summer is warmest but often foggy mornings. Year-round destination."}	3 hours	\N	{"scenic_beauty": 4, "solitude_level": 1, "adventure_level": 4, "family_friendly": 5, "relaxation_factor": 4}	{"topics": ["monarch butterfly migration", "dune ecology", "Pismo clam biology"], "visitor_center": false, "ranger_programs": false, "junior_ranger_program": false}	{"parker": {"notes": "Oceano Dunes will blow Parker's mind—riding on sand dunes is an unforgettable adventure.", "suitable": true, "activities": ["ATV/dune buggy experience at Oceano Dunes", "Clam digging on the beach", "Mini golf and arcade at resort", "Biking on the beach"], "engagement_level": 5}, "xander": {"notes": "Between the beach, pool, and butterflies, Xander will be in sensory heaven.", "suitable": true, "activities": ["Beach sand play", "Pool time", "Butterflies", "Watching dune buggies"], "engagement_level": 5}, "charlotte": {"notes": "Thousands of monarch butterflies clustering in trees is magical for a 5-year-old. The Dinosaur Caves Park has a great themed playground.", "suitable": true, "activities": ["Monarch Butterfly Grove", "Shell collecting on beach", "Dinosaur Caves Park playground", "Pool and hot tub at resort"], "engagement_level": 5}}	http://www.pismocoastvillage.com/	(888) 782-3224	\N	researching	0	{beach,full-hookups,resort,atv,butterflies,family-friendly,pool}	{"Full hookups and resort amenities—pool, hot tub, mini golf, arcade","Walk to the beach from your site","Oceano Dunes are a unique adventure you can't get elsewhere","Monarch Butterfly Grove is one of the largest winter roosts in the US","Easy access, no mountain driving"}	{"Large commercial RV park feel—not a nature campground","Pricey compared to state parks","Can be crowded and noisy on weekends"}	\N	\N	2026-02-04 15:15:18.873+00	2026-02-06 02:13:49.952683+00	[{"name": "places/ChIJ8eyjrthY7IARxYyy8ZMcRxE/reviews/Ci9DQUlRQUNvZENodHljRjlvT25sVmFrOVBNRzAzVDJ0WlUzbGFiRVZaVERWSVJFRRAB", "text": {"text": "Nicely maintained facilities. The on prem food is just OK. Most fellow RVers are nice, but you get an occasional person who could care less who is around them. They don’t do much to moderate them. Lots of dogs, we usually keep our big guy inside. Lots of small barky dogs usually fenced in front of RVs. One big request, it would be so nice to have an online reservation system and have the ability to pick spots. It’s hit or miss. We usually get in around 3pm and have had OK luck the 4 times we have stayed over the last year. Little pricey. The beach access is worth the hassles. Lots of kids and families. Pismo has lots of good food. Just be patient with rude folks now and then.", "languageCode": "en"}, "rating": 4, "publishTime": "2026-01-04T19:56:11.911326910Z", "originalText": {"text": "Nicely maintained facilities. The on prem food is just OK. Most fellow RVers are nice, but you get an occasional person who could care less who is around them. They don’t do much to moderate them. Lots of dogs, we usually keep our big guy inside. Lots of small barky dogs usually fenced in front of RVs. One big request, it would be so nice to have an online reservation system and have the ability to pick spots. It’s hit or miss. We usually get in around 3pm and have had OK luck the 4 times we have stayed over the last year. Little pricey. The beach access is worth the hassles. Lots of kids and families. Pismo has lots of good food. Just be patient with rude folks now and then.", "languageCode": "en"}, "googleMapsUri": "https://www.google.com/maps/reviews/data=!4m6!14m5!1m4!2m3!1sCi9DQUlRQUNvZENodHljRjlvT25sVmFrOVBNRzAzVDJ0WlUzbGFiRVZaVERWSVJFRRAB!2m1!1s0x80ec58d8aea3ecf1:0x11471c93f1b28cc5", "flagContentUri": "https://www.google.com/local/content/rap/report?postId=Ci9DQUlRQUNvZENodHljRjlvT25sVmFrOVBNRzAzVDJ0WlUzbGFiRVZaVERWSVJFRRAB&d=17924085&t=1", "authorAttribution": {"uri": "https://www.google.com/maps/contrib/113948703677187849968/reviews", "photoUri": "https://lh3.googleusercontent.com/a-/ALV-UjU3R0T0FXq7BXU1jLeM9ANNyo6DZv5SNLLay4eHB_f0EyEHX_s=s128-c0x00000000-cc-rp-mo-ba2", "displayName": "Eric Garza"}, "relativePublishTimeDescription": "a month ago"}, {"name": "places/ChIJ8eyjrthY7IARxYyy8ZMcRxE/reviews/Ci9DQUlRQUNvZENodHljRjlvT21SdFlpMUJZMWRGTFhaTmNpMU1NMmxMVDJoQ1pGRRAB", "text": {"text": "First time here.  First time using our camper we purchased and it was also stored here. The place is pretty well kept. There was lots of maintenance and stuff members, and they were very polite and helpful. The beach view was beautiful at sunset! There’s a general store and a restaurant and laundry mate. We didn’t get to the pool, but it looks heated. Great experience.", "languageCode": "en"}, "rating": 5, "publishTime": "2025-11-30T20:43:32.995088082Z", "originalText": {"text": "First time here.  First time using our camper we purchased and it was also stored here. The place is pretty well kept. There was lots of maintenance and stuff members, and they were very polite and helpful. The beach view was beautiful at sunset! There’s a general store and a restaurant and laundry mate. We didn’t get to the pool, but it looks heated. Great experience.", "languageCode": "en"}, "googleMapsUri": "https://www.google.com/maps/reviews/data=!4m6!14m5!1m4!2m3!1sCi9DQUlRQUNvZENodHljRjlvT21SdFlpMUJZMWRGTFhaTmNpMU1NMmxMVDJoQ1pGRRAB!2m1!1s0x80ec58d8aea3ecf1:0x11471c93f1b28cc5", "flagContentUri": "https://www.google.com/local/content/rap/report?postId=Ci9DQUlRQUNvZENodHljRjlvT21SdFlpMUJZMWRGTFhaTmNpMU1NMmxMVDJoQ1pGRRAB&d=17924085&t=1", "authorAttribution": {"uri": "https://www.google.com/maps/contrib/113910994811306728299/reviews", "photoUri": "https://lh3.googleusercontent.com/a/ACg8ocL1ECr7kwVs1osbbPEyZVWjbiIjN3OGObgDx_guvMXwcOvD5Yg=s128-c0x00000000-cc-rp-mo-ba3", "displayName": "Brian Samarripa"}, "relativePublishTimeDescription": "2 months ago"}, {"name": "places/ChIJ8eyjrthY7IARxYyy8ZMcRxE/reviews/Ci9DQUlRQUNvZENodHljRjlvT2pOSFVWSldkMHQ2TFdSS1NIZGxXbFpJY0RkVlVVRRAB", "text": {"text": "Our go to place when we come to visit Pismo. You can walk to the beach from the little entrances they have throughout the RV park. There's mini golf, general store,bike rentals,heated pool, huge restrooms with showers and other amenities. Most spaces are a good size, although this time we got a smaller space and we're staying at space 283. Normally we can set up a 10x10 canopy but we couldn't do that here. That is the ONLY downfall for this trip. Other trips we stayed on the next row over,closer to the restrooms and kids play area and it was perfect. I would recommend this for anyone who likes to RV camp. You're also only about 10 min away from Pismos center attractions. 5min on a scooter.", "languageCode": "en"}, "rating": 5, "publishTime": "2025-10-18T16:50:16.783700609Z", "originalText": {"text": "Our go to place when we come to visit Pismo. You can walk to the beach from the little entrances they have throughout the RV park. There's mini golf, general store,bike rentals,heated pool, huge restrooms with showers and other amenities. Most spaces are a good size, although this time we got a smaller space and we're staying at space 283. Normally we can set up a 10x10 canopy but we couldn't do that here. That is the ONLY downfall for this trip. Other trips we stayed on the next row over,closer to the restrooms and kids play area and it was perfect. I would recommend this for anyone who likes to RV camp. You're also only about 10 min away from Pismos center attractions. 5min on a scooter.", "languageCode": "en"}, "googleMapsUri": "https://www.google.com/maps/reviews/data=!4m6!14m5!1m4!2m3!1sCi9DQUlRQUNvZENodHljRjlvT2pOSFVWSldkMHQ2TFdSS1NIZGxXbFpJY0RkVlVVRRAB!2m1!1s0x80ec58d8aea3ecf1:0x11471c93f1b28cc5", "flagContentUri": "https://www.google.com/local/content/rap/report?postId=Ci9DQUlRQUNvZENodHljRjlvT2pOSFVWSldkMHQ2TFdSS1NIZGxXbFpJY0RkVlVVRRAB&d=17924085&t=1", "authorAttribution": {"uri": "https://www.google.com/maps/contrib/103848483499872460869/reviews", "photoUri": "https://lh3.googleusercontent.com/a/ACg8ocLlLp3MiZAxtc8eTJq5NM_TueXSpqUd4AO-JgYde6NH3zCzvg=s128-c0x00000000-cc-rp-mo-ba4", "displayName": "Sharon Moya"}, "relativePublishTimeDescription": "3 months ago"}, {"name": "places/ChIJ8eyjrthY7IARxYyy8ZMcRxE/reviews/Ci9DQUlRQUNvZENodHljRjlvT25WbVNIRm1UUzF3WWt0SlJFUlNTMkUzVjNwRlVGRRAB", "text": {"text": "We love it here! We live near the S.F. Bay Area so Pismo Beach, San Simeon, and Morro Bay have always been some of our favorite weekend getaways--for decades before we owned an RV. But now that we own a share at PCV, we will be able to get down here for weeks at a time! And if future weeks are anything like this first week was, we can't wait to get back here again! 😁", "languageCode": "en"}, "rating": 5, "publishTime": "2025-11-03T21:34:55.609630744Z", "originalText": {"text": "We love it here! We live near the S.F. Bay Area so Pismo Beach, San Simeon, and Morro Bay have always been some of our favorite weekend getaways--for decades before we owned an RV. But now that we own a share at PCV, we will be able to get down here for weeks at a time! And if future weeks are anything like this first week was, we can't wait to get back here again! 😁", "languageCode": "en"}, "googleMapsUri": "https://www.google.com/maps/reviews/data=!4m6!14m5!1m4!2m3!1sCi9DQUlRQUNvZENodHljRjlvT25WbVNIRm1UUzF3WWt0SlJFUlNTMkUzVjNwRlVGRRAB!2m1!1s0x80ec58d8aea3ecf1:0x11471c93f1b28cc5", "flagContentUri": "https://www.google.com/local/content/rap/report?postId=Ci9DQUlRQUNvZENodHljRjlvT25WbVNIRm1UUzF3WWt0SlJFUlNTMkUzVjNwRlVGRRAB&d=17924085&t=1", "authorAttribution": {"uri": "https://www.google.com/maps/contrib/117318892450500664455/reviews", "photoUri": "https://lh3.googleusercontent.com/a/ACg8ocI8-w5kz8ZF2cf19-ZdeeZjfNJRU2CKOFcDdwCNKEanYtCdMw=s128-c0x00000000-cc-rp-mo-ba5", "displayName": "William Vlach"}, "relativePublishTimeDescription": "3 months ago"}, {"name": "places/ChIJ8eyjrthY7IARxYyy8ZMcRxE/reviews/Ci9DQUlRQUNvZENodHljRjlvT21Vd1VVcGhhM2RrUkZsSlZVOUtSVjh6WWpKRk1VRRAB", "text": {"text": "Been coming here for about 8 years now - it's a nice resort but somehow we keep getting placed in the same crappy area.  Against the State Park wall, spaces are narrow and tight with barely enough room for our vehicle.  Can't use the fire rig - it's too close to the neighboring rig.  All dirt.  Picnic table is up against our neighbors sewage line - really appealing.  Would like to know what I have to do to get a halfway decent space next time - if there is a next time.  Usually we make our reservations months (six this time) in advance.", "languageCode": "en"}, "rating": 1, "publishTime": "2025-10-18T15:32:47.366735067Z", "originalText": {"text": "Been coming here for about 8 years now - it's a nice resort but somehow we keep getting placed in the same crappy area.  Against the State Park wall, spaces are narrow and tight with barely enough room for our vehicle.  Can't use the fire rig - it's too close to the neighboring rig.  All dirt.  Picnic table is up against our neighbors sewage line - really appealing.  Would like to know what I have to do to get a halfway decent space next time - if there is a next time.  Usually we make our reservations months (six this time) in advance.", "languageCode": "en"}, "googleMapsUri": "https://www.google.com/maps/reviews/data=!4m6!14m5!1m4!2m3!1sCi9DQUlRQUNvZENodHljRjlvT21Vd1VVcGhhM2RrUkZsSlZVOUtSVjh6WWpKRk1VRRAB!2m1!1s0x80ec58d8aea3ecf1:0x11471c93f1b28cc5", "flagContentUri": "https://www.google.com/local/content/rap/report?postId=Ci9DQUlRQUNvZENodHljRjlvT21Vd1VVcGhhM2RrUkZsSlZVOUtSVjh6WWpKRk1VRRAB&d=17924085&t=1", "authorAttribution": {"uri": "https://www.google.com/maps/contrib/117041948968174471656/reviews", "photoUri": "https://lh3.googleusercontent.com/a/ACg8ocJci9DHbVw4q8JGrssv39kvylbO82N5WilHemmVmqzEsDMWKg=s128-c0x00000000-cc-rp-mo-ba2", "displayName": "Tammi Meeks"}, "relativePublishTimeDescription": "3 months ago"}]	Pismo Coast Village RV Resort is a well-maintained family-friendly destination that offers direct beach access and numerous amenities including mini golf, heated pool, and kids' play areas. While most guests love the beautiful beach views and convenient location near Pismo attractions, some experience issues with inconsistent site assignments and occasional crowding. The resort appears ideal for families despite being somewhat pricey and having variable site quality.	{"summary": "Pismo Coast Village RV Resort is a well-maintained family-friendly destination that offers direct beach access and numerous amenities including mini golf, heated pool, and kids' play areas. While most guests love the beautiful beach views and convenient location near Pismo attractions, some experience issues with inconsistent site assignments and occasional crowding. The resort appears ideal for families despite being somewhat pricey and having variable site quality.", "negative": [{"text": "Somehow we keep getting placed in the same crappy area. Spaces are narrow and tight with barely enough room for our vehicle.", "author": "Tammi Meeks", "rating": 1}, {"text": "One big request, it would be so nice to have an online reservation system and have the ability to pick spots. It's hit or miss.", "author": "Eric Garza", "rating": 4}], "positive": [{"text": "There's mini golf, general store, bike rentals, heated pool, huge restrooms with showers and other amenities.", "author": "Sharon Moya", "rating": 5}, {"text": "You can walk to the beach from the little entrances they have throughout the RV park.", "author": "Sharon Moya", "rating": 5}, {"text": "Lots of kids and families. The beach access is worth the hassles.", "author": "Eric Garza", "rating": 4}], "last_updated": "2026-02-06T02:13:49.845Z"}	2026-02-06 02:13:43.62+00	private_rv_park	\N	\N
d3fe091c-ea89-4d48-b68a-737dbd26bc29	b201a860-05a3-4ddc-bb89-4c4271177271	Morro Bay State Park Campground	Morro Bay State Park is tucked into the hills above Morro Bay, offering sheltered campsites in a eucalyptus and oak grove with glimpses of the bay and Morro Rock. The campground has water and electric hookups on many sites and can accommodate larger rigs. Sea otters are visible from the shoreline daily, kayaking and paddleboarding in the protected bay is world-class, and nearby Montana de Oro State Park offers some of the best coastal hiking in California. The town of Morro Bay is charming, walkable, and kid-friendly.	Camp in a eucalyptus grove overlooking one of California's most iconic bays, where sea otters float on their backs, a volcanic rock dominates the skyline, and Montana de Oro's wild coastline is just 15 minutes away.	state_parks	\N	Main St, Morro Bay, CA 93442, USA	Morro Bay	CA	35.3467304	-120.8408780	ChIJCZKi2tHj7IARqTtt5HpK0QY	4.5	882	\N	{"hookups": "water_electric", "cell_coverage": "good", "road_accessibility": "Paved roads throughout. Some campground roads have moderate grades but manageable for 5th wheels. Sites vary in size—book carefully.", "max_trailer_length_ft": 35, "fifth_wheel_accessible": true}	t	\N	Book via ReserveCalifornia.com up to 6 months in advance. Less competitive than SoCal beaches but still fills on summer weekends.	50.00	USD	\N	{"best": ["april", "may", "june", "september", "october"], "avoid": [], "notes": "Year-round destination. Summer is foggy but warm. Spring and fall are often the sunniest. Winter is mild with whale migration. No bad time to visit."}	3.5 hours	\N	{"scenic_beauty": 5, "solitude_level": 3, "adventure_level": 4, "family_friendly": 5, "relaxation_factor": 5}	{"topics": ["marine ecology", "sea otters", "volcanic geology", "estuary habitats", "Chumash history"], "visitor_center": true, "ranger_programs": true, "junior_ranger_program": true}	{"parker": {"notes": "Black Hill summit is a real achievement hike with panoramic views. Montana de Oro's rocky coastline is adventure paradise.", "suitable": true, "activities": ["Black Hill summit hike", "Montana de Oro bluff trail scrambling", "Kayaking in the bay", "Morro Rock scramble at base"], "engagement_level": 5}, "xander": {"notes": "Xander can watch sea otters for hours. The beach at Morro Rock is gentle. The heron rookery behind the museum is close and fascinating.", "suitable": true, "activities": ["Sea otter watching", "Beach sand play at Morro Rock", "Heron rookery bird watching", "Museum animals and exhibits"], "engagement_level": 5}, "charlotte": {"notes": "Charlotte will be mesmerized by the sea otters—visible from multiple spots around the bay. Montana de Oro tide pools are exceptional.", "suitable": true, "activities": ["Sea otter watching from shore", "Montana de Oro tide pools", "Museum of Natural History exhibits", "Kayaking with parent"], "engagement_level": 5}}	http://www.parks.ca.gov/?page_id=594	(805) 772-2560	\N	researching	0	{sea-otters,kayaking,paddleboarding,coastal-hiking,state-park,tide-pools,water-electric}	{"Sea otters visible daily—unforgettable for kids","Water/electric hookups available","Montana de Oro next door offers world-class coastal hiking","Protected bay perfect for family kayaking/paddleboarding","Charming walkable town with great seafood"}	{"Fog can be persistent in summer","3.5-hour drive from LA makes this a full weekend commitment","Some sites are small for larger rigs—book carefully"}	\N	\N	2026-02-04 15:15:18.127+00	2026-02-06 02:14:42.232298+00	[{"name": "places/ChIJCZKi2tHj7IARqTtt5HpK0QY/reviews/Ci9DQUlRQUNvZENodHljRjlvT2tOME5FOVBOVVY2VERCTWVYZEdWSG8yT1RaRGQyYxAB", "text": {"text": "I did not camp here but did take a drive through. The campsites are tiny and offer little to no privacy. While the location itself deserves five stars, camping in what essentially amounts to a grassy parking lot prevents this campground from earning a five-star rating.", "languageCode": "en"}, "rating": 4, "publishTime": "2026-01-16T23:20:08.194571712Z", "originalText": {"text": "I did not camp here but did take a drive through. The campsites are tiny and offer little to no privacy. While the location itself deserves five stars, camping in what essentially amounts to a grassy parking lot prevents this campground from earning a five-star rating.", "languageCode": "en"}, "googleMapsUri": "https://www.google.com/maps/reviews/data=!4m6!14m5!1m4!2m3!1sCi9DQUlRQUNvZENodHljRjlvT2tOME5FOVBOVVY2VERCTWVYZEdWSG8yT1RaRGQyYxAB!2m1!1s0x80ece3d1daa29209:0x6d14a7ae46d3ba9", "flagContentUri": "https://www.google.com/local/content/rap/report?postId=Ci9DQUlRQUNvZENodHljRjlvT2tOME5FOVBOVVY2VERCTWVYZEdWSG8yT1RaRGQyYxAB&d=17924085&t=1", "authorAttribution": {"uri": "https://www.google.com/maps/contrib/117943216766504912788/reviews", "photoUri": "https://lh3.googleusercontent.com/a-/ALV-UjX-23xaPKlKKDNTOjomEbjNV5b0V8BXYwjVu6LCgjPgMlmdrmJHFQ=s128-c0x00000000-cc-rp-mo-ba5", "displayName": "Wayne Clark"}, "relativePublishTimeDescription": "2 weeks ago"}, {"name": "places/ChIJCZKi2tHj7IARqTtt5HpK0QY/reviews/Ci9DQUlRQUNvZENodHljRjlvT200dGFESnhRM1JPWm1KZlEyRlRWSEJPUmxOeE9XYxAB", "text": {"text": "Would never camp here again. The bathrooms are fine, they have showers and restrooms and washing up stations. The whole camp ground is dirt/ dirty loose sand. There is no separation between camp sites, no privacy what so ever, no nature, just dirty. There is no quiet hours, the place was a party all night long. All our neighbors had like 4-6 tents per site, cars were everywhere. There was loud music and just yelling and parting. Nothing wrong with having a good time but midnight at a family camp ground with crazy music is a bit much. Car alarms were going off. We’re packed in so tight I couldn’t sleep cuz of the dude at the next camp site snoring. It was just not  peaceful or relaxing experience. I would not be back here again. Possibly the worst night of camping I’ve ever had", "languageCode": "en"}, "rating": 1, "publishTime": "2025-08-16T17:42:01.986625024Z", "originalText": {"text": "Would never camp here again. The bathrooms are fine, they have showers and restrooms and washing up stations. The whole camp ground is dirt/ dirty loose sand. There is no separation between camp sites, no privacy what so ever, no nature, just dirty. There is no quiet hours, the place was a party all night long. All our neighbors had like 4-6 tents per site, cars were everywhere. There was loud music and just yelling and parting. Nothing wrong with having a good time but midnight at a family camp ground with crazy music is a bit much. Car alarms were going off. We’re packed in so tight I couldn’t sleep cuz of the dude at the next camp site snoring. It was just not  peaceful or relaxing experience. I would not be back here again. Possibly the worst night of camping I’ve ever had", "languageCode": "en"}, "googleMapsUri": "https://www.google.com/maps/reviews/data=!4m6!14m5!1m4!2m3!1sCi9DQUlRQUNvZENodHljRjlvT200dGFESnhRM1JPWm1KZlEyRlRWSEJPUmxOeE9XYxAB!2m1!1s0x80ece3d1daa29209:0x6d14a7ae46d3ba9", "flagContentUri": "https://www.google.com/local/content/rap/report?postId=Ci9DQUlRQUNvZENodHljRjlvT200dGFESnhRM1JPWm1KZlEyRlRWSEJPUmxOeE9XYxAB&d=17924085&t=1", "authorAttribution": {"uri": "https://www.google.com/maps/contrib/104413672797595820104/reviews", "photoUri": "https://lh3.googleusercontent.com/a/ACg8ocIX8f5Tip176zuV4l213qZzHXZI1KnbeDnAtMX3zvEgKSYMKQ=s128-c0x00000000-cc-rp-mo-ba5", "displayName": "Leslie Iacono"}, "relativePublishTimeDescription": "5 months ago"}, {"name": "places/ChIJCZKi2tHj7IARqTtt5HpK0QY/reviews/Ci9DQUlRQUNvZENodHljRjlvT2pKdVNuRjBUVzF0YkZoTE1VODBha2xIVUVZelkxRRAB", "text": {"text": "Nice campground ,  FAIRLY flat RV pads ,  nice fire rings, most have masonry BBQ pits,  mostly quiet at night, at least the nights we were there.   Walking distance to the south marina which is more of a sanctuary.    There is a great little restaurant in the harbor.     Dog friendly.   Lots of sooty type dirt around the campground,  but we put a rug out that pretty much kept us from tracking the soil into the RV.    There are very few full hook-up site, but there is a dump station.   Fill your water tanks elsewhere, as there was no portable water available for filling.", "languageCode": "en"}, "rating": 5, "publishTime": "2025-10-27T11:35:51.507350974Z", "originalText": {"text": "Nice campground ,  FAIRLY flat RV pads ,  nice fire rings, most have masonry BBQ pits,  mostly quiet at night, at least the nights we were there.   Walking distance to the south marina which is more of a sanctuary.    There is a great little restaurant in the harbor.     Dog friendly.   Lots of sooty type dirt around the campground,  but we put a rug out that pretty much kept us from tracking the soil into the RV.    There are very few full hook-up site, but there is a dump station.   Fill your water tanks elsewhere, as there was no portable water available for filling.", "languageCode": "en"}, "googleMapsUri": "https://www.google.com/maps/reviews/data=!4m6!14m5!1m4!2m3!1sCi9DQUlRQUNvZENodHljRjlvT2pKdVNuRjBUVzF0YkZoTE1VODBha2xIVUVZelkxRRAB!2m1!1s0x80ece3d1daa29209:0x6d14a7ae46d3ba9", "flagContentUri": "https://www.google.com/local/content/rap/report?postId=Ci9DQUlRQUNvZENodHljRjlvT2pKdVNuRjBUVzF0YkZoTE1VODBha2xIVUVZelkxRRAB&d=17924085&t=1", "authorAttribution": {"uri": "https://www.google.com/maps/contrib/115349222778200569967/reviews", "photoUri": "https://lh3.googleusercontent.com/a/ACg8ocJze3f504NNk1nx7tg-oh6ERbxF5m45fanPS7o7BhfQeCn_GA=s128-c0x00000000-cc-rp-mo-ba5", "displayName": "Hal Walker"}, "relativePublishTimeDescription": "3 months ago"}, {"name": "places/ChIJCZKi2tHj7IARqTtt5HpK0QY/reviews/Ci9DQUlRQUNvZENodHljRjlvT2xOa2MwSnFRMGRqYmswemRWODNSSE4wU1dNMU4wRRAB", "text": {"text": "We were visiting Morro Bay for several days before Thanksgiving and hiked up to Black Hills lookout from the lower trailhead.  We went through Morro Bay State Park Campground which was spacious.", "languageCode": "en"}, "rating": 3, "publishTime": "2025-12-23T06:40:45.569442428Z", "originalText": {"text": "We were visiting Morro Bay for several days before Thanksgiving and hiked up to Black Hills lookout from the lower trailhead.  We went through Morro Bay State Park Campground which was spacious.", "languageCode": "en"}, "googleMapsUri": "https://www.google.com/maps/reviews/data=!4m6!14m5!1m4!2m3!1sCi9DQUlRQUNvZENodHljRjlvT2xOa2MwSnFRMGRqYmswemRWODNSSE4wU1dNMU4wRRAB!2m1!1s0x80ece3d1daa29209:0x6d14a7ae46d3ba9", "flagContentUri": "https://www.google.com/local/content/rap/report?postId=Ci9DQUlRQUNvZENodHljRjlvT2xOa2MwSnFRMGRqYmswemRWODNSSE4wU1dNMU4wRRAB&d=17924085&t=1", "authorAttribution": {"uri": "https://www.google.com/maps/contrib/103112219754407036497/reviews", "photoUri": "https://lh3.googleusercontent.com/a-/ALV-UjWYH-I4RvrfRUXl77LorTgEYOQ9Iu5u4MQ2EyTsBvUTqYmBsYb3iA=s128-c0x00000000-cc-rp-mo-ba7", "displayName": "Catherine Hunt"}, "relativePublishTimeDescription": "a month ago"}, {"name": "places/ChIJCZKi2tHj7IARqTtt5HpK0QY/reviews/Ci9DQUlRQUNvZENodHljRjlvT2pkME9WOU5YMUo2Y0haaE1FWk1aVTlaV0Y5S1dWRRAB", "text": {"text": "This is a very popular campground. The campsites are nice. And there's good access to the beach and harbor.\\n\\nThe restrooms are clean and have showers as well.", "languageCode": "en"}, "rating": 4, "publishTime": "2025-10-15T01:01:29.169364839Z", "originalText": {"text": "This is a very popular campground. The campsites are nice. And there's good access to the beach and harbor.\\n\\nThe restrooms are clean and have showers as well.", "languageCode": "en"}, "googleMapsUri": "https://www.google.com/maps/reviews/data=!4m6!14m5!1m4!2m3!1sCi9DQUlRQUNvZENodHljRjlvT2pkME9WOU5YMUo2Y0haaE1FWk1aVTlaV0Y5S1dWRRAB!2m1!1s0x80ece3d1daa29209:0x6d14a7ae46d3ba9", "flagContentUri": "https://www.google.com/local/content/rap/report?postId=Ci9DQUlRQUNvZENodHljRjlvT2pkME9WOU5YMUo2Y0haaE1FWk1aVTlaV0Y5S1dWRRAB&d=17924085&t=1", "authorAttribution": {"uri": "https://www.google.com/maps/contrib/116052163994442728657/reviews", "photoUri": "https://lh3.googleusercontent.com/a-/ALV-UjUYWSqbFibjR8SgFBMqdEMfczHcDNhwDJNcXGO6T4i_buL3e0gU=s128-c0x00000000-cc-rp-mo-ba5", "displayName": "Tino Plank"}, "relativePublishTimeDescription": "3 months ago"}]	Morro Bay State Park Campground offers an excellent location with walking access to the beach, harbor, and marina, making it very popular among visitors. However, the campground suffers from significant privacy issues with cramped sites that feel like a 'grassy parking lot,' and experiences can vary dramatically depending on neighboring campers. While some visitors enjoy peaceful nights, others report loud partying that makes it unsuitable for families seeking a relaxing camping experience.	{"summary": "Morro Bay State Park Campground offers an excellent location with walking access to the beach, harbor, and marina, making it very popular among visitors. However, the campground suffers from significant privacy issues with cramped sites that feel like a 'grassy parking lot,' and experiences can vary dramatically depending on neighboring campers. While some visitors enjoy peaceful nights, others report loud partying that makes it unsuitable for families seeking a relaxing camping experience.", "negative": [{"text": "There is no quiet hours, the place was a party all night long. Nothing wrong with having a good time but midnight at a family camp ground with crazy music is a bit much.", "author": "Leslie Iacono", "rating": 1}, {"text": "The campsites are tiny and offer little to no privacy. Camping in what essentially amounts to a grassy parking lot prevents this campground from earning a five-star rating.", "author": "Wayne Clark", "rating": 4}], "positive": [{"text": "There is a great little restaurant in the harbor. Dog friendly.", "author": "Hal Walker", "rating": 5}, {"text": "There's good access to the beach and harbor. The restrooms are clean and have showers as well.", "author": "Tino Plank", "rating": 4}], "last_updated": "2026-02-06T02:14:42.060Z"}	2026-02-06 02:14:35.335+00	state_park	\N	\N
54c6a16e-8380-4fa1-9c62-69fe522774f4	b201a860-05a3-4ddc-bb89-4c4271177271	Ventura Beach RV Resort	Ventura Beach RV Resort sits right on the Ventura Promenade, steps from the beach and a short walk to the Channel Islands National Park visitor center and harbor. Full hookups, paved sites, and a pool make this a comfortable base for exploring both the Channel Islands and the Ventura coast. While it's an RV park rather than a nature campground, the location is unbeatable for families staging a Channel Islands trip. Downtown Ventura's restaurants and shops are walkable.	The only full-hookup RV resort within walking distance of both the Channel Islands visitor center and the Island Packers ferry terminal—your perfect base camp for exploring America's least-visited national park.	other	\N	800 W Main St, Ventura, CA 93001, USA	Ventura	CA	34.2817432	-119.3120535	ChIJNXrGIYms6YAR4UlHsyJ4yKg	3.5	959	\N	{"hookups": "full", "cell_coverage": "excellent", "road_accessibility": "Easy urban access, flat paved roads. No issues for 5th wheels.", "max_trailer_length_ft": 40, "fifth_wheel_accessible": true}	t	\N	Book directly through resort website. Weekend rates higher. Can often get midweek availability. Book Island Packers boats well in advance for Channel Islands day trips.	85.00	USD	\N	{"best": ["march", "april", "may", "june", "september", "october"], "avoid": [], "notes": "Year-round destination. Spring and fall are ideal for Channel Islands trips with calmer seas. Summer has best weather but boats book up fast. Whale watching peaks January-April."}	1.5 hours	\N	{"scenic_beauty": 3, "solitude_level": 1, "adventure_level": 4, "family_friendly": 4, "relaxation_factor": 3}	{"topics": ["island ecology", "marine biology", "Chumash maritime culture", "endemic species", "ocean conservation"], "visitor_center": true, "ranger_programs": true, "junior_ranger_program": true}	{"parker": {"notes": "The Channel Islands adventure will be a highlight—Parker will love the boat ride and island exploration.", "suitable": true, "activities": ["Channel Islands boat trip and island hiking", "Kayaking sea caves", "Bike riding along Ventura Promenade", "Ventura Pier fishing"], "engagement_level": 5}, "xander": {"notes": "The Channel Islands boat trip is long for Xander (1 hour each way). He'd do better with beach and harbor activities. Consider splitting the group.", "suitable": true, "activities": ["Beach sand play", "Watching boats at harbor", "Pool at RV resort", "Ventura Pier walk"], "engagement_level": 3}, "charlotte": {"notes": "The visitor center has excellent hands-on exhibits. Charlotte will love the island wildlife—island foxes, sea lions, and tide pools.", "suitable": true, "activities": ["Channel Islands tide pools and wildlife", "Channel Islands visitor center exhibits", "Shell collecting on Ventura Beach", "Whale watching boat trip"], "engagement_level": 4}}	http://www.vbrvresort.com/	(805) 643-9137	\N	researching	0	{channel-islands,full-hookups,urban,ferry-access,whale-watching,kayaking}	{"Walking distance to Channel Islands NP visitor center and Island Packers ferry","Full hookups with pool—comfortable base camp","Walkable to downtown Ventura restaurants and shops","Ventura Promenade bike path right outside"}	{"Urban RV park feel—not a nature campground","Expensive compared to state park camping","Highway noise from nearby US-101"}	\N	\N	2026-02-04 15:15:17.477+00	2026-02-06 02:15:50.989801+00	[{"name": "places/ChIJNXrGIYms6YAR4UlHsyJ4yKg/reviews/Ci9DQUlRQUNvZENodHljRjlvT2tsWUxVSmhPRU0yTmtsV2JuTXpZV2N4YTJkbWExRRAB", "text": {"text": "What a great RV park location- you can ride your bike from the RV park to the beach without ever being in the road.  And then ride  on the boardwalk, past the pier and the beach and through a city park and back.  Watching surfers run barefoot with their boards from their cars on Main Street to the surf was a favorite of mine.  And Cody, told me to check out the end of Main Street where u can walk to and that was such a long blocked off area of the historic district protected from cars, and patrolled; an area to feel safe, shop, walk, bike, and eat and drink, and then walk back to the park.  Ventura is simply an awesome historic town.  I met a woman there named Martha who owns Ecugreen and now I have a new friend for life. She greets you for the first time as if she knew you for a lifetime. Great store with Ecuadorian goods and such a lovely person she is.\\nThe park is so pretty and I love the long wide roads and the many beautiful trees.\\nGreat stay- Great staff.  We always say RV parks are only as good as the people at the front desk.  Of course we had a couple of issues like anywhere else but the difference is, it is run by a man named Kylie, and he could not have been more accommodating, respectful, and just a nice person.   We would definitely stop in there again when on the west coast.\\nSpecial thanks to Kylie, Adrianna, Cody, Beverly, Sam, Tilia, Christine, Megan, Ventura, Juda, Ceaser, Rob, and I apologize, but I can’t recall the women’s name in admin who passed me off to Kylie, after she validated our minor complaint about our neighbor.  Spike (?) working the security was a great guy too.  So if you ever want to park and party, or park and relax on weekdays, this is a wonderful place to do so!", "languageCode": "en"}, "rating": 4, "publishTime": "2026-01-18T02:53:39.688638169Z", "originalText": {"text": "What a great RV park location- you can ride your bike from the RV park to the beach without ever being in the road.  And then ride  on the boardwalk, past the pier and the beach and through a city park and back.  Watching surfers run barefoot with their boards from their cars on Main Street to the surf was a favorite of mine.  And Cody, told me to check out the end of Main Street where u can walk to and that was such a long blocked off area of the historic district protected from cars, and patrolled; an area to feel safe, shop, walk, bike, and eat and drink, and then walk back to the park.  Ventura is simply an awesome historic town.  I met a woman there named Martha who owns Ecugreen and now I have a new friend for life. She greets you for the first time as if she knew you for a lifetime. Great store with Ecuadorian goods and such a lovely person she is.\\nThe park is so pretty and I love the long wide roads and the many beautiful trees.\\nGreat stay- Great staff.  We always say RV parks are only as good as the people at the front desk.  Of course we had a couple of issues like anywhere else but the difference is, it is run by a man named Kylie, and he could not have been more accommodating, respectful, and just a nice person.   We would definitely stop in there again when on the west coast.\\nSpecial thanks to Kylie, Adrianna, Cody, Beverly, Sam, Tilia, Christine, Megan, Ventura, Juda, Ceaser, Rob, and I apologize, but I can’t recall the women’s name in admin who passed me off to Kylie, after she validated our minor complaint about our neighbor.  Spike (?) working the security was a great guy too.  So if you ever want to park and party, or park and relax on weekdays, this is a wonderful place to do so!", "languageCode": "en"}, "googleMapsUri": "https://www.google.com/maps/reviews/data=!4m6!14m5!1m4!2m3!1sCi9DQUlRQUNvZENodHljRjlvT2tsWUxVSmhPRU0yTmtsV2JuTXpZV2N4YTJkbWExRRAB!2m1!1s0x80e9ac8921c67a35:0xa8c87822b34749e1", "flagContentUri": "https://www.google.com/local/content/rap/report?postId=Ci9DQUlRQUNvZENodHljRjlvT2tsWUxVSmhPRU0yTmtsV2JuTXpZV2N4YTJkbWExRRAB&d=17924085&t=1", "authorAttribution": {"uri": "https://www.google.com/maps/contrib/105833683900401845133/reviews", "photoUri": "https://lh3.googleusercontent.com/a/ACg8ocI-DbF9-DTomqdLig4oBm9kBHgNefo71GlSvxtjs0dKk5pT_Q=s128-c0x00000000-cc-rp-mo", "displayName": "Pamela Berg"}, "relativePublishTimeDescription": "2 weeks ago"}, {"name": "places/ChIJNXrGIYms6YAR4UlHsyJ4yKg/reviews/Ci9DQUlRQUNvZENodHljRjlvT25sd1FUaERjWEZCUjJKWmMxTkRPSHBOTlRBMVEwRRAB", "text": {"text": "It is a beautiful RV Park and very well maintained.  Amazing concrete pads, good size and nice healthy grass at each site. We knew going in that there would be a pretty good amount of road noise and we were not wrong. What we did not know is if you happen to book on a holiday weekend (we spent 3 nights during Veterans Day weekend)or literally anytime a group books multiple sites, they pretty much have carte blanche to make as much noise as they want.  That includes playing music at concert levels until 1:00 AM and shouting F bombs at each other. We like a good time as much as anybody, but common decency and courtesy calls for taking the noise level down at say 10:00.  Not so here, we asked if there is a quiet time and were told sort of but if a group wants to party we kind of just let them.   We were two sites away from the main party location and believe me sleep was not an option, and the policies of the park are no refunds for any reason. I can say with certainty that we won't be booking here again.  Two stars for the beautiful amenities and no more for the lack of sleep. Ventura is a really great town even when you are forced into zombie mode when trying to enjoy it.\\nSo, with all that said book at your own tolerance levels.", "languageCode": "en"}, "rating": 2, "publishTime": "2025-11-13T22:04:10.311458973Z", "originalText": {"text": "It is a beautiful RV Park and very well maintained.  Amazing concrete pads, good size and nice healthy grass at each site. We knew going in that there would be a pretty good amount of road noise and we were not wrong. What we did not know is if you happen to book on a holiday weekend (we spent 3 nights during Veterans Day weekend)or literally anytime a group books multiple sites, they pretty much have carte blanche to make as much noise as they want.  That includes playing music at concert levels until 1:00 AM and shouting F bombs at each other. We like a good time as much as anybody, but common decency and courtesy calls for taking the noise level down at say 10:00.  Not so here, we asked if there is a quiet time and were told sort of but if a group wants to party we kind of just let them.   We were two sites away from the main party location and believe me sleep was not an option, and the policies of the park are no refunds for any reason. I can say with certainty that we won't be booking here again.  Two stars for the beautiful amenities and no more for the lack of sleep. Ventura is a really great town even when you are forced into zombie mode when trying to enjoy it.\\nSo, with all that said book at your own tolerance levels.", "languageCode": "en"}, "googleMapsUri": "https://www.google.com/maps/reviews/data=!4m6!14m5!1m4!2m3!1sCi9DQUlRQUNvZENodHljRjlvT25sd1FUaERjWEZCUjJKWmMxTkRPSHBOTlRBMVEwRRAB!2m1!1s0x80e9ac8921c67a35:0xa8c87822b34749e1", "flagContentUri": "https://www.google.com/local/content/rap/report?postId=Ci9DQUlRQUNvZENodHljRjlvT25sd1FUaERjWEZCUjJKWmMxTkRPSHBOTlRBMVEwRRAB&d=17924085&t=1", "authorAttribution": {"uri": "https://www.google.com/maps/contrib/112141665682959244786/reviews", "photoUri": "https://lh3.googleusercontent.com/a/ACg8ocIk80f76x_zN_sD5-hETEjRSxbu60q84SkNx3Qh8js8O82e=s128-c0x00000000-cc-rp-mo", "displayName": "Ken Adams"}, "relativePublishTimeDescription": "2 months ago"}, {"name": "places/ChIJNXrGIYms6YAR4UlHsyJ4yKg/reviews/Ci9DQUlRQUNvZENodHljRjlvT25wbVFsVkNiRmhKUWs5MmRHcENRV3BwYTNWd00xRRAB", "text": {"text": "This place feels like a small community in the best way. Good neighbors, very welcoming atmosphere, and staff that is always positive and helpful. The mountain views are beautiful, the trees smell amazing, and the palms make it feel like a true California getaway.\\nVentura Beach RV Resort has propane refill station.You can get everything you need in store.\\nOnly 5 minutes to the ocean and walking distance to grocery stores and restaurants. Highly recommended.", "languageCode": "en"}, "rating": 5, "publishTime": "2026-01-07T00:46:07.152534891Z", "originalText": {"text": "This place feels like a small community in the best way. Good neighbors, very welcoming atmosphere, and staff that is always positive and helpful. The mountain views are beautiful, the trees smell amazing, and the palms make it feel like a true California getaway.\\nVentura Beach RV Resort has propane refill station.You can get everything you need in store.\\nOnly 5 minutes to the ocean and walking distance to grocery stores and restaurants. Highly recommended.", "languageCode": "en"}, "googleMapsUri": "https://www.google.com/maps/reviews/data=!4m6!14m5!1m4!2m3!1sCi9DQUlRQUNvZENodHljRjlvT25wbVFsVkNiRmhKUWs5MmRHcENRV3BwYTNWd00xRRAB!2m1!1s0x80e9ac8921c67a35:0xa8c87822b34749e1", "flagContentUri": "https://www.google.com/local/content/rap/report?postId=Ci9DQUlRQUNvZENodHljRjlvT25wbVFsVkNiRmhKUWs5MmRHcENRV3BwYTNWd00xRRAB&d=17924085&t=1", "authorAttribution": {"uri": "https://www.google.com/maps/contrib/104861532304020350058/reviews", "photoUri": "https://lh3.googleusercontent.com/a-/ALV-UjUMZaxPzltYRn1Nl2A28MMk656UnTto0VO4WF_s0_WPNLp_qo5F=s128-c0x00000000-cc-rp-mo", "displayName": "Dmytro Afanasiv"}, "relativePublishTimeDescription": "a month ago"}, {"name": "places/ChIJNXrGIYms6YAR4UlHsyJ4yKg/reviews/Ci9DQUlRQUNvZENodHljRjlvT21ac2NYcG1Ta1JCUW1zeVJrWXhlVGs0UzIxek0xRRAB", "text": {"text": "First-time customer traveling in a 45-ft Class A.\\n\\nI would not recommend this park for larger Class A coaches (40 ft+) unless you don’t mind scratches. Trees are not trimmed up, and when combined with cars parked on the roads, you’ll often end up hugging one side and scraping branches down your rig.\\n\\nThe park is also extremely strict, with rules that seem more about making money than hospitality. Even family members stopping by for a few minutes have to check in and pay for a pass. I understand the need for check-in, but charging for a quick visit or drop-off feels excessive. If you have friends or relatives in the area who might want to swing by, this is not the place to stay.\\n\\nFor the price, the restrictions are disappointing. On top of that, the freeway noise is constant, so it’s not exactly a peaceful stay.\\n\\nThat said, there are positives:\\n•\\tThe landscaping is beautiful.\\n•\\tThe park is very clean.\\n•\\tConcrete parking pads are a nice touch.\\n•\\tExtra water hookups at the site are convenient.\\n\\nOverall, while it’s a clean and well-kept park with nice features, the strict rules, freeway noise, and lack of attention to tree trimming make it a poor choice for big rigs.", "languageCode": "en"}, "rating": 1, "publishTime": "2025-09-22T02:17:46.624321517Z", "originalText": {"text": "First-time customer traveling in a 45-ft Class A.\\n\\nI would not recommend this park for larger Class A coaches (40 ft+) unless you don’t mind scratches. Trees are not trimmed up, and when combined with cars parked on the roads, you’ll often end up hugging one side and scraping branches down your rig.\\n\\nThe park is also extremely strict, with rules that seem more about making money than hospitality. Even family members stopping by for a few minutes have to check in and pay for a pass. I understand the need for check-in, but charging for a quick visit or drop-off feels excessive. If you have friends or relatives in the area who might want to swing by, this is not the place to stay.\\n\\nFor the price, the restrictions are disappointing. On top of that, the freeway noise is constant, so it’s not exactly a peaceful stay.\\n\\nThat said, there are positives:\\n•\\tThe landscaping is beautiful.\\n•\\tThe park is very clean.\\n•\\tConcrete parking pads are a nice touch.\\n•\\tExtra water hookups at the site are convenient.\\n\\nOverall, while it’s a clean and well-kept park with nice features, the strict rules, freeway noise, and lack of attention to tree trimming make it a poor choice for big rigs.", "languageCode": "en"}, "googleMapsUri": "https://www.google.com/maps/reviews/data=!4m6!14m5!1m4!2m3!1sCi9DQUlRQUNvZENodHljRjlvT21ac2NYcG1Ta1JCUW1zeVJrWXhlVGs0UzIxek0xRRAB!2m1!1s0x80e9ac8921c67a35:0xa8c87822b34749e1", "flagContentUri": "https://www.google.com/local/content/rap/report?postId=Ci9DQUlRQUNvZENodHljRjlvT21ac2NYcG1Ta1JCUW1zeVJrWXhlVGs0UzIxek0xRRAB&d=17924085&t=1", "authorAttribution": {"uri": "https://www.google.com/maps/contrib/104452685888485064504/reviews", "photoUri": "https://lh3.googleusercontent.com/a/ACg8ocIxUoMAXXsWNe3gB_aFZe_F9yEhNFWjUva56qUJzhDrEiJWYA=s128-c0x00000000-cc-rp-mo-ba2", "displayName": "Ed T"}, "relativePublishTimeDescription": "4 months ago"}, {"name": "places/ChIJNXrGIYms6YAR4UlHsyJ4yKg/reviews/Ci9DQUlRQUNvZENodHljRjlvT2pjMFRsYzBUbTVFYTBkbVRVVjNUVzlrU1hWTmFIYxAB", "text": {"text": "Ventura Beach RV Resort has become one of my absolute favorite places to stay. As the owner of Seaward Brewing, I’m constantly looking for spaces that inspire creativity, offer comfort, and allow me to recharge — and this resort delivers every single time.\\n\\nFrom the moment you arrive, you can feel how much pride the team takes in keeping the property clean, welcoming, and truly guest-focused. The sites are well-maintained, the amenities are convenient, and the location is unbeatable — peaceful, beautiful, and just steps from everything Ventura has to offer.\\n\\nWhat I value most is the genuine hospitality. Every stay feels personal. The staff always goes above and beyond to make sure we’re comfortable and enjoying our time. As someone who runs a business built on community, I really appreciate that same energy here.\\n\\nIf you’re looking for a relaxing getaway, a place to unwind between workweeks, or just a well-run resort that treats you like family — Ventura Beach RV Resort is the spot. Highly recommended.”\\n\\n— Monique, Seaward Brewing", "languageCode": "en"}, "rating": 5, "publishTime": "2025-11-19T00:03:34.172542105Z", "originalText": {"text": "Ventura Beach RV Resort has become one of my absolute favorite places to stay. As the owner of Seaward Brewing, I’m constantly looking for spaces that inspire creativity, offer comfort, and allow me to recharge — and this resort delivers every single time.\\n\\nFrom the moment you arrive, you can feel how much pride the team takes in keeping the property clean, welcoming, and truly guest-focused. The sites are well-maintained, the amenities are convenient, and the location is unbeatable — peaceful, beautiful, and just steps from everything Ventura has to offer.\\n\\nWhat I value most is the genuine hospitality. Every stay feels personal. The staff always goes above and beyond to make sure we’re comfortable and enjoying our time. As someone who runs a business built on community, I really appreciate that same energy here.\\n\\nIf you’re looking for a relaxing getaway, a place to unwind between workweeks, or just a well-run resort that treats you like family — Ventura Beach RV Resort is the spot. Highly recommended.”\\n\\n— Monique, Seaward Brewing", "languageCode": "en"}, "googleMapsUri": "https://www.google.com/maps/reviews/data=!4m6!14m5!1m4!2m3!1sCi9DQUlRQUNvZENodHljRjlvT2pjMFRsYzBUbTVFYTBkbVRVVjNUVzlrU1hWTmFIYxAB!2m1!1s0x80e9ac8921c67a35:0xa8c87822b34749e1", "flagContentUri": "https://www.google.com/local/content/rap/report?postId=Ci9DQUlRQUNvZENodHljRjlvT2pjMFRsYzBUbTVFYTBkbVRVVjNUVzlrU1hWTmFIYxAB&d=17924085&t=1", "authorAttribution": {"uri": "https://www.google.com/maps/contrib/115160851250940158722/reviews", "photoUri": "https://lh3.googleusercontent.com/a/ACg8ocKfEwAE5LjD9z6YOQLwxyWC8ir_WADDWdYE807wNk3dEUe3KA=s128-c0x00000000-cc-rp-mo", "displayName": "Monique Magdaleno"}, "relativePublishTimeDescription": "2 months ago"}]	Ventura Beach RV Resort is a beautifully maintained park with excellent amenities and location just minutes from the beach, but it has significant issues with noise from both freeway traffic and late-night partying groups. While the staff is praised for being welcoming and helpful, the park's inconsistent noise policies and strict rules may not make it ideal for families seeking a peaceful getaway.	{"summary": "Ventura Beach RV Resort is a beautifully maintained park with excellent amenities and location just minutes from the beach, but it has significant issues with noise from both freeway traffic and late-night partying groups. While the staff is praised for being welcoming and helpful, the park's inconsistent noise policies and strict rules may not make it ideal for families seeking a peaceful getaway.", "negative": [{"text": "If you happen to book on a holiday weekend or literally anytime a group books multiple sites, they pretty much have carte blanche to make as much noise as they want. That includes playing music at concert levels until 1:00 AM and shouting F bombs at each other.", "author": "Ken Adams", "rating": 2}, {"text": "The freeway noise is constant, so it's not exactly a peaceful stay.", "author": "Ed T", "rating": 1}], "positive": [{"text": "You can ride your bike from the RV park to the beach without ever being in the road. And then ride on the boardwalk, past the pier and the beach and through a city park and back.", "author": "Pamela Berg", "rating": 4}, {"text": "This place feels like a small community in the best way. Good neighbors, very welcoming atmosphere, and staff that is always positive and helpful.", "author": "Dmytro Afanasiv", "rating": 5}, {"text": "Only 5 minutes to the ocean and walking distance to grocery stores and restaurants.", "author": "Dmytro Afanasiv", "rating": 5}], "last_updated": "2026-02-06T02:15:50.853Z"}	2026-02-06 02:15:43.046+00	private_rv_park	\N	\N
e4500982-a9cb-4239-987b-17ddead1b516	b201a860-05a3-4ddc-bb89-4c4271177271	Joshua Tree via Sky Valley Resort	Sky Valley Resort offers 13 hot spring pools ranging from 90°F to 104°F, with sulfur-free mineral water pumped from deep aquifers. Unlike age-restricted Desert Hot Springs resorts, this one explicitly welcomes multigenerational families. Your 5th wheel fits easily in full-hookup sites, and Joshua Tree National Park sits 45 minutes away for morning adventures before afternoon pool time.	Soak in natural mineral hot springs after scrambling on otherworldly boulder piles—the only family-friendly hot springs resort near Joshua Tree that welcomes all ages.	hot_springs	\N	74711 Dillon Rd, Desert Hot Springs, CA 92241, USA	Desert Hot Springs	CA	33.9018402	-116.3621558	ChIJpeiQMWPh2oAR_6XAOf6VBsg	4.4	620	\N	{"hookups": "full", "cell_coverage": "good"}	t	\N	\N	\N	USD	\N	{"best": ["october", "november", "december", "january", "february", "march", "april"], "avoid": ["june", "july", "august"], "notes": "Summer exceeds 110°F"}	2 hours	\N	{"scenic_beauty": 4, "solitude_level": 3, "adventure_level": 4, "family_friendly": 5, "relaxation_factor": 5}	\N	{"parker": {"suitable": true, "activities": ["Boulder climbing at Joshua Tree", "Skull Rock exploration"], "engagement_level": 5}, "xander": {"suitable": true, "activities": ["Cholla Cactus Garden boardwalk", "Hot spring pools"], "engagement_level": 4}, "charlotte": {"suitable": true, "activities": ["Skull Rock treasure hunt", "Hidden Valley rock playground"], "engagement_level": 4}}	https://www.skyvalleyresort.com/	(760) 329-2900	\N	researching	0	{hot-springs,family-friendly,joshua-tree}	{}	{}	\N	\N	2026-02-02 15:20:30.465+00	2026-02-06 04:10:02.865672+00	[{"name": "places/ChIJpeiQMWPh2oAR_6XAOf6VBsg/reviews/Ci9DQUlRQUNvZENodHljRjlvT25aVlJWVmZlRXM1UWxCWFlXZHFhVXhLYXpaM2RuYxAB", "text": {"text": "Sky Valley is an absolutely incredible resort. We stayed at the resort in our fifth-wheel and our RV space was clean and quiet. The resort is pristine, has exceptional amenities, and the employees are very helpful and friendly. My only issue during our stay was with the nearly nonexistent WiFi service.", "languageCode": "en"}, "rating": 5, "publishTime": "2025-10-15T04:28:29.762144694Z", "originalText": {"text": "Sky Valley is an absolutely incredible resort. We stayed at the resort in our fifth-wheel and our RV space was clean and quiet. The resort is pristine, has exceptional amenities, and the employees are very helpful and friendly. My only issue during our stay was with the nearly nonexistent WiFi service.", "languageCode": "en"}, "googleMapsUri": "https://www.google.com/maps/reviews/data=!4m6!14m5!1m4!2m3!1sCi9DQUlRQUNvZENodHljRjlvT25aVlJWVmZlRXM1UWxCWFlXZHFhVXhLYXpaM2RuYxAB!2m1!1s0x80dae1633190e8a5:0xc80695fe39c0a5ff", "flagContentUri": "https://www.google.com/local/content/rap/report?postId=Ci9DQUlRQUNvZENodHljRjlvT25aVlJWVmZlRXM1UWxCWFlXZHFhVXhLYXpaM2RuYxAB&d=17924085&t=1", "authorAttribution": {"uri": "https://www.google.com/maps/contrib/102933466156757360835/reviews", "photoUri": "https://lh3.googleusercontent.com/a-/ALV-UjXkqULgTRpy41NxgdfzEZERoDbtoR8vPgC9bOmdRzWipnBMwgDT=s128-c0x00000000-cc-rp-mo", "displayName": "Rosie Diaz"}, "relativePublishTimeDescription": "3 months ago"}, {"name": "places/ChIJpeiQMWPh2oAR_6XAOf6VBsg/reviews/Ci9DQUlRQUNvZENodHljRjlvT2xSbldWQktRMU5xV214Q05UUlRjVEF5U21aZmRFRRAB", "text": {"text": "Very nice resort, quiet, friendly located in the Palm Springs area.  Magnificant natural mineral hot springs on site which is the ultimate in relaxing.", "languageCode": "en"}, "rating": 5, "publishTime": "2026-01-18T14:49:25.095339882Z", "originalText": {"text": "Very nice resort, quiet, friendly located in the Palm Springs area.  Magnificant natural mineral hot springs on site which is the ultimate in relaxing.", "languageCode": "en"}, "googleMapsUri": "https://www.google.com/maps/reviews/data=!4m6!14m5!1m4!2m3!1sCi9DQUlRQUNvZENodHljRjlvT2xSbldWQktRMU5xV214Q05UUlRjVEF5U21aZmRFRRAB!2m1!1s0x80dae1633190e8a5:0xc80695fe39c0a5ff", "flagContentUri": "https://www.google.com/local/content/rap/report?postId=Ci9DQUlRQUNvZENodHljRjlvT2xSbldWQktRMU5xV214Q05UUlRjVEF5U21aZmRFRRAB&d=17924085&t=1", "authorAttribution": {"uri": "https://www.google.com/maps/contrib/101133663825148278819/reviews", "photoUri": "https://lh3.googleusercontent.com/a/ACg8ocLBh-Morzhm_xMjZXJZvUWeIgu7_ZaGlC5dGItIUclBXGJE5Q=s128-c0x00000000-cc-rp-mo", "displayName": "Robert Castonguay"}, "relativePublishTimeDescription": "2 weeks ago"}, {"name": "places/ChIJpeiQMWPh2oAR_6XAOf6VBsg/reviews/Ci9DQUlRQUNvZENodHljRjlvT2xKUldFUk9SakpPYWpaMlRGb3dOVlEwZEdzNVJsRRAB", "text": {"text": "To visit as a vacation spot or a vacay home, this place is a hit with lots of clean pools and gorgeous landscaping! As a year round - I enjoy it. Purchasing year round comes with pros and cons; high loan rate, hidden fees are few (ranger fee 15 a month, mail fee of 12.50 a month, it's 25 to buy the gate sticker for your car), Electric, water, Internet, cable are less than 100 a month, you can be without utilities for days, not updated on utility emergencies, great security, cafe/store that's closed during summer, Maintenance happens all day every day here and without warning, very quiet, stargazing, lovely residents/employees. So it's like any small community.\\n\\nCome visit, check it out, and see for yourself 😊", "languageCode": "en"}, "rating": 4, "publishTime": "2025-09-19T20:09:06.493327679Z", "originalText": {"text": "To visit as a vacation spot or a vacay home, this place is a hit with lots of clean pools and gorgeous landscaping! As a year round - I enjoy it. Purchasing year round comes with pros and cons; high loan rate, hidden fees are few (ranger fee 15 a month, mail fee of 12.50 a month, it's 25 to buy the gate sticker for your car), Electric, water, Internet, cable are less than 100 a month, you can be without utilities for days, not updated on utility emergencies, great security, cafe/store that's closed during summer, Maintenance happens all day every day here and without warning, very quiet, stargazing, lovely residents/employees. So it's like any small community.\\n\\nCome visit, check it out, and see for yourself 😊", "languageCode": "en"}, "googleMapsUri": "https://www.google.com/maps/reviews/data=!4m6!14m5!1m4!2m3!1sCi9DQUlRQUNvZENodHljRjlvT2xKUldFUk9SakpPYWpaMlRGb3dOVlEwZEdzNVJsRRAB!2m1!1s0x80dae1633190e8a5:0xc80695fe39c0a5ff", "flagContentUri": "https://www.google.com/local/content/rap/report?postId=Ci9DQUlRQUNvZENodHljRjlvT2xKUldFUk9SakpPYWpaMlRGb3dOVlEwZEdzNVJsRRAB&d=17924085&t=1", "authorAttribution": {"uri": "https://www.google.com/maps/contrib/100453646725181757696/reviews", "photoUri": "https://lh3.googleusercontent.com/a/ACg8ocIoNeG_SHYgQXsPBPUE4_I0dDB0uyUNpVJY56D3GQTx0OBWyQ=s128-c0x00000000-cc-rp-mo", "displayName": "F McNamee"}, "relativePublishTimeDescription": "4 months ago"}, {"name": "places/ChIJpeiQMWPh2oAR_6XAOf6VBsg/reviews/Ci9DQUlRQUNvZENodHljRjlvT21STlIyRTVWVnBWVTJWSVVWQnlhMUYyVTBGUlFsRRAB", "text": {"text": "ALERT on Sky Valley home rental. I called to reserve rent a home in 2025 for two months in 2026. Then about 10 days a go I started calling reservations to inquire about their cancellation policy (our dog is sick). No one called me back after leaving three voicemails. Then I pushed a button for RV rentals hoping to get some and Geremie answered the phone. I told him the situation and he said I'll put it on our chat group and everyone including the manager will see it. Before I could hang up with him Ashley from home rentals was calling me to tell me the cancellation policy. I was within days of them keeping my whole months first rent (almost 3k)! Unacceptable no call back and it makes one wonder if they get commission on rentals and the reason Ashley didn't call me back was she didn't want to lose the reservation.....", "languageCode": "en"}, "rating": 1, "publishTime": "2025-11-25T22:05:34.463786178Z", "originalText": {"text": "ALERT on Sky Valley home rental. I called to reserve rent a home in 2025 for two months in 2026. Then about 10 days a go I started calling reservations to inquire about their cancellation policy (our dog is sick). No one called me back after leaving three voicemails. Then I pushed a button for RV rentals hoping to get some and Geremie answered the phone. I told him the situation and he said I'll put it on our chat group and everyone including the manager will see it. Before I could hang up with him Ashley from home rentals was calling me to tell me the cancellation policy. I was within days of them keeping my whole months first rent (almost 3k)! Unacceptable no call back and it makes one wonder if they get commission on rentals and the reason Ashley didn't call me back was she didn't want to lose the reservation.....", "languageCode": "en"}, "googleMapsUri": "https://www.google.com/maps/reviews/data=!4m6!14m5!1m4!2m3!1sCi9DQUlRQUNvZENodHljRjlvT21STlIyRTVWVnBWVTJWSVVWQnlhMUYyVTBGUlFsRRAB!2m1!1s0x80dae1633190e8a5:0xc80695fe39c0a5ff", "flagContentUri": "https://www.google.com/local/content/rap/report?postId=Ci9DQUlRQUNvZENodHljRjlvT21STlIyRTVWVnBWVTJWSVVWQnlhMUYyVTBGUlFsRRAB&d=17924085&t=1", "authorAttribution": {"uri": "https://www.google.com/maps/contrib/103797892447248832074/reviews", "photoUri": "https://lh3.googleusercontent.com/a-/ALV-UjXVFr-9QFnN33BXg8ZQLDT8bhlqXdF2TTu_TGa-o5DNP4UU00w=s128-c0x00000000-cc-rp-mo-ba2", "displayName": "Jacqueline Marcell"}, "relativePublishTimeDescription": "2 months ago"}, {"name": "places/ChIJpeiQMWPh2oAR_6XAOf6VBsg/reviews/ChZDSUhNMG9nS0VQV2FxY25xdmNpcmJnEAE", "text": {"text": "I had the best stay at Sky Valley Resort! Communications leading up to my stay were both consistent and very helpful. Once I arrived, entry to my unit was easy and efficient. It was also very affordable for being a resort. The unit and grounds were clean and very well taken care of. The staff and tenants were all very friendly. The Mountain view’s were stunning! There was even ample activities and events throughout my stay to partake in. For example, the Farmers Market was lovely, as was the delicious produce we bought! The mineral water in the pools and hot tubs was lovely and gave off a very spa like vibe. The resort is about 20 minutes from restaurants and retails stores, but was well worth the drive just for the views alone, but then adding on the feel and vibe of the resort… let’s just say I will absolutely stay again and recommend to everyone I know!", "languageCode": "en"}, "rating": 5, "publishTime": "2025-06-04T02:12:20.244166Z", "originalText": {"text": "I had the best stay at Sky Valley Resort! Communications leading up to my stay were both consistent and very helpful. Once I arrived, entry to my unit was easy and efficient. It was also very affordable for being a resort. The unit and grounds were clean and very well taken care of. The staff and tenants were all very friendly. The Mountain view’s were stunning! There was even ample activities and events throughout my stay to partake in. For example, the Farmers Market was lovely, as was the delicious produce we bought! The mineral water in the pools and hot tubs was lovely and gave off a very spa like vibe. The resort is about 20 minutes from restaurants and retails stores, but was well worth the drive just for the views alone, but then adding on the feel and vibe of the resort… let’s just say I will absolutely stay again and recommend to everyone I know!", "languageCode": "en"}, "googleMapsUri": "https://www.google.com/maps/reviews/data=!4m6!14m5!1m4!2m3!1sChZDSUhNMG9nS0VQV2FxY25xdmNpcmJnEAE!2m1!1s0x80dae1633190e8a5:0xc80695fe39c0a5ff", "flagContentUri": "https://www.google.com/local/content/rap/report?postId=ChZDSUhNMG9nS0VQV2FxY25xdmNpcmJnEAE&d=17924085&t=1", "authorAttribution": {"uri": "https://www.google.com/maps/contrib/101870011979790724137/reviews", "photoUri": "https://lh3.googleusercontent.com/a-/ALV-UjVO2pULVa4mF6CWdC4OU_cxVzg-KHZfT_PtfbfxJwFPc1ZH5INF=s128-c0x00000000-cc-rp-mo", "displayName": "Kari Stollings"}, "relativePublishTimeDescription": "8 months ago"}]	Sky Valley Resort is a highly-rated, family-friendly destination praised for its pristine facilities, natural mineral hot springs, and stunning mountain views in a quiet, secure environment. Guests consistently highlight the clean pools, gorgeous landscaping, friendly staff, and spa-like atmosphere, though some mention WiFi issues and the remote location requiring drives for dining and shopping. The resort appears to excel as a peaceful retreat with excellent amenities, though potential rental customers should be aware of strict cancellation policies.	{"summary": "Sky Valley Resort is a highly-rated, family-friendly destination praised for its pristine facilities, natural mineral hot springs, and stunning mountain views in a quiet, secure environment. Guests consistently highlight the clean pools, gorgeous landscaping, friendly staff, and spa-like atmosphere, though some mention WiFi issues and the remote location requiring drives for dining and shopping. The resort appears to excel as a peaceful retreat with excellent amenities, though potential rental customers should be aware of strict cancellation policies.", "negative": [{"text": "My only issue during our stay was with the nearly nonexistent WiFi service.", "author": "Rosie Diaz", "rating": 5}, {"text": "No one called me back after leaving three voicemails. I was within days of them keeping my whole months first rent (almost 3k)!", "author": "Jacqueline Marcell", "rating": 1}], "positive": [{"text": "To visit as a vacation spot or a vacay home, this place is a hit with lots of clean pools and gorgeous landscaping!", "author": "F McNamee", "rating": 4}, {"text": "The unit and grounds were clean and very well taken care of. The staff and tenants were all very friendly.", "author": "Kari Stollings", "rating": 5}, {"text": "Very nice resort, quiet, friendly located in the Palm Springs area. Magnificant natural mineral hot springs on site which is the ultimate in relaxing.", "author": "Robert Castonguay", "rating": 5}], "last_updated": "2026-02-06T04:10:02.787Z"}	2026-02-06 04:09:54.97+00	private_rv_park	\N	\N
b4f80769-0be6-4e6f-ad06-e55efe176cae	b201a860-05a3-4ddc-bb89-4c4271177271	Serrano Campground (Big Bear Lake)	Serrano Campground is the premier RV-friendly campground at Big Bear Lake, offering full hookups and paved sites in a pine and juniper forest on the north shore. The lake is the main attraction—swimming, kayaking, paddleboarding, and fishing. But Big Bear also has the Alpine Slide, a small zoo, mountain biking, and excellent hiking. The town has restaurants, shops, and a charming mountain village feel. At 6,800 feet, summer temps are 20-30 degrees cooler than LA.	A mountain lake escape at 6,800 feet where you can ride the Alpine Slide, paddle clear water, summit boulders at Castle Rock, and spot bald eagles—all just 2.5 hours from LA with full hookups.	lake_river	\N	40650 N Shore Dr, Fawnskin, CA 92333, USA	Fawnskin	CA	34.2630114	-116.9167746	ChIJv3FC9bSzxIARy2Pk3CxfCVU	4.6	678	\N	{"hookups": "full", "cell_coverage": "good", "road_accessibility": "CRITICAL: Use Highway 38 from Redlands or Highway 18 from Running Springs. Do NOT use Highway 330—too steep and tight for 5th wheels. Highway 38 has long grades but is wider and more manageable.", "max_trailer_length_ft": 35, "fifth_wheel_accessible": true}	t	\N	Book via recreation.gov up to 6 months ahead. Summer weekends fill fast. Midweek availability is better. Request sites near the lake for best access.	42.00	USD	\N	{"best": ["june", "july", "august", "september"], "avoid": ["december", "january", "february"], "notes": "Mountain campground—summer is prime season. Winter brings snow and road chains. Spring (May) can still be cold. Fall (October) is beautiful with changing aspens."}	2.5 hours	\N	{"scenic_beauty": 4, "solitude_level": 2, "adventure_level": 4, "family_friendly": 5, "relaxation_factor": 4}	{"topics": ["mountain ecology", "wildlife rehabilitation", "bald eagle conservation", "forest management"], "visitor_center": true, "ranger_programs": true, "junior_ranger_program": false}	{"parker": {"notes": "Parker will love the scramble to Castle Rock summit and the thrill of the Alpine Slide. This is peak adventure for an 8-year-old.", "suitable": true, "activities": ["Castle Rock summit scramble", "Alpine Slide at Magic Mountain", "Kayaking on the lake", "Mountain biking on trails"], "engagement_level": 5}, "xander": {"notes": "The zoo is perfect for Xander—rescued animals he can observe. The lake has shallow beach areas for safe water play.", "suitable": true, "activities": ["Big Bear Alpine Zoo animals", "Lake beach play", "Pine cone collecting", "Watching fish from shore"], "engagement_level": 5}, "charlotte": {"notes": "The Alpine Zoo is a wildlife rehabilitation center—Charlotte will love seeing rescued bears, eagles, and mountain lions up close.", "suitable": true, "activities": ["Big Bear Alpine Zoo", "Paddleboarding on the lake", "Woodland Trail nature walk", "Alpine Slide ride"], "engagement_level": 4}}	https://www.recreation.gov/camping/campgrounds/232250	(909) 866-8550	\N	researching	0	{mountain-lake,full-hookups,alpine-slide,kayaking,paddleboarding,zoo,summer-escape}	{"Full hookups at a National Forest campground—excellent value","Lake activities: kayaking, paddleboarding, swimming, fishing","Alpine Slide and zoo provide kid entertainment beyond nature","20-30 degrees cooler than LA in summer","Castle Rock hike is an outstanding family challenge"}	{"Mountain road towing—plan your route carefully (Highway 38 recommended)","Gets crowded on summer weekends—popular LA escape","Altitude (6,800 ft) may affect younger kids initially"}	\N	\N	2026-02-04 15:15:20.042+00	2026-02-06 17:40:59.046319+00	[{"name": "places/ChIJv3FC9bSzxIARy2Pk3CxfCVU/reviews/Ci9DQUlRQUNvZENodHljRjlvT2psNGEweGtaR2gwWW10U2FIQnZaM1ZyTjFoMFYxRRAB", "text": {"text": "I had the BEST time at Serrano Campground. The site is located on the north shore (10 min drive from Big Bear). Cougar Crest Trail is in walking distance from the campgrounds (highly recommend if you are looking for a nice hike), and there is a walking/biking path that takes you all the way to the lake.\\nThe campgrounds were clean and in great shape. I was shocked with with how clean the restrooms and showers were. A small win is that the showers are free to use so you don't need to lug around a heavy coin purse.\\n\\nFire wood is available for sale on the grounds if needed and there are park rangers that monitor the entrances which made me feel safe. There are pumps around the sites with water that can be used for drinking or to wash your dishes. The campground is at a distance where it feels like you are out of the city, but there is still cell reception. I will definitely be coming back.", "languageCode": "en"}, "rating": 5, "publishTime": "2025-08-27T16:26:14.412330437Z", "originalText": {"text": "I had the BEST time at Serrano Campground. The site is located on the north shore (10 min drive from Big Bear). Cougar Crest Trail is in walking distance from the campgrounds (highly recommend if you are looking for a nice hike), and there is a walking/biking path that takes you all the way to the lake.\\nThe campgrounds were clean and in great shape. I was shocked with with how clean the restrooms and showers were. A small win is that the showers are free to use so you don't need to lug around a heavy coin purse.\\n\\nFire wood is available for sale on the grounds if needed and there are park rangers that monitor the entrances which made me feel safe. There are pumps around the sites with water that can be used for drinking or to wash your dishes. The campground is at a distance where it feels like you are out of the city, but there is still cell reception. I will definitely be coming back.", "languageCode": "en"}, "googleMapsUri": "https://www.google.com/maps/reviews/data=!4m6!14m5!1m4!2m3!1sCi9DQUlRQUNvZENodHljRjlvT2psNGEweGtaR2gwWW10U2FIQnZaM1ZyTjFoMFYxRRAB!2m1!1s0x80c4b3b4f54271bf:0x55095f2cdce463cb", "flagContentUri": "https://www.google.com/local/content/rap/report?postId=Ci9DQUlRQUNvZENodHljRjlvT2psNGEweGtaR2gwWW10U2FIQnZaM1ZyTjFoMFYxRRAB&d=17924085&t=1", "authorAttribution": {"uri": "https://www.google.com/maps/contrib/112317603408929942639/reviews", "photoUri": "https://lh3.googleusercontent.com/a/ACg8ocLZ61GK8MfpybMqbH7XrqefPoxVxS5WzoKejL7dW-5Ubhq8bg=s128-c0x00000000-cc-rp-mo-ba2", "displayName": "Liv Alexandria"}, "relativePublishTimeDescription": "5 months ago"}, {"name": "places/ChIJv3FC9bSzxIARy2Pk3CxfCVU/reviews/Ci9DQUlRQUNvZENodHljRjlvT21OSWFIRlpOMUl4VTBsd2NXVmZZelkxZUVsSGMxRRAB", "text": {"text": "This is a really nice campground. The people are friendly and the place is clean and well maintained. They have free hot showers and they even sell wood at the camp entrance which is really convenient. The campground is very peaceful. Some large groups were a little loud and allowed to have fun without being bothered. It was a very chill atmosphere which is what you want when camping.", "languageCode": "en"}, "rating": 5, "publishTime": "2025-08-26T22:29:33.357683661Z", "originalText": {"text": "This is a really nice campground. The people are friendly and the place is clean and well maintained. They have free hot showers and they even sell wood at the camp entrance which is really convenient. The campground is very peaceful. Some large groups were a little loud and allowed to have fun without being bothered. It was a very chill atmosphere which is what you want when camping.", "languageCode": "en"}, "googleMapsUri": "https://www.google.com/maps/reviews/data=!4m6!14m5!1m4!2m3!1sCi9DQUlRQUNvZENodHljRjlvT21OSWFIRlpOMUl4VTBsd2NXVmZZelkxZUVsSGMxRRAB!2m1!1s0x80c4b3b4f54271bf:0x55095f2cdce463cb", "flagContentUri": "https://www.google.com/local/content/rap/report?postId=Ci9DQUlRQUNvZENodHljRjlvT21OSWFIRlpOMUl4VTBsd2NXVmZZelkxZUVsSGMxRRAB&d=17924085&t=1", "authorAttribution": {"uri": "https://www.google.com/maps/contrib/113892011008049910811/reviews", "photoUri": "https://lh3.googleusercontent.com/a-/ALV-UjWNXQ8Rc37_hK3ujV7pl0WtBv0LXPvDph34wpuh6byKgAMRp3rpDg=s128-c0x00000000-cc-rp-mo-ba2", "displayName": "Shannon C"}, "relativePublishTimeDescription": "5 months ago"}, {"name": "places/ChIJv3FC9bSzxIARy2Pk3CxfCVU/reviews/Ci9DQUlRQUNvZENodHljRjlvT2kwdE5FeFpaMVJJZVZoaFVXTldUVUZLYlhGTVFVRRAB", "text": {"text": "Beautiful campground. Spacious and very clean, great toilets and hot showers. There is a gorgeous bike path that leads to the lake, campground was very busy  but everyone was quiet and respectful. I gave it 4 stars because we saw mice running around our tent few times and it’s the only thing that might stop me from returning unfortunately:(", "languageCode": "en"}, "rating": 4, "publishTime": "2025-08-14T03:46:58.520134276Z", "originalText": {"text": "Beautiful campground. Spacious and very clean, great toilets and hot showers. There is a gorgeous bike path that leads to the lake, campground was very busy  but everyone was quiet and respectful. I gave it 4 stars because we saw mice running around our tent few times and it’s the only thing that might stop me from returning unfortunately:(", "languageCode": "en"}, "googleMapsUri": "https://www.google.com/maps/reviews/data=!4m6!14m5!1m4!2m3!1sCi9DQUlRQUNvZENodHljRjlvT2kwdE5FeFpaMVJJZVZoaFVXTldUVUZLYlhGTVFVRRAB!2m1!1s0x80c4b3b4f54271bf:0x55095f2cdce463cb", "flagContentUri": "https://www.google.com/local/content/rap/report?postId=Ci9DQUlRQUNvZENodHljRjlvT2kwdE5FeFpaMVJJZVZoaFVXTldUVUZLYlhGTVFVRRAB&d=17924085&t=1", "authorAttribution": {"uri": "https://www.google.com/maps/contrib/117187705147254638005/reviews", "photoUri": "https://lh3.googleusercontent.com/a/ACg8ocJC0wXmTrNoeJVsH2HIcf5iVvsQelnHMDHO1QEa_DXs359IsQ=s128-c0x00000000-cc-rp-mo-ba3", "displayName": "Luna Viola"}, "relativePublishTimeDescription": "5 months ago"}, {"name": "places/ChIJv3FC9bSzxIARy2Pk3CxfCVU/reviews/Ci9DQUlRQUNvZENodHljRjlvT25ob1kxWlJWRXgxWTI5MVgxUTVRV1J6Y25OdlQwRRAB", "text": {"text": "CONS:\\nShowers were not so great.\\nI had some unreasonably loud neighbors.\\nUnattended kids and families were continuously walking through my site.\\nPROS:\\nPlenty of spots to hang my hammock\\nGreat cell service to get work done\\nClose to town and easy bikeway access", "languageCode": "en"}, "rating": 3, "publishTime": "2025-09-25T19:12:23.072850823Z", "originalText": {"text": "CONS:\\nShowers were not so great.\\nI had some unreasonably loud neighbors.\\nUnattended kids and families were continuously walking through my site.\\nPROS:\\nPlenty of spots to hang my hammock\\nGreat cell service to get work done\\nClose to town and easy bikeway access", "languageCode": "en"}, "googleMapsUri": "https://www.google.com/maps/reviews/data=!4m6!14m5!1m4!2m3!1sCi9DQUlRQUNvZENodHljRjlvT25ob1kxWlJWRXgxWTI5MVgxUTVRV1J6Y25OdlQwRRAB!2m1!1s0x80c4b3b4f54271bf:0x55095f2cdce463cb", "flagContentUri": "https://www.google.com/local/content/rap/report?postId=Ci9DQUlRQUNvZENodHljRjlvT25ob1kxWlJWRXgxWTI5MVgxUTVRV1J6Y25OdlQwRRAB&d=17924085&t=1", "authorAttribution": {"uri": "https://www.google.com/maps/contrib/116685957751577346134/reviews", "photoUri": "https://lh3.googleusercontent.com/a-/ALV-UjWx4fu2PlZOpn1X4vCladOXzrVnYMJJTZnbD6XoSzEAtJ3P_Q0=s128-c0x00000000-cc-rp-mo-ba2", "displayName": "Molly Alvarado"}, "relativePublishTimeDescription": "4 months ago"}, {"name": "places/ChIJv3FC9bSzxIARy2Pk3CxfCVU/reviews/Ci9DQUlRQUNvZENodHljRjlvT2t4dGEzazViSFZGVEhGdmJFTk1OVWhFY1dGeGNuYxAB", "text": {"text": "2nd time staying at this campground. We enjoyed it a lot 2 years/2 summers ago and returning 08.13-15.25 for another family summer camping trip.\\n\\nWe're at Campground # 28\\n\\nCampground # 27 is accommodating for disabilities.\\nWhich was right across from our campground # 28.\\n\\n#27 had majority all pavement in the campsite. Around the picnic table along they have their own water spout for water use. Also located closest to the restroom/showers, has a pavement road leading up to it for easy access.\\n\\nREMINDER there is no washing dishes sink available on these campgrounds nor can you use the restroom sinks to wash anything.\\nThere is a sign that it isn't allowed.\\nSo make sure to bring your own water!\\nThis time around downfall is the electrical plugs in both of the restrooms, weren't working the 2 nights stay we were there.\\nI asked the associates that were driving around daily regards to the power.\\nThey told me it's a hit or miss.\\nSometimes the power isn't working and there's nothing that can be done to fix it. The downfall.\\n\\nLove the Serrano campground since it’s not far from the actual Big Bear village.\\nStill definitely recommend it.\\nReally clean & everyone is respecting each other especially at night.", "languageCode": "en"}, "rating": 5, "publishTime": "2025-08-23T00:01:13.927098719Z", "originalText": {"text": "2nd time staying at this campground. We enjoyed it a lot 2 years/2 summers ago and returning 08.13-15.25 for another family summer camping trip.\\n\\nWe're at Campground # 28\\n\\nCampground # 27 is accommodating for disabilities.\\nWhich was right across from our campground # 28.\\n\\n#27 had majority all pavement in the campsite. Around the picnic table along they have their own water spout for water use. Also located closest to the restroom/showers, has a pavement road leading up to it for easy access.\\n\\nREMINDER there is no washing dishes sink available on these campgrounds nor can you use the restroom sinks to wash anything.\\nThere is a sign that it isn't allowed.\\nSo make sure to bring your own water!\\nThis time around downfall is the electrical plugs in both of the restrooms, weren't working the 2 nights stay we were there.\\nI asked the associates that were driving around daily regards to the power.\\nThey told me it's a hit or miss.\\nSometimes the power isn't working and there's nothing that can be done to fix it. The downfall.\\n\\nLove the Serrano campground since it’s not far from the actual Big Bear village.\\nStill definitely recommend it.\\nReally clean & everyone is respecting each other especially at night.", "languageCode": "en"}, "googleMapsUri": "https://www.google.com/maps/reviews/data=!4m6!14m5!1m4!2m3!1sCi9DQUlRQUNvZENodHljRjlvT2t4dGEzazViSFZGVEhGdmJFTk1OVWhFY1dGeGNuYxAB!2m1!1s0x80c4b3b4f54271bf:0x55095f2cdce463cb", "flagContentUri": "https://www.google.com/local/content/rap/report?postId=Ci9DQUlRQUNvZENodHljRjlvT2t4dGEzazViSFZGVEhGdmJFTk1OVWhFY1dGeGNuYxAB&d=17924085&t=1", "authorAttribution": {"uri": "https://www.google.com/maps/contrib/101056306346246141243/reviews", "photoUri": "https://lh3.googleusercontent.com/a-/ALV-UjWaVH7GeYhrdwRFfzj5RgqG0-cou8oZH4-nJs7rfylmzrNsGS0=s128-c0x00000000-cc-rp-mo-ba5", "displayName": "Mimi Jung"}, "relativePublishTimeDescription": "5 months ago"}]	Serrano Campground is a highly-rated, clean and well-maintained campground that offers the perfect balance of nature and convenience, located just 10 minutes from Big Bear with easy lake access via walking/biking paths. Families consistently praise the free hot showers, respectful atmosphere, and safety features like park rangers monitoring entrances. While most visitors love the peaceful environment and cleanliness, some minor issues include occasional mice sightings and inconsistent electrical outlets in restrooms.	{"summary": "Serrano Campground is a highly-rated, clean and well-maintained campground that offers the perfect balance of nature and convenience, located just 10 minutes from Big Bear with easy lake access via walking/biking paths. Families consistently praise the free hot showers, respectful atmosphere, and safety features like park rangers monitoring entrances. While most visitors love the peaceful environment and cleanliness, some minor issues include occasional mice sightings and inconsistent electrical outlets in restrooms.", "negative": [{"text": "I gave it 4 stars because we saw mice running around our tent few times and it's the only thing that might stop me from returning unfortunately:(", "author": "Luna Viola", "rating": 4}, {"text": "Unattended kids and families were continuously walking through my site.", "author": "Molly Alvarado", "rating": 3}], "positive": [{"text": "The campgrounds were clean and in great shape. I was shocked with with how clean the restrooms and showers were.", "author": "Liv Alexandria", "rating": 5}, {"text": "The campground is very peaceful. Some large groups were a little loud and allowed to have fun without being bothered.", "author": "Shannon C", "rating": 5}, {"text": "Really clean & everyone is respecting each other especially at night.", "author": "Mimi Jung", "rating": 5}], "last_updated": "2026-02-06T17:40:58.916Z"}	2026-02-06 17:40:52.451+00	national_forest	\N	serrano-campground-big-bear-lake
1df8d107-9902-468d-bf37-889ffa42dd47	b201a860-05a3-4ddc-bb89-4c4271177271	Santa Barbara Sunrise RV Park	Santa Barbara Sunrise is a small urban RV park right in the city of Santa Barbara, offering full hookups and walkability to everything. It's not scenic—it's utilitarian—but the location is unbeatable for families wanting to explore Santa Barbara without driving. Stearns Wharf, the Santa Barbara Zoo, the harbor, the mission, and State Street shopping are all walkable or a short drive. Use this as a base camp for a city exploration weekend.	The only RV park IN the city of Santa Barbara—walk to Stearns Wharf, the zoo, the harbor, and the mission from your full-hookup site for the ultimate 'urban base camp' weekend.	other	\N	516 S Salinas St, Santa Barbara, CA 93103, USA	Santa Barbara	CA	34.4217827	-119.6666313	ChIJxYlDnbsT6YARb2jrQad1OMU	4.2	422	\N	{"hookups": "full", "cell_coverage": "excellent", "road_accessibility": "Urban streets—manageable for 5th wheel but tight getting into the park. Call ahead for guidance on approach route.", "max_trailer_length_ft": 35, "fifth_wheel_accessible": true}	t	\N	Book directly through website. Small park with limited sites—book well ahead. Most expensive option on this list but saves on parking and transportation costs.	95.00	USD	\N	{"best": ["march", "april", "may", "september", "october", "november"], "avoid": [], "notes": "Year-round destination. Summer is busy and more expensive. Spring and fall are perfect."}	2 hours	\N	{"scenic_beauty": 2, "solitude_level": 1, "adventure_level": 3, "family_friendly": 4, "relaxation_factor": 3}	{"topics": ["marine biology", "California mission history", "Spanish colonial architecture", "marine mammals"], "visitor_center": true, "ranger_programs": false, "junior_ranger_program": false}	{"parker": {"notes": "A city exploration weekend with lots of variety. Parker will enjoy the active pace.", "suitable": true, "activities": ["Santa Barbara Zoo", "Harbor kayaking", "Stearns Wharf fishing", "Shoreline Park bike ride"], "engagement_level": 4}, "xander": {"notes": "Between the zoo, wharf, and beach, Xander will have a full day of animals and sensory fun.", "suitable": true, "activities": ["Zoo animals", "Stearns Wharf walking", "Beach play", "Ice cream on State Street"], "engagement_level": 5}, "charlotte": {"notes": "The Sea Center on Stearns Wharf has incredible touch tanks and marine exhibits. Charlotte will love the zoo and mission gardens.", "suitable": true, "activities": ["Santa Barbara Zoo", "Sea Center touch tanks on Stearns Wharf", "Mission gardens", "Beach play"], "engagement_level": 5}}	https://santabarbararv.com/	(805) 966-9954	\N	researching	0	{urban,full-hookups,walkable,zoo,wharf,santa-barbara,city-base-camp}	{"Walking distance to Santa Barbara's best attractions","Full hookups in the city","No driving needed once parked—saves gas and parking hassle","Great restaurants within walking distance"}	{"Not scenic—it's an urban RV park","Most expensive option on this list ($95/night)","Small sites, close quarters","Street noise"}	\N	\N	2026-02-04 15:15:25.006+00	2026-02-06 17:18:47.730254+00	[{"name": "places/ChIJxYlDnbsT6YARb2jrQad1OMU/reviews/Ci9DQUlRQUNvZENodHljRjlvT21KbVFtSkZVRmxUVEU1U1VHVk5RVWN0UmpSU1FYYxAB", "text": {"text": "Very sweet, small RV park.  Manager very nice.  Bathrooms and showers are like private bathrooms and very clean.  Great place to stop over when traveling.  Caution- bring earplugs - you will hear the freeway.", "languageCode": "en"}, "rating": 4, "publishTime": "2026-01-23T16:07:01.854977362Z", "originalText": {"text": "Very sweet, small RV park.  Manager very nice.  Bathrooms and showers are like private bathrooms and very clean.  Great place to stop over when traveling.  Caution- bring earplugs - you will hear the freeway.", "languageCode": "en"}, "googleMapsUri": "https://www.google.com/maps/reviews/data=!4m6!14m5!1m4!2m3!1sCi9DQUlRQUNvZENodHljRjlvT21KbVFtSkZVRmxUVEU1U1VHVk5RVWN0UmpSU1FYYxAB!2m1!1s0x80e913bb9d4389c5:0xc53875a741eb686f", "flagContentUri": "https://www.google.com/local/content/rap/report?postId=Ci9DQUlRQUNvZENodHljRjlvT21KbVFtSkZVRmxUVEU1U1VHVk5RVWN0UmpSU1FYYxAB&d=17924085&t=1", "authorAttribution": {"uri": "https://www.google.com/maps/contrib/112518479671710135672/reviews", "photoUri": "https://lh3.googleusercontent.com/a/ACg8ocL2GHYynEsDyX1_4zCrZJ0_0Tf7fM5PeolvWCjm8LrTlJMpNw=s128-c0x00000000-cc-rp-mo", "displayName": "Kevin Donnelly"}, "relativePublishTimeDescription": "a week ago"}, {"name": "places/ChIJxYlDnbsT6YARb2jrQad1OMU/reviews/Ci9DQUlRQUNvZENodHljRjlvT2tsbk5tVlpaR3hPY1VodFpuaHpiRFpsY0c5NGVFRRAB", "text": {"text": "I’ve driven past this place for years but never had the need to stop in.   This week I needed a place to stay for a few days during a construction project.    Yes it’s close to freeway, but that’s the point- it’s in a busy tourist town and provides a convenient, clean and friendly environment. From the initial conversation on the phone for reservations to a quick introduction when I arrived, they are focused on what they can provide and what you can do rather than some places that are all about restrictions. it is clean and well maintained. I imagine as a tourist coming through for a couple days. This would be a great base camp.", "languageCode": "en"}, "rating": 5, "publishTime": "2025-08-17T14:51:25.029701248Z", "originalText": {"text": "I’ve driven past this place for years but never had the need to stop in.   This week I needed a place to stay for a few days during a construction project.    Yes it’s close to freeway, but that’s the point- it’s in a busy tourist town and provides a convenient, clean and friendly environment. From the initial conversation on the phone for reservations to a quick introduction when I arrived, they are focused on what they can provide and what you can do rather than some places that are all about restrictions. it is clean and well maintained. I imagine as a tourist coming through for a couple days. This would be a great base camp.", "languageCode": "en"}, "googleMapsUri": "https://www.google.com/maps/reviews/data=!4m6!14m5!1m4!2m3!1sCi9DQUlRQUNvZENodHljRjlvT2tsbk5tVlpaR3hPY1VodFpuaHpiRFpsY0c5NGVFRRAB!2m1!1s0x80e913bb9d4389c5:0xc53875a741eb686f", "flagContentUri": "https://www.google.com/local/content/rap/report?postId=Ci9DQUlRQUNvZENodHljRjlvT2tsbk5tVlpaR3hPY1VodFpuaHpiRFpsY0c5NGVFRRAB&d=17924085&t=1", "authorAttribution": {"uri": "https://www.google.com/maps/contrib/104936259770172968456/reviews", "photoUri": "https://lh3.googleusercontent.com/a/ACg8ocLztsfBXh5fJWfmUBC02TuSDWcohjG-aU-58qNC-1fuS7Soow=s128-c0x00000000-cc-rp-mo", "displayName": "Glen L"}, "relativePublishTimeDescription": "5 months ago"}, {"name": "places/ChIJxYlDnbsT6YARb2jrQad1OMU/reviews/Ci9DQUlRQUNvZENodHljRjlvT2xWeWRYRTNaMjlLTFZWclJXUmxTWEZUVVZwTVUyYxAB", "text": {"text": "We stay here every year and we love the location.  Short bike ride to beach and state street. Also bathrooms/showers are nice and private. Staff is always friendly and price is reasonable.", "languageCode": "en"}, "rating": 4, "publishTime": "2025-08-18T03:15:08.337865320Z", "originalText": {"text": "We stay here every year and we love the location.  Short bike ride to beach and state street. Also bathrooms/showers are nice and private. Staff is always friendly and price is reasonable.", "languageCode": "en"}, "googleMapsUri": "https://www.google.com/maps/reviews/data=!4m6!14m5!1m4!2m3!1sCi9DQUlRQUNvZENodHljRjlvT2xWeWRYRTNaMjlLTFZWclJXUmxTWEZUVVZwTVUyYxAB!2m1!1s0x80e913bb9d4389c5:0xc53875a741eb686f", "flagContentUri": "https://www.google.com/local/content/rap/report?postId=Ci9DQUlRQUNvZENodHljRjlvT2xWeWRYRTNaMjlLTFZWclJXUmxTWEZUVVZwTVUyYxAB&d=17924085&t=1", "authorAttribution": {"uri": "https://www.google.com/maps/contrib/107857689285700559194/reviews", "photoUri": "https://lh3.googleusercontent.com/a-/ALV-UjWCwkQ6sgfYvH0Mq5ArS4NGV8PhjgtIl2ia6gkOr7ttlF87zuMScQ=s128-c0x00000000-cc-rp-mo-ba4", "displayName": "Traycee Whichello"}, "relativePublishTimeDescription": "5 months ago"}, {"name": "places/ChIJxYlDnbsT6YARb2jrQad1OMU/reviews/Ci9DQUlRQUNvZENodHljRjlvT2pNNFQyc3laMVpsVWtka05FUk9iazlpV1Y5U2QyYxAB", "text": {"text": "2 stars only because the staff were very friendly and kept the place very clean. The place is literally steps away from the 101. Some reviews said the 12 ft barrier wall helped block highway noise. It doesn't. Very odd place for an RV park. Friend couldn't put his awning out because it would hit his neighbor. Can't recommend at all.", "languageCode": "en"}, "rating": 2, "publishTime": "2025-09-04T20:35:06.072192531Z", "originalText": {"text": "2 stars only because the staff were very friendly and kept the place very clean. The place is literally steps away from the 101. Some reviews said the 12 ft barrier wall helped block highway noise. It doesn't. Very odd place for an RV park. Friend couldn't put his awning out because it would hit his neighbor. Can't recommend at all.", "languageCode": "en"}, "googleMapsUri": "https://www.google.com/maps/reviews/data=!4m6!14m5!1m4!2m3!1sCi9DQUlRQUNvZENodHljRjlvT2pNNFQyc3laMVpsVWtka05FUk9iazlpV1Y5U2QyYxAB!2m1!1s0x80e913bb9d4389c5:0xc53875a741eb686f", "flagContentUri": "https://www.google.com/local/content/rap/report?postId=Ci9DQUlRQUNvZENodHljRjlvT2pNNFQyc3laMVpsVWtka05FUk9iazlpV1Y5U2QyYxAB&d=17924085&t=1", "authorAttribution": {"uri": "https://www.google.com/maps/contrib/116780412554220348253/reviews", "photoUri": "https://lh3.googleusercontent.com/a-/ALV-UjVkpViQRlZULinnT71rseg8l9b1XeNRFj4RcPuCElSNT3WtRpY=s128-c0x00000000-cc-rp-mo", "displayName": "Tim Zimmer"}, "relativePublishTimeDescription": "5 months ago"}, {"name": "places/ChIJxYlDnbsT6YARb2jrQad1OMU/reviews/ChdDSUhNMG9nS0VJQ0FnTUNvbjdyOXVBRRAB", "text": {"text": "The location is a polarizing conversation.  On the one hand you're close to and accessibly quick to pretty much anything in Santa Barbara.  That, because you're 50 feet and a 9 foot wall away from the 101 Freeway.  But then, you're 50 feet away from the 101...... Forget doing anything outside unless you are ok with yelling to converse.  The noise is outrageously bad for an RV park.  Even off peak hours it is a steady stream of cars, trucks and motorcycle wizzing and/or screaming by.   For us it's ok.  We don't care much about amenities and we liked the central location but you will not spend your time here having family fun outside your coach.  You're in a 90 decibel environment under good conditions.  You will also not get a pool, clubhouse, dog run or any now expected RV park niceties.   22 lots, weird, urban layout, old bathrooms and laundry.  Both are serviceable but they won't remind you of the last RV \\"resort\\" you went to.  This is a bare bones RV park with severe limitations.  All that said, staff was great, price was right and you really are 10 minutes from almost anything in town.  We may even be back because of that but it won't be because the park itself is nice, it isn't but hop in your car and downtown Santa Barbara, beaches and the like are a stones throw away and at a reasonable price.", "languageCode": "en"}, "rating": 4, "publishTime": "2025-04-21T01:07:20.655340Z", "originalText": {"text": "The location is a polarizing conversation.  On the one hand you're close to and accessibly quick to pretty much anything in Santa Barbara.  That, because you're 50 feet and a 9 foot wall away from the 101 Freeway.  But then, you're 50 feet away from the 101...... Forget doing anything outside unless you are ok with yelling to converse.  The noise is outrageously bad for an RV park.  Even off peak hours it is a steady stream of cars, trucks and motorcycle wizzing and/or screaming by.   For us it's ok.  We don't care much about amenities and we liked the central location but you will not spend your time here having family fun outside your coach.  You're in a 90 decibel environment under good conditions.  You will also not get a pool, clubhouse, dog run or any now expected RV park niceties.   22 lots, weird, urban layout, old bathrooms and laundry.  Both are serviceable but they won't remind you of the last RV \\"resort\\" you went to.  This is a bare bones RV park with severe limitations.  All that said, staff was great, price was right and you really are 10 minutes from almost anything in town.  We may even be back because of that but it won't be because the park itself is nice, it isn't but hop in your car and downtown Santa Barbara, beaches and the like are a stones throw away and at a reasonable price.", "languageCode": "en"}, "googleMapsUri": "https://www.google.com/maps/reviews/data=!4m6!14m5!1m4!2m3!1sChdDSUhNMG9nS0VJQ0FnTUNvbjdyOXVBRRAB!2m1!1s0x80e913bb9d4389c5:0xc53875a741eb686f", "flagContentUri": "https://www.google.com/local/content/rap/report?postId=ChdDSUhNMG9nS0VJQ0FnTUNvbjdyOXVBRRAB&d=17924085&t=1", "authorAttribution": {"uri": "https://www.google.com/maps/contrib/117385085742447651262/reviews", "photoUri": "https://lh3.googleusercontent.com/a-/ALV-UjXvg6fAKLVP8FnBpNPhsHDiehwjlKrHF7EYt_vY0hbzTmIMSgI=s128-c0x00000000-cc-rp-mo-ba7", "displayName": "KT Webb"}, "relativePublishTimeDescription": "9 months ago"}]	Santa Barbara Sunrise RV Park is a small, bare-bones facility that offers excellent location and convenience for accessing downtown Santa Barbara and beaches, but comes with significant freeway noise that dominates the experience. While the staff is friendly and facilities are clean, the proximity to Highway 101 makes outdoor family activities challenging due to constant traffic noise.	{"summary": "Santa Barbara Sunrise RV Park is a small, bare-bones facility that offers excellent location and convenience for accessing downtown Santa Barbara and beaches, but comes with significant freeway noise that dominates the experience. While the staff is friendly and facilities are clean, the proximity to Highway 101 makes outdoor family activities challenging due to constant traffic noise.", "negative": [{"text": "Forget doing anything outside unless you are ok with yelling to converse. You will not spend your time here having family fun outside your coach.", "author": "KT Webb", "rating": 4}, {"text": "Friend couldn't put his awning out because it would hit his neighbor. Can't recommend at all.", "author": "Tim Zimmer", "rating": 2}], "positive": [{"text": "Short bike ride to beach and state street. Also bathrooms/showers are nice and private.", "author": "Traycee Whichello", "rating": 4}, {"text": "Bathrooms and showers are like private bathrooms and very clean.", "author": "Kevin Donnelly", "rating": 4}, {"text": "You really are 10 minutes from almost anything in town... downtown Santa Barbara, beaches and the like are a stones throw away.", "author": "KT Webb", "rating": 4}], "last_updated": "2026-02-06T00:35:23.227Z"}	2026-02-06 00:35:17.324+00	private_rv_park	\N	santa-barbara-sunrise-rv-park
2b3de818-dfd0-4284-a646-01feb979a5b3	b201a860-05a3-4ddc-bb89-4c4271177271	William Heise County Park (Julian)	William Heise County Park is a San Diego County park in the Cuyamaca Mountains near Julian. The campground sits at 4,200 feet in a forest of oaks and pines, offering a cool mountain escape. Julian itself is the draw—a historic gold mining town famous for its apple orchards, pie shops, and small-town charm. The California Wolf Center offers close encounters with wolves, the Eagle and High Peak Mine lets kids pan for gold, and the surrounding mountains have excellent hiking.	Camp in a Cuyamaca mountain pine forest near the gold rush town where apple pie is a way of life, wolves howl at a conservation center, and kids can pan for gold in a real mine—all at 4,200 feet elevation.	other	\N	4945 Heise Park Rd, Julian, CA 92036, USA	Julian	CA	33.0402052	-116.5878279	ChIJU4RolwzQ24ARbnxsak_grSc	4.7	764	\N	{"hookups": "water_electric", "cell_coverage": "spotty", "road_accessibility": "Highway 78/79 to Julian is manageable for 5th wheels. The road into Heise Park has some curves but is paved. Take slowly.", "max_trailer_length_ft": 40, "fifth_wheel_accessible": true}	t	\N	Book through San Diego County Parks (sdparks.org). Easier to get than most campgrounds on this list. Very affordable.	33.00	USD	\N	{"best": ["september", "october", "november", "april", "may"], "avoid": [], "notes": "Apple season peaks September-November. Spring has wildflowers. Summer is warm but pleasant at elevation. Winter can get cold with occasional snow."}	2.5 hours	\N	{"scenic_beauty": 4, "solitude_level": 4, "adventure_level": 3, "family_friendly": 5, "relaxation_factor": 4}	{"topics": ["wolf conservation", "gold rush history", "apple agriculture", "mountain ecology"], "visitor_center": false, "ranger_programs": false, "junior_ranger_program": false}	{"parker": {"notes": "Gold panning gives Parker a goal and the Wolf Center is genuinely fascinating. Volcan Mountain is a real hiking challenge.", "suitable": true, "activities": ["Gold panning at Eagle Mine", "Volcan Mountain trail scramble", "Wolf Center visit", "Mountain biking in park"], "engagement_level": 4}, "xander": {"notes": "Wolves howling will be unforgettable for Xander. Apple cider donuts are a guaranteed hit.", "suitable": true, "activities": ["Wolf Center animals", "Apple cider donuts", "Pine forest exploring", "Campfire time"], "engagement_level": 5}, "charlotte": {"notes": "Charlotte will be captivated by the wolves and thrilled by apple picking. Julian's pie shops are a treasure hunt of their own.", "suitable": true, "activities": ["California Wolf Center wolves", "Apple picking in orchards", "Gold panning", "Pie shop tasting tour"], "engagement_level": 5}}	http://www.sdparks.org/content/sdparks/en/park-pages/WilliamHeise.html	(760) 765-0650	\N	researching	0	{mountain,wolves,gold-mining,apple-pie,water-electric,small-town,affordable}	{"California Wolf Center is a unique, unforgettable family experience","Julian's pie shops and gold mining history are perfect for kids","Affordable water/electric hookups in a beautiful mountain setting","Much less crowded than Big Bear or coastal campgrounds","Apple season (Sept-Nov) is magical"}	{"Julian town is small—can see everything in a half day","Cell coverage is spotty","Less lake/water activities compared to Big Bear"}	\N	\N	2026-02-04 15:15:21.759+00	2026-02-06 00:39:27.329391+00	[{"name": "places/ChIJU4RolwzQ24ARbnxsak_grSc/reviews/Ci9DQUlRQUNvZENodHljRjlvT2xkbmFYUldZakpaWVZZemNuVlZZVkpJTTJZdFYzYxAB", "text": {"text": "This may be a better park than just our overnight stay indicated, but for folks who spend a lot of time in the outdoors this was not a great park. It was at least fairly clean and well kept except for a LOT of dog poop, but that is on the thoughtless users not the staff.\\n\\nWe picked the wrong trail to do, the Cedar Trail, because we arrived late in the afternoon and only had time for a short hike. I think the other trails must be better based on other reviews. The Cedar Trail was just a mile of rough wash going up and down steep hills with no views to reward the climbs.\\n\\nThe campground loop that we stayed in (1-20) had sites very crowded together and only 2 or 3 that were even close to level. Other areas we walked through didn’t appear much better and the tent area was a muddy mess with one bathroom for 40 sites. The bathrooms themselves were nice, basic and clean with flush toilets and pay showers. The cabin loop was a nice area with cute basic cabins, but they also were right on top of each other.\\n\\nPower and water is available on the RV sites as well as picnic tables and fire rings. There is a dump station on site which was why we came in out of the forest to this park in the first place. Not someplace we would visit again.", "languageCode": "en"}, "rating": 3, "publishTime": "2025-11-20T16:31:29.217540300Z", "originalText": {"text": "This may be a better park than just our overnight stay indicated, but for folks who spend a lot of time in the outdoors this was not a great park. It was at least fairly clean and well kept except for a LOT of dog poop, but that is on the thoughtless users not the staff.\\n\\nWe picked the wrong trail to do, the Cedar Trail, because we arrived late in the afternoon and only had time for a short hike. I think the other trails must be better based on other reviews. The Cedar Trail was just a mile of rough wash going up and down steep hills with no views to reward the climbs.\\n\\nThe campground loop that we stayed in (1-20) had sites very crowded together and only 2 or 3 that were even close to level. Other areas we walked through didn’t appear much better and the tent area was a muddy mess with one bathroom for 40 sites. The bathrooms themselves were nice, basic and clean with flush toilets and pay showers. The cabin loop was a nice area with cute basic cabins, but they also were right on top of each other.\\n\\nPower and water is available on the RV sites as well as picnic tables and fire rings. There is a dump station on site which was why we came in out of the forest to this park in the first place. Not someplace we would visit again.", "languageCode": "en"}, "googleMapsUri": "https://www.google.com/maps/reviews/data=!4m6!14m5!1m4!2m3!1sCi9DQUlRQUNvZENodHljRjlvT2xkbmFYUldZakpaWVZZemNuVlZZVkpJTTJZdFYzYxAB!2m1!1s0x80dbd00c97688453:0x27ade04f6a6c7c6e", "flagContentUri": "https://www.google.com/local/content/rap/report?postId=Ci9DQUlRQUNvZENodHljRjlvT2xkbmFYUldZakpaWVZZemNuVlZZVkpJTTJZdFYzYxAB&d=17924085&t=1", "authorAttribution": {"uri": "https://www.google.com/maps/contrib/111935334243771439890/reviews", "photoUri": "https://lh3.googleusercontent.com/a-/ALV-UjUbesVl_QXx52sHQtVkYKSXCnI8DspMgbxu_pWFfsn330bQYKRz-g=s128-c0x00000000-cc-rp-mo-ba5", "displayName": "Amanda Mueller"}, "relativePublishTimeDescription": "2 months ago"}, {"name": "places/ChIJU4RolwzQ24ARbnxsak_grSc/reviews/Ci9DQUlRQUNvZENodHljRjlvT25obWNqUndjekowY0ZkVllYcFBWSEZyTkMwMmIxRRAB", "text": {"text": "We had such a wonderful experience camping here in our little RV.  The park is very clean and well kept. The hiking trails were beautiful and well maintained. What a nice park nestled in a well-forested area with beautiful views, lots of wildlife, and clearings for stargazing. Just a mile away from Julian, I wish we had planned a trip into town before we headed back down the hill. We loved seeing all a variety of hawks, woodpeckers, blue jays, and the resident flock of wild turkeys! Delightful!", "languageCode": "en"}, "rating": 5, "publishTime": "2025-08-17T23:00:39.672633344Z", "originalText": {"text": "We had such a wonderful experience camping here in our little RV.  The park is very clean and well kept. The hiking trails were beautiful and well maintained. What a nice park nestled in a well-forested area with beautiful views, lots of wildlife, and clearings for stargazing. Just a mile away from Julian, I wish we had planned a trip into town before we headed back down the hill. We loved seeing all a variety of hawks, woodpeckers, blue jays, and the resident flock of wild turkeys! Delightful!", "languageCode": "en"}, "googleMapsUri": "https://www.google.com/maps/reviews/data=!4m6!14m5!1m4!2m3!1sCi9DQUlRQUNvZENodHljRjlvT25obWNqUndjekowY0ZkVllYcFBWSEZyTkMwMmIxRRAB!2m1!1s0x80dbd00c97688453:0x27ade04f6a6c7c6e", "flagContentUri": "https://www.google.com/local/content/rap/report?postId=Ci9DQUlRQUNvZENodHljRjlvT25obWNqUndjekowY0ZkVllYcFBWSEZyTkMwMmIxRRAB&d=17924085&t=1", "authorAttribution": {"uri": "https://www.google.com/maps/contrib/113850808637335049400/reviews", "photoUri": "https://lh3.googleusercontent.com/a-/ALV-UjXielruv-f-h3kEUhH5dvVgEQos4VWybzaNwMgt8rkzhdcyvrR0hg=s128-c0x00000000-cc-rp-mo-ba3", "displayName": "LeeAnn N"}, "relativePublishTimeDescription": "5 months ago"}, {"name": "places/ChIJU4RolwzQ24ARbnxsak_grSc/reviews/Ci9DQUlRQUNvZENodHljRjlvT2xKSUxUTndaVkpYYjBwRE1ucHRTamhvYW1KclFrRRAB", "text": {"text": "Beautiful campground for our travel trailer. Lots of trees for shade. Well maintained roads. Mostly level RV site. Partial hookups a plus. Only wish they had more trash dumpsters near the campsite.", "languageCode": "en"}, "rating": 4, "publishTime": "2025-08-24T01:54:20.499755851Z", "originalText": {"text": "Beautiful campground for our travel trailer. Lots of trees for shade. Well maintained roads. Mostly level RV site. Partial hookups a plus. Only wish they had more trash dumpsters near the campsite.", "languageCode": "en"}, "googleMapsUri": "https://www.google.com/maps/reviews/data=!4m6!14m5!1m4!2m3!1sCi9DQUlRQUNvZENodHljRjlvT2xKSUxUTndaVkpYYjBwRE1ucHRTamhvYW1KclFrRRAB!2m1!1s0x80dbd00c97688453:0x27ade04f6a6c7c6e", "flagContentUri": "https://www.google.com/local/content/rap/report?postId=Ci9DQUlRQUNvZENodHljRjlvT2xKSUxUTndaVkpYYjBwRE1ucHRTamhvYW1KclFrRRAB&d=17924085&t=1", "authorAttribution": {"uri": "https://www.google.com/maps/contrib/108853545049130709438/reviews", "photoUri": "https://lh3.googleusercontent.com/a-/ALV-UjWS3vn0Pxc2Ps8tZDQ6z1nwW7srWZw7E-KeveYQv7idMiZUzXo66A=s128-c0x00000000-cc-rp-mo-ba3", "displayName": "Susan Logan Eubanks"}, "relativePublishTimeDescription": "5 months ago"}, {"name": "places/ChIJU4RolwzQ24ARbnxsak_grSc/reviews/Ci9DQUlRQUNvZENodHljRjlvT2pJMFRGVXdVRVJJU1RaV1VqSjFZVGx6VkZOWFptYxAB", "text": {"text": "July 2025 was our first visit since 1986.  Much has been added and improved since then.  The hiking trails are outstanding, nothing long, but well maintained.  The scenery is worth the effort.  Desert and ocean (marine layer) views along with cedar forest (Watch out for the abundant poison oak!)  Spacious, private, level camp sites and parking for the most part.  Clean restrooms and simple pay showers starting at 4 minutes for two quarters (no controls on hot/cold/flow rate; my 6 minute shower during a mid-day lull offered no warm water at all ... hence the 4 not 5 star rating.", "languageCode": "en"}, "rating": 4, "publishTime": "2025-07-29T06:50:59.262402931Z", "originalText": {"text": "July 2025 was our first visit since 1986.  Much has been added and improved since then.  The hiking trails are outstanding, nothing long, but well maintained.  The scenery is worth the effort.  Desert and ocean (marine layer) views along with cedar forest (Watch out for the abundant poison oak!)  Spacious, private, level camp sites and parking for the most part.  Clean restrooms and simple pay showers starting at 4 minutes for two quarters (no controls on hot/cold/flow rate; my 6 minute shower during a mid-day lull offered no warm water at all ... hence the 4 not 5 star rating.", "languageCode": "en"}, "googleMapsUri": "https://www.google.com/maps/reviews/data=!4m6!14m5!1m4!2m3!1sCi9DQUlRQUNvZENodHljRjlvT2pJMFRGVXdVRVJJU1RaV1VqSjFZVGx6VkZOWFptYxAB!2m1!1s0x80dbd00c97688453:0x27ade04f6a6c7c6e", "flagContentUri": "https://www.google.com/local/content/rap/report?postId=Ci9DQUlRQUNvZENodHljRjlvT2pJMFRGVXdVRVJJU1RaV1VqSjFZVGx6VkZOWFptYxAB&d=17924085&t=1", "authorAttribution": {"uri": "https://www.google.com/maps/contrib/100010343816728607286/reviews", "photoUri": "https://lh3.googleusercontent.com/a-/ALV-UjXRP6Pe01byixKpN9wtg6fF3DMC38D6yNOJPAhmMn8MeYpIjoibwg=s128-c0x00000000-cc-rp-mo-ba6", "displayName": "Daniel Marler"}, "relativePublishTimeDescription": "6 months ago"}, {"name": "places/ChIJU4RolwzQ24ARbnxsak_grSc/reviews/Ci9DQUlRQUNvZENodHljRjlvT2pScE5rdG5SMFJFYlZGcmFIbExPR0p1UmtWalVFRRAB", "text": {"text": "We had a great time! The park was clean and well maintained. We rented a cabin for our trip, between the roof and the close proximity to the town we had an easy time. Great for beginners or weekenders.", "languageCode": "en"}, "rating": 5, "publishTime": "2025-10-21T00:24:19.201438936Z", "originalText": {"text": "We had a great time! The park was clean and well maintained. We rented a cabin for our trip, between the roof and the close proximity to the town we had an easy time. Great for beginners or weekenders.", "languageCode": "en"}, "googleMapsUri": "https://www.google.com/maps/reviews/data=!4m6!14m5!1m4!2m3!1sCi9DQUlRQUNvZENodHljRjlvT2pScE5rdG5SMFJFYlZGcmFIbExPR0p1UmtWalVFRRAB!2m1!1s0x80dbd00c97688453:0x27ade04f6a6c7c6e", "flagContentUri": "https://www.google.com/local/content/rap/report?postId=Ci9DQUlRQUNvZENodHljRjlvT2pScE5rdG5SMFJFYlZGcmFIbExPR0p1UmtWalVFRRAB&d=17924085&t=1", "authorAttribution": {"uri": "https://www.google.com/maps/contrib/113955789966454771341/reviews", "photoUri": "https://lh3.googleusercontent.com/a/ACg8ocLlO4R5JInyLabGTAKrWHZaqeHAOazEaVLRoHN5PCcEmGxG6g=s128-c0x00000000-cc-rp-mo", "displayName": "Durand Smiley"}, "relativePublishTimeDescription": "3 months ago"}]	William Heise County Park is generally well-regarded as a clean, well-maintained family camping destination nestled in a forested area near Julian. Most visitors appreciate the beautiful hiking trails, abundant wildlife viewing opportunities, and convenient amenities, though some find the campsites crowded and trail quality variable.	{"summary": "William Heise County Park is generally well-regarded as a clean, well-maintained family camping destination nestled in a forested area near Julian. Most visitors appreciate the beautiful hiking trails, abundant wildlife viewing opportunities, and convenient amenities, though some find the campsites crowded and trail quality variable.", "negative": [{"text": "The campground loop that we stayed in (1-20) had sites very crowded together and only 2 or 3 that were even close to level.", "author": "Amanda Mueller", "rating": 3}, {"text": "It was at least fairly clean and well kept except for a LOT of dog poop, but that is on the thoughtless users not the staff.", "author": "Amanda Mueller", "rating": 3}], "positive": [{"text": "What a nice park nestled in a well-forested area with beautiful views, lots of wildlife, and clearings for stargazing.", "author": "LeeAnn N", "rating": 5}, {"text": "We loved seeing all a variety of hawks, woodpeckers, blue jays, and the resident flock of wild turkeys!", "author": "LeeAnn N", "rating": 5}, {"text": "Great for beginners or weekenders.", "author": "Durand Smiley", "rating": 5}], "last_updated": "2026-02-06T00:39:27.205Z"}	2026-02-06 00:39:21.754+00	county_park	\N	\N
cb297a8f-e0a8-49b3-bfa8-3935ad227a1a	b201a860-05a3-4ddc-bb89-4c4271177271	Camp Comfort Park (Ojai)	Camp Comfort is a Ventura County park tucked along San Antonio Creek in a grove of towering oaks in Ojai. It's small, affordable, and wonderfully low-key. Ojai itself is a special place—a bohemian valley town known for its arts scene, the famous 'Pink Moment' sunset that turns the Topa Topa Mountains pink, excellent restaurants, and the Ojai Valley Trail bike path. It's a different vibe from coastal camping—more spiritual, artsy, and relaxed.	A creekside campground in the spiritual heart of Ojai Valley where the famous 'Pink Moment' sunset paints the mountains, world-class olive oil is made next door, and a 16-mile bike path winds through paradise.	other	\N	11969 N Creek Rd, Ojai, CA 93023, USA	Ojai	CA	34.4263381	-119.2583236	ChIJVVVVVYWy6YARJ0DfXC6Wotc	4.5	143	\N	{"hookups": "full", "cell_coverage": "good", "road_accessibility": "Highway 33 from Ventura is straightforward. Some turns entering the campground—take slowly with a 5th wheel. Camp road is narrow in spots.", "max_trailer_length_ft": 34, "fifth_wheel_accessible": true}	t	\N	Book through Ventura County Parks website. Much easier to get than state beach campgrounds. Very affordable.	32.00	USD	\N	{"best": ["march", "april", "may", "october", "november"], "avoid": ["july", "august"], "notes": "Summer gets very hot in Ojai Valley (100°F+). Spring and fall are ideal with moderate temps and clear skies. The Pink Moment is visible year-round but clearest in spring and fall."}	1.5 hours	\N	{"scenic_beauty": 4, "solitude_level": 3, "adventure_level": 2, "family_friendly": 4, "relaxation_factor": 5}	{"topics": ["olive oil production", "California arts and culture", "creek ecology"], "visitor_center": false, "ranger_programs": false, "junior_ranger_program": false}	{"parker": {"notes": "Ojai is more of a relaxation destination. Parker will enjoy the bike path but may want more adventure.", "suitable": true, "activities": ["Ojai Valley Trail biking", "Creek play", "Rock scrambling in creek bed"], "engagement_level": 3}, "xander": {"notes": "The creek is perfect for Xander—shallow water play, rocks to throw, and shade from the big oaks.", "suitable": true, "activities": ["Creek water play", "Campsite under big oaks", "Feeding ducks", "Walking in town"], "engagement_level": 4}, "charlotte": {"notes": "Charlotte will love Bart's Books—an outdoor bookstore where you browse among trees. The creek has rocks and small pools to explore.", "suitable": true, "activities": ["Bart's Books outdoor bookstore", "Ojai Olive Oil tasting", "Creek exploration", "Farmers market (Sunday)"], "engagement_level": 4}}	https://www.ventura.org/parks-department/inland-parks/camp-comfort-ojai/	(805) 654-3951	\N	researching	0	{artsy,full-hookups,biking,creek,relaxation,affordable,unique-town}	{"Very affordable full-hookup camping","Ojai's unique artsy/spiritual vibe is unlike anywhere else nearby","Ojai Valley Trail is a phenomenal family bike path","The 'Pink Moment' sunset is genuinely breathtaking","Close to LA—easy weekend trip"}	{"Camp Comfort is small and basic—not a scenic campground itself","Summer heat makes it uncomfortable (100°F+)","Less outdoor adventure than other destinations on this list"}	\N	\N	2026-02-04 15:15:21.198+00	2026-02-06 00:40:42.312337+00	[{"name": "places/ChIJVVVVVYWy6YARJ0DfXC6Wotc/reviews/Ci9DQUlRQUNvZENodHljRjlvT2trdE5taEJYMDVsY25NNGNXRTBOMTlaTURNNFdGRRAB", "text": {"text": "Great place but they double booked my campsite which was strange. We worked it out with the people next to us but I suggest booking only from the county website so you know you have a reservation. The other people booked through another site and only got one of the sites the wanted and then I was in the other. The ranger tried to help but we just split the site with the people it felt rude to make them leave even though it felt rude that they put their tent up in my site with a note to move my car, it worked out. The creek is right off the camp site, not a lot of water but enough that the kids were amused", "languageCode": "en"}, "rating": 4, "publishTime": "2025-07-31T15:27:07.623031264Z", "originalText": {"text": "Great place but they double booked my campsite which was strange. We worked it out with the people next to us but I suggest booking only from the county website so you know you have a reservation. The other people booked through another site and only got one of the sites the wanted and then I was in the other. The ranger tried to help but we just split the site with the people it felt rude to make them leave even though it felt rude that they put their tent up in my site with a note to move my car, it worked out. The creek is right off the camp site, not a lot of water but enough that the kids were amused", "languageCode": "en"}, "googleMapsUri": "https://www.google.com/maps/reviews/data=!4m6!14m5!1m4!2m3!1sCi9DQUlRQUNvZENodHljRjlvT2trdE5taEJYMDVsY25NNGNXRTBOMTlaTURNNFdGRRAB!2m1!1s0x80e9b28555555555:0xd7a2962e5cdf4027", "flagContentUri": "https://www.google.com/local/content/rap/report?postId=Ci9DQUlRQUNvZENodHljRjlvT2trdE5taEJYMDVsY25NNGNXRTBOMTlaTURNNFdGRRAB&d=17924085&t=1", "authorAttribution": {"uri": "https://www.google.com/maps/contrib/115470540110289732480/reviews", "photoUri": "https://lh3.googleusercontent.com/a-/ALV-UjVCdHHAmrChhOQXmL7qQnZbuicrSYyWMWK3Zt5tPqN37DtJB37jzA=s128-c0x00000000-cc-rp-mo-ba6", "displayName": "Jessica Watson (Psychomelon)"}, "relativePublishTimeDescription": "6 months ago"}, {"name": "places/ChIJVVVVVYWy6YARJ0DfXC6Wotc/reviews/Ci9DQUlRQUNvZENodHljRjlvT2pCNFYzaGtlVEF4WDBKMWNpMDJibGRCVkhZMmQxRRAB", "text": {"text": "We had a great weekend at Camp Comfort!  With four toddlers in our group, the clean and quiet campsites by the excellent playground made for an excellent and enriching experience enjoyed by all. Not sure where the camp host was, but the park ranger was very friendly, as were the other camp patrons (including the rooster).", "languageCode": "en"}, "rating": 5, "publishTime": "2025-10-20T01:58:51.916946187Z", "originalText": {"text": "We had a great weekend at Camp Comfort!  With four toddlers in our group, the clean and quiet campsites by the excellent playground made for an excellent and enriching experience enjoyed by all. Not sure where the camp host was, but the park ranger was very friendly, as were the other camp patrons (including the rooster).", "languageCode": "en"}, "googleMapsUri": "https://www.google.com/maps/reviews/data=!4m6!14m5!1m4!2m3!1sCi9DQUlRQUNvZENodHljRjlvT2pCNFYzaGtlVEF4WDBKMWNpMDJibGRCVkhZMmQxRRAB!2m1!1s0x80e9b28555555555:0xd7a2962e5cdf4027", "flagContentUri": "https://www.google.com/local/content/rap/report?postId=Ci9DQUlRQUNvZENodHljRjlvT2pCNFYzaGtlVEF4WDBKMWNpMDJibGRCVkhZMmQxRRAB&d=17924085&t=1", "authorAttribution": {"uri": "https://www.google.com/maps/contrib/105112631685521863729/reviews", "photoUri": "https://lh3.googleusercontent.com/a-/ALV-UjUPlsjNkpjUQVoxAnDuQ5sBFRJw-UQUVgyGaUfEj9iKGrhfk17Fzg=s128-c0x00000000-cc-rp-mo-ba2", "displayName": "Amanda Shue"}, "relativePublishTimeDescription": "3 months ago"}, {"name": "places/ChIJVVVVVYWy6YARJ0DfXC6Wotc/reviews/ChdDSUhNMG9nS0VJQ0FnSUNIOUxqN2dRRRAB", "text": {"text": "This smaller campground is awesome. The camp host is friendly. He maintains the campground well. People are pleasant. The restroom is clean and it has coin operated hot showers and laundry room. Each campsite has electrical, water and sewerage hookup.  There is creek with running water behind the campground. There is a clubhouse and a park for dayuse people.  We would come back to camp.", "languageCode": "en"}, "rating": 5, "publishTime": "2024-09-01T19:12:49.732786Z", "originalText": {"text": "This smaller campground is awesome. The camp host is friendly. He maintains the campground well. People are pleasant. The restroom is clean and it has coin operated hot showers and laundry room. Each campsite has electrical, water and sewerage hookup.  There is creek with running water behind the campground. There is a clubhouse and a park for dayuse people.  We would come back to camp.", "languageCode": "en"}, "googleMapsUri": "https://www.google.com/maps/reviews/data=!4m6!14m5!1m4!2m3!1sChdDSUhNMG9nS0VJQ0FnSUNIOUxqN2dRRRAB!2m1!1s0x80e9b28555555555:0xd7a2962e5cdf4027", "flagContentUri": "https://www.google.com/local/content/rap/report?postId=ChdDSUhNMG9nS0VJQ0FnSUNIOUxqN2dRRRAB&d=17924085&t=1", "authorAttribution": {"uri": "https://www.google.com/maps/contrib/112024749517365224475/reviews", "photoUri": "https://lh3.googleusercontent.com/a/ACg8ocIv27xcNFz5_n5ZEnA-Bk1q1fzJ-DOUGdCS_s-kdVRA2ZG2sXs=s128-c0x00000000-cc-rp-mo", "displayName": "Smiley Stevie"}, "relativePublishTimeDescription": "a year ago"}, {"name": "places/ChIJVVVVVYWy6YARJ0DfXC6Wotc/reviews/Ci9DQUlRQUNvZENodHljRjlvT2w5M2RGUnpibUZVV0Y5SWNVTkZhVE5mV1c5WFVtYxAB", "text": {"text": "This place is NOT big rig friendly though they booked me knowing I had a 40 ft fifth wheel. Beware the overhanging trees at the entrance. I tore 5-10 ft gouges in my roof and the side of my RV. The attitude of the park ranger was that it happens all the time.", "languageCode": "en"}, "rating": 3, "publishTime": "2025-07-23T23:59:08.054064624Z", "originalText": {"text": "This place is NOT big rig friendly though they booked me knowing I had a 40 ft fifth wheel. Beware the overhanging trees at the entrance. I tore 5-10 ft gouges in my roof and the side of my RV. The attitude of the park ranger was that it happens all the time.", "languageCode": "en"}, "googleMapsUri": "https://www.google.com/maps/reviews/data=!4m6!14m5!1m4!2m3!1sCi9DQUlRQUNvZENodHljRjlvT2w5M2RGUnpibUZVV0Y5SWNVTkZhVE5mV1c5WFVtYxAB!2m1!1s0x80e9b28555555555:0xd7a2962e5cdf4027", "flagContentUri": "https://www.google.com/local/content/rap/report?postId=Ci9DQUlRQUNvZENodHljRjlvT2w5M2RGUnpibUZVV0Y5SWNVTkZhVE5mV1c5WFVtYxAB&d=17924085&t=1", "authorAttribution": {"uri": "https://www.google.com/maps/contrib/115114450489014257672/reviews", "photoUri": "https://lh3.googleusercontent.com/a/ACg8ocILU3lHKFPtNIiqT0alSZlIFL3PD1ag32D4TCYq-dbR2BsmeQ=s128-c0x00000000-cc-rp-mo-ba4", "displayName": "Paul Pelsinski"}, "relativePublishTimeDescription": "6 months ago"}, {"name": "places/ChIJVVVVVYWy6YARJ0DfXC6Wotc/reviews/Ci9DQUlRQUNvZENodHljRjlvT21WNGNVZFRhVU53UVdjM1RqaHdPWEI0VVRsWE9IYxAB", "text": {"text": "Great camping experience, clean restrooms (with showers), next to a really nice, lush park with a playground for kids. The RV area seemed nice as well, although pretty packed.\\n\\nCampsites are past the RV area in a more secluded area, although most campsites, minus the two on the ends, are close to each other.\\n\\nAlso, this area is haunted by a few spirits, and there’s a wild rooster that hangs out.", "languageCode": "en"}, "rating": 5, "publishTime": "2025-10-14T17:16:36.250967220Z", "originalText": {"text": "Great camping experience, clean restrooms (with showers), next to a really nice, lush park with a playground for kids. The RV area seemed nice as well, although pretty packed.\\n\\nCampsites are past the RV area in a more secluded area, although most campsites, minus the two on the ends, are close to each other.\\n\\nAlso, this area is haunted by a few spirits, and there’s a wild rooster that hangs out.", "languageCode": "en"}, "googleMapsUri": "https://www.google.com/maps/reviews/data=!4m6!14m5!1m4!2m3!1sCi9DQUlRQUNvZENodHljRjlvT21WNGNVZFRhVU53UVdjM1RqaHdPWEI0VVRsWE9IYxAB!2m1!1s0x80e9b28555555555:0xd7a2962e5cdf4027", "flagContentUri": "https://www.google.com/local/content/rap/report?postId=Ci9DQUlRQUNvZENodHljRjlvT21WNGNVZFRhVU53UVdjM1RqaHdPWEI0VVRsWE9IYxAB&d=17924085&t=1", "authorAttribution": {"uri": "https://www.google.com/maps/contrib/114401050546363520205/reviews", "photoUri": "https://lh3.googleusercontent.com/a/ACg8ocJl4DYIkcUu10ItJ-KHPF6qvN-H4fOUPhwg0b3RfPS_IBecAw=s128-c0x00000000-cc-rp-mo-ba2", "displayName": "Tori Morrison"}, "relativePublishTimeDescription": "3 months ago"}]	Camp Comfort Park is a well-maintained, family-friendly campground that's particularly loved by visitors with young children due to its excellent playground, clean facilities, and peaceful atmosphere. While most guests have wonderful experiences, there are occasional issues with booking mix-ups and the campground isn't suitable for large RVs due to low-hanging trees at the entrance.	{"summary": "Camp Comfort Park is a well-maintained, family-friendly campground that's particularly loved by visitors with young children due to its excellent playground, clean facilities, and peaceful atmosphere. While most guests have wonderful experiences, there are occasional issues with booking mix-ups and the campground isn't suitable for large RVs due to low-hanging trees at the entrance.", "negative": [{"text": "Great place but they double booked my campsite which was strange.", "author": "Jessica Watson", "rating": 4}, {"text": "This place is NOT big rig friendly though they booked me knowing I had a 40 ft fifth wheel. I tore 5-10 ft gouges in my roof and the side of my RV.", "author": "Paul Pelsinski", "rating": 3}], "positive": [{"text": "With four toddlers in our group, the clean and quiet campsites by the excellent playground made for an excellent and enriching experience enjoyed by all.", "author": "Amanda Shue", "rating": 5}, {"text": "The restroom is clean and it has coin operated hot showers and laundry room.", "author": "Smiley Stevie", "rating": 5}, {"text": "Great camping experience, clean restrooms (with showers), next to a really nice, lush park with a playground for kids.", "author": "Tori Morrison", "rating": 5}], "last_updated": "2026-02-06T00:40:42.211Z"}	2026-02-06 00:40:34.966+00	county_park	\N	\N
c3eb2f18-c2d0-4e8d-adb7-cf2b18ffd4a4	b201a860-05a3-4ddc-bb89-4c4271177271	Lake Cachuma Recreation Area	Lake Cachuma is a reservoir nestled in the Santa Ynez Valley behind the Santa Ynez Mountains, offering a completely different experience from the coastal campgrounds. Full hookup sites sit among live oaks with lake views. No body-contact water sports are allowed (it's a drinking water reservoir), but fishing, kayaking on calm waters, and the excellent naturalist-led wildlife cruises make this a special destination. Bald eagles winter here, and the 2-hour Eagle Cruises are a highlight.	A hidden inland lake in the Santa Ynez Valley where bald eagles nest in winter, the wildlife cruises bring nature right to your kids, and full hookups mean you can actually relax while surrounded by oak-studded hills.	lake_river	\N	1 Lakeview Dr, Santa Barbara, CA 93105, USA	Santa Barbara	CA	34.5754323	-119.9587994	ChIJM-NXp7la6YART5xc7pZUuhs	4.5	2748	\N	{"hookups": "full", "cell_coverage": "spotty", "road_accessibility": "Highway 154 (San Marcos Pass) has curves but is 5th-wheel manageable. Take it easy on the descent. Alternatively, take US-101 to Buellton and approach from the north—flatter.", "max_trailer_length_ft": 60, "fifth_wheel_accessible": true}	t	\N	Book via cachuma.com. Full hookup sites book ahead in eagle season. General store and dump station on-site.	50.00	USD	\N	{"best": ["november", "december", "january", "february", "march", "april"], "avoid": ["july", "august"], "notes": "Bald eagle season is November-February (Eagle Cruises run during this period). Summer gets hot (90s+) with no swimming allowed. Spring is gorgeous with wildflowers."}	2.5 hours	\N	{"scenic_beauty": 4, "solitude_level": 3, "adventure_level": 2, "family_friendly": 5, "relaxation_factor": 5}	{"topics": ["bald eagle conservation", "freshwater ecology", "oak woodland habitats", "bird migration"], "visitor_center": true, "ranger_programs": true, "junior_ranger_program": false}	{"parker": {"notes": "Parker may want more adventure than Cachuma offers—this is more of a relaxation spot. Good for a mellow day.", "suitable": true, "activities": ["Kayaking on the lake", "Fishing from shore", "Sweetwater Trail hike", "Bike riding around the lake"], "engagement_level": 3}, "xander": {"notes": "The boat cruise is the perfect length for Xander, and the birds are endlessly entertaining.", "suitable": true, "activities": ["Wildlife cruise boat ride", "Bird watching", "Playground", "Campsite exploring"], "engagement_level": 4}, "charlotte": {"notes": "The wildlife/eagle cruises are excellent for Charlotte—guided by naturalists who explain everything.", "suitable": true, "activities": ["Wildlife cruise", "Bird identification", "Nature center exhibits", "Fishing"], "engagement_level": 4}}	http://countyofsb.org/parks/cachuma	(805) 568-2460	\N	researching	0	{lake,full-hookups,bald-eagles,wildlife-cruises,fishing,relaxation,wine-country}	{"Full hookups with spacious sites in an oak grove","Wildlife/eagle cruises are outstanding educational experiences","Bald eagles nest here November-February","Very relaxing atmosphere—slower pace than coastal campgrounds","Santa Ynez wine country and Solvang are nearby for parents"}	{"No swimming or body contact with water (drinking water reservoir)","Less adventurous than other destinations—may bore active kids on longer stays","Summer heat without swimming option makes it less appealing June-August"}	\N	\N	2026-02-04 15:15:20.66+00	2026-02-06 00:41:28.274585+00	[{"name": "places/ChIJM-NXp7la6YART5xc7pZUuhs/reviews/Ci9DQUlRQUNvZENodHljRjlvT21ad1dWOXpSVk53VUhkWE9FcFVPRE5zYzBSVllVRRAB", "text": {"text": "This campground is really nice and reasonably priced! Several lake front sites (no hook ups) and many other partial and full hook up sites that are not far from the lake. Has a playground, pool, a store and decent bathrooms. They also have a restaurant and boat dock/launch ramp with boat rentals as well. Not a swimming lake however. We will definitely be coming back!", "languageCode": "en"}, "rating": 5, "publishTime": "2026-01-23T18:33:54.149524455Z", "originalText": {"text": "This campground is really nice and reasonably priced! Several lake front sites (no hook ups) and many other partial and full hook up sites that are not far from the lake. Has a playground, pool, a store and decent bathrooms. They also have a restaurant and boat dock/launch ramp with boat rentals as well. Not a swimming lake however. We will definitely be coming back!", "languageCode": "en"}, "googleMapsUri": "https://www.google.com/maps/reviews/data=!4m6!14m5!1m4!2m3!1sCi9DQUlRQUNvZENodHljRjlvT21ad1dWOXpSVk53VUhkWE9FcFVPRE5zYzBSVllVRRAB!2m1!1s0x80e95ab9a757e333:0x1bba5496ee5c9c4f", "flagContentUri": "https://www.google.com/local/content/rap/report?postId=Ci9DQUlRQUNvZENodHljRjlvT21ad1dWOXpSVk53VUhkWE9FcFVPRE5zYzBSVllVRRAB&d=17924085&t=1", "authorAttribution": {"uri": "https://www.google.com/maps/contrib/107892917243194090741/reviews", "photoUri": "https://lh3.googleusercontent.com/a-/ALV-UjXKDaW8EeZe8eY8E3S5_U8vBvgvn0PGV0Ni0En4nx-EQr-w8ppI=s128-c0x00000000-cc-rp-mo-ba4", "displayName": "Taylor Jones"}, "relativePublishTimeDescription": "a week ago"}, {"name": "places/ChIJM-NXp7la6YART5xc7pZUuhs/reviews/Ci9DQUlRQUNvZENodHljRjlvT2w5VGVIcEJPV0ppT0doRFVuUm9ZVkJwVURselMyYxAB", "text": {"text": "Beautiful and peaceful spot!\\nI had an amazing time here — the lake views are incredible, and the sunset was absolutely stunning. The weather was perfect, and it’s a great place for a relaxing BBQ with friends. Everything felt calm and refreshing, away from the city noise. Definitely one of my favorite places around Goleta! 🌅🔥💧", "languageCode": "en"}, "rating": 5, "publishTime": "2025-10-15T00:33:50.256357703Z", "originalText": {"text": "Beautiful and peaceful spot!\\nI had an amazing time here — the lake views are incredible, and the sunset was absolutely stunning. The weather was perfect, and it’s a great place for a relaxing BBQ with friends. Everything felt calm and refreshing, away from the city noise. Definitely one of my favorite places around Goleta! 🌅🔥💧", "languageCode": "en"}, "googleMapsUri": "https://www.google.com/maps/reviews/data=!4m6!14m5!1m4!2m3!1sCi9DQUlRQUNvZENodHljRjlvT2w5VGVIcEJPV0ppT0doRFVuUm9ZVkJwVURselMyYxAB!2m1!1s0x80e95ab9a757e333:0x1bba5496ee5c9c4f", "flagContentUri": "https://www.google.com/local/content/rap/report?postId=Ci9DQUlRQUNvZENodHljRjlvT2w5VGVIcEJPV0ppT0doRFVuUm9ZVkJwVURselMyYxAB&d=17924085&t=1", "authorAttribution": {"uri": "https://www.google.com/maps/contrib/101893741697813001944/reviews", "photoUri": "https://lh3.googleusercontent.com/a-/ALV-UjWDbN6IstBqxmUFTb9jKN50-GH10_Phkc4dembVvtUatX3OD2_k=s128-c0x00000000-cc-rp-mo-ba3", "displayName": "Ratul R."}, "relativePublishTimeDescription": "3 months ago"}, {"name": "places/ChIJM-NXp7la6YART5xc7pZUuhs/reviews/Ci9DQUlRQUNvZENodHljRjlvT2xSQmFYbEdORXhzWnpWWlNqQlRSSFJPUldSWFNXYxAB", "text": {"text": "Beautiful scenery but a poorly maintained campground. Dingy bathrooms and three different showers took quarters and no water came out at all. Rude gatehouse woman rolled her eyes like it was an inconvenience to help us. Could be great but it's not.", "languageCode": "en"}, "rating": 1, "publishTime": "2025-11-27T04:26:29.141046846Z", "originalText": {"text": "Beautiful scenery but a poorly maintained campground. Dingy bathrooms and three different showers took quarters and no water came out at all. Rude gatehouse woman rolled her eyes like it was an inconvenience to help us. Could be great but it's not.", "languageCode": "en"}, "googleMapsUri": "https://www.google.com/maps/reviews/data=!4m6!14m5!1m4!2m3!1sCi9DQUlRQUNvZENodHljRjlvT2xSQmFYbEdORXhzWnpWWlNqQlRSSFJPUldSWFNXYxAB!2m1!1s0x80e95ab9a757e333:0x1bba5496ee5c9c4f", "flagContentUri": "https://www.google.com/local/content/rap/report?postId=Ci9DQUlRQUNvZENodHljRjlvT2xSQmFYbEdORXhzWnpWWlNqQlRSSFJPUldSWFNXYxAB&d=17924085&t=1", "authorAttribution": {"uri": "https://www.google.com/maps/contrib/109007777427871648699/reviews", "photoUri": "https://lh3.googleusercontent.com/a-/ALV-UjWAffhzxrzihwWkpweNMhqAOsavj6dPBfNXfimGImq1FkNEm-X0=s128-c0x00000000-cc-rp-mo-ba4", "displayName": "Goldie Gibbon"}, "relativePublishTimeDescription": "2 months ago"}, {"name": "places/ChIJM-NXp7la6YART5xc7pZUuhs/reviews/Ci9DQUlRQUNvZENodHljRjlvT21GemFuTnZXVmR1UzFOdE5FdE5NRFZvZWxkaWNFRRAB", "text": {"text": "Cachuma Lake is a great spot for camping – peaceful, with clean restrooms and showers. There are plenty of tent sites and nice trails to explore. Just keep in mind that little animals, like raccoons, might come by. Don’t leave food out on the tables!", "languageCode": "en"}, "rating": 5, "publishTime": "2025-08-28T05:26:31.484385410Z", "originalText": {"text": "Cachuma Lake is a great spot for camping – peaceful, with clean restrooms and showers. There are plenty of tent sites and nice trails to explore. Just keep in mind that little animals, like raccoons, might come by. Don’t leave food out on the tables!", "languageCode": "en"}, "googleMapsUri": "https://www.google.com/maps/reviews/data=!4m6!14m5!1m4!2m3!1sCi9DQUlRQUNvZENodHljRjlvT21GemFuTnZXVmR1UzFOdE5FdE5NRFZvZWxkaWNFRRAB!2m1!1s0x80e95ab9a757e333:0x1bba5496ee5c9c4f", "flagContentUri": "https://www.google.com/local/content/rap/report?postId=Ci9DQUlRQUNvZENodHljRjlvT21GemFuTnZXVmR1UzFOdE5FdE5NRFZvZWxkaWNFRRAB&d=17924085&t=1", "authorAttribution": {"uri": "https://www.google.com/maps/contrib/118174888164780263112/reviews", "photoUri": "https://lh3.googleusercontent.com/a-/ALV-UjWJbTYCJ2ByodcNcmcgZe5A4RQh-JUW8OQLslXZ7sNfSpNBgYOFJg=s128-c0x00000000-cc-rp-mo-ba6", "displayName": "Olga Opara"}, "relativePublishTimeDescription": "5 months ago"}, {"name": "places/ChIJM-NXp7la6YART5xc7pZUuhs/reviews/Ci9DQUlRQUNvZENodHljRjlvT2pSU1EzZHlObnBJUWpGbGJUbHFhR1pHYmtsSGJWRRAB", "text": {"text": "I am a local from Santa Ynez and I spend most of my free time down at the lake fishing along the shore or out in our boat. The fishing here is terrific. I do very well off of the shore and even better on a boat. They have several boats for rent. I believe they offer 2 hour, half day and full day rentals. Really nice Easy start aluminum and/or pontoon boats. They also have kayak rentals. The boys at the tackle shop are great. We hit it off right away. Great bunch of guys and gal🙂\\n\\nI frequent the restaurant and bar often while im there. Sometimes ill just go there to hang out at the restaurant. It has a terrific vibe. Brad and Natalie are amongst the very best leaders in service. They always greet me with a smile. The food is excellent. I recommend the BLT. I get it every single time😄 The restaurant and bar area are pristine. The Bar has 3 big screen tv's, multiple beers on tap and every mixed drink you could possibly think of. Everybody there is just outstanding so I apologize for the names I did not mention. Im just drawing a blank right now. Its been a great day of fishing 🎣 and im burnt😄\\n\\nI have never camped here however i have camped at several other locations. They have many spaces for RV's, 5th wheels, tents, chairs, benches etc....clean and flat grounds....it's all in very good condition. They offer camping, hiking, disc golf, kayaking, boating and fishing. They also have waterfront bungalows for rent.", "languageCode": "en"}, "rating": 5, "publishTime": "2025-09-18T02:50:43.919700142Z", "originalText": {"text": "I am a local from Santa Ynez and I spend most of my free time down at the lake fishing along the shore or out in our boat. The fishing here is terrific. I do very well off of the shore and even better on a boat. They have several boats for rent. I believe they offer 2 hour, half day and full day rentals. Really nice Easy start aluminum and/or pontoon boats. They also have kayak rentals. The boys at the tackle shop are great. We hit it off right away. Great bunch of guys and gal🙂\\n\\nI frequent the restaurant and bar often while im there. Sometimes ill just go there to hang out at the restaurant. It has a terrific vibe. Brad and Natalie are amongst the very best leaders in service. They always greet me with a smile. The food is excellent. I recommend the BLT. I get it every single time😄 The restaurant and bar area are pristine. The Bar has 3 big screen tv's, multiple beers on tap and every mixed drink you could possibly think of. Everybody there is just outstanding so I apologize for the names I did not mention. Im just drawing a blank right now. Its been a great day of fishing 🎣 and im burnt😄\\n\\nI have never camped here however i have camped at several other locations. They have many spaces for RV's, 5th wheels, tents, chairs, benches etc....clean and flat grounds....it's all in very good condition. They offer camping, hiking, disc golf, kayaking, boating and fishing. They also have waterfront bungalows for rent.", "languageCode": "en"}, "googleMapsUri": "https://www.google.com/maps/reviews/data=!4m6!14m5!1m4!2m3!1sCi9DQUlRQUNvZENodHljRjlvT2pSU1EzZHlObnBJUWpGbGJUbHFhR1pHYmtsSGJWRRAB!2m1!1s0x80e95ab9a757e333:0x1bba5496ee5c9c4f", "flagContentUri": "https://www.google.com/local/content/rap/report?postId=Ci9DQUlRQUNvZENodHljRjlvT2pSU1EzZHlObnBJUWpGbGJUbHFhR1pHYmtsSGJWRRAB&d=17924085&t=1", "authorAttribution": {"uri": "https://www.google.com/maps/contrib/113809407930339169374/reviews", "photoUri": "https://lh3.googleusercontent.com/a/ACg8ocKHF0R2JcW9rCbC3wAKh1fpU8RoYYSTToRnb23qZJZb44Za3A=s128-c0x00000000-cc-rp-mo-ba3", "displayName": "DANTE FERRARINI"}, "relativePublishTimeDescription": "4 months ago"}]	Lake Cachuma Recreation Area is a beloved lakeside destination that offers excellent fishing, camping, and family amenities with stunning scenery and peaceful atmosphere. Most visitors praise the reasonable prices, clean facilities, restaurant, and variety of activities including boat rentals and a playground. However, some visitors have encountered maintenance issues with showers and unhelpful staff that detract from the otherwise beautiful location.	{"summary": "Lake Cachuma Recreation Area is a beloved lakeside destination that offers excellent fishing, camping, and family amenities with stunning scenery and peaceful atmosphere. Most visitors praise the reasonable prices, clean facilities, restaurant, and variety of activities including boat rentals and a playground. However, some visitors have encountered maintenance issues with showers and unhelpful staff that detract from the otherwise beautiful location.", "negative": [{"text": "Dingy bathrooms and three different showers took quarters and no water came out at all. Rude gatehouse woman rolled her eyes like it was an inconvenience to help us.", "author": "Goldie Gibbon", "rating": 1}, {"text": "Not a swimming lake however.", "author": "Taylor Jones", "rating": 5}], "positive": [{"text": "Has a playground, pool, a store and decent bathrooms. They also have a restaurant and boat dock/launch ramp with boat rentals as well.", "author": "Taylor Jones", "rating": 5}, {"text": "Cachuma Lake is a great spot for camping – peaceful, with clean restrooms and showers. There are plenty of tent sites and nice trails to explore.", "author": "Olga Opara", "rating": 5}, {"text": "This campground is really nice and reasonably priced! Several lake front sites (no hook ups) and many other partial and full hook up sites that are not far from the lake.", "author": "Taylor Jones", "rating": 5}], "last_updated": "2026-02-06T00:41:28.173Z"}	2026-02-06 00:41:20.655+00	county_park	\N	\N
cd6791f7-7b57-42b3-b7e8-9c8838db6ba8	b201a860-05a3-4ddc-bb89-4c4271177271	Dogwood Campground (Lake Arrowhead)	Dogwood Campground is a USFS campground nestled in dense pine and cedar forest near Lake Arrowhead in the San Bernardino Mountains. The towering trees provide deep shade and a genuine forest atmosphere. While the campground doesn't have hookups, the real draw is nearby SkyPark at Santa's Village—a reimagined theme park with zip lines, mountain biking, rock climbing, and seasonal events. Lake Arrowhead Village offers lake views, shops, and boat tours.	A shaded mountain retreat in towering pines where SkyPark at Santa's Village turns Christmas into a year-round adventure and the forest canopy makes every campsite feel like a treehouse.	other	\N	26898 Rim of the World Hwy, Lake Arrowhead, CA 92378, USA	Rimforest	CA	34.2355458	-117.2113583	ChIJO_9en85Xw4ARZEavg9jfTY8	4.7	624	\N	{"hookups": "none", "cell_coverage": "spotty", "road_accessibility": "Highway 18 from Running Springs is the best route for larger rigs. Avoid Highway 138 from I-15—narrow and steep. Some campground sites have tight access.", "max_trailer_length_ft": 30, "fifth_wheel_accessible": true}	t	\N	Book via recreation.gov up to 6 months ahead. Less competitive than Big Bear. 30ft max is tight for your rig—measure carefully and check specific site dimensions.	32.00	USD	\N	{"best": ["june", "july", "august", "september"], "avoid": ["december", "january", "february"], "notes": "Summer mountain campground. Winter brings snow and road chains. SkyPark has seasonal events (Halloween, Christmas) that are popular."}	2 hours	\N	{"scenic_beauty": 4, "solitude_level": 3, "adventure_level": 4, "family_friendly": 5, "relaxation_factor": 4}	{"topics": ["mountain forest ecology", "tree identification", "outdoor recreation skills"], "visitor_center": false, "ranger_programs": false, "junior_ranger_program": false}	{"parker": {"notes": "SkyPark is Parker's playground—zip lines, rock walls, mountain biking courses. He could spend an entire day here.", "suitable": true, "activities": ["SkyPark zip lines and climbing wall", "Mountain biking at SkyPark", "Heaps Peak Arboretum nature walk", "Lake Arrowhead boat tour"], "engagement_level": 5}, "xander": {"notes": "SkyPark has activities for little ones too. The forest campsite gives Xander pinecones, sticks, and nature to explore.", "suitable": true, "activities": ["SkyPark age-appropriate rides", "Forest play at campsite", "Lake Arrowhead playground", "Arboretum walk"], "engagement_level": 4}, "charlotte": {"notes": "The Santa's Village theming is magical for Charlotte. Gem panning and fairy-themed trails appeal to her explorer nature.", "suitable": true, "activities": ["SkyPark Santa's Village theme", "Panning for gems", "Forest fairy trails", "Lake village shopping"], "engagement_level": 5}}	https://www.recreation.gov/camping/campgrounds/232037	(877) 444-6777	\N	researching	0	{mountain,forest,theme-park,zip-lines,family-friendly,dry-camping}	{"SkyPark at Santa's Village is a unique mountain adventure park","Dense forest setting feels like a real mountain escape","Less crowded and cheaper than Big Bear","Heaps Peak Arboretum is a gentle nature walk","Only 2 hours from LA"}	{"No hookups—dry camping only","30ft max length is very tight for your 30ft 5th wheel—verify site dimensions","Less lake access than Big Bear (Lake Arrowhead is largely private)","Cell service is spotty"}	\N	\N	2026-02-04 15:15:22.991+00	2026-02-06 00:37:47.928713+00	[{"name": "places/ChIJO_9en85Xw4ARZEavg9jfTY8/reviews/Ci9DQUlRQUNvZENodHljRjlvT20xVmVGOVBYMmh1VlU1VWJsWkNkRk5ZTTJGUVIzYxAB", "text": {"text": "One of our favorite campsites in SoCal! Beautiful and clean campground! Bathrooms are super clean and well maintained. Showers are free with hot water. Potable water stations are spread out through the campground.\\n\\nThe campsite hosts are friendly and helpful. The fire pits have a built in grill on them. Our campsite that I chose was huge with room for 3, 10 person tents maybe. I'm not going to divulge which one it is, but I'll say it's in the 80+ as a hint. There are trails nearby that you can explore. Firewood is sold near the entrance.\\n\\nMy only complaint is that some campers are very inconsiderate, especially during quiet hours which is 10PM - 6AM. Not a deal breaker but could get really annoying if you're a light sleeper. Overall, we enjoyed this campground so much that we plan on coming back! Maybe with more family members in tow.", "languageCode": "en"}, "rating": 5, "publishTime": "2025-09-24T08:53:08.948860311Z", "originalText": {"text": "One of our favorite campsites in SoCal! Beautiful and clean campground! Bathrooms are super clean and well maintained. Showers are free with hot water. Potable water stations are spread out through the campground.\\n\\nThe campsite hosts are friendly and helpful. The fire pits have a built in grill on them. Our campsite that I chose was huge with room for 3, 10 person tents maybe. I'm not going to divulge which one it is, but I'll say it's in the 80+ as a hint. There are trails nearby that you can explore. Firewood is sold near the entrance.\\n\\nMy only complaint is that some campers are very inconsiderate, especially during quiet hours which is 10PM - 6AM. Not a deal breaker but could get really annoying if you're a light sleeper. Overall, we enjoyed this campground so much that we plan on coming back! Maybe with more family members in tow.", "languageCode": "en"}, "googleMapsUri": "https://www.google.com/maps/reviews/data=!4m6!14m5!1m4!2m3!1sCi9DQUlRQUNvZENodHljRjlvT20xVmVGOVBYMmh1VlU1VWJsWkNkRk5ZTTJGUVIzYxAB!2m1!1s0x80c357ce9f5eff3b:0x8f4ddfd883af4664", "flagContentUri": "https://www.google.com/local/content/rap/report?postId=Ci9DQUlRQUNvZENodHljRjlvT20xVmVGOVBYMmh1VlU1VWJsWkNkRk5ZTTJGUVIzYxAB&d=17924085&t=1", "authorAttribution": {"uri": "https://www.google.com/maps/contrib/106667560933024241507/reviews", "photoUri": "https://lh3.googleusercontent.com/a-/ALV-UjVcJQ4jQ15miFkg7CLvGSxep5-lZ_E0iNuSrDbuKvnDha9o1Fkj=s128-c0x00000000-cc-rp-mo-ba5", "displayName": "Joe Joe H"}, "relativePublishTimeDescription": "4 months ago"}, {"name": "places/ChIJO_9en85Xw4ARZEavg9jfTY8/reviews/Ci9DQUlRQUNvZENodHljRjlvT2kxNWJWZHFPVVJsWVRoNFdreENWVlJZT0ZCRE1WRRAB", "text": {"text": "Dogwood camping is pretty cool. Lot of trees and the smell of the fire wood burning and seeing the stars above at night, just chilling with your friends & having some beers and some barbecue is a must for everyone! The best part is.... no one bothers you & everybody keeps quiet around 10PM.\\nThe restrooms and the showers are pretty clean as well.", "languageCode": "en"}, "rating": 5, "publishTime": "2025-09-28T22:20:10.575776187Z", "originalText": {"text": "Dogwood camping is pretty cool. Lot of trees and the smell of the fire wood burning and seeing the stars above at night, just chilling with your friends & having some beers and some barbecue is a must for everyone! The best part is.... no one bothers you & everybody keeps quiet around 10PM.\\nThe restrooms and the showers are pretty clean as well.", "languageCode": "en"}, "googleMapsUri": "https://www.google.com/maps/reviews/data=!4m6!14m5!1m4!2m3!1sCi9DQUlRQUNvZENodHljRjlvT2kxNWJWZHFPVVJsWVRoNFdreENWVlJZT0ZCRE1WRRAB!2m1!1s0x80c357ce9f5eff3b:0x8f4ddfd883af4664", "flagContentUri": "https://www.google.com/local/content/rap/report?postId=Ci9DQUlRQUNvZENodHljRjlvT2kxNWJWZHFPVVJsWVRoNFdreENWVlJZT0ZCRE1WRRAB&d=17924085&t=1", "authorAttribution": {"uri": "https://www.google.com/maps/contrib/115815308148104050756/reviews", "photoUri": "https://lh3.googleusercontent.com/a/ACg8ocJWAmSyCPvDmk09vtj8dKMmmWNPMxGk2rLqvW3Tt9scpcIimQ=s128-c0x00000000-cc-rp-mo-ba5", "displayName": "christopher lee"}, "relativePublishTimeDescription": "4 months ago"}, {"name": "places/ChIJO_9en85Xw4ARZEavg9jfTY8/reviews/Ci9DQUlRQUNvZENodHljRjlvT2tGRGNFbFROUzFrTW1kc2IzVmFhbTk1TUVabE1IYxAB", "text": {"text": "Beautiful place, perfect for children to play and explore. It's much colder than the surrounding area, so remember to bring extra clothes. Most campsites have electricity, but no water. There are public water points, so you can bring some water containers. Book four to five months in advance to get the spot you want.", "languageCode": "en"}, "rating": 5, "publishTime": "2025-10-06T16:38:51.546893259Z", "originalText": {"text": "Beautiful place, perfect for children to play and explore. It's much colder than the surrounding area, so remember to bring extra clothes. Most campsites have electricity, but no water. There are public water points, so you can bring some water containers. Book four to five months in advance to get the spot you want.", "languageCode": "en"}, "googleMapsUri": "https://www.google.com/maps/reviews/data=!4m6!14m5!1m4!2m3!1sCi9DQUlRQUNvZENodHljRjlvT2tGRGNFbFROUzFrTW1kc2IzVmFhbTk1TUVabE1IYxAB!2m1!1s0x80c357ce9f5eff3b:0x8f4ddfd883af4664", "flagContentUri": "https://www.google.com/local/content/rap/report?postId=Ci9DQUlRQUNvZENodHljRjlvT2tGRGNFbFROUzFrTW1kc2IzVmFhbTk1TUVabE1IYxAB&d=17924085&t=1", "authorAttribution": {"uri": "https://www.google.com/maps/contrib/103554021438610582208/reviews", "photoUri": "https://lh3.googleusercontent.com/a/ACg8ocJGZB3oN3t7nTsykQG6ImjXsvBivMm4iiJKlMxC0G0FgzK05w=s128-c0x00000000-cc-rp-mo-ba3", "displayName": "TIANROU RAN"}, "relativePublishTimeDescription": "4 months ago"}, {"name": "places/ChIJO_9en85Xw4ARZEavg9jfTY8/reviews/Ci9DQUlRQUNvZENodHljRjlvT25aVWVYQk1aWGxHYm1wWVZGcENjM2xqWm05UmFXYxAB", "text": {"text": "Loved our stay at Dogwood Campground!\\nWe stayed in site#12. When we made the reservation it was noted that it could be difficult to back into, and indeed if our 21ft trailer had been any longer, it may not have worked, but we were prepared, and we appreciated the advanced warning. But after a few tries we got it, and we were extremely pleased with the results!\\nOur campsite upon our arrival was spotless, and had clearly been raked and tidied for us.\\nThe bathrooms were nearby, but not right next to. Restrooms were clean, not stinky at all, flush toilets and even soap, which is not always provided, but very much appreciated!\\nThe campground itself was quiet and peaceful.\\nFire rings were in good working condition, and water spigot was outside the nearby restroom.\\nArrowhead village was a short drive away.\\nWe definitely recommend this campground!😃", "languageCode": "en"}, "rating": 5, "publishTime": "2025-07-20T00:38:39.784572422Z", "originalText": {"text": "Loved our stay at Dogwood Campground!\\nWe stayed in site#12. When we made the reservation it was noted that it could be difficult to back into, and indeed if our 21ft trailer had been any longer, it may not have worked, but we were prepared, and we appreciated the advanced warning. But after a few tries we got it, and we were extremely pleased with the results!\\nOur campsite upon our arrival was spotless, and had clearly been raked and tidied for us.\\nThe bathrooms were nearby, but not right next to. Restrooms were clean, not stinky at all, flush toilets and even soap, which is not always provided, but very much appreciated!\\nThe campground itself was quiet and peaceful.\\nFire rings were in good working condition, and water spigot was outside the nearby restroom.\\nArrowhead village was a short drive away.\\nWe definitely recommend this campground!😃", "languageCode": "en"}, "googleMapsUri": "https://www.google.com/maps/reviews/data=!4m6!14m5!1m4!2m3!1sCi9DQUlRQUNvZENodHljRjlvT25aVWVYQk1aWGxHYm1wWVZGcENjM2xqWm05UmFXYxAB!2m1!1s0x80c357ce9f5eff3b:0x8f4ddfd883af4664", "flagContentUri": "https://www.google.com/local/content/rap/report?postId=Ci9DQUlRQUNvZENodHljRjlvT25aVWVYQk1aWGxHYm1wWVZGcENjM2xqWm05UmFXYxAB&d=17924085&t=1", "authorAttribution": {"uri": "https://www.google.com/maps/contrib/103208379769220715562/reviews", "photoUri": "https://lh3.googleusercontent.com/a/ACg8ocKVBDzKqrAPjGRZ8l4nq0_KofNFq5qAQmcbSNrm_LW2nZkARw=s128-c0x00000000-cc-rp-mo", "displayName": "Michele Perez"}, "relativePublishTimeDescription": "6 months ago"}, {"name": "places/ChIJO_9en85Xw4ARZEavg9jfTY8/reviews/Ci9DQUlRQUNvZENodHljRjlvT20xcmNVZEVNbTlxWVdoZkxXdFNUbFZsZVV0S01WRRAB", "text": {"text": "Our favorite campground with our little teardrop trailer. Very large campground with varied sites- tent to RV with electricity. Surrounded by cedars and plenty of shade. Grounds well maintained and staff easy-going and friendly. Jennifer at the front booth was very helpful. Lots of trails in park and nearby. We’ll be back multiple times. Only 2 hours from San Diego.", "languageCode": "en"}, "rating": 5, "publishTime": "2025-07-07T21:09:32.118019880Z", "originalText": {"text": "Our favorite campground with our little teardrop trailer. Very large campground with varied sites- tent to RV with electricity. Surrounded by cedars and plenty of shade. Grounds well maintained and staff easy-going and friendly. Jennifer at the front booth was very helpful. Lots of trails in park and nearby. We’ll be back multiple times. Only 2 hours from San Diego.", "languageCode": "en"}, "googleMapsUri": "https://www.google.com/maps/reviews/data=!4m6!14m5!1m4!2m3!1sCi9DQUlRQUNvZENodHljRjlvT20xcmNVZEVNbTlxWVdoZkxXdFNUbFZsZVV0S01WRRAB!2m1!1s0x80c357ce9f5eff3b:0x8f4ddfd883af4664", "flagContentUri": "https://www.google.com/local/content/rap/report?postId=Ci9DQUlRQUNvZENodHljRjlvT20xcmNVZEVNbTlxWVdoZkxXdFNUbFZsZVV0S01WRRAB&d=17924085&t=1", "authorAttribution": {"uri": "https://www.google.com/maps/contrib/108300840781266888023/reviews", "photoUri": "https://lh3.googleusercontent.com/a-/ALV-UjV3eFLXu8cZQmYvbVVwNdY6zBLPvbam4vO1JHOgtckFu1I4_9fn=s128-c0x00000000-cc-rp-mo", "displayName": "David Harris"}, "relativePublishTimeDescription": "7 months ago"}]	Dogwood Campground at Lake Arrowhead is a beloved, well-maintained family destination that consistently earns 5-star reviews for its cleanliness, beautiful natural setting among cedars, and peaceful atmosphere. Families particularly appreciate the spacious sites, clean facilities with free hot showers, and kid-friendly environment with plenty of trails to explore. The campground offers a perfect balance of natural beauty and convenience, located just a short drive from Arrowhead village.	{"summary": "Dogwood Campground at Lake Arrowhead is a beloved, well-maintained family destination that consistently earns 5-star reviews for its cleanliness, beautiful natural setting among cedars, and peaceful atmosphere. Families particularly appreciate the spacious sites, clean facilities with free hot showers, and kid-friendly environment with plenty of trails to explore. The campground offers a perfect balance of natural beauty and convenience, located just a short drive from Arrowhead village.", "negative": [{"text": "My only complaint is that some campers are very inconsiderate, especially during quiet hours which is 10PM - 6AM.", "author": "Joe Joe H", "rating": 5}, {"text": "It's much colder than the surrounding area, so remember to bring extra clothes.", "author": "TIANROU RAN", "rating": 5}], "positive": [{"text": "Beautiful place, perfect for children to play and explore.", "author": "TIANROU RAN", "rating": 5}, {"text": "Bathrooms are super clean and well maintained. Showers are free with hot water.", "author": "Joe Joe H", "rating": 5}, {"text": "Our campsite that I chose was huge with room for 3, 10 person tents maybe.", "author": "Joe Joe H", "rating": 5}], "last_updated": "2026-02-06T00:37:47.812Z"}	2026-02-06 00:37:40.091+00	national_forest	\N	\N
eac8cc06-8dd8-4d68-8a19-6a48a1882e81	b201a860-05a3-4ddc-bb89-4c4271177271	Avila Pismo Beach KOA	This well-maintained KOA sits in the hills above Avila Beach, providing a comfortable base for exploring the Avila/Pismo Beach/San Luis Obispo area. Full hookups, a pool, playground, and jumping pillow keep kids entertained at camp, while the world-class Bob Jones Trail bike path connects you directly to Avila Beach. Sycamore Mineral Springs Resort next door offers hot spring soaking. Port San Luis has fresh seafood and a working fishing pier.	Soak in natural hot springs overlooking a creek, bike a shaded trail to the beach, explore a historic port, and eat fish tacos at a pier—all from a comfortable KOA with pool and playground 3 hours from LA.	other	\N	7075 Ontario Rd, San Luis Obispo, CA 93405, USA	San Luis Obispo	CA	35.1833450	-120.7025814	ChIJt2twCo_37IAROWZO8p3MyIg	3.9	624	\N	{"hookups": "full", "cell_coverage": "good", "road_accessibility": "Easy access off US-101. Ontario Road has a gentle grade—no issues for 5th wheels.", "max_trailer_length_ft": 40, "fifth_wheel_accessible": true}	t	\N	Book through KOA website. Popular weekends book early. Midweek availability is usually good.	75.00	USD	\N	{"best": ["april", "may", "june", "september", "october"], "avoid": [], "notes": "Year-round destination. Summer is great but busy. Spring and fall are perfect with warm days, fewer crowds. Winter is mild."}	3 hours	\N	{"scenic_beauty": 3, "solitude_level": 2, "adventure_level": 3, "family_friendly": 5, "relaxation_factor": 5}	{"topics": ["hot springs geology", "commercial fishing", "coastal ecology"], "visitor_center": false, "ranger_programs": false, "junior_ranger_program": false}	{"parker": {"notes": "The bike path to the beach is a fun family adventure. Parker will enjoy the independence of biking and fishing.", "suitable": true, "activities": ["Bob Jones Trail bike ride to beach", "Fishing at Port San Luis pier", "Jumping pillow at KOA", "Pool time"], "engagement_level": 4}, "xander": {"notes": "Between the KOA pool, jumping pillow, beach, and hot springs, Xander will be in his element.", "suitable": true, "activities": ["Pool and jumping pillow at KOA", "Beach sand play at Avila", "Watching fishing boats", "Hot tub soaking"], "engagement_level": 5}, "charlotte": {"notes": "Charlotte will love the hot springs (outdoor tubs in the forest) and the sea lions at the port.", "suitable": true, "activities": ["Avila Beach play", "Hot springs soaking", "Port San Luis sea lions", "KOA playground"], "engagement_level": 4}}	https://www.avilapismorv.com/?utm_source=google&utm_medium=organic&utm_campaign=gbp	(805) 595-7111	\N	researching	0	{hot-springs,full-hookups,biking,beach,koa,pool,family-friendly}	{"Full hookups with pool, playground, and jumping pillow","Bob Jones Trail connects directly to Avila Beach by bike","Sycamore Mineral Springs hot spring soaking next door","Port San Luis has excellent fresh seafood","Close to both Avila Beach and Pismo Beach"}	{"KOA pricing is higher than state/county parks","The campground itself is not scenic—it's in the hills","3-hour drive makes this a full weekend commitment"}	\N	\N	2026-02-04 15:15:22.422+00	2026-02-06 00:38:34.840506+00	[{"name": "places/ChIJt2twCo_37IAROWZO8p3MyIg/reviews/Ci9DQUlRQUNvZENodHljRjlvT2psNE0weERSRmxsZFhwRVJURjFUelZJYW1aWWNIYxAB", "text": {"text": "Such a beautiful experience and staff that gave top notch service.  From the welcome with fresh baked cookies to the on-site dog park every part of the experience was amazing.  If you are heading to the area for a stay be ready for a quiet and relaxing vibe, excellent staff (who will show you to your space,  not just give you a map) , a beautiful view and close to so many adventures in Pismo and Avila.  My husband and I will definitely be back for a second visit.  We have stayed at many places,  but this one stole my heart ❤️.  It was like camping in the woods with the amenities of a resort/rv park and they have cabins and site wifi. Biggest plus was the dog park,  swimming pool and outdoor game area.", "languageCode": "en"}, "rating": 5, "publishTime": "2025-12-06T05:51:42.123956335Z", "originalText": {"text": "Such a beautiful experience and staff that gave top notch service.  From the welcome with fresh baked cookies to the on-site dog park every part of the experience was amazing.  If you are heading to the area for a stay be ready for a quiet and relaxing vibe, excellent staff (who will show you to your space,  not just give you a map) , a beautiful view and close to so many adventures in Pismo and Avila.  My husband and I will definitely be back for a second visit.  We have stayed at many places,  but this one stole my heart ❤️.  It was like camping in the woods with the amenities of a resort/rv park and they have cabins and site wifi. Biggest plus was the dog park,  swimming pool and outdoor game area.", "languageCode": "en"}, "googleMapsUri": "https://www.google.com/maps/reviews/data=!4m6!14m5!1m4!2m3!1sCi9DQUlRQUNvZENodHljRjlvT2psNE0weERSRmxsZFhwRVJURjFUelZJYW1aWWNIYxAB!2m1!1s0x80ecf78f0a706bb7:0x88c8cc9df24e6639", "flagContentUri": "https://www.google.com/local/content/rap/report?postId=Ci9DQUlRQUNvZENodHljRjlvT2psNE0weERSRmxsZFhwRVJURjFUelZJYW1aWWNIYxAB&d=17924085&t=1", "authorAttribution": {"uri": "https://www.google.com/maps/contrib/102210561535751975783/reviews", "photoUri": "https://lh3.googleusercontent.com/a-/ALV-UjWUdWP6ubFqfcAUXtSfi9BTzebzx9CoOukH3mWm_nEBFU8w1WnVBQ=s128-c0x00000000-cc-rp-mo-ba2", "displayName": "Timeko Jones"}, "relativePublishTimeDescription": "2 months ago"}, {"name": "places/ChIJt2twCo_37IAROWZO8p3MyIg/reviews/Ci9DQUlRQUNvZENodHljRjlvT2xWcE5VODNNVUZJZVRoRlpFZFpORGxsYldjemExRRAB", "text": {"text": "The staff here is beyond helpful and accommodating! The back- in sites are beautiful and private. The grounds, bathrooms and showers are spotless; great place for families. Avila and Pismo beaches are minutes away. Farmers market, ice cream shop and petting zoo right across the street…..We’d definitely stay here again", "languageCode": "en"}, "rating": 5, "publishTime": "2026-01-14T20:33:42.856407603Z", "originalText": {"text": "The staff here is beyond helpful and accommodating! The back- in sites are beautiful and private. The grounds, bathrooms and showers are spotless; great place for families. Avila and Pismo beaches are minutes away. Farmers market, ice cream shop and petting zoo right across the street…..We’d definitely stay here again", "languageCode": "en"}, "googleMapsUri": "https://www.google.com/maps/reviews/data=!4m6!14m5!1m4!2m3!1sCi9DQUlRQUNvZENodHljRjlvT2xWcE5VODNNVUZJZVRoRlpFZFpORGxsYldjemExRRAB!2m1!1s0x80ecf78f0a706bb7:0x88c8cc9df24e6639", "flagContentUri": "https://www.google.com/local/content/rap/report?postId=Ci9DQUlRQUNvZENodHljRjlvT2xWcE5VODNNVUZJZVRoRlpFZFpORGxsYldjemExRRAB&d=17924085&t=1", "authorAttribution": {"uri": "https://www.google.com/maps/contrib/110036224382574098669/reviews", "photoUri": "https://lh3.googleusercontent.com/a/ACg8ocLhXqxnxwh1BLo3JYJxoGXj8nEKhJ-ow3klHKhE4LGpavFgPw=s128-c0x00000000-cc-rp-mo", "displayName": "Tammie Schuett"}, "relativePublishTimeDescription": "3 weeks ago"}, {"name": "places/ChIJt2twCo_37IAROWZO8p3MyIg/reviews/Ci9DQUlRQUNvZENodHljRjlvT2pCS1YwRXpTMEp3WkZaNWQzUm9WREptVUZVd01YYxAB", "text": {"text": "The first night was ok (we didn’t get any fresh baked cookies not that I care but should mention). Freeway noise is real. Glad we did our laundry then because the water was shut off in the morning due to a plumbing mains issue. They said it would only take a few hours but it was off for the rest of the day and the next day. We left early after two nights to get to a new place with water. Then, several weeks after we stayed there I start receiving emails from Highway West Vacations email list, a list I never signed up for. I know it was from them because I create a unique email for every company I do business with using Simple Login. When they asked for my email upon sign in they did not inform me I would be signed up on a marketing email list.", "languageCode": "en"}, "rating": 2, "publishTime": "2026-01-08T17:31:15.952484840Z", "originalText": {"text": "The first night was ok (we didn’t get any fresh baked cookies not that I care but should mention). Freeway noise is real. Glad we did our laundry then because the water was shut off in the morning due to a plumbing mains issue. They said it would only take a few hours but it was off for the rest of the day and the next day. We left early after two nights to get to a new place with water. Then, several weeks after we stayed there I start receiving emails from Highway West Vacations email list, a list I never signed up for. I know it was from them because I create a unique email for every company I do business with using Simple Login. When they asked for my email upon sign in they did not inform me I would be signed up on a marketing email list.", "languageCode": "en"}, "googleMapsUri": "https://www.google.com/maps/reviews/data=!4m6!14m5!1m4!2m3!1sCi9DQUlRQUNvZENodHljRjlvT2pCS1YwRXpTMEp3WkZaNWQzUm9WREptVUZVd01YYxAB!2m1!1s0x80ecf78f0a706bb7:0x88c8cc9df24e6639", "flagContentUri": "https://www.google.com/local/content/rap/report?postId=Ci9DQUlRQUNvZENodHljRjlvT2pCS1YwRXpTMEp3WkZaNWQzUm9WREptVUZVd01YYxAB&d=17924085&t=1", "authorAttribution": {"uri": "https://www.google.com/maps/contrib/100712468240165074939/reviews", "photoUri": "https://lh3.googleusercontent.com/a-/ALV-UjVe4FVrzYqKYugHVhld_Q5s2pfzgLj72y0rucw_YhPM5wCMIm0=s128-c0x00000000-cc-rp-mo", "displayName": "Vic Tory"}, "relativePublishTimeDescription": "4 weeks ago"}, {"name": "places/ChIJt2twCo_37IAROWZO8p3MyIg/reviews/Ci9DQUlRQUNvZENodHljRjlvT2tveFRUTk9lV2g2YkV4V1NFSTBhMXA2UW5kdE9FRRAB", "text": {"text": "We were there this weekend. We had a relaxing time there. Personal helped my husband back up our trailer. We had a perfect spot, next to the pool. We meet some great people. Staff were awesome. An amazing place. We are going to make it our spot to go to.", "languageCode": "en"}, "rating": 5, "publishTime": "2025-09-23T19:58:03.451720697Z", "originalText": {"text": "We were there this weekend. We had a relaxing time there. Personal helped my husband back up our trailer. We had a perfect spot, next to the pool. We meet some great people. Staff were awesome. An amazing place. We are going to make it our spot to go to.", "languageCode": "en"}, "googleMapsUri": "https://www.google.com/maps/reviews/data=!4m6!14m5!1m4!2m3!1sCi9DQUlRQUNvZENodHljRjlvT2tveFRUTk9lV2g2YkV4V1NFSTBhMXA2UW5kdE9FRRAB!2m1!1s0x80ecf78f0a706bb7:0x88c8cc9df24e6639", "flagContentUri": "https://www.google.com/local/content/rap/report?postId=Ci9DQUlRQUNvZENodHljRjlvT2tveFRUTk9lV2g2YkV4V1NFSTBhMXA2UW5kdE9FRRAB&d=17924085&t=1", "authorAttribution": {"uri": "https://www.google.com/maps/contrib/110245532736671228237/reviews", "photoUri": "https://lh3.googleusercontent.com/a/ACg8ocI4o__wBSi9_pGV6npEd0J7ah5H2ux4P0HBd9gza7DklhQiWQ=s128-c0x00000000-cc-rp-mo", "displayName": "Gloria Ortiz"}, "relativePublishTimeDescription": "4 months ago"}, {"name": "places/ChIJt2twCo_37IAROWZO8p3MyIg/reviews/Ci9DQUlRQUNvZENodHljRjlvT21WMFVIaDVkM2gyWTNCWFlVSm1OemxMU0dZelExRRAB", "text": {"text": "We just got home from our stay at the Avila Pismo Rv and resort park. It was very relaxing and peaceful. It's in a beautiful area. The people who work there are very nice and accommodating. Our cabin was on the small side but very functional with 2 bdrms.  It was cute. However the air conditioner didn't work in our place. And the cable was going out intermittently on our 3rd night. We think the place would benefit from a ceiling fan in the master bdrm. But overall we loved staying there and it was close to a lot of beautiful beaches and walking, running trails, hiking. A farm market within walking distance.  Like right down the street. Dogs are also allowed there. That was a big plus for us.😍⛱️💜💙♥️", "languageCode": "en"}, "rating": 4, "publishTime": "20