a dog park, pool, and game areas. Most guests love the peaceful, resort-like experience with easy access to beaches and local attractions. The overwhelming sentiment is positive, with visitors frequently mentioning they plan to return.", "negative": [{"text": "Freeway noise is real. We left early after two nights to get to a new place with water due to a plumbing mains issue that lasted for the rest of the day and the next day.", "author": "Vic Tory", "rating": 2}, {"text": "However the air conditioner didn't work in our place. And the cable was going out intermittently on our 3rd night.", "author": "Wendy Stone", "rating": 4}], "positive": [{"text": "The grounds, bathrooms and showers are spotless; great place for families. Farmers market, ice cream shop and petting zoo right across the street", "author": "Tammie Schuett", "rating": 5}, {"text": "From the welcome with fresh baked cookies to the on-site dog park every part of the experience was amazing. It was like camping in the woods with the amenities of a resort/rv park", "author": "Timeko Jones", "rating": 5}, {"text": "We had a perfect spot, next to the pool. We meet some great people. Staff were awesome.", "author": "Gloria Ortiz", "rating": 5}], "last_updated": "2026-02-06T00:38:34.727Z"}	2026-02-06 00:38:28.219+00	private_campground	\N	\N
29659129-f2f6-4e1f-af11-ebed35f05fc6	b201a860-05a3-4ddc-bb89-4c4271177271	Refugio State Beach	Refugio State Beach is a gem of a campground 20 miles west of Santa Barbara, where palm-lined campsites sit steps from a gorgeous cove beach. The protected waters are perfect for kayaking and swimming. A bike path connects Refugio to El Capitan State Beach along the coast. The beach has lifeguards in summer and a small camp store. The campground's pirate and smuggling history (the Ortega family ran a smuggling operation here in the 1800s) adds character to campfire time.	Camp directly on one of the most beautiful beaches near Santa Barbara with guided kayak tours, a coastal bike trail to El Capitan, and a pirate smuggling history that makes campfire stories legendary.	state_parks	\N	10 Refugio Beach Rd, Goleta, CA 93117, USA	Goleta	CA	34.4631659	-120.0701354	ChIJD98AAh5M6YARLELkWiWUinc	4.6	1531	\N	{"hookups": "none", "cell_coverage": "good", "road_accessibility": "Easy access directly off Highway 101 at Refugio Road exit. Short drive to campground. Paved interior roads.", "max_trailer_length_ft": 30, "fifth_wheel_accessible": true}	t	\N	Book via ReserveCalifornia.com up to 6 months ahead. Summer weekends are extremely competitive. IMPORTANT: Max RV length is 30ft—your 30ft rig is right at the limit. Verify your specific site dimensions before booking.	45.00	USD	\N	{"best": ["april", "may", "june", "september", "october"], "avoid": ["december", "january", "february"], "notes": "Summer is peak but fills up months ahead. Spring and fall have best weather and easier bookings. Winter is mild but campground may close during heavy rains. Subject to rainy season closures Dec-March."}	2 hours	\N	{"scenic_beauty": 5, "solitude_level": 2, "adventure_level": 3, "family_friendly": 5, "relaxation_factor": 5}	{"topics": ["ocean safety", "coastal ecology", "California history", "smuggling history"], "visitor_center": false, "ranger_programs": true, "junior_ranger_program": true}	{"parker": {"notes": "The bike path to El Capitan is a great adventure. Parker will love having the beach right outside the tent.", "suitable": true, "activities": ["Coastal bike ride to El Capitan", "Kayaking in the cove", "Boogie boarding", "Beach basketball"], "engagement_level": 4}, "xander": {"notes": "The cove is calm and safe for toddlers. Xander can play in the sand with the ocean right there.", "suitable": true, "activities": ["Beach sand play all day", "Gentle wave wading", "Squirrel watching at campsite", "Playground swings"], "engagement_level": 5}, "charlotte": {"notes": "Being steps from the beach is Charlotte's dream. The low-tide rock pools and shell collecting are perfect for her.", "suitable": true, "activities": ["Shell hunting at low tide", "Kayak tour", "Beach exploring", "Camp store visits"], "engagement_level": 5}}	https://www.parks.ca.gov/?page_id=603	(805) 968-1033	\N	researching	0	{beach,kayaking,biking,state-park,dry-camping,family-friendly,santa-barbara}	{"Campsites are literally steps from a beautiful beach","Protected cove for safe swimming and kayaking","Bike path to El Capitan State Beach","Junior Ranger program in summer","Pirate/smuggling history for campfire stories"}	{"30ft max RV length—your rig is right at the limit (verify site dimensions)","No hookups—dry camping only","Train noise from adjacent Amtrak tracks","Books up very quickly for summer"}	\N	\N	2026-02-04 15:15:24.327+00	2026-02-06 00:36:18.242159+00	[{"name": "places/ChIJD98AAh5M6YARLELkWiWUinc/reviews/Ci9DQUlRQUNvZENodHljRjlvT2xwaWNra3hNVVo0ZEY5YVgwbDRjbWhoZDFWSFQwRRAB", "text": {"text": "Had a great time with my family, but I do have to warn you about the showers and restrooms.\\n\\nThe showers take tokens for warm water. There's only 1 machine on each side of the lake for both bathrooms. They only take card.\\n\\nNext are the restrooms, no soap or anything to dry your hands with. Be sure to bring your own every time. And to be on the look out for the sparrows above you as you go to the restroom. There's piles of poop under them for a reason.\\n\\nBesides that, the close proximity to the beach and the relative quietness of the other campers make it a great place to camp. The views and the sounds of the ground squirrels during the day and the racoons at night make each day a adventure of its own.\\n\\nDon't forget to read about the beaches history with New Spain!", "languageCode": "en"}, "rating": 5, "publishTime": "2025-06-27T17:33:50.586204599Z", "originalText": {"text": "Had a great time with my family, but I do have to warn you about the showers and restrooms.\\n\\nThe showers take tokens for warm water. There's only 1 machine on each side of the lake for both bathrooms. They only take card.\\n\\nNext are the restrooms, no soap or anything to dry your hands with. Be sure to bring your own every time. And to be on the look out for the sparrows above you as you go to the restroom. There's piles of poop under them for a reason.\\n\\nBesides that, the close proximity to the beach and the relative quietness of the other campers make it a great place to camp. The views and the sounds of the ground squirrels during the day and the racoons at night make each day a adventure of its own.\\n\\nDon't forget to read about the beaches history with New Spain!", "languageCode": "en"}, "googleMapsUri": "https://www.google.com/maps/reviews/data=!4m6!14m5!1m4!2m3!1sCi9DQUlRQUNvZENodHljRjlvT2xwaWNra3hNVVo0ZEY5YVgwbDRjbWhoZDFWSFQwRRAB!2m1!1s0x80e94c1e0200df0f:0x778a94255ae4422c", "flagContentUri": "https://www.google.com/local/content/rap/report?postId=Ci9DQUlRQUNvZENodHljRjlvT2xwaWNra3hNVVo0ZEY5YVgwbDRjbWhoZDFWSFQwRRAB&d=17924085&t=1", "authorAttribution": {"uri": "https://www.google.com/maps/contrib/104154432396323704992/reviews", "photoUri": "https://lh3.googleusercontent.com/a-/ALV-UjXCHcrEa88S3-nZ5zWvqJcyiXK2Ty1eQKjEEiHBzGbsYy0svZ8nXQ=s128-c0x00000000-cc-rp-mo-ba4", "displayName": "Isaiah Sotelo"}, "relativePublishTimeDescription": "7 months ago"}, {"name": "places/ChIJD98AAh5M6YARLELkWiWUinc/reviews/Ci9DQUlRQUNvZENodHljRjlvT2pkWVVqZE1VbVJGYXpNemR6aFRhRVZuV25KWVYzYxAB", "text": {"text": "Incredibly scenic campground. Hiker biker spots for $10 a night right by the beach! Water was perfect.\\nOnly complaint is the lack of outlets for charging.", "languageCode": "en"}, "rating": 5, "publishTime": "2025-09-03T18:35:22.705693662Z", "originalText": {"text": "Incredibly scenic campground. Hiker biker spots for $10 a night right by the beach! Water was perfect.\\nOnly complaint is the lack of outlets for charging.", "languageCode": "en"}, "googleMapsUri": "https://www.google.com/maps/reviews/data=!4m6!14m5!1m4!2m3!1sCi9DQUlRQUNvZENodHljRjlvT2pkWVVqZE1VbVJGYXpNemR6aFRhRVZuV25KWVYzYxAB!2m1!1s0x80e94c1e0200df0f:0x778a94255ae4422c", "flagContentUri": "https://www.google.com/local/content/rap/report?postId=Ci9DQUlRQUNvZENodHljRjlvT2pkWVVqZE1VbVJGYXpNemR6aFRhRVZuV25KWVYzYxAB&d=17924085&t=1", "authorAttribution": {"uri": "https://www.google.com/maps/contrib/110861273488894959342/reviews", "photoUri": "https://lh3.googleusercontent.com/a-/ALV-UjUAK9iUmrJ3xp8Q7dQgmWbXgKH707UQ7mc91y1IGzWM2lwz3ZnLtA=s128-c0x00000000-cc-rp-mo", "displayName": "Ivory MacCracken"}, "relativePublishTimeDescription": "5 months ago"}, {"name": "places/ChIJD98AAh5M6YARLELkWiWUinc/reviews/Ci9DQUlRQUNvZENodHljRjlvT25FNFNWaDRkV0Y1TFd0alQzcG9SVmRvUkhJemFGRRAB", "text": {"text": "Love this beach! Great place to spend the day! They have a little store for campers and beach goers incase you forget anything.", "languageCode": "en"}, "rating": 5, "publishTime": "2025-07-15T23:05:05.868973816Z", "originalText": {"text": "Love this beach! Great place to spend the day! They have a little store for campers and beach goers incase you forget anything.", "languageCode": "en"}, "googleMapsUri": "https://www.google.com/maps/reviews/data=!4m6!14m5!1m4!2m3!1sCi9DQUlRQUNvZENodHljRjlvT25FNFNWaDRkV0Y1TFd0alQzcG9SVmRvUkhJemFGRRAB!2m1!1s0x80e94c1e0200df0f:0x778a94255ae4422c", "flagContentUri": "https://www.google.com/local/content/rap/report?postId=Ci9DQUlRQUNvZENodHljRjlvT25FNFNWaDRkV0Y1TFd0alQzcG9SVmRvUkhJemFGRRAB&d=17924085&t=1", "authorAttribution": {"uri": "https://www.google.com/maps/contrib/109340555768226308555/reviews", "photoUri": "https://lh3.googleusercontent.com/a-/ALV-UjVMly_4exvsGH_kUdyiGkFsEXMtsIyki__kmwthKpekmL76PfQ8lQ=s128-c0x00000000-cc-rp-mo-ba4", "displayName": "Ronnie Tow"}, "relativePublishTimeDescription": "6 months ago"}, {"name": "places/ChIJD98AAh5M6YARLELkWiWUinc/reviews/Ci9DQUlRQUNvZENodHljRjlvT2pCd1pYRk9iSG81T0hoNmFrVTRWWG96VEhnMFgyYxAB", "text": {"text": "Our favorite beach campground bar none! We've been here many times over the years and it never disappoints!", "languageCode": "en"}, "rating": 5, "publishTime": "2025-12-08T02:08:48.411535598Z", "originalText": {"text": "Our favorite beach campground bar none! We've been here many times over the years and it never disappoints!", "languageCode": "en"}, "googleMapsUri": "https://www.google.com/maps/reviews/data=!4m6!14m5!1m4!2m3!1sCi9DQUlRQUNvZENodHljRjlvT2pCd1pYRk9iSG81T0hoNmFrVTRWWG96VEhnMFgyYxAB!2m1!1s0x80e94c1e0200df0f:0x778a94255ae4422c", "flagContentUri": "https://www.google.com/local/content/rap/report?postId=Ci9DQUlRQUNvZENodHljRjlvT2pCd1pYRk9iSG81T0hoNmFrVTRWWG96VEhnMFgyYxAB&d=17924085&t=1", "authorAttribution": {"uri": "https://www.google.com/maps/contrib/113035774564919589056/reviews", "photoUri": "https://lh3.googleusercontent.com/a-/ALV-UjWx7YSVtwRAw1JeMf8jCEbjQrtXLqzO3TFvTlkk_ERXaJp4RUeMiA=s128-c0x00000000-cc-rp-mo-ba2", "displayName": "Steve Sirk"}, "relativePublishTimeDescription": "a month ago"}, {"name": "places/ChIJD98AAh5M6YARLELkWiWUinc/reviews/Ci9DQUlRQUNvZENodHljRjlvT2xGMFkzUjVVbk5aVDBVeU9VUmtSa3ROWDA5amNVRRAB", "text": {"text": "Last weekend I tried out 3 Hike and Bike locations ( Refugio, Carpinteria and Leo Carrillo) around Santa Barbara.  Refugio is the closest to the beach and an optimal location right next to the beach but it is also next to the kids playground.", "languageCode": "en"}, "rating": 4, "publishTime": "2025-06-30T15:13:12.948540331Z", "originalText": {"text": "Last weekend I tried out 3 Hike and Bike locations ( Refugio, Carpinteria and Leo Carrillo) around Santa Barbara.  Refugio is the closest to the beach and an optimal location right next to the beach but it is also next to the kids playground.", "languageCode": "en"}, "googleMapsUri": "https://www.google.com/maps/reviews/data=!4m6!14m5!1m4!2m3!1sCi9DQUlRQUNvZENodHljRjlvT2xGMFkzUjVVbk5aVDBVeU9VUmtSa3ROWDA5amNVRRAB!2m1!1s0x80e94c1e0200df0f:0x778a94255ae4422c", "flagContentUri": "https://www.google.com/local/content/rap/report?postId=Ci9DQUlRQUNvZENodHljRjlvT2xGMFkzUjVVbk5aVDBVeU9VUmtSa3ROWDA5amNVRRAB&d=17924085&t=1", "authorAttribution": {"uri": "https://www.google.com/maps/contrib/105143391725000303125/reviews", "photoUri": "https://lh3.googleusercontent.com/a-/ALV-UjVa0lvjX94Kbf8W7pBYS5mSr7CRF_Lf-S6Fn8peGhTAFKDSiv45=s128-c0x00000000-cc-rp-mo-ba5", "displayName": "E David Callender"}, "relativePublishTimeDescription": "7 months ago"}]	Refugio State Beach is a beloved scenic campground with direct beach access that consistently delights families and campers. The location offers incredible views, affordable hiker/biker spots, and a peaceful atmosphere, though visitors should be prepared for basic facility limitations. Despite minor inconveniences with restrooms and amenities, it's considered a top-choice destination that keeps families returning year after year.	{"summary": "Refugio State Beach is a beloved scenic campground with direct beach access that consistently delights families and campers. The location offers incredible views, affordable hiker/biker spots, and a peaceful atmosphere, though visitors should be prepared for basic facility limitations. Despite minor inconveniences with restrooms and amenities, it's considered a top-choice destination that keeps families returning year after year.", "negative": [{"text": "The showers take tokens for warm water... Next are the restrooms, no soap or anything to dry your hands with.", "author": "Isaiah Sotelo", "rating": 5}, {"text": "Only complaint is the lack of outlets for charging.", "author": "Ivory MacCracken", "rating": 5}], "positive": [{"text": "Our favorite beach campground bar none! We've been here many times over the years and it never disappoints!", "author": "Steve Sirk", "rating": 5}, {"text": "Hiker biker spots for $10 a night right by the beach! Water was perfect.", "author": "Ivory MacCracken", "rating": 5}, {"text": "They have a little store for campers and beach goers incase you forget anything.", "author": "Ronnie Tow", "rating": 5}], "last_updated": "2026-02-06T00:36:18.165Z"}	2026-02-06 00:36:11.093+00	state_park	\N	\N
6fa35c8e-4c2e-4040-a65a-471e3d90cec8	b201a860-05a3-4ddc-bb89-4c4271177271	Idyllwild Regional Park	Idyllwild is a charming mountain town in the San Jacinto Mountains that feels like a small slice of the Pacific Northwest transplanted to Southern California. The regional park campground has water/electric hookups and sits in a beautiful pine forest. The town has an arts scene, the Idyllwild Nature Center (one of the best in SoCal), excellent family hiking, and a famously quirky small-town character. The honorary mayor is a golden retriever, there's a summer concert series, and the forest trails are stunning.	A mountain artist colony at 5,400 feet tucked among towering pines where a world-class nature center teaches kids about local wildlife and the town's quirky mayor is a golden retriever named Max.	other	\N	54000 Riverside County Playground Rd, Idyllwild-Pine Cove, CA 92549, USA	Idyllwild	CA	33.7436783	-116.7241027	ChIJ4w-hCRIS24ARNi89W_frHlE	4.7	693	\N	{"hookups": "water_electric", "cell_coverage": "good", "road_accessibility": "IMPORTANT: Take Highway 74 from Hemet (the 'Palms to Pines Scenic Byway'). Do NOT take Highway 243 from Banning—too narrow and steep for 5th wheels. Highway 74 has wide lanes and manageable grades.", "max_trailer_length_ft": 34, "fifth_wheel_accessible": true}	t	\N	Book through Riverside County Parks (rivcoparks.org). Generally easier to book than Big Bear. Campground has a small camp store.	35.00	USD	\N	{"best": ["may", "june", "july", "august", "september", "october"], "avoid": ["january", "february"], "notes": "Summer is perfect at elevation. Fall is gorgeous. Winter can bring snow—roads may require chains. Spring is cool and pleasant."}	2.5 hours	\N	{"scenic_beauty": 5, "solitude_level": 3, "adventure_level": 3, "family_friendly": 5, "relaxation_factor": 5}	{"topics": ["mountain ecology", "San Jacinto wilderness", "local wildlife", "Native American history"], "visitor_center": true, "ranger_programs": true, "junior_ranger_program": false}	{"parker": {"notes": "The forest trails offer good hiking challenges. Parker will enjoy the boulder fields and nature center's wildlife exhibits.", "suitable": true, "activities": ["Ernie Maxwell Scenic Trail hike", "Rock climbing area near town", "Nature Center exhibits", "Biking through town"], "engagement_level": 4}, "xander": {"notes": "The Nature Center's live animals and the creek behind the campground give Xander plenty of sensory stimulation.", "suitable": true, "activities": ["Nature Center animals", "Creek play", "Pine forest exploring", "Town playground"], "engagement_level": 4}, "charlotte": {"notes": "The Nature Center has live reptiles and exhibits. Charlotte will love the mountain town charm and meeting the dog mayor.", "suitable": true, "activities": ["Idyllwild Nature Center live animals", "Forest fairy houses trail", "Art gallery browsing", "Meeting Mayor Max the dog"], "engagement_level": 5}}	https://rivcoparks.org/regional-parks-campgrounds/idyllwild-regional-park	(951) 659-2656	\N	researching	0	{mountain,nature-center,forest,art-town,water-electric,hiking,charming}	{"Idyllwild Nature Center is one of the best nature education centers in SoCal","Pacific Northwest forest feel just 2.5 hours from LA","Charming mountain town with art galleries and restaurants","Water/electric hookups at a reasonable price","Beautiful Ernie Maxwell Trail for family hiking"}	{"Road access requires careful route planning for 5th wheels","Town is small—1-2 day maximum for most families","Limited lake/water activities compared to Big Bear"}	\N	\N	2026-02-04 15:15:23.487+00	2026-02-06 00:36:56.129278+00	[{"name": "places/ChIJ4w-hCRIS24ARNi89W_frHlE/reviews/Ci9DQUlRQUNvZENodHljRjlvT200dGIxOXhUM05CY2tOQ1MwZGlSMVZvUlRaUlQwRRAB", "text": {"text": "This is a really nice campground! Some sites are on a slant, so it helps to research before booking. We stayed at site #58, which was a great choice—it was close enough to the restrooms for convenience (especially helpful since we had a pregnant friend with us) but not so close that it was noisy. The restrooms are flushable and well-kept, though I wouldn’t recommend the sites directly behind them since you’ll hear a lot of flushing. It’s also super convenient that the campground is right in town, so we had quick access to anything we needed. One thing to note is that hammocks aren’t allowed, but overall we really enjoyed our stay.", "languageCode": "en"}, "rating": 5, "publishTime": "2025-09-08T20:15:31.895230751Z", "originalText": {"text": "This is a really nice campground! Some sites are on a slant, so it helps to research before booking. We stayed at site #58, which was a great choice—it was close enough to the restrooms for convenience (especially helpful since we had a pregnant friend with us) but not so close that it was noisy. The restrooms are flushable and well-kept, though I wouldn’t recommend the sites directly behind them since you’ll hear a lot of flushing. It’s also super convenient that the campground is right in town, so we had quick access to anything we needed. One thing to note is that hammocks aren’t allowed, but overall we really enjoyed our stay.", "languageCode": "en"}, "googleMapsUri": "https://www.google.com/maps/reviews/data=!4m6!14m5!1m4!2m3!1sCi9DQUlRQUNvZENodHljRjlvT200dGIxOXhUM05CY2tOQ1MwZGlSMVZvUlRaUlQwRRAB!2m1!1s0x80db121209a10fe3:0x511eebf75b3d2f36", "flagContentUri": "https://www.google.com/local/content/rap/report?postId=Ci9DQUlRQUNvZENodHljRjlvT200dGIxOXhUM05CY2tOQ1MwZGlSMVZvUlRaUlQwRRAB&d=17924085&t=1", "authorAttribution": {"uri": "https://www.google.com/maps/contrib/100300379804538470730/reviews", "photoUri": "https://lh3.googleusercontent.com/a-/ALV-UjXz6Qpu10xGdimh0t4kziy1tgZb5-Jv60qhJJmIFZAXviBehq_J=s128-c0x00000000-cc-rp-mo-ba3", "displayName": "Jessica"}, "relativePublishTimeDescription": "5 months ago"}, {"name": "places/ChIJ4w-hCRIS24ARNi89W_frHlE/reviews/Ci9DQUlRQUNvZENodHljRjlvT25CVU1UaHRWMlZOVlU5dlowWktWbEJNYUdkVWRtYxAB", "text": {"text": "Needs to update payment system. Their online payment service doesn’t work, you would need exact cash. Bring your own pen. Not much to see for the $6 fee and additional $2 pet fee for day use. Recommend going elsewhere.", "languageCode": "en"}, "rating": 1, "publishTime": "2025-12-19T19:12:51.852145984Z", "originalText": {"text": "Needs to update payment system. Their online payment service doesn’t work, you would need exact cash. Bring your own pen. Not much to see for the $6 fee and additional $2 pet fee for day use. Recommend going elsewhere.", "languageCode": "en"}, "googleMapsUri": "https://www.google.com/maps/reviews/data=!4m6!14m5!1m4!2m3!1sCi9DQUlRQUNvZENodHljRjlvT25CVU1UaHRWMlZOVlU5dlowWktWbEJNYUdkVWRtYxAB!2m1!1s0x80db121209a10fe3:0x511eebf75b3d2f36", "flagContentUri": "https://www.google.com/local/content/rap/report?postId=Ci9DQUlRQUNvZENodHljRjlvT25CVU1UaHRWMlZOVlU5dlowWktWbEJNYUdkVWRtYxAB&d=17924085&t=1", "authorAttribution": {"uri": "https://www.google.com/maps/contrib/108855687959105122024/reviews", "photoUri": "https://lh3.googleusercontent.com/a/ACg8ocJgxII7Z6vaQwVPfmQGSoS1H_5Ee9YNY8f4sqg9lE2tx5ufwQ=s128-c0x00000000-cc-rp-mo", "displayName": "Marilu Viveros"}, "relativePublishTimeDescription": "a month ago"}, {"name": "places/ChIJ4w-hCRIS24ARNi89W_frHlE/reviews/ChZDSUhNMG9nS0VNNmV1TmZWcnZpeWZnEAE", "text": {"text": "Tucked away in the mountains, Idyllwild Regional Park is pure magic. The trails weave through towering pines and massive boulders, with quiet pockets of shade that feel like secret hideouts. Campsites are clean, well-spaced, and you actually get some real peace and quiet without feeling packed in like sardines. Morning walks here are insane — crisp air, birds everywhere, and those slow-burn sunrise colors bleeding through the trees. If you want that old-school California mountain town vibe without the chaos, this place hits different.", "languageCode": "en"}, "rating": 5, "publishTime": "2025-05-13T06:34:39.958179Z", "originalText": {"text": "Tucked away in the mountains, Idyllwild Regional Park is pure magic. The trails weave through towering pines and massive boulders, with quiet pockets of shade that feel like secret hideouts. Campsites are clean, well-spaced, and you actually get some real peace and quiet without feeling packed in like sardines. Morning walks here are insane — crisp air, birds everywhere, and those slow-burn sunrise colors bleeding through the trees. If you want that old-school California mountain town vibe without the chaos, this place hits different.", "languageCode": "en"}, "googleMapsUri": "https://www.google.com/maps/reviews/data=!4m6!14m5!1m4!2m3!1sChZDSUhNMG9nS0VNNmV1TmZWcnZpeWZnEAE!2m1!1s0x80db121209a10fe3:0x511eebf75b3d2f36", "flagContentUri": "https://www.google.com/local/content/rap/report?postId=ChZDSUhNMG9nS0VNNmV1TmZWcnZpeWZnEAE&d=17924085&t=1", "authorAttribution": {"uri": "https://www.google.com/maps/contrib/108103198969373327200/reviews", "photoUri": "https://lh3.googleusercontent.com/a-/ALV-UjU25z2UDTD-lXUtmtxRgVWm46M3STXEwCZhcPwux40BgvOl3w0d=s128-c0x00000000-cc-rp-mo-ba5", "displayName": "Richard Hawkins"}, "relativePublishTimeDescription": "8 months ago"}, {"name": "places/ChIJ4w-hCRIS24ARNi89W_frHlE/reviews/ChZDSUhNMG9nS0VKaVByNGFuc2RiUVJ3EAE", "text": {"text": "Was really hoping that this was going to be a good campground but unfortunately I can't say it is. It more like a city of campers and just to crowded for us. We did go in June so we knew it would be busy but not like this. I won't fault the campground for the people that camp and dont follow the rules but I will fault the for not enforcing their own rules. Quite time 10pm, try people yelling and screaming at 2am. Not hanging things from the trees, try walking and counting all the hammocks hanging from trees. Who ever designed this place must have just placed a number in every spot they could find and called it a camp site. There is no organization and the sites all just melt together. We had people walking right thru our site because that was the way to the road. We also listened to our neighbors talk all night because they were sooo close. The bathrooms were a little old feeling and again just cant keep up with all the people. If you dont mind the super tight spacing and no privacy at all come give it a try. We will continue to go to Idyllwild Campground and listen to some road noise over this all day because we do love Idyllwild.", "languageCode": "en"}, "rating": 3, "publishTime": "2025-06-09T02:36:48.202859Z", "originalText": {"text": "Was really hoping that this was going to be a good campground but unfortunately I can't say it is. It more like a city of campers and just to crowded for us. We did go in June so we knew it would be busy but not like this. I won't fault the campground for the people that camp and dont follow the rules but I will fault the for not enforcing their own rules. Quite time 10pm, try people yelling and screaming at 2am. Not hanging things from the trees, try walking and counting all the hammocks hanging from trees. Who ever designed this place must have just placed a number in every spot they could find and called it a camp site. There is no organization and the sites all just melt together. We had people walking right thru our site because that was the way to the road. We also listened to our neighbors talk all night because they were sooo close. The bathrooms were a little old feeling and again just cant keep up with all the people. If you dont mind the super tight spacing and no privacy at all come give it a try. We will continue to go to Idyllwild Campground and listen to some road noise over this all day because we do love Idyllwild.", "languageCode": "en"}, "googleMapsUri": "https://www.google.com/maps/reviews/data=!4m6!14m5!1m4!2m3!1sChZDSUhNMG9nS0VKaVByNGFuc2RiUVJ3EAE!2m1!1s0x80db121209a10fe3:0x511eebf75b3d2f36", "flagContentUri": "https://www.google.com/local/content/rap/report?postId=ChZDSUhNMG9nS0VKaVByNGFuc2RiUVJ3EAE&d=17924085&t=1", "authorAttribution": {"uri": "https://www.google.com/maps/contrib/117703163346047663574/reviews", "photoUri": "https://lh3.googleusercontent.com/a-/ALV-UjVrq_Igl6jcPP2lTaID3iHoAiXgDyZU9Ha7Eo9o_HendVVgRgZBOQ=s128-c0x00000000-cc-rp-mo-ba5", "displayName": "Doug Rosson"}, "relativePublishTimeDescription": "8 months ago"}, {"name": "places/ChIJ4w-hCRIS24ARNi89W_frHlE/reviews/Ci9DQUlRQUNvZENodHljRjlvT21kaWF6UlViRjlxWmpkSWNsSkJkVmhZWVZGQlFuYxAB", "text": {"text": "The only reason I gave it 3 stars was because the creek that runs through camp was all dried up, and you seemed to be packed in with too many people around. It's a nice camp, but I like to be a little further away and not so close to other campers. Overall, it was okay. They have wifi so that alone can ruin someone's campaign experience or make it better. The park rangers are very friendly. U pay 60 dollars per spot.", "languageCode": "en"}, "rating": 3, "publishTime": "2025-07-20T20:50:25.303414256Z", "originalText": {"text": "The only reason I gave it 3 stars was because the creek that runs through camp was all dried up, and you seemed to be packed in with too many people around. It's a nice camp, but I like to be a little further away and not so close to other campers. Overall, it was okay. They have wifi so that alone can ruin someone's campaign experience or make it better. The park rangers are very friendly. U pay 60 dollars per spot.", "languageCode": "en"}, "googleMapsUri": "https://www.google.com/maps/reviews/data=!4m6!14m5!1m4!2m3!1sCi9DQUlRQUNvZENodHljRjlvT21kaWF6UlViRjlxWmpkSWNsSkJkVmhZWVZGQlFuYxAB!2m1!1s0x80db121209a10fe3:0x511eebf75b3d2f36", "flagContentUri": "https://www.google.com/local/content/rap/report?postId=Ci9DQUlRQUNvZENodHljRjlvT21kaWF6UlViRjlxWmpkSWNsSkJkVmhZWVZGQlFuYxAB&d=17924085&t=1", "authorAttribution": {"uri": "https://www.google.com/maps/contrib/116812235053612789379/reviews", "photoUri": "https://lh3.googleusercontent.com/a-/ALV-UjUBY2_LqTZeBB3BacWAKBLQ9-tKZOlJ2Ewwy08uhrr_xkrCpLRmNg=s128-c0x00000000-cc-rp-mo-ba3", "displayName": "Maleena Pham"}, "relativePublishTimeDescription": "6 months ago"}]	Idyllwild Regional Park offers a beautiful mountain setting with clean facilities and convenient town access, but suffers from overcrowding and cramped campsites that reduce privacy. While some visitors find it magical with towering pines and peaceful trails, others are frustrated by the packed-in feeling and lack of rule enforcement.	{"summary": "Idyllwild Regional Park offers a beautiful mountain setting with clean facilities and convenient town access, but suffers from overcrowding and cramped campsites that reduce privacy. While some visitors find it magical with towering pines and peaceful trails, others are frustrated by the packed-in feeling and lack of rule enforcement.", "negative": [{"text": "It more like a city of campers and just to crowded for us. There is no organization and the sites all just melt together.", "author": "Doug Rosson", "rating": 3}, {"text": "Their online payment service doesn't work, you would need exact cash. Not much to see for the $6 fee.", "author": "Marilu Viveros", "rating": 1}], "positive": [{"text": "It was close enough to the restrooms for convenience (especially helpful since we had a pregnant friend with us) but not so close that it was noisy. The restrooms are flushable and well-kept.", "author": "Jessica", "rating": 5}, {"text": "It's also super convenient that the campground is right in town, so we had quick access to anything we needed.", "author": "Jessica", "rating": 5}, {"text": "Campsites are clean, well-spaced, and you actually get some real peace and quiet without feeling packed in like sardines.", "author": "Richard Hawkins", "rating": 5}], "last_updated": "2026-02-06T00:36:56.031Z"}	2026-02-06 00:36:49.688+00	county_park	\N	\N
a2d81291-0464-4068-9dc8-413cf662eb69	b201a860-05a3-4ddc-bb89-4c4271177271	San Simeon Creek Campground	San Simeon Creek Campground sits in a sheltered creek valley just minutes from some of the Central Coast's most extraordinary attractions. Hearst Castle perches on the hill above, the Piedras Blancas elephant seal rookery hosts one of the largest colonies in the world, and Moonstone Beach's boardwalk offers beachcombing and whale watching. The campground itself is pleasant with shaded sites in a eucalyptus and pine grove. Nearby Cambria is a charming art town with excellent restaurants.	Watch 15,000 elephant seals from a boardwalk, tour the outrageous opulence of Hearst Castle, and beachcomb for moonstones on a jade-colored shore—all within 10 minutes of your campsite.	state_parks	\N	500 San Simeon-Monterey Creek Rd, Cambria, CA 93428, USA	San Simeon	CA	35.5973309	-121.1241760	ChIJ2bJcaisy7YARdzS8trZ53UI	4.4	695	\N	{"hookups": "none", "cell_coverage": "spotty", "road_accessibility": "Highway 1 is well-maintained and 5th-wheel friendly in this section. The campground road is paved but has some turns.", "max_trailer_length_ft": 35, "fifth_wheel_accessible": true}	t	\N	Book via ReserveCalifornia.com up to 6 months ahead. Less competitive than SoCal beaches. Washburn Campground next door is an alternative if San Simeon Creek is full.	35.00	USD	\N	{"best": ["january", "february", "march", "april", "october", "november"], "avoid": [], "notes": "Elephant seal birthing season peaks January-February (best for pups). Molting season is April-May. Whale migration is December-April. Summer is pleasant but foggy."}	4 hours	\N	{"scenic_beauty": 5, "solitude_level": 3, "adventure_level": 3, "family_friendly": 5, "relaxation_factor": 4}	{"topics": ["marine mammals", "California history", "art and architecture", "whale migration", "coastal geology"], "visitor_center": true, "ranger_programs": true, "junior_ranger_program": false}	{"parker": {"notes": "Parker will be impressed by Hearst Castle's scale and the drama of bull elephant seals fighting.", "suitable": true, "activities": ["Hearst Castle architecture tour", "Elephant seal watching", "Moonstone Beach boardwalk hike", "Piedras Blancas lighthouse area"], "engagement_level": 4}, "xander": {"notes": "The elephant seal rookery is like a live nature show—Xander could watch the blubbery chaos for hours.", "suitable": true, "activities": ["Elephant seals (endless entertainment)", "Beach play", "Boardwalk walking", "Animal sounds"], "engagement_level": 5}, "charlotte": {"notes": "Moonstone Beach is literally named for the gems Charlotte can find. Baby elephant seals are impossibly cute.", "suitable": true, "activities": ["Moonstone collecting on the beach", "Elephant seal pup watching", "Hearst Castle pools and gardens", "Shell hunting"], "engagement_level": 5}}	http://www.parks.ca.gov/pages/590/files/SanSimeon_CampMap041515.pdf	(805) 927-2035	\N	researching	0	{elephant-seals,hearst-castle,beachcombing,wildlife,state-park,coastal,dry-camping}	{"Piedras Blancas elephant seal rookery is free and jaw-dropping","Hearst Castle is a unique historical/architectural experience","Moonstone Beach boardwalk is gentle and beautiful for all ages","Affordable compared to other coastal campgrounds","Cambria is a lovely walkable art town"}	{"No hookups—dry camping only (you have Starlink for connectivity)","Cell coverage is spotty","4-hour drive makes this a 3+ night trip to justify"}	\N	\N	2026-02-04 15:15:19.498+00	2026-02-06 02:12:56.603744+00	[{"name": "places/ChIJ2bJcaisy7YARdzS8trZ53UI/reviews/Ci9DQUlRQUNvZENodHljRjlvT2paM1NsRkJNVGd6Y2w5UmRGTlFkMTlyWnpKSWFXYxAB", "text": {"text": "Great campground. Clean bathrooms with flush toilets and pay showers. You can easily walk to the beach and there are nice fire pits at every site. Water is at most sites or really close, and there are nice dishwashing stations by the bathrooms.\\n\\nSome sites are pretty small, but others are quite large- so if you have a large camper or trailer plan ahead and scope out the right spot.  Maybe call the park ranger and ask.\\n\\nLots of raccoons at night, so put away your food. And we had some crazy squirrels that loved coming into the site to steal food in the morning. So keep all food locked up.", "languageCode": "en"}, "rating": 5, "publishTime": "2026-01-25T17:12:15.901754032Z", "originalText": {"text": "Great campground. Clean bathrooms with flush toilets and pay showers. You can easily walk to the beach and there are nice fire pits at every site. Water is at most sites or really close, and there are nice dishwashing stations by the bathrooms.\\n\\nSome sites are pretty small, but others are quite large- so if you have a large camper or trailer plan ahead and scope out the right spot.  Maybe call the park ranger and ask.\\n\\nLots of raccoons at night, so put away your food. And we had some crazy squirrels that loved coming into the site to steal food in the morning. So keep all food locked up.", "languageCode": "en"}, "googleMapsUri": "https://www.google.com/maps/reviews/data=!4m6!14m5!1m4!2m3!1sCi9DQUlRQUNvZENodHljRjlvT2paM1NsRkJNVGd6Y2w5UmRGTlFkMTlyWnpKSWFXYxAB!2m1!1s0x80ed322b6a5cb2d9:0x42dd79b6b6bc3477", "flagContentUri": "https://www.google.com/local/content/rap/report?postId=Ci9DQUlRQUNvZENodHljRjlvT2paM1NsRkJNVGd6Y2w5UmRGTlFkMTlyWnpKSWFXYxAB&d=17924085&t=1", "authorAttribution": {"uri": "https://www.google.com/maps/contrib/114325658113266771138/reviews", "photoUri": "https://lh3.googleusercontent.com/a/ACg8ocJo6g3tGYYsyNiV0dzm7esrbpps6PzHaaidJ_XYIuaL_qP9hMk=s128-c0x00000000-cc-rp-mo-ba3", "displayName": "David Stachura"}, "relativePublishTimeDescription": "a week ago"}, {"name": "places/ChIJ2bJcaisy7YARdzS8trZ53UI/reviews/Ci9DQUlRQUNvZENodHljRjlvT25KV2JIbDFkMHBHU0d3NVpXVmthSEJGVXpJeFFXYxAB", "text": {"text": "This is a really cool campground.  You almost feel like your in a jungle. Lots of wildlife. Plenty of places to ride your bikes and a wood plank pathway to the beach, that u can ride on. Here is a tip, no service for T-Mobile at the lower campground, but if u go to the upper campgrounds, you can get service. You can buy firewood, they have water and a dump station.  We saw bats, raccoon s and squirrels. At the beach ⛱️ seagulls and pelicans. It's approximately 10 to 15 min drive to the Hurst Castle Visitors Center.", "languageCode": "en"}, "rating": 5, "publishTime": "2025-09-19T01:33:40.925722064Z", "originalText": {"text": "This is a really cool campground.  You almost feel like your in a jungle. Lots of wildlife. Plenty of places to ride your bikes and a wood plank pathway to the beach, that u can ride on. Here is a tip, no service for T-Mobile at the lower campground, but if u go to the upper campgrounds, you can get service. You can buy firewood, they have water and a dump station.  We saw bats, raccoon s and squirrels. At the beach ⛱️ seagulls and pelicans. It's approximately 10 to 15 min drive to the Hurst Castle Visitors Center.", "languageCode": "en"}, "googleMapsUri": "https://www.google.com/maps/reviews/data=!4m6!14m5!1m4!2m3!1sCi9DQUlRQUNvZENodHljRjlvT25KV2JIbDFkMHBHU0d3NVpXVmthSEJGVXpJeFFXYxAB!2m1!1s0x80ed322b6a5cb2d9:0x42dd79b6b6bc3477", "flagContentUri": "https://www.google.com/local/content/rap/report?postId=Ci9DQUlRQUNvZENodHljRjlvT25KV2JIbDFkMHBHU0d3NVpXVmthSEJGVXpJeFFXYxAB&d=17924085&t=1", "authorAttribution": {"uri": "https://www.google.com/maps/contrib/105673203220024092804/reviews", "photoUri": "https://lh3.googleusercontent.com/a/ACg8ocKKjqTKxnQNwq0T-5OCkgsPmgnBPKl2z5QBuTww4Zm5IJZbNA=s128-c0x00000000-cc-rp-mo-ba4", "displayName": "John Baker"}, "relativePublishTimeDescription": "4 months ago"}, {"name": "places/ChIJ2bJcaisy7YARdzS8trZ53UI/reviews/Ci9DQUlRQUNvZENodHljRjlvT2tsMk5HVnllV3g0YXpCSmFreHlMVFpNZFZFeFRIYxAB", "text": {"text": "Bathroms were clean but little dated and needed some repare. Paved campsites. Ours was mostly level. Hike to Cambria, great long board walk. Around 3.5 miles one way. They had scare crow fest.", "languageCode": "en"}, "rating": 5, "publishTime": "2025-10-08T21:38:08.177630380Z", "originalText": {"text": "Bathroms were clean but little dated and needed some repare. Paved campsites. Ours was mostly level. Hike to Cambria, great long board walk. Around 3.5 miles one way. They had scare crow fest.", "languageCode": "en"}, "googleMapsUri": "https://www.google.com/maps/reviews/data=!4m6!14m5!1m4!2m3!1sCi9DQUlRQUNvZENodHljRjlvT2tsMk5HVnllV3g0YXpCSmFreHlMVFpNZFZFeFRIYxAB!2m1!1s0x80ed322b6a5cb2d9:0x42dd79b6b6bc3477", "flagContentUri": "https://www.google.com/local/content/rap/report?postId=Ci9DQUlRQUNvZENodHljRjlvT2tsMk5HVnllV3g0YXpCSmFreHlMVFpNZFZFeFRIYxAB&d=17924085&t=1", "authorAttribution": {"uri": "https://www.google.com/maps/contrib/108137302586359046512/reviews", "photoUri": "https://lh3.googleusercontent.com/a/ACg8ocJTYhlNT7CV8naRrYWw_sfhKtkg2BzcT07RWLDAbtdCyAr2hA=s128-c0x00000000-cc-rp-mo-ba4", "displayName": "Rolling Dunes"}, "relativePublishTimeDescription": "4 months ago"}, {"name": "places/ChIJ2bJcaisy7YARdzS8trZ53UI/reviews/Ci9DQUlRQUNvZENodHljRjlvT2pGVWFtMTNhRloxVjJONWRIVTRSbXRyV1hBeFNsRRAB", "text": {"text": "We enjoyed our stay here. The campground is will maintained. The spaces are not too close to each other with some bushes separating them. The fire pits are really deep and they sell firewood on site.  There is a nice walkway that takes you over to the beach and ocean. Overall it was well worth the price.", "languageCode": "en"}, "rating": 5, "publishTime": "2025-07-22T00:52:49.367271653Z", "originalText": {"text": "We enjoyed our stay here. The campground is will maintained. The spaces are not too close to each other with some bushes separating them. The fire pits are really deep and they sell firewood on site.  There is a nice walkway that takes you over to the beach and ocean. Overall it was well worth the price.", "languageCode": "en"}, "googleMapsUri": "https://www.google.com/maps/reviews/data=!4m6!14m5!1m4!2m3!1sCi9DQUlRQUNvZENodHljRjlvT2pGVWFtMTNhRloxVjJONWRIVTRSbXRyV1hBeFNsRRAB!2m1!1s0x80ed322b6a5cb2d9:0x42dd79b6b6bc3477", "flagContentUri": "https://www.google.com/local/content/rap/report?postId=Ci9DQUlRQUNvZENodHljRjlvT2pGVWFtMTNhRloxVjJONWRIVTRSbXRyV1hBeFNsRRAB&d=17924085&t=1", "authorAttribution": {"uri": "https://www.google.com/maps/contrib/114300880383616626361/reviews", "photoUri": "https://lh3.googleusercontent.com/a-/ALV-UjUcxvBR3Uvi0qxhKc97lCgl0Z91SLxnqONVWxAhVO4sohEvIMQQ5w=s128-c0x00000000-cc-rp-mo-ba6", "displayName": "Curtis Lannom"}, "relativePublishTimeDescription": "6 months ago"}, {"name": "places/ChIJ2bJcaisy7YARdzS8trZ53UI/reviews/ChZDSUhNMG9nS0VJQ0FnTUNRcHMzOVFREAE", "text": {"text": "A very nice, well maintained campground with lots of trees, birds, and wildlife. We even saw bald eagles, which was a treat.\\nThere's a short boardwalk type trail to the beach alongside a sream.\\nIt's a beautiful walk.\\nThere's other trails in the area too that we didn't go on. We ran out of time.\\nWe stayed in the lower campground where there are very clean restrooms and showers.\\nCampground hosts are super nice. They sell firewood.\\nIt's an enjoyable place to stay.\\nIt's a short drive to the cute quaint little town of Cambria.\\nHearst Castle is also nearby. There's also Elephant Seal Vista Point. We visited when there were many young pups with their parents. (February 2025) It's quite the amazing sight.", "languageCode": "en"}, "rating": 5, "publishTime": "2025-03-04T00:23:26.886182Z", "originalText": {"text": "A very nice, well maintained campground with lots of trees, birds, and wildlife. We even saw bald eagles, which was a treat.\\nThere's a short boardwalk type trail to the beach alongside a sream.\\nIt's a beautiful walk.\\nThere's other trails in the area too that we didn't go on. We ran out of time.\\nWe stayed in the lower campground where there are very clean restrooms and showers.\\nCampground hosts are super nice. They sell firewood.\\nIt's an enjoyable place to stay.\\nIt's a short drive to the cute quaint little town of Cambria.\\nHearst Castle is also nearby. There's also Elephant Seal Vista Point. We visited when there were many young pups with their parents. (February 2025) It's quite the amazing sight.", "languageCode": "en"}, "googleMapsUri": "https://www.google.com/maps/reviews/data=!4m6!14m5!1m4!2m3!1sChZDSUhNMG9nS0VJQ0FnTUNRcHMzOVFREAE!2m1!1s0x80ed322b6a5cb2d9:0x42dd79b6b6bc3477", "flagContentUri": "https://www.google.com/local/content/rap/report?postId=ChZDSUhNMG9nS0VJQ0FnTUNRcHMzOVFREAE&d=17924085&t=1", "authorAttribution": {"uri": "https://www.google.com/maps/contrib/104752023609114509240/reviews", "photoUri": "https://lh3.googleusercontent.com/a/ACg8ocIsGdTKo-iCioFaz_tFci6MJuRnF2VxAXRteqA9ytfe_xd4eQ=s128-c0x00000000-cc-rp-mo-ba3", "displayName": "Annemarie Vaughn"}, "relativePublishTimeDescription": "11 months ago"}]	San Simeon Creek Campground is a well-maintained, family-friendly destination that offers a unique jungle-like atmosphere with abundant wildlife and easy beach access via a wooden boardwalk. Visitors consistently praise the clean facilities, spacious sites with fire pits, and the campground's proximity to popular attractions like Hearst Castle and Cambria. The campground provides a perfect base for families wanting to experience nature while having modern amenities.	{"summary": "San Simeon Creek Campground is a well-maintained, family-friendly destination that offers a unique jungle-like atmosphere with abundant wildlife and easy beach access via a wooden boardwalk. Visitors consistently praise the clean facilities, spacious sites with fire pits, and the campground's proximity to popular attractions like Hearst Castle and Cambria. The campground provides a perfect base for families wanting to experience nature while having modern amenities.", "negative": [{"text": "Lots of raccoons at night, so put away your food. And we had some crazy squirrels that loved coming into the site to steal food in the morning.", "author": "David Stachura", "rating": 5}, {"text": "No service for T-Mobile at the lower campground.", "author": "John Baker", "rating": 5}], "positive": [{"text": "You can easily walk to the beach and there are nice fire pits at every site.", "author": "David Stachura", "rating": 5}, {"text": "You almost feel like your in a jungle. Lots of wildlife... a wood plank pathway to the beach, that u can ride on.", "author": "John Baker", "rating": 5}, {"text": "We even saw bald eagles, which was a treat. There's a short boardwalk type trail to the beach alongside a stream.", "author": "Annemarie Vaughn", "rating": 5}], "last_updated": "2026-02-06T02:12:56.496Z"}	2026-02-06 02:12:47.382+00	state_park	\N	\N
7c98b050-12b7-4801-abd7-8695368d8904	b201a860-05a3-4ddc-bb89-4c4271177271	Carpinteria State Beach	Carpinteria State Beach is one of the most sought-after family campgrounds on the Southern California coast. With 200+ sites across four loops, including full hookups in the Santa Rosa loop, it's one of the rare beachfront state parks that can properly accommodate a 5th wheel. A mile of sandy beach, outstanding tide pools, a harbor seal preserve, and walkable downtown Carpinteria with restaurants and shops make this an easy win for families. The Tomol Interpretive Play Area—a replica Chumash village—gives kids a hands-on history lesson between beach sessions.	Camp steps from the safest swimming beach in California with full hookups, harbor seal rookery within walking distance, and a Chumash village replica playground that turns history into adventure for kids.	state_parks	\N	205 Palm Ave, Carpinteria, CA 93013, USA	Carpinteria	CA	34.3924868	-119.5213439	ChIJi6LIDiwP6YAR35YCu2H-KR8	4.7	4744	\N	{"hookups": "full", "cell_coverage": "excellent", "road_accessibility": "Easy highway access directly off US-101. No steep grades or tight turns. Paved interior roads.", "max_trailer_length_ft": 35, "fifth_wheel_accessible": true}	t	\N	Book via ReserveCalifornia.com up to 6 months in advance. Summer weekends sell out immediately. Request Santa Rosa loop (sites 306-380) for full hookups. Sites are measured—ensure your rig fits the specific site's posted max.	65.00	USD	\N	{"best": ["april", "may", "june", "september", "october"], "avoid": ["july", "august"], "notes": "Summer is peak season and extremely hard to book. Spring and fall offer warm weather, fewer crowds, and easier reservations. Winter is mild but some rainy days. Harbor seal pupping season is December-May."}	1.5 hours	\N	{"scenic_beauty": 4, "solitude_level": 2, "adventure_level": 3, "family_friendly": 5, "relaxation_factor": 4}	{"topics": ["Chumash history", "marine biology", "tide pool ecology", "harbor seal behavior", "tar seeps geology"], "visitor_center": true, "ranger_programs": true, "junior_ranger_program": true}	{"parker": {"notes": "Parker will love the challenge of finding specific tide pool creatures and boogie boarding. The bike path gives him distance to cover.", "suitable": true, "activities": ["Tide pool exploration at low tide with identification challenges", "Bike ride along coastal path to Rincon Point", "Boogie boarding and body surfing", "Carpinteria Bluffs trail hiking"], "engagement_level": 4}, "xander": {"notes": "Perfect for Xander—contained beach for sand play, animals to watch, and a playground right in camp. The gentle waves are safe for toddlers.", "suitable": true, "activities": ["Beach sand and wave play", "Harbor seal watching", "Tomol play area climbing", "Squirrel and bird watching at campsite"], "engagement_level": 5}, "charlotte": {"notes": "This is Charlotte's dream destination. Tide pools for collecting, seal pups to watch, a play village to explore, and treasures on the beach.", "suitable": true, "activities": ["Harbor seal rookery viewing", "Tide pool treasure hunting", "Tomol Chumash village play area", "Shell and sea glass collecting on beach", "Junior Ranger program (summer)"], "engagement_level": 5}}	http://www.parks.ca.gov/?page_id=599	(805) 684-2811	\N	researching	0	{beach,full-hookups,tide-pools,seals,family-friendly,walkable-town,state-park}	{"Full hookups available in Santa Rosa loop—rare for beachfront state parks","Harbor seal rookery within walking distance—incredible for kids","Walkable to downtown Carpinteria restaurants and shops","Outstanding tide pools at low tide","Tomol Chumash play area is unique educational playground"}	{"Sites are very close together, especially in RV loops—hear your neighbors","Books up months in advance for summer","Train noise from Amtrak line running adjacent to campground"}	\N	\N	2026-02-04 15:15:16.257+00	2026-02-06 02:16:48.652747+00	[{"name": "places/ChIJi6LIDiwP6YAR35YCu2H-KR8/reviews/Ci9DQUlRQUNvZENodHljRjlvT214bFlURnBaMkptTFVvM1dXTnJWbTl1TWtkWVFrRRAB", "text": {"text": "A nice place to camp! We did dry camping with our 28' trailer. Very easy to back the trailer in our site (123). Bathrooms and showers were very clean. A lot of fun trails that are very easy to walk/ run or ride bikes on. A four minute walk to resturants and breweries from our site. We will be going back to try a full-hookup site in the future!", "languageCode": "en"}, "rating": 5, "publishTime": "2026-01-04T00:13:28.893169342Z", "originalText": {"text": "A nice place to camp! We did dry camping with our 28' trailer. Very easy to back the trailer in our site (123). Bathrooms and showers were very clean. A lot of fun trails that are very easy to walk/ run or ride bikes on. A four minute walk to resturants and breweries from our site. We will be going back to try a full-hookup site in the future!", "languageCode": "en"}, "googleMapsUri": "https://www.google.com/maps/reviews/data=!4m6!14m5!1m4!2m3!1sCi9DQUlRQUNvZENodHljRjlvT214bFlURnBaMkptTFVvM1dXTnJWbTl1TWtkWVFrRRAB!2m1!1s0x80e90f2c0ec8a28b:0x1f29fe61bb0296df", "flagContentUri": "https://www.google.com/local/content/rap/report?postId=Ci9DQUlRQUNvZENodHljRjlvT214bFlURnBaMkptTFVvM1dXTnJWbTl1TWtkWVFrRRAB&d=17924085&t=1", "authorAttribution": {"uri": "https://www.google.com/maps/contrib/105641429069794851184/reviews", "photoUri": "https://lh3.googleusercontent.com/a/ACg8ocK7W1AmJh-HQFDclcVVdPgdiQfOquvqdBkbi8MoQmQ7uzpBpjDt=s128-c0x00000000-cc-rp-mo-ba2", "displayName": "Mike Collins"}, "relativePublishTimeDescription": "a month ago"}, {"name": "places/ChIJi6LIDiwP6YAR35YCu2H-KR8/reviews/Ci9DQUlRQUNvZENodHljRjlvT2sxbFdVTktVak5vUW5RelZIZ3pVRnBNUjBOdlQwRRAB", "text": {"text": "Carpinteria is one of my favorite places in the country, and like all CA State Beaches, the views are incredible. But with that beauty comes everyone wanting to be there as well. The campground is challenging to book a spot at, but once you secure one, you’re set with the sounds of waves, beautiful beach path, and short walk to town w great dining options. The downside —- the sites are essentially a closely packed parking lot and, if you’re not on a beach front spot, outdoor seating is non-existent. Spots are so close together, you’re not opening your windows and pulling in/out is extremely difficult on a busy day. Worth it for a night if your focus is enjoying the town, but any longer would feel claustrophobic.", "languageCode": "en"}, "rating": 3, "publishTime": "2026-01-03T07:30:28.458667603Z", "originalText": {"text": "Carpinteria is one of my favorite places in the country, and like all CA State Beaches, the views are incredible. But with that beauty comes everyone wanting to be there as well. The campground is challenging to book a spot at, but once you secure one, you’re set with the sounds of waves, beautiful beach path, and short walk to town w great dining options. The downside —- the sites are essentially a closely packed parking lot and, if you’re not on a beach front spot, outdoor seating is non-existent. Spots are so close together, you’re not opening your windows and pulling in/out is extremely difficult on a busy day. Worth it for a night if your focus is enjoying the town, but any longer would feel claustrophobic.", "languageCode": "en"}, "googleMapsUri": "https://www.google.com/maps/reviews/data=!4m6!14m5!1m4!2m3!1sCi9DQUlRQUNvZENodHljRjlvT2sxbFdVTktVak5vUW5RelZIZ3pVRnBNUjBOdlQwRRAB!2m1!1s0x80e90f2c0ec8a28b:0x1f29fe61bb0296df", "flagContentUri": "https://www.google.com/local/content/rap/report?postId=Ci9DQUlRQUNvZENodHljRjlvT2sxbFdVTktVak5vUW5RelZIZ3pVRnBNUjBOdlQwRRAB&d=17924085&t=1", "authorAttribution": {"uri": "https://www.google.com/maps/contrib/102721929375619312585/reviews", "photoUri": "https://lh3.googleusercontent.com/a-/ALV-UjWX7Y_okRTZ4PtKHkQsQJdtDznoGUnO3BC0dif0_NGD6-ZKLmaCbA=s128-c0x00000000-cc-rp-mo-ba3", "displayName": "Elizabeth Stefan"}, "relativePublishTimeDescription": "a month ago"}, {"name": "places/ChIJi6LIDiwP6YAR35YCu2H-KR8/reviews/Ci9DQUlRQUNvZENodHljRjlvT2tsaFVYWXhRa1pqVjFsTmFHbHRlRXRPUkVZelpIYxAB", "text": {"text": "Carpinteria State Beach is wonderful for camping. Very mellow surf and great for walking. The campground itself is relatively quiet, but the train tracks are adjacent, so you hear several Amtrak trains and a couple of freight trains per day.", "languageCode": "en"}, "rating": 5, "publishTime": "2026-01-13T21:13:09.304842086Z", "originalText": {"text": "Carpinteria State Beach is wonderful for camping. Very mellow surf and great for walking. The campground itself is relatively quiet, but the train tracks are adjacent, so you hear several Amtrak trains and a couple of freight trains per day.", "languageCode": "en"}, "googleMapsUri": "https://www.google.com/maps/reviews/data=!4m6!14m5!1m4!2m3!1sCi9DQUlRQUNvZENodHljRjlvT2tsaFVYWXhRa1pqVjFsTmFHbHRlRXRPUkVZelpIYxAB!2m1!1s0x80e90f2c0ec8a28b:0x1f29fe61bb0296df", "flagContentUri": "https://www.google.com/local/content/rap/report?postId=Ci9DQUlRQUNvZENodHljRjlvT2tsaFVYWXhRa1pqVjFsTmFHbHRlRXRPUkVZelpIYxAB&d=17924085&t=1", "authorAttribution": {"uri": "https://www.google.com/maps/contrib/108537848060611100948/reviews", "photoUri": "https://lh3.googleusercontent.com/a/ACg8ocL6tYqcKmRzhmkwE4Q4MmvNmbPMia72KuMCPZu-LDG_sUPJGghJ=s128-c0x00000000-cc-rp-mo-ba3", "displayName": "P & N Acosta"}, "relativePublishTimeDescription": "3 weeks ago"}, {"name": "places/ChIJi6LIDiwP6YAR35YCu2H-KR8/reviews/Ci9DQUlRQUNvZENodHljRjlvT2psRE0yNW1XazV0TnpWM1JuTlhVa1JWUjNGbFUzYxAB", "text": {"text": "A great location close to the beach and walking distance to the city center.\\n\\nSome spots are very small, be Mindful when booking.\\n\\nWe noticed that the rangers were approaching RV's not obeying to the quiet hours. Much appreciated.\\n\\nWe did notice many dogs without a leash and dog poop at several places. This is against the park rules. Being more strict on this would have been appreciated by us.", "languageCode": "en"}, "rating": 5, "publishTime": "2025-09-29T04:44:59.836583752Z", "originalText": {"text": "A great location close to the beach and walking distance to the city center.\\n\\nSome spots are very small, be Mindful when booking.\\n\\nWe noticed that the rangers were approaching RV's not obeying to the quiet hours. Much appreciated.\\n\\nWe did notice many dogs without a leash and dog poop at several places. This is against the park rules. Being more strict on this would have been appreciated by us.", "languageCode": "en"}, "googleMapsUri": "https://www.google.com/maps/reviews/data=!4m6!14m5!1m4!2m3!1sCi9DQUlRQUNvZENodHljRjlvT2psRE0yNW1XazV0TnpWM1JuTlhVa1JWUjNGbFUzYxAB!2m1!1s0x80e90f2c0ec8a28b:0x1f29fe61bb0296df", "flagContentUri": "https://www.google.com/local/content/rap/report?postId=Ci9DQUlRQUNvZENodHljRjlvT2psRE0yNW1XazV0TnpWM1JuTlhVa1JWUjNGbFUzYxAB&d=17924085&t=1", "authorAttribution": {"uri": "https://www.google.com/maps/contrib/114444685006761012461/reviews", "photoUri": "https://lh3.googleusercontent.com/a/ACg8ocKBBxk0Am7GHwxPxgjPQrHWdra6Zb2dHskSADtcxpgXh9O7KQ=s128-c0x00000000-cc-rp-mo-ba4", "displayName": "Michiel Teunissen"}, "relativePublishTimeDescription": "4 months ago"}, {"name": "places/ChIJi6LIDiwP6YAR35YCu2H-KR8/reviews/Ci9DQUlRQUNvZENodHljRjlvT2tWU1QxbE9RamczV2xCcU9VTm9PVVJyYTNkNlpVRRAB", "text": {"text": "Beautiful beach walks.  Cute shops and restaurants.  And a wonderful quilt fabric and yarn store called Roxanne's Wish and a Dream", "languageCode": "en"}, "rating": 4, "publishTime": "2026-01-26T00:11:59.748256934Z", "originalText": {"text": "Beautiful beach walks.  Cute shops and restaurants.  And a wonderful quilt fabric and yarn store called Roxanne's Wish and a Dream", "languageCode": "en"}, "googleMapsUri": "https://www.google.com/maps/reviews/data=!4m6!14m5!1m4!2m3!1sCi9DQUlRQUNvZENodHljRjlvT2tWU1QxbE9RamczV2xCcU9VTm9PVVJyYTNkNlpVRRAB!2m1!1s0x80e90f2c0ec8a28b:0x1f29fe61bb0296df", "flagContentUri": "https://www.google.com/local/content/rap/report?postId=Ci9DQUlRQUNvZENodHljRjlvT2tWU1QxbE9RamczV2xCcU9VTm9PVVJyYTNkNlpVRRAB&d=17924085&t=1", "authorAttribution": {"uri": "https://www.google.com/maps/contrib/110533617749244303650/reviews", "photoUri": "https://lh3.googleusercontent.com/a-/ALV-UjUmPcuFdRgJYBK0B_KgETWF8bRs0NWQU0Mw3_fDEpWNOywy9zaO_g=s128-c0x00000000-cc-rp-mo-ba4", "displayName": "Marcia Greiten"}, "relativePublishTimeDescription": "a week ago"}]	Carpinteria State Beach offers stunning ocean views and convenient access to town amenities, making it popular with families despite some limitations. While the camping sites are very close together and can feel cramped, visitors consistently praise the easy beach access, clean facilities, and gentle surf perfect for families. The location provides an ideal base for enjoying both beach activities and local dining and shopping.	{"summary": "Carpinteria State Beach offers stunning ocean views and convenient access to town amenities, making it popular with families despite some limitations. While the camping sites are very close together and can feel cramped, visitors consistently praise the easy beach access, clean facilities, and gentle surf perfect for families. The location provides an ideal base for enjoying both beach activities and local dining and shopping.", "negative": [{"text": "The sites are essentially a closely packed parking lot and, if you're not on a beach front spot, outdoor seating is non-existent.", "author": "Elizabeth Stefan", "rating": 3}, {"text": "We did notice many dogs without a leash and dog poop at several places.", "author": "Michiel Teunissen", "rating": 5}], "positive": [{"text": "Very mellow surf and great for walking. The campground itself is relatively quiet", "author": "P & N Acosta", "rating": 5}, {"text": "Bathrooms and showers were very clean. A lot of fun trails that are very easy to walk/ run or ride bikes on.", "author": "Mike Collins", "rating": 5}, {"text": "A four minute walk to resturants and breweries from our site.", "author": "Mike Collins", "rating": 5}], "last_updated": "2026-02-06T02:16:48.538Z"}	2026-02-06 02:16:42.372+00	state_park	\N	\N
2ff000be-4a64-4754-bffb-afdcc5c61bde	b201a860-05a3-4ddc-bb89-4c4271177271	Rancho Oso (Santa Ynez Valley)	Los Olivos wineries 30 minutes away. Historic ranch atmosphere with full-hookup RV sites.	Historic 1800s ranch on 300+ acres with horseback riding, covered wagons, and mountain views. Rustic romance in wine country.	couples_getaway	\N	3750 Paradise Rd, Santa Barbara, CA 93105, USA	Santa Barbara	CA	34.5363550	-119.7713184	ChIJ-fxsGPJp6YAROETEDpRVGsY	4.2	205	\N	{"hookups": "full"}	f	\N	\N	\N	USD	\N	\N	2.5 hours	\N	{"scenic_beauty": 4, "solitude_level": 4, "adventure_level": 3, "family_friendly": 4, "relaxation_factor": 5}	\N	\N	https://thousandtrails.com/california/rancho-oso-rv-camping-resort?utm_source=BirdEye&utm_medium=directory&utm_campaign=BirdEye%20Directory%20Listing	(805) 683-5686	\N	researching	0	{couples,ranch,horseback-riding,wine-country}	{}	{}	\N	\N	2026-02-02 15:20:44.237+00	2026-02-06 02:55:02.391585+00	[{"name": "places/ChIJ-fxsGPJp6YAROETEDpRVGsY/reviews/Ci9DQUlRQUNvZENodHljRjlvT2s1SlVUSlpVMlJ4ZVhWb2RGVkVOM041Y0RkNWFFRRAB", "text": {"text": "This park is really beautiful, with a pool, jacuzzi, and large playground area, however, the administration failed to show competence in an extreme way.  Additionally, their \\"wi-fi\\" was on a low-range antenna at the club-house, not reaching even the closest RVs during my stay, and there is virtually 0 cell signal there.  I was able to use a cell signal booster to receive a tolerable cell signal, however, and of course, Starlink will likely work most of the time, though it is situated in a valley with a bridge passing over nearby.\\nThe major issue I ran into was because I had auto-billing set up, and had them just auto-renewing my contract with them continually so that I could stay there indefinitely.  While this worked most of the time, at one point they lost my billing info somehow, and then, when I had guests who used their credit card to pay the gate fee, they charged my $700 rent to my guests credit card.  Needless to say, my friends, who did not have $700 to spare until the credit card would refund it, freaked out, and the park was not helpful when we contacted them about the error.  That being bad enough, several months later, the manager failed to set my lot to auto-renew, as it had the previous 6 months, and then contacted me on a Friday telling me I had something like 3 days to remove all of my possessions from the park.. I was out of town at the time, and if you've ever expanded a pop-out camper to live in indefinitely, you would know that it takes a good bit of preparation to be ready to relocate again.  I ended up leaving that park in an undue rush, with the manager indicating they couldn't resolve their error for me because they had booked the spot out to someone else.\\nIt's hard not to give this location 1 star for these reasons, but it was quite beautiful and peaceful.. though the management operated as though their operation is part of the filming of \\"trailer park boys\\".", "languageCode": "en"}, "rating": 2, "publishTime": "2025-06-27T10:03:28.771900337Z", "originalText": {"text": "This park is really beautiful, with a pool, jacuzzi, and large playground area, however, the administration failed to show competence in an extreme way.  Additionally, their \\"wi-fi\\" was on a low-range antenna at the club-house, not reaching even the closest RVs during my stay, and there is virtually 0 cell signal there.  I was able to use a cell signal booster to receive a tolerable cell signal, however, and of course, Starlink will likely work most of the time, though it is situated in a valley with a bridge passing over nearby.\\nThe major issue I ran into was because I had auto-billing set up, and had them just auto-renewing my contract with them continually so that I could stay there indefinitely.  While this worked most of the time, at one point they lost my billing info somehow, and then, when I had guests who used their credit card to pay the gate fee, they charged my $700 rent to my guests credit card.  Needless to say, my friends, who did not have $700 to spare until the credit card would refund it, freaked out, and the park was not helpful when we contacted them about the error.  That being bad enough, several months later, the manager failed to set my lot to auto-renew, as it had the previous 6 months, and then contacted me on a Friday telling me I had something like 3 days to remove all of my possessions from the park.. I was out of town at the time, and if you've ever expanded a pop-out camper to live in indefinitely, you would know that it takes a good bit of preparation to be ready to relocate again.  I ended up leaving that park in an undue rush, with the manager indicating they couldn't resolve their error for me because they had booked the spot out to someone else.\\nIt's hard not to give this location 1 star for these reasons, but it was quite beautiful and peaceful.. though the management operated as though their operation is part of the filming of \\"trailer park boys\\".", "languageCode": "en"}, "googleMapsUri": "https://www.google.com/maps/reviews/data=!4m6!14m5!1m4!2m3!1sCi9DQUlRQUNvZENodHljRjlvT2s1SlVUSlpVMlJ4ZVhWb2RGVkVOM041Y0RkNWFFRRAB!2m1!1s0x80e969f2186cfcf9:0xc61a55940ec44438", "flagContentUri": "https://www.google.com/local/content/rap/report?postId=Ci9DQUlRQUNvZENodHljRjlvT2s1SlVUSlpVMlJ4ZVhWb2RGVkVOM041Y0RkNWFFRRAB&d=17924085&t=1", "authorAttribution": {"uri": "https://www.google.com/maps/contrib/112858356317767560149/reviews", "photoUri": "https://lh3.googleusercontent.com/a-/ALV-UjWimkmmdH6KSEQpU64O0vf_Ne0TR_6aYSWiw2pGS8oPdiN91krZbQ=s128-c0x00000000-cc-rp-mo-ba4", "displayName": "Critical Insights"}, "relativePublishTimeDescription": "7 months ago"}, {"name": "places/ChIJ-fxsGPJp6YAROETEDpRVGsY/reviews/Ci9DQUlRQUNvZENodHljRjlvT2xObmIwSnZjVTV1UlRsdWRuSlZVbHBCVUhSc2JrRRAB", "text": {"text": "I was really looking forward to staying at this beautiful place, but unfortunately, my plans were disrupted. I had booked it for July 4th, but a month prior, I received a cancellation notice due to renovations. What's disappointing is that I was allowed to make the booking in the first place, despite the planned closure. As a result, my family and I will now have to spend our long weekend at home, which is really frustrating", "languageCode": "en"}, "rating": 1, "publishTime": "2025-06-05T00:01:02.301315562Z", "originalText": {"text": "I was really looking forward to staying at this beautiful place, but unfortunately, my plans were disrupted. I had booked it for July 4th, but a month prior, I received a cancellation notice due to renovations. What's disappointing is that I was allowed to make the booking in the first place, despite the planned closure. As a result, my family and I will now have to spend our long weekend at home, which is really frustrating", "languageCode": "en"}, "googleMapsUri": "https://www.google.com/maps/reviews/data=!4m6!14m5!1m4!2m3!1sCi9DQUlRQUNvZENodHljRjlvT2xObmIwSnZjVTV1UlRsdWRuSlZVbHBCVUhSc2JrRRAB!2m1!1s0x80e969f2186cfcf9:0xc61a55940ec44438", "flagContentUri": "https://www.google.com/local/content/rap/report?postId=Ci9DQUlRQUNvZENodHljRjlvT2xObmIwSnZjVTV1UlRsdWRuSlZVbHBCVUhSc2JrRRAB&d=17924085&t=1", "authorAttribution": {"uri": "https://www.google.com/maps/contrib/118259339551661064475/reviews", "photoUri": "https://lh3.googleusercontent.com/a/ACg8ocJrcZh2nfDiJSH_ToRZcA1RlqxlHTUmb3UG5q73ZNJJ-z896A=s128-c0x00000000-cc-rp-mo-ba3", "displayName": "Artem Gorbunov"}, "relativePublishTimeDescription": "8 months ago"}, {"name": "places/ChIJ-fxsGPJp6YAROETEDpRVGsY/reviews/ChdDSUhNMG9nS0VJQ0FnSUNXcTRqeThBRRAB", "text": {"text": "Beautiful scenery and the unique opportunity to go horse back riding on a trail with a guide! Make sure to make reservations for your ride at least the day before. Laura and Alexis at the barn and stables were very friendly and knowledgeable. The horses were well taken care of and very well trained. I've never heard of campgrounds offering activities like horse back riding, so this campground really stands out. In the barn you can also go see other animals like goats, pigs, and bunnies if you're not keen on riding horses. Either way, I totally recommend the horse back riding experience and staying here! We had an amazing time and would love to visit again in the future ✨", "languageCode": "en"}, "rating": 5, "publishTime": "2022-03-06T21:38:33.037624Z", "originalText": {"text": "Beautiful scenery and the unique opportunity to go horse back riding on a trail with a guide! Make sure to make reservations for your ride at least the day before. Laura and Alexis at the barn and stables were very friendly and knowledgeable. The horses were well taken care of and very well trained. I've never heard of campgrounds offering activities like horse back riding, so this campground really stands out. In the barn you can also go see other animals like goats, pigs, and bunnies if you're not keen on riding horses. Either way, I totally recommend the horse back riding experience and staying here! We had an amazing time and would love to visit again in the future ✨", "languageCode": "en"}, "googleMapsUri": "https://www.google.com/maps/reviews/data=!4m6!14m5!1m4!2m3!1sChdDSUhNMG9nS0VJQ0FnSUNXcTRqeThBRRAB!2m1!1s0x80e969f2186cfcf9:0xc61a55940ec44438", "flagContentUri": "https://www.google.com/local/content/rap/report?postId=ChdDSUhNMG9nS0VJQ0FnSUNXcTRqeThBRRAB&d=17924085&t=1", "authorAttribution": {"uri": "https://www.google.com/maps/contrib/115016791082821155395/reviews", "photoUri": "https://lh3.googleusercontent.com/a-/ALV-UjVSeVOMVZkrVtS1kTyiICsumCHHOZqXO7p8EmQ6DniM7dQoWj1nUg=s128-c0x00000000-cc-rp-mo-ba2", "displayName": "Faith Thomas"}, "relativePublishTimeDescription": "3 years ago"}, {"name": "places/ChIJ-fxsGPJp6YAROETEDpRVGsY/reviews/ChZDSUhNMG9nS0VJQ0FnSURxc2VQNVBREAE", "text": {"text": "It was kind of a first come first serve when it came to RV spots which was nice. Staff at the front gate immediately tried selling us a membership before we even pulled in. It was very very hot. Make your horse riding reservations before you even get there. It books up very fast. The pool. Where do I start. No one monitors the pool. Ever.  The rules are very clear at the pool. Common sense rules. Every day there was dogs, glass bottles, alcohol and food. I even heard about a near drowning of a 2 year old during the 4th of July weekend due to the mom being too under the influence to properly take care of her child. The pool was crowded and kids running. I was just waiting for someone to slip and fall. I spoke with the store employee and she said there wasn't enough staff to monitor the pool and if I saw a problem to go to the start of the park and call a ranger. She stated that the other thousand trails have someone watching the pool, but they don't have the staff. Even after talking to the store employee and making my concerns known on the first day we were there, I never once saw a ranger and we were there for 4 days. The worst. My husband took my 9 year old daughter to the bathroom. Waited outside and while she was in there a couple,a man and a young woman came out of the bathroom together. Maybe he was just changing or maybe something worse, I can't take that chance with my daughter. The bathroom next to us was not kept up either. 2 out of the 4 days it was not cleaned. It showed and was obvious. I can definitely say I'm glad we did not sign up for a membership and we will never go back to this site.", "languageCode": "en"}, "rating": 2, "publishTime": "2021-07-12T01:25:14.681961Z", "originalText": {"text": "It was kind of a first come first serve when it came to RV spots which was nice. Staff at the front gate immediately tried selling us a membership before we even pulled in. It was very very hot. Make your horse riding reservations before you even get there. It books up very fast. The pool. Where do I start. No one monitors the pool. Ever.  The rules are very clear at the pool. Common sense rules. Every day there was dogs, glass bottles, alcohol and food. I even heard about a near drowning of a 2 year old during the 4th of July weekend due to the mom being too under the influence to properly take care of her child. The pool was crowded and kids running. I was just waiting for someone to slip and fall. I spoke with the store employee and she said there wasn't enough staff to monitor the pool and if I saw a problem to go to the start of the park and call a ranger. She stated that the other thousand trails have someone watching the pool, but they don't have the staff. Even after talking to the store employee and making my concerns known on the first day we were there, I never once saw a ranger and we were there for 4 days. The worst. My husband took my 9 year old daughter to the bathroom. Waited outside and while she was in there a couple,a man and a young woman came out of the bathroom together. Maybe he was just changing or maybe something worse, I can't take that chance with my daughter. The bathroom next to us was not kept up either. 2 out of the 4 days it was not cleaned. It showed and was obvious. I can definitely say I'm glad we did not sign up for a membership and we will never go back to this site.", "languageCode": "en"}, "googleMapsUri": "https://www.google.com/maps/reviews/data=!4m6!14m5!1m4!2m3!1sChZDSUhNMG9nS0VJQ0FnSURxc2VQNVBREAE!2m1!1s0x80e969f2186cfcf9:0xc61a55940ec44438", "flagContentUri": "https://www.google.com/local/content/rap/report?postId=ChZDSUhNMG9nS0VJQ0FnSURxc2VQNVBREAE&d=17924085&t=1", "authorAttribution": {"uri": "https://www.google.com/maps/contrib/105496060076518064205/reviews", "photoUri": "https://lh3.googleusercontent.com/a-/ALV-UjUjkPtNp6W4yGqTi56lQ-JKM8qEwboDM5T8ECH2KXJ5QUDgJasu=s128-c0x00000000-cc-rp-mo-ba4", "displayName": "Diana Cannizzo"}, "relativePublishTimeDescription": "4 years ago"}, {"name": "places/ChIJ-fxsGPJp6YAROETEDpRVGsY/reviews/ChZDSUhNMG9nS0VJQ0FnSURhX3Y3aUpBEAE", "text": {"text": "I really enjoyed my 4 days in the Western Cabin...it was clean and tidy, and conducive to curling up with a good book in the evenings!  The horses were well looked after by guide, Torrey, who was so friendly and pleasant.  The barn was \\"spit spot.\\"  I would recommend this place to anyone looking for a retreat in mountains.", "languageCode": "en"}, "rating": 5, "publishTime": "2021-08-23T07:37:37.019817Z", "originalText": {"text": "I really enjoyed my 4 days in the Western Cabin...it was clean and tidy, and conducive to curling up with a good book in the evenings!  The horses were well looked after by guide, Torrey, who was so friendly and pleasant.  The barn was \\"spit spot.\\"  I would recommend this place to anyone looking for a retreat in mountains.", "languageCode": "en"}, "googleMapsUri": "https://www.google.com/maps/reviews/data=!4m6!14m5!1m4!2m3!1sChZDSUhNMG9nS0VJQ0FnSURhX3Y3aUpBEAE!2m1!1s0x80e969f2186cfcf9:0xc61a55940ec44438", "flagContentUri": "https://www.google.com/local/content/rap/report?postId=ChZDSUhNMG9nS0VJQ0FnSURhX3Y3aUpBEAE&d=17924085&t=1", "authorAttribution": {"uri": "https://www.google.com/maps/contrib/115239007757835260051/reviews", "photoUri": "https://lh3.googleusercontent.com/a-/ALV-UjXGOlpQlse7OuHXcd55CCNRrGzqTLt6A_zMESdrCdllPCi2Wjlu=s128-c0x00000000-cc-rp-mo-ba3", "displayName": "Margo Devlin"}, "relativePublishTimeDescription": "4 years ago"}]	Rancho Oso is a beautiful mountain retreat with unique amenities like horseback riding and farm animals that families love, but it suffers from significant management and safety issues. While the natural setting and activities receive praise, multiple reviewers cite problems with administration, pool supervision, and facility maintenance that raise concerns for families with children.	{"summary": "Rancho Oso is a beautiful mountain retreat with unique amenities like horseback riding and farm animals that families love, but it suffers from significant management and safety issues. While 