e2728369-a7d5-4e0b-af13-1cf4621923f1	b201a860-05a3-4ddc-bb89-4c4271177271	Lassen Volcanic National Park	Manzanita Lake Campground accepts RVs up to 45 feet with 179 sites plus pull-throughs, camp store, coin showers, and laundry. Bumpass Hell trail (3 miles round trip) boardwalks through the largest hydrothermal area in the park—bubbling mud and sulfur steam everywhere. Sulphur Works pull-off lets Xander see steam vents without leaving the car.	The world's largest plug dome volcano with all four volcano types in one park—boiling mud pots, steaming fumaroles, and stinky sulfur vents make kids feel like they're on another planet.	national_parks	\N	California, USA	Mineral	CA	40.4976600	-121.4206552	ChIJvzhBwQdWnYARQmdmeqfYNI8	4.8	4628	\N	{"hookups": "dry", "cell_coverage": "very limited", "max_trailer_length_ft": 45}	t	\N	\N	26.00	USD	Manzanita Lake $26/night (no hookups). Mt. Lassen/Shingletown KOA offers full hookups 20 minutes from park	{"best": ["june", "july", "august", "september", "october"], "notes": "June-October operation; heavy snow closes most of park in winter"}	8+ hours	\N	{"scenic_beauty": 5, "solitude_level": 4, "adventure_level": 5, "family_friendly": 4, "relaxation_factor": 3}	{"topics": ["Volcanology", "Hydrothermal activity", "All four volcano types"]}	{"parker": {"suitable": true, "activities": ["Lassen Peak summit (10,457 ft) or Cinder Cone"], "engagement_level": 5}, "xander": {"suitable": true, "activities": ["Sulphur Works from parking lot", "Wading at Manzanita Lake"], "engagement_level": 4}, "charlotte": {"suitable": true, "activities": ["Bumpass Hell boardwalks", "Smelling sulfur", "Identifying volcano types"], "engagement_level": 5}}	https://www.nps.gov/lavo/index.htm	(530) 595-6100	\N	researching	0	{national-park,volcanic,geothermal,mud-pots}	{"All four volcano types in one park","45-foot RV capacity","Unique geothermal features"}	{"8+ hour drive","Very limited cell coverage","Altitude 6,000-10,000 ft affects small children"}	Altitude warning: Elevations range 6,000-10,000 feet. Altitude affects small children—acclimate slowly and watch for symptoms	\N	2026-02-02 15:20:41.653+00	2026-02-06 03:28:54.899895+00	[{"name": "places/ChIJvzhBwQdWnYARQmdmeqfYNI8/reviews/Ci9DQUlRQUNvZENodHljRjlvT2tGUGMzaEtibTFDYTFFdFgzTnRSMEl6ZVZaRE9FRRAB", "text": {"text": "We went on Nov. 3 only to find out the road to the park was closed to vehicles. Possibly due to snow and rock slides. Nevertheless, we tried to enjoy whatever we could get access to like the Sulphur works. Got some nice pictures. We would like to visit again in the spring and fully enjoy what the park has to offer.", "languageCode": "en"}, "rating": 5, "publishTime": "2025-11-13T21:31:32.541318316Z", "originalText": {"text": "We went on Nov. 3 only to find out the road to the park was closed to vehicles. Possibly due to snow and rock slides. Nevertheless, we tried to enjoy whatever we could get access to like the Sulphur works. Got some nice pictures. We would like to visit again in the spring and fully enjoy what the park has to offer.", "languageCode": "en"}, "googleMapsUri": "https://www.google.com/maps/reviews/data=!4m6!14m5!1m4!2m3!1sCi9DQUlRQUNvZENodHljRjlvT2tGUGMzaEtibTFDYTFFdFgzTnRSMEl6ZVZaRE9FRRAB!2m1!1s0x809d5607c14138bf:0x8f34d8a77a666742", "flagContentUri": "https://www.google.com/local/content/rap/report?postId=Ci9DQUlRQUNvZENodHljRjlvT2tGUGMzaEtibTFDYTFFdFgzTnRSMEl6ZVZaRE9FRRAB&d=17924085&t=1", "authorAttribution": {"uri": "https://www.google.com/maps/contrib/106667560933024241507/reviews", "photoUri": "https://lh3.googleusercontent.com/a-/ALV-UjVcJQ4jQ15miFkg7CLvGSxep5-lZ_E0iNuSrDbuKvnDha9o1Fkj=s128-c0x00000000-cc-rp-mo-ba5", "displayName": "Joe Joe H"}, "relativePublishTimeDescription": "2 months ago"}, {"name": "places/ChIJvzhBwQdWnYARQmdmeqfYNI8/reviews/Ci9DQUlRQUNvZENodHljRjlvT2padVRVeFdNa3N3Y0hObWRUTlZhbHBKUjBOM2VHYxAB", "text": {"text": "What an amazing hidden gem! This was well worth the drive from Seattle to spend a few days. Our first day we did multiple smaller trails that took us to amazing lakes and vents. The second day we hiked Mount Lassen and it was defiantly something to remember. Would 100% come back next season as a weekend adventure.", "languageCode": "en"}, "rating": 5, "publishTime": "2025-08-15T16:51:28.621998669Z", "originalText": {"text": "What an amazing hidden gem! This was well worth the drive from Seattle to spend a few days. Our first day we did multiple smaller trails that took us to amazing lakes and vents. The second day we hiked Mount Lassen and it was defiantly something to remember. Would 100% come back next season as a weekend adventure.", "languageCode": "en"}, "googleMapsUri": "https://www.google.com/maps/reviews/data=!4m6!14m5!1m4!2m3!1sCi9DQUlRQUNvZENodHljRjlvT2padVRVeFdNa3N3Y0hObWRUTlZhbHBKUjBOM2VHYxAB!2m1!1s0x809d5607c14138bf:0x8f34d8a77a666742", "flagContentUri": "https://www.google.com/local/content/rap/report?postId=Ci9DQUlRQUNvZENodHljRjlvT2padVRVeFdNa3N3Y0hObWRUTlZhbHBKUjBOM2VHYxAB&d=17924085&t=1", "authorAttribution": {"uri": "https://www.google.com/maps/contrib/109041776817003111637/reviews", "photoUri": "https://lh3.googleusercontent.com/a-/ALV-UjVyIFE9Z4PHZCcKsMaTdkZgaB7FWqpnpvM31K_1FC-V6o5ZOKHc=s128-c0x00000000-cc-rp-mo-ba4", "displayName": "Sarah Leedom"}, "relativePublishTimeDescription": "5 months ago"}, {"name": "places/ChIJvzhBwQdWnYARQmdmeqfYNI8/reviews/Ci9DQUlRQUNvZENodHljRjlvT2xwalQxQkxiek5DZUhVM1YySXdPRkpqZWxkVGVuYxAB", "text": {"text": "Beautiful park with various sights to check out and enjoy! Lots of hiking trails. It wasn’t busy when we went which was lovely. So many unique features that we appreciated! If you get the opportunity to go during summer or early fall, definitely check it out!", "languageCode": "en"}, "rating": 5, "publishTime": "2025-10-06T02:57:48.915744940Z", "originalText": {"text": "Beautiful park with various sights to check out and enjoy! Lots of hiking trails. It wasn’t busy when we went which was lovely. So many unique features that we appreciated! If you get the opportunity to go during summer or early fall, definitely check it out!", "languageCode": "en"}, "googleMapsUri": "https://www.google.com/maps/reviews/data=!4m6!14m5!1m4!2m3!1sCi9DQUlRQUNvZENodHljRjlvT2xwalQxQkxiek5DZUhVM1YySXdPRkpqZWxkVGVuYxAB!2m1!1s0x809d5607c14138bf:0x8f34d8a77a666742", "flagContentUri": "https://www.google.com/local/content/rap/report?postId=Ci9DQUlRQUNvZENodHljRjlvT2xwalQxQkxiek5DZUhVM1YySXdPRkpqZWxkVGVuYxAB&d=17924085&t=1", "authorAttribution": {"uri": "https://www.google.com/maps/contrib/116841758469291172005/reviews", "photoUri": "https://lh3.googleusercontent.com/a/ACg8ocJr7RgEHdQX2Lxy7KJpPjwu1_l-1uoJBAZdDg1lbqO1iB_aqg=s128-c0x00000000-cc-rp-mo-ba5", "displayName": "Zoe Littmann"}, "relativePublishTimeDescription": "4 months ago"}, {"name": "places/ChIJvzhBwQdWnYARQmdmeqfYNI8/reviews/Ci9DQUlRQUNvZENodHljRjlvT2xobWEwUlVNRGg0VVVwMldGTllZamhCWW1adFdsRRAB", "text": {"text": "Excellent park, with easy access via a main loop.  Bumpass Hell is a must see.  Be prepared for elevation - arid, with walking being more strenuous than normal.  Take plenty of water, snacks, and sunscreen even in cooler weather.", "languageCode": "en"}, "rating": 5, "publishTime": "2025-10-25T16:18:25.722440129Z", "originalText": {"text": "Excellent park, with easy access via a main loop.  Bumpass Hell is a must see.  Be prepared for elevation - arid, with walking being more strenuous than normal.  Take plenty of water, snacks, and sunscreen even in cooler weather.", "languageCode": "en"}, "googleMapsUri": "https://www.google.com/maps/reviews/data=!4m6!14m5!1m4!2m3!1sCi9DQUlRQUNvZENodHljRjlvT2xobWEwUlVNRGg0VVVwMldGTllZamhCWW1adFdsRRAB!2m1!1s0x809d5607c14138bf:0x8f34d8a77a666742", "flagContentUri": "https://www.google.com/local/content/rap/report?postId=Ci9DQUlRQUNvZENodHljRjlvT2xobWEwUlVNRGg0VVVwMldGTllZamhCWW1adFdsRRAB&d=17924085&t=1", "authorAttribution": {"uri": "https://www.google.com/maps/contrib/112623092917391144957/reviews", "photoUri": "https://lh3.googleusercontent.com/a/ACg8ocKTCp0XRLKLHw_hJ5G0S8zzSRqDbKF9O4uFG957E8OQIRjlRw=s128-c0x00000000-cc-rp-mo-ba6", "displayName": "Michael Lynch"}, "relativePublishTimeDescription": "3 months ago"}, {"name": "places/ChIJvzhBwQdWnYARQmdmeqfYNI8/reviews/Ci9DQUlRQUNvZENodHljRjlvT201bWEwMDVSMjVFZGxoNFdFbHFSREZoU1cwM2NHYxAB", "text": {"text": "This was our first time in Lassen Volcanic National Park.    We visited in mid-October during the government shutdown.  On our first day, we learned that Lassen Volcanic National Park Highway was closed to vehicles except for some workers.  We were told that it was due to rock slides.  It rained/snowed the day before.  Of course, this didn’t stop my husband to explore the park when we learned that we were allowed to walk the highway and the trails.   We decided to walk to Bumpass Trailhead to Bumpass Hell.  We only met 3 visitors during our visit and we were the only ones walking the highway.  We walked around 14 miles and exhausted since it was uphill (~5 miles) to Bumpass Trailhead.  The views were amazing and rewarding which made the hike worthwhile.  On our second day, we were relieved that the Lassen Volcanic National Park Highway was opened later in the morning.   The view along the way was beautiful & it was ~30 miles to the other end (North Entrance) we hiked around Manzanita Lake.", "languageCode": "en"}, "rating": 5, "publishTime": "2025-11-10T04:21:18.231298573Z", "originalText": {"text": "This was our first time in Lassen Volcanic National Park.    We visited in mid-October during the government shutdown.  On our first day, we learned that Lassen Volcanic National Park Highway was closed to vehicles except for some workers.  We were told that it was due to rock slides.  It rained/snowed the day before.  Of course, this didn’t stop my husband to explore the park when we learned that we were allowed to walk the highway and the trails.   We decided to walk to Bumpass Trailhead to Bumpass Hell.  We only met 3 visitors during our visit and we were the only ones walking the highway.  We walked around 14 miles and exhausted since it was uphill (~5 miles) to Bumpass Trailhead.  The views were amazing and rewarding which made the hike worthwhile.  On our second day, we were relieved that the Lassen Volcanic National Park Highway was opened later in the morning.   The view along the way was beautiful & it was ~30 miles to the other end (North Entrance) we hiked around Manzanita Lake.", "languageCode": "en"}, "googleMapsUri": "https://www.google.com/maps/reviews/data=!4m6!14m5!1m4!2m3!1sCi9DQUlRQUNvZENodHljRjlvT201bWEwMDVSMjVFZGxoNFdFbHFSREZoU1cwM2NHYxAB!2m1!1s0x809d5607c14138bf:0x8f34d8a77a666742", "flagContentUri": "https://www.google.com/local/content/rap/report?postId=Ci9DQUlRQUNvZENodHljRjlvT201bWEwMDVSMjVFZGxoNFdFbHFSREZoU1cwM2NHYxAB&d=17924085&t=1", "authorAttribution": {"uri": "https://www.google.com/maps/contrib/103112219754407036497/reviews", "photoUri": "https://lh3.googleusercontent.com/a-/ALV-UjWYH-I4RvrfRUXl77LorTgEYOQ9Iu5u4MQ2EyTsBvUTqYmBsYb3iA=s128-c0x00000000-cc-rp-mo-ba7", "displayName": "Catherine Hunt"}, "relativePublishTimeDescription": "2 months ago"}]	Lassen Volcanic National Park is consistently praised as an amazing hidden gem with unique volcanic features, beautiful lakes, and diverse hiking trails that aren't crowded. Visitors love the park's distinctive attractions like Bumpass Hell and the scenic main loop road, though seasonal road closures due to snow and rockslides can limit access during certain times of year.	{"summary": "Lassen Volcanic National Park is consistently praised as an amazing hidden gem with unique volcanic features, beautiful lakes, and diverse hiking trails that aren't crowded. Visitors love the park's distinctive attractions like Bumpass Hell and the scenic main loop road, though seasonal road closures due to snow and rockslides can limit access during certain times of year.", "negative": [{"text": "Be prepared for elevation - arid, with walking being more strenuous than normal.", "author": "Michael Lynch", "rating": 5}, {"text": "We went on Nov. 3 only to find out the road to the park was closed to vehicles. Possibly due to snow and rock slides.", "author": "Joe Joe H", "rating": 5}], "positive": [{"text": "What an amazing hidden gem! Our first day we did multiple smaller trails that took us to amazing lakes and vents.", "author": "Sarah Leedom", "rating": 5}, {"text": "It wasn't busy when we went which was lovely. So many unique features that we appreciated!", "author": "Zoe Littmann", "rating": 5}, {"text": "Excellent park, with easy access via a main loop. Bumpass Hell is a must see.", "author": "Michael Lynch", "rating": 5}], "last_updated": "2026-02-06T03:28:54.713Z"}	2026-02-06 03:28:48.978+00	national_park	\N	\N
c510c0a1-b4e7-459f-aee5-80a2c5fd563f	b201a860-05a3-4ddc-bb89-4c4271177271	Humboldt Redwoods via Giant Redwoods RV Park	Giant Redwoods RV & Cabin Destination accepts big rigs with full hookups, a private Eel River beach, playground, and outdoor movie theater. It sits steps from the 32-mile Avenue of the Giants. The park also houses the Kellogg Travel Log—the world's first RV, carved from a single redwood log. Ancient Redwoods RV Park offers similar big-rig access near the Immortal Tree.	17,000 acres of the largest remaining old-growth redwood forest on Earth—including the 362-foot fallen Dyerville Giant—but state park campgrounds max at 24 feet.	state_parks	\N	400 Myers Ave, Myers Flat, CA 95554, USA	Weott	CA	40.2622575	-123.8777408	ChIJI_oU-YWJ1FQRrqUEysgo4WY	4.5	643	\N	{"hookups": "full", "cell_coverage": "poor", "road_accessibility": "State park max 24ft—use Giant Redwoods RV Park for big rigs"}	f	\N	\N	55.00	USD	$55-65/night with full hookups at Giant Redwoods RV Park	{"best": ["march", "april", "may", "june", "july", "august", "september", "october", "november"], "notes": "Open March-November"}	6-7 hours	\N	{"scenic_beauty": 5, "solitude_level": 3, "adventure_level": 3, "family_friendly": 5, "relaxation_factor": 5}	{"topics": ["Redwood ecology", "Fire resistance", "Old-growth forests"]}	{"parker": {"suitable": true, "activities": ["Measuring tree circumference", "Learning why redwoods survive fire", "Tracking hiking distances"], "engagement_level": 5}, "xander": {"suitable": true, "activities": ["Running through fern undergrowth", "Splashing in Eel River", "Looking UP at giants"], "engagement_level": 5}, "charlotte": {"suitable": true, "activities": ["Walking through hollow logs", "Handling banana slugs gently", "Making bark rubbings"], "engagement_level": 5}}	http://giantredwoodsrv.com/	(707) 943-9999	\N	researching	0	{redwoods,old-growth,avenue-of-giants}	{}	{}	\N	\N	2026-02-02 15:20:39.135+00	2026-02-06 03:49:25.604889+00	[{"name": "places/ChIJI_oU-YWJ1FQRrqUEysgo4WY/reviews/Ci9DQUlRQUNvZENodHljRjlvT2pSeU5FZExWalJUT1hWTFpXWlZhRWRrZVROb1EyYxAB", "text": {"text": "What a fantastic stay! Kimberley was so friendly and helpful during our check in and for the duration of our stay. The site is well maintained, very clean and well laid out, and in a beautiful and tranquil setting on the river. We initially only booked a 1 night stay but extended it as we loved the campground so much. The sites are spacious and not too close together. Playground a huge hit with our toddler too. We would definitely visit again.", "languageCode": "en"}, "rating": 5, "publishTime": "2025-10-25T23:40:40.059383656Z", "originalText": {"text": "What a fantastic stay! Kimberley was so friendly and helpful during our check in and for the duration of our stay. The site is well maintained, very clean and well laid out, and in a beautiful and tranquil setting on the river. We initially only booked a 1 night stay but extended it as we loved the campground so much. The sites are spacious and not too close together. Playground a huge hit with our toddler too. We would definitely visit again.", "languageCode": "en"}, "googleMapsUri": "https://www.google.com/maps/reviews/data=!4m6!14m5!1m4!2m3!1sCi9DQUlRQUNvZENodHljRjlvT2pSeU5FZExWalJUT1hWTFpXWlZhRWRrZVROb1EyYxAB!2m1!1s0x54d48985f914fa23:0x66e128c8ca04a5ae", "flagContentUri": "https://www.google.com/local/content/rap/report?postId=Ci9DQUlRQUNvZENodHljRjlvT2pSeU5FZExWalJUT1hWTFpXWlZhRWRrZVROb1EyYxAB&d=17924085&t=1", "authorAttribution": {"uri": "https://www.google.com/maps/contrib/103646399944437111897/reviews", "photoUri": "https://lh3.googleusercontent.com/a/ACg8ocKK010tp6GeSTm9IbSklijQqR-qLxZ9gy7gO1FZuuvn8yGjVPA=s128-c0x00000000-cc-rp-mo", "displayName": "Georgina Eales"}, "relativePublishTimeDescription": "3 months ago"}, {"name": "places/ChIJI_oU-YWJ1FQRrqUEysgo4WY/reviews/Ci9DQUlRQUNvZENodHljRjlvT2xaSVVIRlhNV05LYkRCR2NFbHdUMUZyVm5aaGRWRRAB", "text": {"text": "My wife and I recently camped in our RV at Giant Redwoods RV and couldn’t be happier we did!  From the moment we arrived, we knew we were in for something special.  Very friendly and accommodating owners who keep their park in immaculate condition.  Everything is clean and tidy!  Loved the peace and serenity of the redwoods, river, and layout of the park.  The park is set in the perfect location to view the various redwood groves along the Avenue of the Giants.  They are definitely the most prestigious of all other camping spots in the area.  We look forward to another visit someday soon!", "languageCode": "en"}, "rating": 5, "publishTime": "2025-10-24T16:36:33.465422023Z", "originalText": {"text": "My wife and I recently camped in our RV at Giant Redwoods RV and couldn’t be happier we did!  From the moment we arrived, we knew we were in for something special.  Very friendly and accommodating owners who keep their park in immaculate condition.  Everything is clean and tidy!  Loved the peace and serenity of the redwoods, river, and layout of the park.  The park is set in the perfect location to view the various redwood groves along the Avenue of the Giants.  They are definitely the most prestigious of all other camping spots in the area.  We look forward to another visit someday soon!", "languageCode": "en"}, "googleMapsUri": "https://www.google.com/maps/reviews/data=!4m6!14m5!1m4!2m3!1sCi9DQUlRQUNvZENodHljRjlvT2xaSVVIRlhNV05LYkRCR2NFbHdUMUZyVm5aaGRWRRAB!2m1!1s0x54d48985f914fa23:0x66e128c8ca04a5ae", "flagContentUri": "https://www.google.com/local/content/rap/report?postId=Ci9DQUlRQUNvZENodHljRjlvT2xaSVVIRlhNV05LYkRCR2NFbHdUMUZyVm5aaGRWRRAB&d=17924085&t=1", "authorAttribution": {"uri": "https://www.google.com/maps/contrib/105172064373967382307/reviews", "photoUri": "https://lh3.googleusercontent.com/a/ACg8ocKVCZ8coUYqzYa93Ak7rvElTXwkfSr3PjsX_pR7imyPy_DOyQ=s128-c0x00000000-cc-rp-mo", "displayName": "Greg Bostrom"}, "relativePublishTimeDescription": "3 months ago"}, {"name": "places/ChIJI_oU-YWJ1FQRrqUEysgo4WY/reviews/Ci9DQUlRQUNvZENodHljRjlvT2xJMmJXMTNhM2x2UWxCUlJFVnVTbFp2Tm1aeE0zYxAB", "text": {"text": "Visited from Pleasanton, CA/Washington D.C. to run the Humboldt Redwoods Half Marathon!!! It was such a treat to stay here. The cabin was so cute and the amenities were awesome! It's so close to the redwood forests for hiking (or in our case, running). We are forever grateful that the owners let us do a late checkout so we could come back to the cabin and shower after our race before the 5 hour drive home.\\n\\nWe will be back! My expectations were significantly exceeded. The hot shower was amazing and loved the private bathroom. The fridge with the freezer & microwave was  very helpful for our food!\\n\\nAnd Maya (camp pup) was adorable!", "languageCode": "en"}, "rating": 5, "publishTime": "2025-10-13T21:46:03.616814170Z", "originalText": {"text": "Visited from Pleasanton, CA/Washington D.C. to run the Humboldt Redwoods Half Marathon!!! It was such a treat to stay here. The cabin was so cute and the amenities were awesome! It's so close to the redwood forests for hiking (or in our case, running). We are forever grateful that the owners let us do a late checkout so we could come back to the cabin and shower after our race before the 5 hour drive home.\\n\\nWe will be back! My expectations were significantly exceeded. The hot shower was amazing and loved the private bathroom. The fridge with the freezer & microwave was  very helpful for our food!\\n\\nAnd Maya (camp pup) was adorable!", "languageCode": "en"}, "googleMapsUri": "https://www.google.com/maps/reviews/data=!4m6!14m5!1m4!2m3!1sCi9DQUlRQUNvZENodHljRjlvT2xJMmJXMTNhM2x2UWxCUlJFVnVTbFp2Tm1aeE0zYxAB!2m1!1s0x54d48985f914fa23:0x66e128c8ca04a5ae", "flagContentUri": "https://www.google.com/local/content/rap/report?postId=Ci9DQUlRQUNvZENodHljRjlvT2xJMmJXMTNhM2x2UWxCUlJFVnVTbFp2Tm1aeE0zYxAB&d=17924085&t=1", "authorAttribution": {"uri": "https://www.google.com/maps/contrib/110837332805628568911/reviews", "photoUri": "https://lh3.googleusercontent.com/a-/ALV-UjWHaCBK5kp3tiKJVhxejp6V9bB_bV0WzmTmBRdd9Z0iKBpWigQ=s128-c0x00000000-cc-rp-mo", "displayName": "Jessica"}, "relativePublishTimeDescription": "3 months ago"}, {"name": "places/ChIJI_oU-YWJ1FQRrqUEysgo4WY/reviews/Ci9DQUlRQUNvZENodHljRjlvT21GRFowUnhRelI0U2pKSFVGOUNZMU40Tm5wdGRVRRAB", "text": {"text": "An exceptional park located in the heart of Humboldt Redwoods State Park. Easy access to many prominent groves (Founder’s and Rockefeller are as good as it gets!) and beautiful trails. Have stayed here on 3  to 4 occasions over past few years and have had a pleasant experience each time. If you plan to be out late into the night be sure to coordinate with park staff to ensure gate access after 9pm. You DO NOT want to be locked out on the other side of the gate. It’s unfortunate that surrounding neighborhood is depressed (similar to much of the area) and a bit spooky, yet the park is secure and very nice. Will surely stay here again.", "languageCode": "en"}, "rating": 5, "publishTime": "2025-10-15T02:46:04.352947943Z", "originalText": {"text": "An exceptional park located in the heart of Humboldt Redwoods State Park. Easy access to many prominent groves (Founder’s and Rockefeller are as good as it gets!) and beautiful trails. Have stayed here on 3  to 4 occasions over past few years and have had a pleasant experience each time. If you plan to be out late into the night be sure to coordinate with park staff to ensure gate access after 9pm. You DO NOT want to be locked out on the other side of the gate. It’s unfortunate that surrounding neighborhood is depressed (similar to much of the area) and a bit spooky, yet the park is secure and very nice. Will surely stay here again.", "languageCode": "en"}, "googleMapsUri": "https://www.google.com/maps/reviews/data=!4m6!14m5!1m4!2m3!1sCi9DQUlRQUNvZENodHljRjlvT21GRFowUnhRelI0U2pKSFVGOUNZMU40Tm5wdGRVRRAB!2m1!1s0x54d48985f914fa23:0x66e128c8ca04a5ae", "flagContentUri": "https://www.google.com/local/content/rap/report?postId=Ci9DQUlRQUNvZENodHljRjlvT21GRFowUnhRelI0U2pKSFVGOUNZMU40Tm5wdGRVRRAB&d=17924085&t=1", "authorAttribution": {"uri": "https://www.google.com/maps/contrib/101311661556124789419/reviews", "photoUri": "https://lh3.googleusercontent.com/a/ACg8ocIdVjN1ULNhathkE3HBP6VAlN5MpDw9yCblLRU7APjLcisCRA=s128-c0x00000000-cc-rp-mo", "displayName": "Eric Bergh"}, "relativePublishTimeDescription": "3 months ago"}, {"name": "places/ChIJI_oU-YWJ1FQRrqUEysgo4WY/reviews/Ci9DQUlRQUNvZENodHljRjlvT2pSUFRGUmlVM2syYjBoeFVGVjVZVkIzVDBoQk4xRRAB", "text": {"text": "Drove in late and were very well received and accommodated by our host, Mike. This was our first experience with our camper. The facility was incredibly clean and woodsy along the Eel River.\\nOn our way back down the coast, we again stayed here. Mike remembered us and again we were perfectly hosted. We will make a point of staying here on our way to Alaska next year. Our rescue dog (border collie), Rosie, loved exploring along the Eel River adjacent to rv park.", "languageCode": "en"}, "rating": 5, "publishTime": "2025-10-26T00:04:19.382053124Z", "originalText": {"text": "Drove in late and were very well received and accommodated by our host, Mike. This was our first experience with our camper. The facility was incredibly clean and woodsy along the Eel River.\\nOn our way back down the coast, we again stayed here. Mike remembered us and again we were perfectly hosted. We will make a point of staying here on our way to Alaska next year. Our rescue dog (border collie), Rosie, loved exploring along the Eel River adjacent to rv park.", "languageCode": "en"}, "googleMapsUri": "https://www.google.com/maps/reviews/data=!4m6!14m5!1m4!2m3!1sCi9DQUlRQUNvZENodHljRjlvT2pSUFRGUmlVM2syYjBoeFVGVjVZVkIzVDBoQk4xRRAB!2m1!1s0x54d48985f914fa23:0x66e128c8ca04a5ae", "flagContentUri": "https://www.google.com/local/content/rap/report?postId=Ci9DQUlRQUNvZENodHljRjlvT2pSUFRGUmlVM2syYjBoeFVGVjVZVkIzVDBoQk4xRRAB&d=17924085&t=1", "authorAttribution": {"uri": "https://www.google.com/maps/contrib/109552680024956866511/reviews", "photoUri": "https://lh3.googleusercontent.com/a/ACg8ocJ6GJStqU8Htqkjr4twrTmf0cEC5ughXTOzzzN1wMXfnIOSVA=s128-c0x00000000-cc-rp-mo", "displayName": "Bruce Bell"}, "relativePublishTimeDescription": "3 months ago"}]	Giant Redwoods RV Park receives exceptional praise for its pristine condition, friendly hosts, and prime location along the Eel River with easy access to redwood groves. Guests consistently highlight the peaceful, well-maintained setting and accommodating staff who go above and beyond to make stays memorable. The park appears to be a standout destination that exceeds expectations and keeps visitors coming back.	{"summary": "Giant Redwoods RV Park receives exceptional praise for its pristine condition, friendly hosts, and prime location along the Eel River with easy access to redwood groves. Guests consistently highlight the peaceful, well-maintained setting and accommodating staff who go above and beyond to make stays memorable. The park appears to be a standout destination that exceeds expectations and keeps visitors coming back.", "negative": [{"text": "It's unfortunate that surrounding neighborhood is depressed (similar to much of the area) and a bit spooky, yet the park is secure and very nice.", "author": "Eric Bergh", "rating": 5}], "positive": [{"text": "Playground a huge hit with our toddler too. The sites are spacious and not too close together.", "author": "Georgina Eales", "rating": 5}, {"text": "Our rescue dog (border collie), Rosie, loved exploring along the Eel River adjacent to rv park.", "author": "Bruce Bell", "rating": 5}, {"text": "Very friendly and accommodating owners who keep their park in immaculate condition. Everything is clean and tidy!", "author": "Greg Bostrom", "rating": 5}], "last_updated": "2026-02-06T03:49:25.525Z"}	2026-02-06 03:49:20.27+00	private_rv_park	\N	\N
\.
